pe":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aad443b7b4887d0b35b8b645b50e0ba","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b4d1-89b2-74e3-a6c3-9629e0e8826a"},"summary":[{"text":"**Inspecting Composio tools list**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_iwNq7qUbOyL7EKEx3O4Qk1k0","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aad443cbdac87d08897b3845bd72328","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\n  cmd: \"composio --help\\ncomposio tools --help\",\n  workdir: \"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170\",\n  yield_time_ms: 10000,\n  max_output_tokens: 20000\n});\ntext(r.output);","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789740088.728119,"turn_id":"01a0b4d1-89b2-74e3-a6c3-9629e0e8826a"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_iwNq7qUbOyL7EKEx3O4Qk1k0","id":"ctco_01a0b4d2-953c-77d1-838c-141ee04a5f5d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789740094.780661,"turn_id":"01a0b4d1-89b2-74e3-a6c3-9629e0e8826a"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.0 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\nConnect AI agents to external tools. search, execute, link, proxy, and run let you\ntake actions across 1000+ apps directly; if you can describe it, it is probably supported.\nTry execute sooner than you'd think — it validates inputs, checks connections, and tells\nyou what to fix.\n\nUse dev when you are building an agent with Composio's SDK and want scaffolding,\nplayground execution, logs, and developer-scoped management commands.\n\nUSAGE\n  composio \u003ccommand\u003e [options]\n  composio --help [simple|default|full]\n\nMODE\n  default help\n\nCORE COMMANDS\n  search\n    Find tools by use case across all toolkits/apps.\n    Usage: composio search \u003cquery...\u003e [--toolkits text] [--limit integer] [--human]\n      \u003cquery...\u003e          One or more semantic use-case queries (e.g. \"send emails\" \"github issues\")\n      --toolkits          Filter by toolkit slugs, comma-separated\n      --limit             Maximum number of results (1-1000)\n      --human             Show formatted output instead of default JSON\n\n  execute\n    Execute a tool. Validates inputs and connections automatically; use it aggressively.\n    Usage: composio execute \u003cslug\u003e [-d, --data text] [--account selector] [--file path] [--dry-run] [--get-schema] | execute -p \u003cslug\u003e -d \u003ctext\u003e \u003cslug\u003e -d \u003ctext\u003e ...\n      \u003cslug\u003e              Tool slug (e.g. \"GITHUB_CREATE_ISSUE\")\n      -d, --data          JSON or JS-style object arguments, e.g. -d '{ repo: \"foo\" }', @file, or - for stdin\n      -p, --parallel      Execute repeated \u003cslug\u003e -d \u003ctext\u003e pairs concurrently\n      --account           Select a connected account by alias, word_id, or account ID\n      --file              Inject a local file path into the single file_uploadable input\n      --dry-run           Validate and preview the tool call without executing it\n      --get-schema        Fetch and print the CLI-facing input schema\n\n  link\n    Connect your account for a toolkit/app.\n    Usage: composio link [\u003ctoolkit\u003e] [--alias text]\n      \u003ctoolkit\u003e           Toolkit slug to link (e.g. \"github\", \"gmail\")\n      --alias             Alias for this connected account\n\n  run\n    Run inline TS/JS code with shimmed CLI commands; injected execute(), search(), proxy(), experimental_subAgent(), and z (zod).\n    Usage: composio run \u003ccode\u003e [-- ...args] | run [-f, --file text] [-- ...args] [--dry-run]\n      \u003ccode\u003e              Inline Bun ESNext code to evaluate\n      -f, --file          Run a TS/JS file instead of inline code\n      --dry-run           Preview execute() calls without running remote actions\n\n  proxy\n    curl-like access to any toolkit API through Composio using your connected account.\n    Usage: composio proxy \u003curl\u003e --toolkit text [--account selector] [-X method] [-H header]... [-d data]\n      \u003curl\u003e               Full API endpoint URL\n      --toolkit           Toolkit slug whose connected account should be used\n      --account           Connected account alias, word_id, or account ID\n      -X, --method        HTTP method (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, PATCH)\n      -H, --header        Header in \"Name: value\" format. Repeat for multiple.\n      -d, --data          Request body as raw text, JSON, @file, or - for stdin\n\n  Typical flow: search → execute (link and tools when needed)\n\nTOOLS\n  composio tools info \u003cslug\u003e        Print tool summary and cache its schema\n  composio tools list \u003ctoolkit\u003e     List tools available in a toolkit\n  composio triggers info \u003cslug\u003e     Print trigger type details and schema summaries\n  composio triggers list \u003ctoolkit\u003e  List available trigger types in a toolkit\n  composio artifacts cwd            Print the cwd-scoped session artifact directory\n\n\nEXAMPLES\n  # Find tools — supports multiple queries at once\n  composio search \"send an email\" \"create github issue\"\n  composio search \"list calendar events\" --toolkits google_calendar --limit 5\n\n  # Connect your account for a toolkit\n  composio link github\n\n  # Execute a tool\n  composio execute GITHUB_CREATE_ISSUE -d '{ owner: \"acme\", repo: \"app\", title: \"Bug\" }'\n\n  # Execute multiple tools in parallel\n  composio execute -p GMAIL_SEND_EMAIL -d '{ recipient_email: \"a@b.com\", subject: \"Hi\" }' \\\n                     SLACK_SEND_A_MESSAGE_TO_A_SLACK_CHANNEL -d '{ channel: \"general\", text: \"Hello\" }'\n\n  # Call an API directly through proxy\n  composio proxy https://gmail.googleapis.com/gmail/v1/users/me/profile --toolkit gmail\n\n  # Run a script with injected helpers\n  composio run 'const me = await execute(\"GITHUB_GET_THE_AUTHENTICATED_USER\"); console.log(me)'\n\n  # Manually install the composio skill when auto-install fails\n  composio --install-skill claude\n  composio --install-skill composio-cli codex\n\n  # Run a multi-step script with Promise.all\n  composio run '\n    const [emails, issues] = await Promise.all([\n      execute(\"GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS\", { max_results: 5 }),\n      execute(\"GITHUB_LIST_REPOSITORY_ISSUES\", { owner: \"acme\", repo: \"app\", state: \"open\" }),\n    ]);\n    const brief = await experimental_subAgent(`Summarize:\\n${emails.prompt()}\\n${issues.prompt()}`);\n    console.log(brief);\n  '\n\nDEVELOPER COMMANDS\n  dev       Developer workflows and management: init, logs, projects, toolkits, accounts, and triggers.\n  generate  Generate type stubs for toolkits, tools, and triggers (TypeScript | Python).\n\nACCOUNT\n  setup    Install or uninstall agent plugins\n  login    Log in to Composio\n  logout   Log out from Composio\n  whoami   Show current account info\n  orgs     Manage current organization context (list, switch)\n  version  Display CLI version\n  upgrade  Upgrade CLI to the latest version\n  config   View and manage CLI configuration\n\nFILES  (composio files --help)\n  ~/.composio/\n    CLI configuration and cache directory. Contains your auth state\n    (user_data.json), runtime settings (config.json), cached tool definitions\n    (tools.json, toolkits.json),\n    trigger types, and per-org consumer caches. These caches speed up\n    repeated commands — safe to delete, they will be re-fetched on next use.\n\n  /tmp/composio/\n    Session artifacts directory. Each CLI session gets a unique subdirectory\n    scoped to your working directory. Stores session history and files\n    created during run and execute commands (e.g. downloaded attachments,\n    generated outputs). Use `composio artifacts cwd` to print the path for\n    the current directory's session.\n\nFLAGS\n  -h, --help [mode]  Show help for command (simple, default, full)\n  --version      Show composio version\n  --install-skill [skill-name] \u003cclaude|codex|openclaw\u003e\n                  Manually install the composio skill for a supported agent\n\nLEARN MORE\n  Use `composio \u003ccommand\u003e --help` for more information about a command.\n  Documentation: https://docs.composio.dev\n\n\nUSAGE\n  composio tools \u003ccommand\u003e\n\nDESCRIPTION\n  Browse and inspect tools before executing them.\n\nEXAMPLES\n  composio tools list gmail\n  composio tools info GMAIL_SEND_EMAIL\n\nSEE ALSO\n  composio search \"\u003cquery\u003e\"               Find tools by use case\n  composio execute \u003cslug\u003e -d '{ ... }'    Execute a tool directly\n\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aad4442a5a887d08269db6cf8c4e621","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b4d1-89b2-74e3-a6c3-9629e0e8826a"},"summary":[{"text":"**Exploring custom_skillplane tools list**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_Au0Z8wkFmDwF2Sw8CYPe0rg1","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aad4443997887d0a68dd7ae13f11a66","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\n  cmd: \"composio tools list custom_skillplane\",\n  workdir: \"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170\",\n  yield_time_ms: 10000,\n  max_output_tokens: 20000\n});\ntext(r.output);","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789740095.325142,"turn_id":"01a0b4d1-89b2-74e3-a6c3-9629e0e8826a"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_Au0Z8wkFmDwF2Sw8CYPe0rg1","id":"ctco_01a0b4d2-afcb-7770-9f22-fac04efcce83","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789740101.579272,"turn_id":"01a0b4d1-89b2-74e3-a6c3-9629e0e8826a"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.0 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aad444c8a3887d09c81c5d848be713b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b4d1-89b2-74e3-a6c3-9629e0e8826a"},"summary":[{"text":"**Planning MCP resource exploration**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_XT6pv8J1gdoxuTQDfzbatuo8","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aad444ef11c87d0a60db20f07f28420","input":"const out = await Promise.all([\n  tools.list_mcp_resources({}),\n  tools.list_mcp_resource_templates({})\n]);\ntext(JSON.stringify(out));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789740102.106707,"turn_id":"01a0b4d1-89b2-74e3-a6c3-9629e0e8826a"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_XT6pv8J1gdoxuTQDfzbatuo8","id":"ctco_01a0b4d2-e415-7c13-a7e9-3087b5ff3e62","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789740114.965544,"turn_id":"01a0b4d1-89b2-74e3-a6c3-9629e0e8826a"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.8 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 12773)\nTotal output lines: 1\n\n[\"{\\\"resources\\\":[{\\\"server\\\":\\\"codex_apps\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"plugin://plugins~Plugin_b141909e13248191b34f99e93996a4a1\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"plugins~Plugin_b141909e13248191b34f99e93996a4a1\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Cloudflare\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Cloudflare platform plugin with curated skills for Workers, Wrangler, and Agents SDK plus the official Cloudflare API MCP server.\\\",\\\"mimeType\\\":\\\"mcp/plugin\\\",\\\"_meta\\\":{\\\"plugin_id\\\":\\\"plugins~Plugin_b141909e13248191b34f99e93996a4a1\\\",\\\"plugin_name\\\":\\\"cloudflare\\\",\\\"plugin_release_id\\\":\\\"pluginrel_6a27315580188191b2288f4ebfdce52a\\\",\\\"plugin_release_version\\\":\\\"0.1.2\\\",\\\"apps\\\":[],\\\"skills\\\":[\\\"skill://plugins~Plugin_b141909e13248191b34f99e93996a4a1/agents-sdk\\\",\\\"skill://plugins~Plugin_b141909e13248191b34f99e93996a4a1/building-ai-agent-on-cloudflare\\\",\\\"skill://plugins~Plugin_b141909e13248191b34f99e93996a4a1/building-mcp-server-on-cloudflare\\\",\\\"skill://plugins~Plugin_b141909e13248191b34f99e93996a4a1/cloudflare\\\",\\\"skill://plugins~Plugin_b141909e13248191b34f99e93996a4a1/durable-objects\\\",\\\"skill://plugins~Plugin_b141909e13248191b34f99e93996a4a1/sandbox-sdk\\\",\\\"skill://plugins~Plugin_b141909e13248191b34f99e93996a4a1/web-perf\\\",\\\"skill://plugins~Plugin_b141909e13248191b34f99e93996a4a1/workers-best-practices\\\",\\\"skill://plugins~Plugin_b141909e13248191b34f99e93996a4a1/wrangler\\\"],\\\"requires_executor\\\":false,\\\"mcp_servers\\\":[{\\\"key\\\":\\\"cloudflare-api\\\",\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"http\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://mcp.cloudflare.com/mcp\\\",\\\"note\\\":\\\"Official Cloudflare API MCP server. Uses OAuth on first connection, with optional bearer-token auth for automation. Provides token-efficient access to the Cloudflare API via search() and execute().\\\"}}],\\\"contents\\\":[\\\"bundle\\\"],\\\"bundle\\\":\\\"plugin://plugins~Plugin_b141909e13248191b34f99e93996a4a1/bundle\\\"}},{\\\"server\\\":\\\"codex_apps\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"plugin://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Default templates\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"OpenAI default document, presentation, and spreadsheet templates.\\\",\\\"mimeType\\\":\\\"mcp/plugin\\\",\\\"_meta\\\":{\\\"plugin_id\\\":\\\"plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f\\\",\\\"plugin_name\\\":\\\"openai-templates\\\",\\\"plugin_release_id\\\":\\\"pluginrel_6a6ced4ebc8c8191bf7c17972c03db1c\\\",\\\"plugin_release_version\\\":\\\"0.1.1\\\",\\\"apps\\\":[\\\"app://connector_openai_default_templates\\\"],\\\"skills\\\":[\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-analytics-dashboard\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-business-review\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-design-report\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-experiment-analysis\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-financial-budget\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-investment-committee-memo\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-legal-memorandum\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-market-trends-report\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-minimal-letterhead\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-operating-calendar\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-operating-review\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-project-kickoff\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-project-tracker\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-sales-pipeline\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-simple-dark-mode\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-simple-light-mode\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-strategy-memorandum\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-system-design\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-team-alignment\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/artifact-template-three-statement-forecast\\\"],\\\"requires_executor\\\":false,\\\"mcp_servers\\\":[],\\\"contents\\\":[\\\"bundle\\\"],\\\"bundle\\\":\\\"plugin://plugin_connector_1p_2330815c823c8191941e5dc465bb899f/bundle\\\"}},{\\\"server\\\":\\\"codex_apps\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"plugin://plugin_connector_68df038e0ba48191908c8434991bbac2\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"plugin_connector_68df038e0ba48191908c8434991bbac2\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Figma\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Bring your Figma workflows for creating, reviewing, and implementing designs into your ChatGPT and Codex conversations. Send your product screens to Figma where they become editable layers using your designs system components. Share these designs and collaborate with your team, or send them back to Codex to implement the designs in your codebase. You can also create and edit polished decks in Figma Slides, or generate diagrams in FigJam.\\\",\\\"mimeType\\\":\\\"mcp/plugin\\\",\\\"_meta\\\":{\\\"plugin_id\\\":\\\"plugin_connector_68df038e0ba48191908c8434991bbac2\\\",\\\"plugin_name\\\":\\\"figma\\\",\\\"plugin_release_id\\\":\\\"pluginrel_e7c1b4716d248191a704bf905d490b71\\\",\\\"plugin_release_version\\\":\\\"11.0.0\\\",\\\"apps\\\":[\\\"app://connector_68df038e0ba48191908c8434991bbac2\\\"],\\\"skills\\\":[\\\"skill://plugin_connector_68df038e0ba48191908c8434991bbac2/figma-code-connect\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_68df038e0ba48191908c8434991bbac2/figma-create-new-file\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_68df038e0ba48191908c8434991bbac2/figma-design-to-code\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_68df038e0ba48191908c8434991bbac2/figma-generate-design\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_68df038e0ba48191908c8434991bbac2/figma-generate-diagram\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_68df038e0ba48191908c8434991bbac2/figma-generate-library\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_68df038e0ba48191908c8434991bbac2/figma-generative-plugins\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_68df038e0ba48191908c8434991bbac2/figma-implement-motion\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_68df038e0ba48191908c8434991bbac2/figma-shaders\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_68df038e0ba48191908c8434991bbac2/figma-swiftui\\\",\\\"skill://plugin_connector_68df038e0ba48191908c8434991bbac2/figma-use\\\",\\\"skil