I, wait for reviewers, merge the PR, resolve threads, dismiss reviews, or begin another round in this run.\\n\\nExecution requirements:\\n\\n- Work only in `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170` on branch `codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910` for PR 170. Confirm the branch, full Git state, remote, PR head, and the `thyaravind` GitHub account before edits. Use `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other` for every `gh` command and the existing `origin` remote for pushes.\\n- Retrieve the pinned hosted version through Skillplane on every run and verify its semantic version, revision, and digest before acting. If it is unavailable or differs, do not mutate the repo; report the drift and disable this automation.\\n- Reuse `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170/.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md` as the compact persistent handoff. Create it if absent. Never stage or commit the ledger. Record skill identity/version/digest, round number, snapshot/head SHA, stable defect-family IDs, deduplicated valid root causes, affected contracts, dispositions, first-seen and last-attempted rounds, attempted repairs, regressions, verification evidence, required-check snapshot, convergence trend, and clean-streak state.\\n- Because the user requested convergence, perform the hosted workflow's broader subsystem assessment immediately on the first scheduled run before selecting a patch. State the shared invariant, producers/consumers, failure boundaries, coordinated repair, and verification criteria in the ledger. On later reset triggers, switch the ledger mode to assessment and reassess before further mutation. Do not publish another symptom patch if a complete repair cannot be established.\\n- Count root causes rather than comments. Preserve older valid blockers and deferred findings. Never infer convergence from missing history, an outdated hunk, resolved thread count, test count, or one clean snapshot.\\n\\nConvergence and stopping rules:\\n\\n1. Reset the clean streak whenever the complete snapshot has an Actionable defect, a valid Not Attempted code defect, a new defect, a recurring family, a fix-induced regression, a changed PR head between assessments, or any required CI/reviewer check is pending or failing in the single allowed immediate check snapshot.\\n2. A clean assessment requires: no code change or push in that round; zero Actionable root causes; zero valid Not Attempted code root causes; no unassessed review items; no recurring/deferred blocker; the PR head stayed stable; and all required CI/reviewer checks are terminal and successful in the one allowed immediate snapshot.\\n3. Declare convergence only after two consecutive clean scheduled assessments at the same PR head. Then update the ledger, disable automation `4442e7f3-60f4-4125-a8e4-c818ac40fc82` with `orca automations edit 4442e7f3-60f4-4125-a8e4-c818ac40fc82 --disabled --json`, verify with `orca automations show 4442e7f3-60f4-4125-a8e4-c818ac40fc82 --json`, report convergence, and stop.\\n4. If PR 170 is merged or closed, record the terminal state, disable and verify this automation, report that the schedule stopped, and stop without mutation.\\n5. If a reset-trigger assessment cannot establish a complete coordinated repair, or an external dependency blocks further progress, record the blocker, disable and verify this automation so it cannot repeat unsafe mutations, report the blocker, and stop.\\n\\nEnd every nonterminal run with the hosted workflow's explicit result buckets and: `One review round is complete. No post-push refetch or additional review loop was performed.`\",\n      \"precheck\": null,\n      \"agentId\": \"codex\",\n      \"runContext\": {\n        \"kind\": \"workspace-run\",\n        \"projectId\": \"github:21nco/super-functions\",\n        \"hostId\": \"local\",\n        \"projectHostSetupId\": \"940d3c77-482f-4eb2-8be7-88b4976ed269\",\n        \"repoId\": \"940d3c77-482f-4eb2-8be7-88b4976ed269\",\n        \"path\": \"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions\"\n      },\n      \"sourceContext\": {\n        \"kind\": \"task-source\",\n        \"provider\": \"github\",\n        \"projectId\": \"github:21nco/super-functions\",\n        \"hostId\": \"local\",\n        \"projectHostSetupId\": \"940d3c77-482f-4eb2-8be7-88b4976ed269\",\n        \"repoId\": \"940d3c77-482f-4eb2-8be7-88b4976ed269\",\n        \"providerIdentity\": {\n          \"provider\": \"github\",\n          \"owner\": \"21nCo\",\n          \"repo\": \"super-functions\"\n        },\n        \"accountLabel\": null\n      },\n      \"projectId\": \"940d3c77-482f-4eb2-8be7-88b4976ed269\",\n      \"executionTargetType\": \"local\",\n      \"executionTargetId\": \"local\",\n      \"schedulerOwner\": \"local_host_service\",\n      \"workspaceMode\": \"existing\",\n      \"workspaceId\": \"940d3c77-482f-4eb2-8be7-88b4976ed269::/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170\",\n      \"baseBranch\": null,\n      \"reuseSession\": true,\n      \"timezone\": \"Asia/Calcutta\",\n      \"rrule\": \"*/30 * * * *\",\n      \"dtstart\": 1789724424920,\n      \"enabled\": false,\n      \"nextRunAt\": 1789741800000,\n      \"missedRunPolicy\": \"run_once_within_grace\",\n      \"missedRunGraceMinutes\": 30,\n      \"createdAt\": 1789724424940,\n      \"updatedAt\": 1789740175175,\n      \"lastRunAt\": 1789740026262\n    },\n    \"owner\": {\n      \"selector\": {\n        \"kind\": \"self\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"_meta\": {\n    \"runtimeId\": \"d65efe84-489d-416f-8496-de36978a7659\"\n  }\n}\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aad4492c63487d0aa14a4ea7cdca276","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b4d1-89b2-74e3-a6c3-9629e0e8826a"},"summary":[{"text":"**Confirming terminal run due to automation disablement**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Verifying rollout IDs in memory lines**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_2bBdwSYISAVlALXxufJi8THc","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aad4497dbe087d08192e52919ed2399","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\n  cmd: \"sed -n '309,347p' /Users/serro/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\",\n  workdir: \"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170\",\n  yield_time_ms: 10000,\n  max_output_tokens: 12000\n});\ntext(r.output);","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789740175.988609,"turn_id":"01a0b4d1-89b2-74e3-a6c3-9629e0e8826a"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_2bBdwSYISAVlALXxufJi8THc","id":"ctco_01a0b4d3-f5c8-74d0-a1c2-9fca3adfd932","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789740185.032251,"turn_id":"01a0b4d1-89b2-74e3-a6c3-9629e0e8826a"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"# Task Group: September 15 Superfunctions PR #170 bounded remediation and dirty-dev reconciliation\nscope: Use for live hosted `pr-refetch-fix` work on McpFn PR #170, or scoped publication/reconciliation from a dirty, stale Superfunctions dev checkout.\napplies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev and /private/tmp/pr170-refetch-fix.h2yq4m; reuse_rule=PR threads, heads, hosted checks, and checkout state must be revalidated live; preserve unrelated dirty state.\n\n## Task 1: Harden PR #170 redaction/export invariants in a bounded hosted round, success\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-09-15T12-55-27-j4bW-pr_170_bounded_redaction_cleanup_remediation.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/15/rollout-2026-09-15T18-25-27-01a0a522-f7e4-7422-a0fb-002c30b622cc.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-16T12:17:41+00:00, thread_id=01a0a522-f7e4-7422-a0fb-002c30b622cc, Node 22 release gate passed; PR remained DIRTY)\n- rollout_summaries/2026-09-16T12-42-40-ubr7-pr170_refetch_fix_single_round_cleanup_contracts.md (cwd=/private/tmp/pr170-refetch-fix.h2yq4m, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/16/rollout-2026-09-16T18-12-40-01a0aa3d-a004-7df3-b812-85a576729d2d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-16T15:30:05+00:00, thread_id=01a0aa3d-a004-7df3-b812-85a576729d2d, 1e45b794 pushed; PR API head stale)\n- rollout_summaries/2026-09-15T10-22-33-ZW8E-pr_170_bounded_review_remediation.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/15/rollout-2026-09-15T15-52-33-01a0a496-fa30-7f70-ac42-1e7080963f28.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T11:26:48+00:00, thread_id=01a0a496-fa30-7f70-ac42-1e7080963f28, earlier bounded remediation and full release gate)\n\n### keywords\n\n- PR #170, pr-refetch-fix, reviewThreads, GH_CONFIG_DIR, gate:mcpfn-release, McpFnRemoteCredentialLease, cleanupPhase, redaction, 8b23aaa, 1e45b794\n\n## Task 2: Push only generated Entire hooks, then reconcile stale dev safely, success\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-09-15T13-26-45-jo2H-isolated_entire_hooks_push_and_dev_worktree_reconciliation.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/15/rollout-2026-09-15T18-56-46-01a0a53f-a1e6-7cc3-b676-4786df1a293f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T14:02:01+00:00, thread_id=01a0a53f-a1e6-7cc3-b676-4786df1a293f, explicit allowlist pushed; unique SFNS-2 evidence preserved before fast-forward)\n\n### keywords\n\n- origin/dev, explicit allowlist, .factory/settings.json, .opencode/plugins/entire.ts, .pi/extensions/entire/index.ts, git merge --ff-only, SFNS-2, /usr/bin/trash\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when the user invokes `use-skillplane PR #170 pr-refetch-fix` -\u003e retrieve the exact live hosted workflow; make one snapshot/fix/verify/commit/push pass, verify the required head once, then stop without refetching reviews, polling CI, or merging. [Task 1]\n- when the user says “Commit and push directly to origin dev only those changes” -\u003e use a clean worktree and an explicit file allowlist; never stage the whole dirty checkout. [Task 2]\n- when the user asks what to preserve versus delete and then says “proceed” -\u003e classify every path, preserve unique evidence, and use recoverable Trash only for clearly obsolete artifacts. [Task 2]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- Use `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other` for GitHub commands. Page every GraphQL `reviewThreads` cursor: PR #170’s first 100-thread result had `hasNextPage: true`; only a three-page, 284-thread snapshot was complete. [Task 1]\n- Treat credential-safe redaction, omission accounting, structural integrity, and replayable inspector exports as one contract. Reject variable-expanded and scrubbed duplicate keys before `Object.fromEntries()` silently drops data; never echo a resolved key that could be a credential; export a collision-free `${UPPER_CASE_VARIABLE}` marker or an explicitly incomplete safe artifact. [Task 1]\n- `npm run gate:mcpfn-release` is the validated Node 22 release gate. Local green gate and matching pushed heads do not prove hosted CI or merge readiness. [Task 1]\n- Track credential cleanup dynamically: revoke failures are `token-revocation`, disposal failures after successful revoke are `transport-close`; redact reconstructed fields including target `kind`, and keep CLI failure safe when cleanup has no report. [Task 1]\n- For a stale dirty dev checkout: fetch `origin/dev`, create a clean detached worktree, stage the exact allowlist, verify the commit parent equals the fetched tip, push `HEAD:dev`, verify remote SHA, and explain that the original checkout remains stale until separately reconciled. Compare apparent changes byte-for-byte to remote before treating them as unique. [Task 2]\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aad449b0c8087d09a586588ec1aeca6","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b4d1-89b2-74e3-a6c3-9629e0e8826a"},"summary":[{"text":"**Clarifying result buckets and ledger update policy**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Planning non-mutating error reporting**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"The run stopped safely before review collection because the pinned Skillplane workflow could not be retrieved or verified.\n\n- Direct Skillplane MCP/CLI: unavailable.\n- Composio fallback: retrieval tool returned `404 ToolNotFound`; discovery found no replacement.\n- Rex fallback: unavailable.\n- Repository: unchanged; no ledger edit, review fetch, commit, or push.\n- PR 170: open at `dfaeef0d1a4b25cc2ae9e10ccde0481b255637ad`, matching local and upstream.\n- Account: confirmed active GitHub user `thyaravind`.\n- Automation `4442e7f3-60f4-4125-a8e4-c818ac40fc82`: disabled and independently verified with `enabled: false`.\n\nThe schedule has stopped to prevent unverified workflow execution.\n\n\u003coai-mem-citation\u003e\n\u003ccitation_entries\u003e\nMEMORY.md:309-343|note=[prior PR 170 single-round boundaries and account requirements]\n\u003c/citation_entries\u003e\n\u003crollout_ids\u003e\n01a0a522-f7e4-7422-a0fb-002c30b622cc\n01a0aa3d-a004-7df3-b812-85a576729d2d\n01a0a496-fa30-7f70-ac42-1e7080963f28\n\u003c/rollout_ids\u003e\n\u003c/oai-mem-citation\u003e","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aad44a174b887d0b1d93a24aa7c23e1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1789740185.694143,"turn_id":"01a0b4d1-89b2-74e3-a6c3-9629e0e8826a"},"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"skillplane should be accessible via Composio CLI - retry","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0b4f9-6516-7721-ab05-6fcbef4ee5dc","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789742638.358609,"turn_id":"01a0b4f9-6008-7481-8c13-f3c8d9cbf433"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"encrypted_conte