report date and Product Hunt day differ. Cause: the report treats capture date as sufficient provenance. Fix: keep the Product Hunt day caveat explicit in both the HTML and automation memory. [Task 2][Task 3]\n7750:- Retryable cleanup flows that disable DB state and delete external resources should delete the external resource first; otherwise a failed external call leaves the row disabled and unretryable. [Task 25]\n7798:- Symptom: a background/cleanup patch becomes unretryable after one external failure. Cause: the implementation disables the DB row before deleting the external schedule. Fix: delete the external schedule first and only then persist the disabled state. [Task 25]\n7984:- Symptom: workflow-created Chrome tabs remain, including a Chrome Web Store tab that automation cannot script closed. Cause: not all tabs are Playwright-scriptable. Fix: expect occasional native-Chrome cleanup for leftover non-scriptable tabs after long runs. [Task 2]\n7987:scope: Use for creating or rerunning the Hacker News front-page workflow in `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/workflows`, especially when the user wants the first 100 posts analyzed from `news.ycombinator.com` with direct HTTP/API fetching instead of browser automation. Boundaries: HN front-page ordering, page volatility, and linked-page fetch outcomes are run-specific and should be revalidated live.\n8084:- when the user asked \"chrome isn't needed unlike PH or TwitteR?\" -> for HN, default to direct HTTP/API fetching rather than Chrome/browser automation. [Task 1]\n8096:- When `$CODEX_HOME` is unset, use `/Users/serro/.codex/automations/contem-daily-hacker-news-front-page-analysis/memory.md` explicitly; an empty expansion targets unwritable `/automations`. [Task 3]\n8121:- Automation memory for this workflow lives at `/Users/serro/.codex/automations/contem-daily-hacker-news-front-page-analysis/memory.md`; update it with the new archive path plus validated counts after each successful rerun. [Task 1]\n8218:- Automation memory for this workflow lives at `/Users/serro/.codex/automations/contem-daily-lobsters-frontpage-analysis/memory.md`; update it after the archive-backed readout is prepared. [Task 2]\n8245:- Symptom: automation-memory lookup fails through `$CODEX_HOME`. Cause: this shell often has `CODEX_HOME` unset. Fix: use the literal `/Users/serro/.codex/automations/...` path in this environment. [Task 2]\n8251:scope: Use for weekly contem summary runs in `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/workflows`, especially when the user wants a seven-day source-first synthesis with a self-contained HTML report, JSON sidecar, and weekly automation-memory update. Boundaries: the date window, latest-per-day archive selection, and cross-workflow ranking logic are run-specific and should be revalidated each week.\n8270:- weekly-contem-summary, 2026-07-28..2026-08-03, summary-report, source-first, latest-per-day, Product Hunt provenance, Playwright, automation memory, partial\n8294:- Symptom: the weekly run stops after generating HTML but before memory update or handoff. Cause: those steps are treated as separate housekeeping. Fix: complete visual QA, automation-memory update, and concise chat handoff before success. [Task 4]\n8324:applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane; reuse_rule=retrieve the currently published MCP workflow and re-resolve project/team/state before every mutation; issue IDs and links are time-specific.\n8330:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/archived_sessions/rollout-2026-08-22T12-23-50-01a0283e-c238-7442-8966-c1e348f270a1_01a0283f-44f7-7211-addd-bbb177f4a903.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-22T07:01:22+00:00, SKI-11 and SKI-12 with verified documents/links)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":4000},"formatted_output":"---\nname: orca-cli\ndescription: >-\n  Operate Orca-managed worktrees, folder contexts, terminals, repos, automations, artifacts,\n  skill sharing, worktree comments, and Orca's embedded browser through the `orca` CLI. Use\n  when the user says \"$orca-cli\", \"Orca worktree\", \"child worktree\", \"spawn codex/claude in a\n  worktree\", \"read/wait/send Orca terminal\", \"handoff\" / \"handover\" / \"give this to another\n  agent\", \"Orca browser\", \"orca artifacts\", or \"share skills\". Prefer it over raw git\n  worktree, ad hoc PTYs, or Computer Use when Orca state is involved. Use Computer Use only\n  for external windows or desktop UI that needs OS-level control, and Playwright or CDP for\n  external pages.\n---\n\n# Orca CLI\n\nThis discovery stub loads the version-matched guide from the Orca executable used for this session.\n\n## Resolve the CLI for this session\n\nChoose the executable once and reuse it for every later command:\n\n- If the `ORCA_CLI_COMMAND` environment variable is set, use its value. Orca exports this\n  for managed WSL sessions.\n- Otherwise, in a dev checkout whose session exposes `ORCA_DEV_REPO_ROOT`, use `orca-dev`.\n- Otherwise, on Linux outside an Orca-managed terminal, use `orca-ide`. Never run bare\n  `orca` there — outside Orca's terminals it normally resolves to the\n  GNOME Orca screen reader (`/usr/bin/orca`) and starts speech on the user's machine.\n- Otherwise, use `orca`.\n\nBelow, `ORCA` is a placeholder for the executable you resolved. Substitute it before\nrunning anything; do not create a shell variable or run `ORCA` literally. This works the\nsame way in POSIX shells, PowerShell, and cmd.exe.\n\nIf the selected executable cannot run, report its exact error and stop. Do not fall through\nto another executable, which could silently target a different Orca build.\n\n## Load the version-matched guide before running Orca commands\n\n```text\nORCA skills get orca-cli\n```\n\nPrefer `--json`. Use the selected executable's `--help` for commands or flags the guide does\nnot cover. If a command reports that Orca is not running, start it with `ORCA open --json`\nand retry. If `skills get` is unknown, explain that updating Orca restores the guide; use\n`--help` for read-only discovery and do not guess unsupported commands.\n---\nname: using-21nco-github\ndescription: Uses the thyaravind GitHub account for repositories under dev/n or with a 21nCo origin. Use for any GitHub CLI, pull request, issue, release, or repository operation in those repositories.\n---\n\n# Using 21nCo GitHub\n\nFor any repository whose path is under `dev/n` or whose Git remote belongs to `21nCo`:\n\n- Run every `gh` command with `GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other`.\n- Verify `GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other gh auth status` reports `thyaravind` as the active account before making changes.\n- Never use the default GitHub account or silently fall back to another account.\n- Use the existing `21nCo` remote for pushes. If `thyaravind` lacks permission, stop and report the denial instead of creating a fork or alternate remote.\n6779:- Symptom: the automated X prompt drifts toward a single-feed capture. Cause: the workflow was automated without carrying forward the proven multi-tab contract. Fix: revalidate visible tabs and bake the tab-partitioned capture rules into the automation prompt. [Task 1]\n6781:- Symptom: an automation search claims nothing exists under `$CODEX_HOME/automations`. Cause: this shell does not expose that path. Fix: use the known absolute Codex automation home under `/Users/serro/.codex/automations`. [Task 3]\n6918:- The August 19 blocked run created no feed snapshots, post captures, or archive; its automation memory is `/Users/serro/.codex/automations/contem-daily-medium-home-posts-analysis/memory.md`. [Task 11]\n6943:- Symptom: Chrome initialization returns `Browser is not available: chrome`. Cause: the required extension/profile binding is absent. Fix: reconnect Google Chrome/`Ar@fyweb` through Settings → Computer use, then rerun; do not use Wavebox/default browser or another profile. Use the explicit automation path if `$CODEX_HOME` expands to `/automations`. [Task 11]\n6944:- Automation memory for this workflow lives at `/Users/serro/.codex/automations/contem-daily-medium-home-posts-analysis/memory.md`; append a compact dated run note with archive path, validation, access counts, first/last titles, and any notable recovery event. [Task 2]\n6979:- Symptom: browser automation reconnect assumptions break after a bundle/cache change. Cause: the active Chrome control bundle path changed between runs. Fix: rediscover the active `control-chrome` bundle before connecting instead of assuming yesterday’s path. [Task 2]\n7073:## Task 5: Validate archive, return a short readout, finalize tabs, and update automation memory, success\n7080:- daily-x-home-timeline-archive, automation memory, short content readout, totalIncomplete: 4, totalNoPostUrl: 1, totalAds: 18, totalRepaired: 50, Chrome finalize\n7152:- The June 30 rerun wrote `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/workflows/x-home-timeline-analysis/archive/2026-06-30-06-34-33.json`, validated `300` posts across six tabs, `3` incomplete promoted cards with no normal `postUrl`, `15` no-status cards, `16` ads, and `122` raw snapshots in `tmp/`; it also created `/Users/serro/.codex/automations/daily-x-home-timeline-archive/memory.md` because no automation memory existed yet. [Task 2][Task 5]\n7179:- The June 23 validation checklist also covered `totalNoPostUrl`, `totalAds`, raw snapshot presence, clean archive hygiene, Chrome finalization, and an automation-memory update at `/Users/serro/.codex/automations/daily-x-home-timeline-archive/memory.md`. [Task 5]\n7208:scope: Use for daily contem summary runs in `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/workflows`, especially when the user wants a concise chat synthesis plus a self-contained HTML artifact with provenance, source links, and automation-memory updates. Boundaries: chosen archive set, same-day capture windows, and cross-source freshness caveats are run-specific and should be revalidated 