{"timestamp":"2026-09-19T09:46:08.230Z","ordinal":4329,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0b3f5-d570-7a72-b668-401efd539e3b","turn_id":"01a0b90d-72f4-76d0-8550-1d4d61d74375","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae59d7fe0c87d0bd21c0f7b74c06c7","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The deferred Sonar family currently contains **38 open code smells**, not 36. The ledger’s count is stale; the latest analysis added two findings after round 9.\n\nSummary:\n\n| Category | Count |\n|---|---:|\n| Cognitive complexity | 8 |\n| Nested ternaries | 10 |\n| Throwing non-`Error` values | 4 |\n| Nested template literals | 2 |\n| Potential regex backtracking | 2 |\n| Other single-rule findings | 12 |\n\nSeverity:\n\n- 9 critical\n- 21 major\n- 8 minor\n- Estimated remediation effort: 578 minutes, roughly 9h 38m\n\nMain hotspots:\n\n- `mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts`: 13\n- `mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts`: 6\n- `mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts`: 5\n- `mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts`: 3\n- `mcpfn/testing/src/reports.ts`: 3\n- Eight remaining findings across inspector, conformance, targets, test support, and the external HTTP example.\n\nThe more behavior-sensitive findings are:\n\n- Two potentially super-linear regular expressions in `remote-target.ts`\n- One swallowed exception in `remote-target.ts`\n- Four locations throwing values that Sonar does not recognize as `Error` objects\n- Very high complexity in credential/redaction paths—reported complexities include 79 and 85 against an allowed 15\n\nMost others are maintainability/readability suggestions: extracting ternaries, splitting authorization-mode logic, removing redundant blocks, preferring `Object.hasOwn`, default parameters, `String.raw`, and similar changes.\n\nThe two newest findings introduced by the latest analysis are:\n\n- `mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts:123`: cognitive complexity 18 versus 15\n- `mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts:399`: nested ternary\n\nSo the deferred item is not one coherent defect. It is an umbrella covering **18 distinct Sonar rule families across 11 files**, with a mixture of potentially meaningful runtime concerns and mechanical refactoring advice. That aggregate requires assessment and deduplication before it can be considered resolved for convergence."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1789811160028,"completed_at_ms":1789811168230}}
