er, disable and verify this automation, report, and stop rather than repeating unsafe mutation attempts.\\n\\nEnd every nonterminal run with the hosted workflow's result buckets and: `One review round is complete. No post-push refetch or additional review loop was performed.`\",\"text_elements\":[]}]},\"started_at_ms\":1789729233083,\"completed_at_ms\":1789729233083}}\n/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T16-30-28-01a0b42c-c4ea-7b61-a3b7-c7fffb0ed31d.jsonl:31:{\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-18T11:00:55.655Z\",\"ordinal\":30,\"type\":\"event_msg\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"item_completed\",\"thread_id\":\"01a0b42c-c4ea-7b61-a3b7-c7fffb0ed31d\",\"turn_id\":\"01a0b42c-c58e-7991-94d6-b0db37dabc67\",\"item\":{\"type\":\"CommandExecution\",\"id\":\"exec-5c9a48e3-a079-4597-ad15-338d7f7bc09d\",\"process_id\":\"82507\",\"command\":[\"/bin/zsh\",\"-lc\",\"command -v skillplane || true\\ncommand -v composio || true\\ncommand -v rex || true\\ncommand -v orca || true\\nprintenv ORCA_CLI_COMMAND\\nprintenv ORCA_DEV_REPO_ROOT\\nsed -n '113,158p' /Users/serro/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\\nsed -n '1,240p' /Users/serro/.codex/memories/rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md\"],\"cwd\":\"file:///Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/SFNS-4\",\"parsed_cmd\":[{\"type\":\"unknown\",\"cmd\":\"command -v skillplane || true\\ncommand -v composio || true\\ncommand -v rex || true\\ncommand -v orca || true\\nprintenv ORCA_CLI_COMMAND\\nprintenv ORCA_DEV_REPO_ROOT\\nsed -n '113,158p' /Users/serro/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\\nsed -n '1,240p' /Users/serro/.codex/memories/rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md\"}],\"source\":\"unified_exec_startup\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"stdout\":\"/Users/serro/.local/bin/composio\\n/usr/local/bin/orca\\n# Task Group: September 15 Rex hosted agent/CLI planning and SFNS-4 PR remediation\\nscope: Use for Rex product planning built on Super Functions/Composio research, or the distinct bounded SFNS-4 remediation that followed.\\napplies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments and /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/SFNS-4; reuse_rule=Rex repository/product decisions need fresh confirmation; PR #179 head and readiness are live state.\\n\\n## Task 1: Research portable hosted Rex agent/CLI architecture, partial\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/2026-09-13T06-43-20-8gX6-rex_planning_and_sfns4_pr_remediation.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/13/rollout-2026-09-13T12-13-20-01a09981-8f95-7e22-90a5-204718c73810.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T06:58:10+00:00, thread_id=01a09981-8f95-7e22-90a5-204718c73810, planning research only; full plan not completed)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- Rex, PlugFn, AuthFn, DataFn, UIFn, Composio, MCP, Cloudflare Hyperdrive, Workflows, hosted service, personal/shared connections\\n\\n## Task 2: Remediate Superfunctions PR #179 in exact worktree, success\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/2026-09-13T06-43-20-8gX6-rex_planning_and_sfns4_pr_remediation.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/SFNS-4, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/13/rollout-2026-09-13T12-13-20-01a09981-8f95-7e22-90a5-204718c73810.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T06:58:10+00:00, thread_id=01a09981-8f95-7e22-90a5-204718c73810, final commit 99ea0ac; no post-push refetch/CI polling)\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/15/rollout-2026-09-15T16-11-28-01a0a4a8-4cc6-7b03-a1c5-d382213eae73.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-16T12:26:25+00:00, thread_id=01a0a4a8-4cc6-7b03-a1c5-d382213eae73, 511c02a pushed; external gates pending)\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/SFNS-4, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/16/rollout-2026-09-16T18-12-50-01a0aa3d-c6e5-7963-9f4b-4f57675b7e35.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-16T15:43:16+00:00, thread_id=01a0aa3d-c6e5-7963-9f4b-4f57675b7e35, e200f50d pushed; merge readiness remains unverified)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- SFNS-4, PR #179, pr-refetch-fix, reviewThreads, adapterNamespace, Retry-After, tenantId, SecFn readJson, e200f50d, 511c02a\\n\\n## User preferences\\n\\n- when planning “Rex, an AI agent and a CLI which a user can take anywhere” -> make portability, centralized reusable connections, CLI access, and MCP interoperability first-class requirements. [Task 1]\\n- when the user selects “Individuals and teams from launch, hosted Rex service” -> include multi-tenant workspaces, personal/shared connections, roles, grants, and audit history by default. [Task 1]\\n- when the user says “retry” after a bounded PR round fails -> start a fresh authorized snapshot/fix/verify/commit/push round; do not silently continue the failed collection. [Task 2]\\n\\n## Reusable knowledge\\n\\n- PlugFn is the integration runtime, but source presence is not production readiness: consult provider readiness matrix and same-commit `npm run gate:plugfn-release`. Keep credential exchange, refresh, credentialed actions, and webhook verification out of browser code. [Task 1]\\n- AuthFn covers sessions/OAuth/API keys/multi-region/native handoff; DataFn covers tenant isolation, transactions, sync, REST, and WebSockets; UIFn Svelte is headless with DOM behavior in `@uifn/dom`. Composio patterns support durable user-scoped connections, account/toolkit restriction, session reuse, hosted MCP, and CLI access. [Task 1]\\n- For PR #179, perform audit scans in one transaction with configurable `repeatable_read`; serialize secret-set mutations with a parent-row lock under `read_committed`; reject duplicate output names; preflight duplicate migration identities with actionable `23505`. [Task 2]\\n- PR #179 later required `adapterNamespace` at DbVectorStore CRUD calls, `Object.hasOwn` coordinator dispatch, finite nonnegative Retry-After values, mandatory MemoryFn `tenantId`, and SecFn 400 only for `SyntaxError`; use streaming Node/files for large GitHub payloads, not shell variables plus `jq`. [Task 2]\\n\\n## Failures and how to do differently\\n\\n- Finish the Rex intent inventory, assumptions, architecture, API/data contracts, phased plan, and remaining questions before pivoting to another task. Local tests, skipped DB tests, a missing terminal GraphQL `pageInfo`, `DIRTY`/conflicting PR state, and failing/pending hosted checks do not establish PR #179 merge readiness. [Task 1][Task 2]\\n\\n# Task Group: September 16 Skillplane SKI-17 read-only review and Linear acceptance completeness\\nscope: Use for strict read-only review of Skillplane DataFn upgrade work, especially when local code looks complete but acceptance criteria may require deployed-region verification.\\napplies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane; reuse_rule=worktree diff, package versions, and issue acceptance status are snapshot-specific; do not mutate under a read-only request.\\nthread_id: 01a0aa3d-c6e5-7963-9f4b-4f57675b7e35\\nupdated_at: 2026-09-16T15:43:16+00:00\\nrollout_path: /Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/16/rollout-2026-09-16T18-12-50-01a0aa3d-c6e5-7963-9f4b-4f57675b7e35.jsonl\\ncwd: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/SFNS-4\\ngit_branch: sfns-4-rex-upstream\\n\\n# Bounded PR review remediation for SFNS-4 completed and pushed\\n\\nRollout context: In `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/SFNS-4`, the user invoked `pr-refetch-fix`, then explicitly authorized a retry after the first round was blocked by `jq: argument list too long`.\\n\\n## Task 1: Review and remediate PR #179\\n\\nOutcome: success\\n\\nPreference signals:\\n- The user invoked `pr-refetch-fix` and then said “retry” after the first bounded attempt failed -> future runs should treat each explicit retry as a new bounded round, not continue the prior one implicitly.\\n- The workflow requires one snapshot/fix/verify/commit/push pass and no post-push refetch, CI polling, or reviewer loop -> preserve this strict single-round boundary.\\n\\nKey steps:\\n- Retrieved hosted `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.2.0`, revision 4, digest `sha256:8781c1c12fe9d5902337d6cf21bfbac49dd3a94c7eadd46bf2622db350444022` through Composio fallback.\\n- Verified GitHub account `thyaravind` using `GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other`; local, remote, and PR #179 heads initially matched `511c02a154a850517522bfc2a3a587769f89ca61`.\\n- Collected review threads, review bodies, issue comments, and raw inline comments with a streaming Node wrapper and before/after head guard. The snapshot returned 100 review-thread nodes, 0 unresolved thread nodes, and 291 raw inline comments; five current-head Cubic findings were identified.\\n- Added regressions first, reproduced failures, then fixed five root causes: RAG adapter namespace propagation, own-key multi-agent dispatch, invalid `Retry-After` handling, mandatory MemoryFn tenant typing, and SecFn request-body error classification.\\n- Focused post-fix tests passed: LangFn 14, MemoryFn 6, SecFn 41. Full suites passed: LangFn 180, MemoryFn 47 with 8 PostgreSQL tests skipped, SecFn 48 with 10 PostgreSQL tests skipped.\\n- LangFn typecheck/build/release gate passed; MemoryFn and SecFn typecheck/build passed; LangFn lint had 0 errors and 42 existing warnings.\\n- Staged exactly 14 tracked files, committed once as `e200f50d639431417e6ec5b3196dcd190414b62f`, pushed once, and verified local, remote, and PR heads matched.\\n\\nFailures and how to do differently:\\n- The initial review aggregation stored huge JSON in shell variables and failed with `argument list too long: jq`; use a streaming Node wrapper or files for large GitHub responses.\\n- The successful snapshot did not retain terminal GraphQL `reviewThreads.pageInfo`, so completeness beyond the 100 returned nodes remained unverified. Preserve page metadata explicitly in future collection scripts.\\n- PR #179 remained merge-conflicting, SonarCloud failed pre-push, live SFNS-4 qualification was not run, and database-backed tests were skipped. Do not claim merge readiness from local green tests.\\n\\nReusable knowledge:\\n- `DbVectorStore` now separates logical document `namespace` from backing adapter `adapterNamespace` and passes the latter to `createMany`/`findMany`.\\n- `MultiAgentCoordinator` uses `Object.hasOwn` before dispatch, preventing inherited keys such as `toString` from causing a `TypeError`.\\n- `RateLimitError`, OpenAI response parsing, and retry scheduling now accept only finite, nonnegative retry delays; invalid headers fall back to exponential backoff.\\n- MemoryFn `searchVectors` requires `tenantId` in its shared interface and both bundled adapters, aligning types with runtime scope enforcement.\\n- SecFn `readJson` maps only `SyntaxError` to `SECFN_BAD_JSON`/400; body transport failures remain internal errors/500.\\n\\nReferences:\\n- PR: https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/179\\n- Commit: `e200f50d639431417e6ec5b3196dcd190414b62f`\\n- Ledger: `.conduct/SFNS-4/pr179-remediation-ledger.json` (untracked evidence; intentionally not committed)\\n- Initial failure: `zsh:12: argument list too long: jq`\\n- Verification commands included `npm test`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`, `npm run lint`, `npm run gate:langfn-release`, `git diff --cached --check`, and one post-push `git ls-remote`/`gh pr view` head comparison.\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"/Users/serro/.local/bin/composio\\n/usr/local/bin/orca\\n# Task Group: September 15 Rex hosted agent/CLI planning and SFNS-4 PR remediation\\nscope: Use for Rex product planning built on Super Functions/Composio research, or the distinct bounded SFNS-4 remediation that followed.\\napplies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments and /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/SFNS-4; reuse_rule=Rex repository/product decisions need fresh confirmation; PR #179 head and readiness are live state.\\n\\n## Task 1: Research portable hosted Rex agent/CLI architecture, partial\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/2026-09-13T06-43-20-8gX6-rex_planning_and_sfns4_pr_remediation.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/13/rollout-2026-09-13T12-13-20-01a09981-8f95-7e22-90a5-204718c73810.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T06:58:10+00:00, thread_id=01a09981-8f95-7e22-90a5-204718c73810, planning research only; full plan not completed)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- Rex, PlugFn, AuthFn, DataFn, UIFn, Composio, MCP, Cloudflare Hyperdrive, Workflows, hosted service, personal/shared connections\\n\\n## Task 2: Remediate Superfunctions PR #179 in exact worktree, success\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/2026-09-13T06-43-20-8gX6-rex_planning_and_sfns4_pr_remediation.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/SFNS-4, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/13/rollout-2026-09-13T12-13-20-01a09981-8f95-7e22-90a5-204718c73810.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T06:58:10+00:00, thread_id=01a09981-8f95-7e22-90a5-204718c73810, final commit 99ea0ac; no post-push refetch/CI polling)\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/15/rollout-2026-09-15T16-11-28-01a0a4a8-4cc6-7b03-a1c5-d382213eae73.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-16T12:26:25+00:00, thread_id=01a0a4a8-4cc6-7b03-a1c5-d382213eae73, 511c02a pushed; external gates pending)\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/SFNS-4, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/16/rollout-2026-09-16T18-12-50-01a0aa3d-c6e5-7963-9f4b-4f57675b7e35.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-16T15:43:16+00:00, thread_id=01a0aa3d-c6e5-7963-9f4b-4f57675b7e35, e200f50d pushed; merge readiness remains unverified)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- SFNS-4, PR #179, pr-refetch-fix, reviewThreads, adapterNamespace, Retry-After, tenantId, SecFn readJson, e200f50d, 511c02a\\n\\n## User preferences\\n\\n- when planning “Rex, an AI agent and a CLI which a user can take anywhere” -> make portability, centralized reusable connections, CLI access, and MCP interoperability first-class requirements. [Task 1]\\n- when the user selects “Individuals and teams from launch, hosted Rex service” -> include multi-tenant workspaces, personal/shared connections, roles, grants, and audit history by default. [Task 1]\\n- when the user says “retry” after a bounded PR round fails -> start a fresh authorized snapshot/fix/verify/commit/push round; do not silently continue the failed collection. [Task 2]\\n\\n## Reusable knowledge\\n\\n- PlugFn is the integration runtime, but source presence is not production readiness: consult provider readiness matrix and same-commit `npm run gate:plugfn-release`. Keep credential exchange, refresh, credentialed actions, and webhook verification out of browser code. [Task 1]\\n- AuthFn covers sessions/OAuth/API keys/multi-region/native handoff; DataFn covers tenant isolation, transactions, sync, REST, and WebSockets; UIFn Svelte is headless with DOM behavior in `@uifn/dom`. Composio patterns support durable user-scoped connections, account/toolkit restriction, session reuse, hosted MCP, and CLI access. [Task 1]\\n- For PR #179, perform audit scans in one transaction with configurable `repeatable_read`; serialize secret-set mutations with a parent-row lock under `read_committed`; reject duplicate output names; preflight duplicate migration identities with actionable `23505`. [Task 2]\\n- PR #179 later required `adapterNamespace` at DbVectorStore CRUD calls, `Object.hasOwn` coordinator dispatch, finite nonnegative Retry-After values, mandatory MemoryFn `tenantId`, and SecFn 400 only for `SyntaxError`; use streaming Node/files for large GitHub payloads, not shell variables plus `jq`. [Task 2]\\n\\n## Failures and how to do differently\\n\\n- Finish the Rex intent inventory, assumptions, architecture, API/data contracts, phased plan, and remaining questions before pivoting to another task. Local tests, skipped DB tests, a missing terminal GraphQL `pageInfo`, `DIRTY`/conflicting PR state, and failing/pending hosted checks do not establish PR #179 merge readiness. [Task 1][Task 2]\\n\\n# Task Group: September 16 Skillplane SKI-17 read-only review and Linear acceptance completeness\\nscope: Use for strict read-only review of Skillplane DataFn upgrade work, especially when local code looks complete but acceptance criteria may require deployed-region verification.\\napplies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane; reuse_rule=worktree diff, package versions, and issue acceptance status are snapshot-specific; do not mutate under a read-only request.\\nthread_id: 01a0aa3d-c6e5-7963-9f4b-4f57675b7e35\\nupdated_at: 2026-09-16T15:43:16+00:00\\nrollout_path: /Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/16/rollout-2026-09-16T18-12-50-01a0aa3d-c6e5-7963-9f4b-4f57675b7e35.jsonl\\ncwd: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/SFNS-4\\ngit_branch: sfns-4-rex-upstream\\n\\n# Bounded PR review remediation for SFNS-4 completed and pushed\\n\\nRollout context: In `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/SFNS-4`, the user invoked `pr-refetch-fix`, then explicitly authorized a retry after the first round was blocked by `jq: argument list too long`.\\n\\n## Task 1: Review and remediate PR #179\\n\\nOutcome: success\\n\\nPreference signals:\\n- The user invoked `pr-refetch-fix` and then said “retry” after the first bounded attempt failed -> future runs should treat each explicit retry as a new bounded round, not continue the prior one implicitly.\\n- The workflow requires one snapshot/fix/verify/commit/push pass and no post-push refetch, CI polling, or reviewer loop -> preserve this strict single-round boundary.\\n\\nKey steps:\\n- Retrieved hosted `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.2.0`, revision 4, digest `sha256:8781c1c12fe9d5902337d6cf21bfbac49dd3a94c7eadd46bf2622db350444022` through Composio fallback.\\n- Verified GitHub account `thyaravind` using `GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other`; local, remote, and PR #179 heads initially matched `511c02a154a850517522bfc2a3a587769f89ca61`.\\n- Collected review threads, review bodies, issue comments, and raw inline comments with a streaming Node wrapper and before/after head guard. The snapshot returned 100 review-thread nodes, 0 unresolved thread nodes, and 291 raw inline comments; five current-head Cubic findings were identified.\\n- Added regressions first, reproduced failures, then fixed five root causes: RAG adapter namespace propagation, own-key multi-agent dispatch, invalid `Retry-After` handling, mandatory MemoryFn tenant typing, and SecFn request-body error classification.\\n- Focused post-fix tests passed: LangFn 14, MemoryFn 6, SecFn 41. Full suites passed: LangFn 180, MemoryFn 47 with 8 PostgreSQL tests skipped, SecFn 48 with 10 PostgreSQL tests skipped.\\n- LangFn typecheck/build/release gate passed; MemoryFn and SecFn typecheck/build passed; LangFn lint had 0 errors and 42 existing warnings.\\n- Staged exactly 14 tracked files, committed once as `e200f50d639431417e6ec5b3196dcd190414b62f`, pushed once, and verified local, remote, and PR heads matched.\\n\\nFailures and how to do differently:\\n- The initial review aggregation stored huge JSON in shell variables and failed with `argument list too long: jq`; use a streaming Node wrapper or files for large GitHub responses.\\n- The successful snapshot did not retain terminal GraphQL `reviewThreads.pageInfo`, so completeness beyond the 100 returned nodes remained unverified. Preserve page metadata explicitly in future collection scripts.\\n- PR #179 remained merge-conflicting, SonarCloud failed pre-push, live SFNS-4 qualification was not run, and database-backed tests were skipped. Do not claim merge readiness from local green tests.\\n\\nReusable knowledge:\\n- `DbVectorStore` now separates logical document `namespace` from backing adapter `adapterNamespace` and passes the latter to `createMany`/`findMany`.\\n- `MultiAgentCoordinator` uses `Object.hasOwn` before dispatch, preventing inherited keys such as `toString` from causing a `TypeError`.\\n- `RateLimitError`, OpenAI response parsing, and retry scheduling now accept only finite, nonnegative retry delays; invalid headers fall back to exponential backoff.\\n- MemoryFn `searchVectors` requires `tenantId` in its shared interface and both bundled adapters, aligning types with runtime scope enforcement.\\n- SecFn `readJson` maps only `SyntaxError` to `SECFN_BAD_JSON`/400; body transport failures remain internal errors/500.\\n\\nReferences:\\n- PR: https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/179\\n- Commit: `e200f50d639431417e6ec5b3196dcd190414b62f`\\n- Ledger: `.conduct/SFNS-4/pr179-remediation-ledger.json` (untracked evidence; intentionally not committed)\\n- Initial failure: `zsh:12: argument list too long: jq`\\n- Verification commands included `npm test`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`, `npm run lint`, `npm run gate:langfn-release`, `git diff --cached --check`, and one post-push `git ls-remote`/`gh pr view` head comparison.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"duration\":{\"secs\":0,\"nanos\":3833},\"formatted_output\":\"/Users/serro/.local/bin/composio\\n/usr/local/bin/orca\\n# Task Group: September 15 Rex hosted agent/CLI planning and SFNS-4 PR remediation\\nscope: Use for Rex product planning built on Super Functions/Composio research, or the distinct bounded SFNS-4 remediation that followed.\\napplies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments and /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/SFNS-4; reuse_rule=Rex repository/product decisions need fresh confirmation; PR #179 head and readiness are live state.\\n\\n## Task 1: Research portable hosted Rex agent/CLI architecture, partial\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/2026-09-13T06-43-20-8gX6-rex_planning_and_sfns4_pr_remediation.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/13/rollout-2026-09-13T12-13-20-01a09981-8f95-7e22-90a5-204718c73810.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T06:58:10+00:00, thread_id=01a09981-8f95-7e22-90a5-204718c73810, planning research only; full plan not completed)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- Rex, PlugFn, AuthFn, DataFn, UIFn, Composio, MCP, Cloudflare Hyperdrive, Workflows, hosted service, personal/shared connections\\n\\n## Task 2: Remediate Superfunctions PR #179 in exact worktree, success\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/2026-09-13T06-43-20-8gX6-rex_planning_and_sfns4_pr_remediation.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/SFNS-4, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/13/rollout-2026-09-13T12-13-20-01a09981-8f95-7e22-90a5-204718c73810.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T06:58:10+00:00, thread_id=01a09981-8f95-7e22-90a5-204718c73810, final commit 99ea0ac; no post-push refetch/CI polling)\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/15/rollout-2026-09-15T16-11-28-01a0a4a8-4cc6-7b03-a1c5-d382213eae73.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-16T12:26:25+00:00, thread_id=01a0a4a8-4cc6-7b03-a1c5-d382213eae73, 511c02a pushed; external gates pending)\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/SFNS-4, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/16/rollout-2026-09-16T18-12-50-01a0aa3d-c6e5-7963-9f4b-4f57675b7e35.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-16T15:43:16+00:00, thread_id=01a0aa3d-c6e5-7963-9f4b-4f57675b7e35, e200f50d pushed; merge readiness remains unverified)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- SFNS-4, PR #179, pr-refetch-fix, reviewThreads, adapterNamespace, Retry-After, tenantId, SecFn readJson, e200f50d, 511c02a\\n\\n## User preferences\\n\\n- when planning “Rex, an AI agent and a CLI which a user can take anywhere” -> make portability, centrali