ete snapshot has an Actionable defect, a valid Not Attempted code defect, a new defect, a recurring family, a fix-induced regression, a changed PR head between assessments, or any required CI/reviewer check is pending or failing in the single allowed immediate check snapshot.\\\\n2. A clean assessment requires: no code change or push in that round; zero Actionable root causes; zero valid Not Attempted code root causes; no unassessed review items; no recurring/deferred blocker; the PR head stayed stable; and all required CI/reviewer checks are terminal and successful in the one allowed immediate snapshot.\\\\n3. Declare convergence only after two consecutive clean scheduled assessments at the same PR head. Then update the ledger, disable automation `AUTOMATION_ID_PLACEHOLDER` with `orca automations edit AUTOMATION_ID_PLACEHOLDER --disabled --json`, verify with `orca automations show AUTOMATION_ID_PLACEHOLDER --json`, report convergence, and stop.\\\\n4. If PR 170 is merged or closed, record the terminal state, disable and verify this automation, report that the schedule stopped, and stop without mutation.\\\\n5. If a reset-trigger assessment cannot establish a complete coordinated repair, or an external dependency blocks further progress, record the blocker, disable and verify this automation so it cannot repeat unsafe mutations, report the blocker, and stop.\\\\n\\\\nEnd every nonterminal run with the hosted workflow's explicit result buckets and: `One review round is complete. No post-push refetch or additional review loop was performed.`\\\",\\n      \\\"precheck\\\": null,\\n      \\\"agentId\\\": \\\"codex\\\",\\n      \\\"runContext\\\": {\\n        \\\"kind\\\": \\\"workspace-run\\\",\\n        \\\"projectId\\\": \\\"github:21nco/super-functions\\\",\\n        \\\"hostId\\\": \\\"local\\\",\\n        \\\"projectHostSetupId\\\": \\\"940d3c77-482f-4eb2-8be7-88b4976ed269\\\",\\n        \\\"repoId\\\": \\\"940d3c77-482f-4eb2-8be7-88b4976ed269\\\",\\n        \\\"pa