ile: r1/superset-automate/SKILL.md)\n- superset-browser: Open, navigate, screenshot, read, click, and type in web pages from an agent. Use when the user asks to open a URL, preview or verify a running web app, check a page's console, fill a form,  (file: r1/superset-browser/SKILL.md)\n- superset-computer: Operate the user's real desktop apps and windows on macOS, Windows, or Linux. Use when the user asks to open or drive a native app, click or type in a desktop UI, inspect or arrange a wind (file: r1/superset-computer/SKILL.md)\n- superset-contribute: Set up a Superset open-source contribution, from forking and cloning superset-sh/superset through local dev setup and the repo's rules to a merge-ready PR. Use when the user wants to contr (file: r1/superset-contribute/SKILL.md)\n- superset-doctor: Diagnose and fix Superset problems such as connection failures, offline hosts, terminals not attaching, auth or update issues. Use when the user reports something broken or misbehaving in  (file: r1/superset-doctor/SKILL.md)\n- superset-feedback: Collect and submit feedback about Superset (bug reports, feature requests, or general feedback) privately to the Superset team or as a public GitHub issue. Use when the user wants to repor (file: r1/superset-feedback/SKILL.md)\n- superset-integrations: Discover and call the tools a connected integration exposes, such as Linear, GitHub, Sentry, or Notion, through `superset mcp`. Use when the user wants something done in a connected servic (file: r1/superset-integrations/SKILL.md)\n- superset-orchestrate: Coordinate several coding agents in parallel through Superset, each in its own workspace, with follow-ups, progress reads, dependency tracking, and structured results. Use when the user asks (file: r1/superset-orchestrate/SKILL.md)\n- superset-page: Build and publish a self-contained HTML page to Superset, then answer the comments readers pin to it. Use when the user asks to make or publish a page, turn a report, dashboard, chart, doc (file: r1/superset-page/SKILL.md)\n- superset-plugins: Install Superset plugins, connect the accounts they need, and call their MCP tools through the credential proxy. Use when the user wants a plugin installed, removed, enabled, or connected, a (file: r1/superset-plugins/SKILL.md)\n- superset-setup: Make a repository Superset-ready by authoring .superset/config.json with setup, teardown, and run scripts so every new workspace boots configured, then verifying with a real workspace. Use w (file: r1/superset-setup/SKILL.md)\n- superset-standup: Digest of what the user's Superset agents did while they were away, sweeping workspaces, tasks, and agent terminals to report what finished, what needs review, and what's blocked. Use when t (file: r1/superset-standup/SKILL.md)\n- sync-sf-next-to-dev: Inventory changes on local Superfunctions `next` that are relevant to local `dev`, limited to functions and shared packages already present on `dev`, ignoring `.conduct` artifacts and igno (file: r0/sync-sf-next-to-dev/SKILL.md)\n- template-creator:template-creator: Create or update a reusable personal Codex artifact-template skill. Use when the user invokes $template-creator or asks in natural language to create a reusable template from a reference docu (file: r11/template-creator/26.909.61513/skills/template-creator/SKILL.md)\n- use-skillplane: Use skillplane to resolve skill (file: r1/skillplane/SKILL.md)\n- using-21nco-github: Uses the thyaravind GitHub account for repositories under dev/n or with a 21nCo origin. Use for any GitHub CLI, pull request, issue, release, or repository operation in those repositories. (file: r1/using-21nco-github/SKILL.md)\n- visualize:visualize: Create visualizations and interactive tools directly in conversation. Proactively use to show how something works; explore 'what happens when', 'what changes', or 'help me understand'; compa (file: r3/visualize/1.0.38/skills/visualize/SKILL.md)\n\u003c/skills_instructions\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0b906-a127-7a50-9024-73391abe298d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["host_skills.instructions"],"create_time":1789810614.567617,"turn_id":"01a0b906-9ffe-70d2-a60f-bf5df14e1e07"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"whats the convergence state?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0b906-a4cb-7512-907c-42a7f5a06786","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789810615.499491,"turn_id":"01a0b906-9ffe-70d2-a60f-bf5df14e1e07"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae57bd3f2887d09de1a3a1e5f0170b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b906-9ffe-70d2-a60f-bf5df14e1e07"},"summary":[{"text":"**Verifying current ledger state**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Assessing merge state and ledger snapshot**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Confirming stalled convergence due to deferred checks**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"I’m checking the ledger’s recorded clean streak against the live PR head and check state. This is a status inspection only—not another review round.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae57c7dd2487d0bc8f82e82f14c079","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1789810618.051394,"turn_id":"01a0b906-9ffe-70d2-a60f-bf5df14e1e07"},"phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_F11BHrv5uYApbMOWeQUkOTeg","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae57c7f9a087d0bdb30242ebed20f5","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,28p' /Users/serro/.agents/skills/using-21nco-github/SKILL.md\\nprintf '\\\\n--- ledger convergence ---\\\\n'\\nrg -n -A12 '^## Round 9 convergence|^## Round 9 termination|^- Clean streak:|^- Result:' .conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md | tail -n 35\\nprintf '\\\\n--- local ---\\\\n'\\nprintf 'branch=' \u0026\u0026 git branch --show-current\\nprintf 'head=' \u0026\u0026 git rev-parse HEAD\\nprintf 'upstream=' \u0026\u0026 git rev-parse '@{upstream}'\\ngit status --short\\nprintf '\\\\n--- live PR ---\\\\n'\\nGH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh auth status\\nGH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh pr view 170 --repo 21nCo/super-functions --json state,headRefOid,mergeStateStatus,reviewDecision,statusCheckRollup,updatedAt\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170\",\"yield_time_ms\":30000,\"max_output_tokens\":26000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789810618.051394,"turn_id":"01a0b906-9ffe-70d2-a60f-bf5df14e1e07"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_F11BHrv5uYApbMOWeQUkOTeg","id":"ctco_01a0b906-fdb7-7440-af23-68a29ffc1756","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789810638.263062,"turn_id":"01a0b906-9ffe-70d2-a60f-bf5df14e1e07"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.0 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"---\nname: using-21nco-github\ndescription: Uses the thyaravind GitHub account for repositories under dev/n or with a 21nCo origin. Use for any GitHub CLI, pull request, issue, release, or repository operation in those repositories.\n---\n\n# Using 21nCo GitHub\n\nFor any repository whose path is under `dev/n` or whose Git remote belongs to `21nCo`:\n\n- Run every `gh` command with `GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other`.\n- Verify `GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other gh auth status` reports `thyaravind` as the active account before making changes.\n- Never use the default GitHub account or silently fall back to another account.\n- Use the existing `21nCo` remote for pushes. If `thyaravind` lacks permission, stop and report the denial instead of creating a fork or alternate remote.\n\n--- ledger convergence ---\n420-## Historical handoff retained\n421-\n422-- Earlier bounded remediation produced `1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f` for credential redaction, cleanup-phase tracking, cleanup-path tests, and safe CLI handling.\n423-- At that round's one allowed immediate comparison, the remote branch matched the new commit while the PR API still reported the prior head `8b23aaa087b60844c63459a1c625a23dc954ba03`; this round must establish current live state independently.\n424-\n425-## Round 9 snapshot dispositions\n426-\n427-- Actionable at snapshot: 4 new unresolved GitHub threads, deduplicated to 4 root causes. All four are fixed in the reviewed local batch; threads remain unresolved and review surfaces will not be refetched after push.\n428-- Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale): 85 older unresolved threads. The two round-8 findings are already repaired at the assessed head; 83 retain earlier current-code evidence. Outdated status was not used as proof.\n429-- Invalid / Accepted Risk: 1 older GitHub finding remains invalid based on observed key-redaction behavior; no accepted risks.\n--\n437:## Round 9 convergence\n438-\n439-- Trend: stalled across scheduled convergence. Four selected roots are repaired locally, but credential-boundary and CLI runtime-output families recurred and the 36-finding analyzer family remains deferred.\n440-- Valid blocking root causes before / after: 4 selected code root causes plus 1 deferred analyzer family / 1 deferred analyzer family.\n441-- New defects: false credential-failure taxonomy for hostile descriptors, classified runtime failure replacement by persistent stderr rejection, fixed-key credential leakage, and unvalidated event/diagnostic target descriptors.\n442-- Recurring families: credential-boundary structural safety and CLI runtime-output classification recurred; the reset-trigger assessment repaired shared producer boundaries before mutation.\n443-- Fix-induced regressions: none remain. The first focused testing run exposed two incorrect new test expectations; the expectations were corrected to distinguish recoverable discriminator-value omission from unrecoverable fixed-key collision, after which all focused suites and the complete release gate passed.\n444-- Oldest deferred blocker: `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY` from round 1, last observed at 36 findings. It remains Not Attempted and prevents a clean assessment despite terminal successful required checks.\n445:- Clean streak: `0` (reset by four actionable/new root causes, recurring families, this code-changing round, and the deferred analyzer family).\n446-- Head stability: the complete snapshot stayed at `dfaeef0d1a4b25cc2ae9e10ccde0481b255637ad`; the authorized round then advanced local, remote, and PR head together to `cf76637ada4ba0263e36f30c23a278826c48dd0a` in the one allowed comparison.\n447-\n448-## Round 9 verification evidence\n449-\n450-- Focused testing: all 41 `@mcpfn/client` tests, 121 target-suite/remote-target `@mcpfn/testing` tests, and 15 conformance-cleanup `@mcpfn/cli` tests passed (177 total).\n451-- Typechecks: `@mcpfn/client`, `@mcpfn/testing`, and `@mcpfn/cli` passed under Node 22.\n452-- Release gate: `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed every reported package test/typecheck/build, Playwright, official conformance, mixed-entry redaction, examples, ESM/CJS imports, dry-run packs, packed-consumer installation, and round trips.\n453-- `git diff --check`: passed; the whole seven-file code/test batch and affected producer/consumer boundaries were reviewed before staging.\n454-- Hosted CI/reviewer state will not be refetched or polled after this snapshot.\n455-\n456:## Round 9 termination\n457-\n458:- Result: nonterminal recurring run; the four selected code roots are fixed and pushed, but the preserved deferred analyzer family prevents a clean assessment.\n459-- Automation remains disabled from the earlier retrieval-discovery stop and was not silently re-enabled during this manual retry.\n460-- No post-push review refetch, CI poll, reviewer wait, thread resolution, review dismissal, merge, or second fix loop will be performed.\n\n--- local ---\nbranch=codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910\nhead=cf76637ada4ba0263e36f30c23a278826c48dd0a\nupstream=cf76637ada4ba0263e36f30c23a278826c48dd0a\n?? .conduct/\n\n--- live PR ---\ngithub.com\n  ✓ Logged in to github.com account thyaravind (keyring)\n  - Active account: true\n  - Git operations protocol: https\n  - Token: gho_************************************\n  - Token scopes: 'gist', 'read:org', 'repo', 'workflow'\n{\"headRefOid\":\"cf76637ada4ba0263e36f30c23a278826c48dd0a\",\"mergeStateStatus\":\"DIRTY\",\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"statusCheckRollup\":[{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-18T15:01:49Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/35359481255/job/105646908168\",\"name\":\"Analyze (javascript-typescript)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:57:54Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"CodeQL - Code Quality\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:58:38Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/35359481136/job/105646907733\",\"name\":\"Analyze (actions)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:57:53Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"CodeQL\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:58:42Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/35359481255/job/105646908342\",\"name\":\"Analyze (python)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:57:53Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"CodeQL - Code Quality\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-18T15:00:04Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/35359481136/job/105646907681\",\"name\":\"Analyze (javascript-typescript)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:57:53Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"CodeQL\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:58:49Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/35359481136/job/105646907631\",\"name\":\"Analyze (python)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:57:53Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"CodeQL\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-18T15:00:02Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/35359481136/job/105646907659\",\"name\":\"Analyze (rust)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:57:53Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"CodeQL\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-18T15:17:46Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/35359481136/job/105646907426\",\"name\":\"Analyze (swift)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:57:58Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"CodeQL\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:59:46Z\",\"conclusion\":\"NEUTRAL\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://socket.dev\",\"name\":\"Socket Security: Pull Request Alerts\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:58:10Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:59:07Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SKIPPED\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://app.graphite.com/github/pr/21nCo/super-functions/170\",\"name\":\"Graphite / AI Reviews\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:59:07Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:57:51Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SKIPPED\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://sourcery.ai\",\"name\":\"Sourcery review\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:57:51Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:57:49Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SKIPPED\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1792335468\u0026installation_model_id=437494\u0026pr_number=170\u0026ref=codesmith_check\u0026repository=21nCo%2Fsuper-functions\u0026return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F170\u0026utm_campaign=21nCo%2Fsuper-functions\u0026utm_source=codesmith-check\u0026signature=d612232aa0af9b55eb351f35ebb571440c582833a6a5e5b6c7151331d3a01550\",\"name\":\"[code]smith\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:57:49Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:58:31Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/runs/105647124662\",\"name\":\"CodeQL\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:58:29Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"\"},{\"__typename\":\"StatusContext\",\"context\":\"CodeRabbit\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:57:58Z\",\"state\":\"SUCCESS\",\"targetUrl\":\"\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:58:05Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://dashboard.gitguardian.com\",\"name\":\"GitGuardian Security Checks\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:57:50Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:58:10Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://socket.dev/dashboard/org/21n/sbom/30e1f510-fa91-4a96-839b-5e175751aa90\",\"name\":\"Socket Security: Project Report\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:57:51Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-18T15:00:50Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://sonarcloud.io/dashboard?id=21nCo_super-functions\u0026pullRequest=170\",\"name\":\"SonarCloud Code Analysis\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:57:58Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-18T15:07:12Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://www.cubic.dev/pr/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170\",\"name\":\"cubic · AI code reviewer\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:58:07Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-18T15:06:43Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/35359486263\",\"name\":\"pullfrog\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-18T14:57:51Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"\"}],\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-18T15:07:07Z\"}\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae57cff90887d09ecbb462dc0d0eaa","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b906-9ffe-70d2-a60f-bf5df14e1e07"},"summary":[{"text":"**Summarizing convergence stall due to automation off**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Clarifying Sonar item resolution and merge conflict impact**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"The workflow is not converged; it is stalled at clean streak `0/2`.\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- Round 9 fixed and pushed four actionable root causes at `cf76637ada4ba0263e36f30c23a278826c48dd0a`.\n- Local, upstream, and PR heads still match.\n- Live checks are terminal: 14 successful, 1 neutral, 3 skipped.\n- One deferred blocker remains: `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY`, representing 36 findings.\n- No post-fix clean review assessment has occurred, so the latest repair round cannot count as clean.\n- PR 170 is open, with GitHub reporting merge state `DIRTY` and no review decision.\n- The automation is disabled, so it cannot accumulate the two required consecutive clean assessments.\n\nTo reach convergence, the deferred family must be resolved or validly disposed, then two complete clean scheduled assessments must occur at the same unchanged PR head. Any new finding, head change, pending/failing required check, or recurrence resets the streak.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae57d57dd887d0866605683662b691","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1789810638.909106,"turn_id":"01a0b906-9ffe-70d2-a60f-bf5df14e1e07"},"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"what does the deferred family contain?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0b90d-78e4-7c10-9f7f-fe2191a86db2","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789811063.0122,"turn_id":"01a0b90d-72f4-76d0-8550-1d4d61d74375"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae597990d887d08ef85cb5850fc4c2","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b90d-72f4-76d0-8550-1d4d61d74375"},"summary":[{"text":"**Planning analysis for Sonar deferred family**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"I’m using the SonarQube issue-listing skill to inspect the deferred family directly. The ledger only preserved the aggregate count, so I’ll distinguish current live findings from what was merely recorded in round 9.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae597bc8b487d0b88f2a9b383dd555","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1789811063.964862,"turn_id":"01a0b90d-72f4-76d0-8550-1d4d61d74375"},"phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_DbDdIp0p8KmY1hSxHvx91X7w","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae597c515c87d0b773d8b3eff07f8a","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,260p' /Users/serro/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/sonarqube/2.5.0/skills/sonar-list-issues/SKILL.md\\nprintf '\\\\n--- memory hits ---\\\\n'\\nrg -n \\\"MCP170-SONAR|Sonar.*36|36.*Sonar|PR #170.*Sonar|Sonar.*PR #170\\\" /Users/serro/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | head -n 40\\nprintf '\\\\n--- project config ---\\\\n'\\nrg -n \\\"sonar.projectKey|sonar.organization\\\" sonar-project.properties **/sonar-project.properties 2\u003e/dev/null || true\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":30000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789811063.964862,"turn_id":"01a0b90d-72f4-76d0-8550-1d4d61d74375"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_DbDdIp0p8KmY1hSxHvx91X7w","id":"ctco_01a0b90d-b249-7730-88c2-272d8062cf54","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789811077.705334,"turn_id":"01a0b90d-72f4-76d0-8550-1d4d61d74375"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 5.5 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"---\r\nname: sonar-list-issues\r\ndescription: Search and filter SonarQube issues for a project, branch, or pull request via sonarqube-cli (`-p` is always required on the CLI; resolve the key from user arguments or sonar-project.properties)\r\nargument-hint: \"[project-key?] [--severities values] [--statuses values] [--branch name]\"\r\nallowed-tools: Read, Grep, Bash(sonar:*)\r\n---\r\n\r\n# SonarQube — List Issues\r\n\r\nSearch for issues in a SonarQube project using the `sonarqube-cli`.\r\n\r\nUnlike SonarQube MCP tools (which may use a default project from integration), **`sonar list issues` always requires `-p \u003cproject-key\u003e`**. Resolve the key from the user-provided arguments or `sonar-project.properties` before running the CLI.\r\n\r\n## Usage\r\n\r\n```\r\nsonar-list-issues                                          # issues in the current project\r\nsonar-list-issues my-project                               # issues in a specific project key\r\nsonar-list-issues my-project --severities CRITICAL,BLOCKER # filter by severities\r\nsonar-list-issues my-project --statuses OPEN,CONFIRMED     # filter by status\r\nsonar-list-issues my-project --branch main                 # on a specific branch\r\nsonar-list-issues my-project --pr 42                       # on a pull request\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Prerequisites\r\n\r\nThis skill uses the `sonarqube-cli` command. The CLI must be installed and authenticated before proceeding.\r\n\r\n**Before proceeding**, verify that `sonar` is available on your PATH and authenticated. If it is not, do not attempt to call any alternative commands or invent alternatives, and show the user:\r\n\r\n\u003e Unable to list issues.\r\n\u003e\r\n\u003e **Possible causes:**\r\n\u003e - `sonarqube-cli` not installed or not authenticated — invoke the sonar-integrate skill\r\n\u003e - Project key is wrong or missing — `-p` is mandatory for `sonar list issues`; invoke the sonar-list-projects skill or set `sonar.projectKey` in `sonar-project.properties`\r\n\r\nThen ask the user (yes/no) whether to run the sonar-integrate skill now. Briefly explain what it does: it checks the SonarQube setup on their machine — installing or updating `sonarqube-cli` and verifying authentication — and re-configures the integration for this agent, including the SonarQube MCP server and secrets-scanning hooks. If they confirm, invoke the sonar-integrate skill yourself and follow it end-to-end in this session, then re-check and continue; if they decline, stop.\r\n\r\n## Instructions\r\n\r\n### Step 1: Resolve the project key\r\n\r\nThis flow uses **`sonar list issues`** (CLI), not MCP. The CLI **always** needs **`-p \u003cproject-key\u003e`** — do not invoke it without a resolved key.\r\n\r\n- If the user provided a project key, use it.\r\n- Otherwise look for `sonar.projectKey` in `sonar-project.properties` at the repo root.\r\n- If still not found, **do not run** `sonar list issues`. Tell the user: *\"Invoke the sonar-list-projects skill to find your project key, then re-run with that key,\"* or add `sonar.projectKey` to `sonar-project.properties`. (MCP integration defaults do **not** apply to this CLI command.)\r\n\r\n### Step 2: Parse optional flags from the user-provided arguments\r\n\r\n| Flag                     | Maps to CLI option |\r\n| ------------------------ | ------------------ |\r\n| `--severities \u003cvalues\u003e`  | `--severities`     |\r\n| `--statuses \u003cvalues\u003e`    | `--statuses`       |\r\n| `--branch \u003cname\u003e`        | `--branch`         |\r\n| `--pr \u003cid\u003e`              | `--pull-request`   |\r\n\r\n\u003e `sonar list issues` does **not** support filtering by issue type, rule, tag, or component, nor a `--resolved` flag. Only the options above (plus `--format`, `--page`, and `--page-size`) exist. To filter by rule/type/tag/component or to drill into a single file, use the MCP-based skills (e.g. sonar-analyze for a file, or `mcp__sonarqube__search_sonar_issues_in_projects`).\r\n\r\n### Step 3: Validate arguments\r\n\r\nBefore building the command, validate each user-supplied value against the following rules. If any value fails validation, stop and tell the user what was rejected and why — do not run the command. Validate the resolved project key (from args or `sonar-project.properties`) against the project-key pattern before running the CLI.\r\n\r\n| Argument       | Allowed pattern                                                                       |\r\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\r\n| project key    | `^[a-zA-Z0-9_\\-\\.:]+$`                                                                |\r\n| `--severities` | comma-separated subset of: `INFO`, `MINOR`, `MAJOR`, `CRITICAL`, `BLOCKER`, `HIGH`, `MEDIUM`, `LOW` |\r\n| `--statuses`   | comma-separated subset of: `OPEN`, `CONFIRMED`, `FALSE_POSITIVE`, `ACCEPTED`, `FIXED` |\r\n| `--branch`     | `^[a-zA-Z0-9_\\-\\./]+$`                                                                |\r\n| `--pr`         | digits only                                                                           |\r\n\r\n### Step 4: Run `sonar list issues`\r\n\r\nBuild and run the command using a shell command. **Always** pass **`-p`** with the key resolved in Step 1.\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nsonar list issues -p \u003cproject-key\u003e --format toon [--severities \u003cvalues\u003e] [--statuses \u003cvalues\u003e] [--branch \u003cname\u003e] [--pull-request \u003cid\u003e]\r\n```\r\n\r\nOnly include optional flags that were provided.\r\n\r\n### Step 5: Format the results\r\n\r\n**If issues are found**, present a summary line then a table sorted by severity then line number:\r\n\r\n```markdown\r\n## SonarQube Issues — `my-project` (branch: `main`)\r\n\r\nFound **12 issue(s)**:\r\n\r\n| File                 | Line | Severity  | Rule         | Message                       |\r\n| -------------------- | ---- | --------- | ------------ | ----------------------------- |\r\n| src/auth/login.py    | 12   | 🔴 Blocker | python:S2077 | SQL injection risk            |\r\n| src/utils/helpers.py | 34   | 🟠 High    | python:S2259 | Null dereference              |\r\n| src/api/routes.py    | 67   | 🟡 Medium  | python:S3776 | Cognitive complexity too high |\r\n```\r\n\r\nSeverity icons (the label depends on the server version):\r\n- 🔴 Blocker\r\n- 🟠 Critical / High\r\n- 🟡 Major / Medium\r\n- 🔵 Minor / Low\r\n- ⚪ Info\r\n\r\n**If no issues are found**:\r\n\r\n```markdown\r\n## SonarQube Issues — `my-project`\r\n\r\n✅ No issues found.\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Step 6: Next steps\r\n\r\n- To fix a specific issue: *\"Ask me to fix `\u003crule\u003e` at `\u003cfile\u003e:\u003cline\u003e`.\"*\r\n- To check the quality gate: *\"Invoke the sonar-quality-gate skill.\"*\r\n\n--- memory hits ---\n1138:- SKI-9, PR #14, mdfn, reviewThreads, exact-head, 0f7e368, pnpm mdfn:verify, Sonar, new_duplicated_lines_density, GH_CONFIG_DIR, git worktree remove\n1556:- GH_CONFIG_DIR, gh pr list, PR #144, PR #145, PR #149, PR #150, PR #151, PR #152, PR #153, PR #155, PR #170, reviewThreads, Sonar, convergence, root-cause\n\n--- project config ---\nzsh:5: no matches found: **/sonar-project.properties\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae5988781087d08e7ffdd7b25e56ed","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b90d-72f4-76d0-8550-1d4d61d74375"},"summary":[{"text":"**Checking Sonar CLI availability and authentication**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_MqGfbzxb2m3pckEmqpNHc4C9","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae598a638887d0883d5cf3d0ff5a3c","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"command -v sonar || true\\nsonar --help 2\u003e\u00261 | sed -n '1,180p'\\nprintf '\\\\n--- sonar project files ---\\\\n'\\nrg --files -g 'sonar-project.properties' -g '!node_modules' .\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":12000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789811078.736854,"turn_id":"01a0b90d-72f4-76d0-8550-1d4d61d74375"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_MqGfbzxb2m3pckEmqpNHc4C9","id":"ctco_01a0b90d-ccd5-7321-9b89-f7f8562cdd17","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789811084.501765,"turn_id":"01a0b90d-72f4-76d0-8550-1d4d61d74375"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.5 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"/Users/serro/.local/share/sonarqube-cli/bin/sonar\n  █▀ █▀█ █▄ █ ▄▀█ █▀█ █▀█ █ █ █▄▄ █▀▀   ▄█▀ █   █\n  ▄█ █▄█ █ ▀█ █▀█ █▀▄ ▀▀█ █▄█ █▄█ ██▄   ▀█▄ ██▄ █\n  v1.8.0\n\n  SonarQube CLI helps you detect security vulnerabilities\n  and code quality issues directly from your terminal.\n\n  QUICKSTART\n    1. Run sonar auth login to authenticate with SonarQube\n    2. Run sonar analyze --file \u003cfile\u003e to scan your code for issues\n\n  COMMANDS\n    analyze                                                  Analyze code for quality and security issues\n    analyze secrets                                          Scan files or stdin for hardcoded secrets\n    analyze dependency-risks                                 Analyze project dependencies for security and license risks\n    analyze agentic                                          Run server-side Vortex analysis. Limitations apply.\n    remediate                                                Trigger AI agent remediation for eligible issues (SonarQube Cloud only)\n    link                                                     Link a project to the active connection in .sonar-config.json\n\n    list \u003cissues|projects\u003e                                   List issues and projects from SonarQube Cloud or Server\n    quality-gate|qg \u003cstatus\u003e                                 Fetch quality gate status from SonarQube Cloud or Server\n    api \u003cmethod\u003e \u003cendpoint\u003e                                  Make authenticated API requests to SonarQube\n    context [action] [args...]                               Augment AI agents with context from your codebase\n\n    integrate \u003cgit|claude|copilot|codex|antigravity|cursor\u003e  Setup SonarQube integration for AI coding agents, git and others.\n\n    auth \u003clogin|logout|status\u003e                               Manage authentication tokens and credentials\n    config \u003ctelemetry\u003e                                       Configure CLI settings\n    system \u003cstatus|reset\u003e                                    System diagnostics and maintenance commands for the SonarQube CLI installation.\n    update                                                   Update SonarQube CLI to the latest version\n\n  OPTIONS\n    -h, --help     Display help for a specific command\n    -v, --version  Show current version\n\n  Read documentation: https://sonarsource.com/sonarqube/cli\n  Share feedback:     https://forms.gle/jrGic3awT5t5vf7V9\n\n--- sonar project files ---\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae598e9f9887d0a9699d5a8ece5e70","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b90d-72f4-76d0-8550-1d4d61d74375"},"summary":[{"text":"**Assessing project key derivation options**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Planning sonar auth check and list projects**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"The repository has no `sonar-project.properties`, so the issue-listing workflow cannot safely guess its project key. I’m resolving the key through the authenticated Sonar project inventory before querying PR 170.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae5993154887d0bcb77e1b566f4c28","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1789811085.713474,"turn_id":"01a0b90d-72f4-76d0-8550-1d4d61d74375"},"phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_AdHpg68Vl2t9ZQgZShH3ijsw","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae5993752487d09dec80d2a118fc2c","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,240p' /Users/serro/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/sonarqube/2.5.0/skills/sonar-list-projects/SKILL.md\\nprintf '\\\\n--- auth ---\\\\n'\\nsonar auth status\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":20000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789811085.713474,"turn_id":"01a0b90d-72f4-76d0-8550-1d4d61d74375"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_AdHpg68Vl2t9ZQgZShH3ijsw","id":"ctco_01a0b90d-f7b0-7f62-ad26-3b44d983c3f2","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789811095.47234,"turn_id":"01a0b90d-72f4-76d0-8550-1d4d61d74375"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.4 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"---\r\nname: sonar-list-projects\r\ndescription: List SonarQube projects accessible to the current user\r\nargument-hint: \"[search-query]\"\r\nallowed-tools: Bash(sonar:*)\r\n---\r\n\r\n# SonarQube — List Projects\r\n\r\nList SonarQube projects accessible to the authenticated user. Useful for discovering project keys before running other skills.\r\n\r\n## Usage\r\n\r\n```\r\nsonar-list-projects                      # list all accessible projects\r\nsonar-list-projects my-project              # search by name or key\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Prerequisites\r\n\r\nThis skill uses the `sonarqube-cli` command. The CLI must be installed and authenticated before proceeding.\r\n\r\n**Before proceeding**, verify that `sonar` is available on your PATH and authenticated. If it is not, do not attempt to call any alternative commands or invent alternatives, and show the user:\r\n\r\n\u003e Unable to list projects.\r\n\u003e\r\n\u003e **Possible causes:**\r\n\u003e - `sonarqube-cli` not installed or not authenticated — invoke the sonar-integrate skill\r\n\r\nThen ask the user (yes/no) whether to run the sonar-integrate skill now. Briefly explain what it does: it checks the SonarQube setup on their machine — installing or updating `sonarqube-cli` and verifying authentication — and re-configures the integration for this agent, including the SonarQube MCP server and secrets-scanning hooks. If they confirm, invoke the sonar-integrate skill yourself and follow it end-to-end in this session, then re-check and continue; if they decline, stop.\r\n\r\n## Instructions\r\n\r\n### Step 1: Parse optional search term from the user-provided arguments\r\n\r\n- If the user provided a search term (not a flag), pass it as `--query`.\r\n\r\n### Step 2: Validate arguments\r\n\r\nIf a `--query` search term was provided, validate it matches `^[a-zA-Z0-9_\\-\\. ]+$`. If it does not, stop and tell the user what was rejected — do not run the command.\r\n\r\n### Step 3: Run `sonar list projects`\r\n\r\nBuild and run the command using a shell command:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nsonar list projects [--query \u003csearch-term\u003e]\r\n```\r\n\r\nOnly include `--query` if a search term was provided.\r\n\r\n### Step 4: Format the results\r\n\r\n**If projects are found**:\r\n\r\n```markdown\r\n## SonarQube Projects\r\n\r\nFound **8 project(s)**:\r\n\r\n| Project key       | Name            |\r\n| ----------------- | --------------- |\r\n| my-org_backend    | Backend Service |\r\n| my-org_frontend   | Frontend App    |\r\n| my-org_shared-lib | Shared Library  |\r\n```\r\n\r\n**If no projects are found**:\r\n\r\n```markdown\r\n## SonarQube Projects\r\n\r\nNo projects found. If you expected results, check your authentication with `sonar auth status`.\r\n```\r\n\r\n**If the result is paginated** (500 projects returned), note: *\"Showing first 500 projects. Use a search term to narrow results.\"*\r\n\r\n### Step 5: Next steps\r\n\r\n- To list issues: *\"Invoke the sonar-list-issues skill with the project key, or ensure `sonar.projectKey` is in `sonar-project.properties` — the CLI always requires `-p`.\"*\r\n- To check the quality gate: *\"Invoke the sonar-quality-gate skill — add a project key only if you are not using the MCP integration default.\"*\r\n\n--- auth ---\nVerifying token......\n[✓ Connected]\nServer  https://sonarcloud.io\nOrg     21nco\nSource  OS Keychain\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae599a46e887d09c345bbd3ea7c01e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b90d-72f4-76d0-8550-1d4d61d74375"},"summary":[{"text":"**Listing valid super-function projects**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_UabKEM2yULE7dViYHu0pMDVR","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae599b000887d087d7b5b375da7502","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sonar list projects --query super-functions\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170\",\"yield_time_ms\":30000,\"max_output_tokens\":20000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789811096.330026,"turn_id":"01a0b90d-72f4-76d0-8550-1d4d61d74375"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"