=new_coverage\u0026view=list)  \\n![](https://sonarsource.github.io/sonarcloud-github-static-resources/v2/common/passed-16px.png '') [2.4% Duplication on New Code](https://sonarcloud.io/component_measures?id=21nCo_super-functions\u0026pullRequest=170\u0026metric=new_duplicated_lines_density\u0026view=list)  \\n  \\n\u003c!-- sqra-placement-anchor --\u003e\\n[See analysis details on SonarQube Cloud](https://sonarcloud.io/dashboard?id=21nCo_super-functions\u0026pullRequest=170)\\n\\n\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"currentThreadIndex\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6hIm1W\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/reports.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-10T15:21:07Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 119,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r3980654436\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Represent incomplete suites as JUnit failures**\\n\\nFor a suite containing only incomplete scenarios, failure elements are emitted for those scenarios but the `testsuite` attribute still declares `failures=\\\"0\\\"` because `safe.incomplete` is omitted here. A suite made incomplete solely by dropped diagnostic events or report truncation has the same zero-failure declaration and may not contain any failure element at all, so JUnit consumers can display a green run while the JSON report has `ok: false`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6hIm1d\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-10T15:21:08Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 218,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r3980654448\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Enforce visible tools without requiring a manifest**\\n\\nWhen `mcpfn test-target` is invoked with `--visible-tools` but without the separately optional `--manifest`, the CLI forwards the expected names, but this condition skips the only call that uses them. The command can therefore exit successfully against a target exposing the wrong tool inventory while silently ignoring an explicitly requested check; either compare the live names independently or reject this option combination.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6hJBPf\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/conformance.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-10T15:38:34Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 384,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r3980817019\",\n        \"body\": \"\u003c!-- cubic:v=af62c06d-a138-4c4d-9e49-6f4e5a3f5aa8 --\u003e\\n\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=2794c884-4528-5630-ad81-9c892ab7aad2 --\u003e\\n\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":5} --\u003e\\nP2: When a library caller acquires credentials from an env var and calls runAuthenticatedOfficialConformance without setting sensitiveEnvironmentVariables (defaults to []), the spawned @modelcontextprotocol/conformance npx process inherits that env var, since buildOfficialConformanceEnvironment only strips explicitly listed names. The CLI wires this correctly, but the library API offers no automatic guard. Note in the credential/headers doc that the credential env must also be listed in sensitiveEnvironmentVariables, or strip credential-source env names automatically.\\n\\n\u003cdetails\u003e\\n\u003csummary\u003ePrompt for AI agents\u003c/summary\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6hds9u\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-11T12:22:45Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 489,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r3989065994\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Redact acquired credential values from artifacts**\\n\\nWhen an authenticated target reflects an opaque credential under a non-sensitive field and a scenario assertion fails, the actual response is embedded in the scenario error, but the acquired header values are never supplied to the redactor. For example, an API key returned as `{ \\\"echo\\\": \\\"opaque-123\\\" }` survives `redactOAuthValue` and is subsequently written to the JSON/JUnit output and CI artifacts. Track the acquired credential values and replace them explicitly before producing diagnostics or reports.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6hds9y\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-11T12:22:45Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 245,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r3989066000\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Validate OAuth error responses before accepting rejections**\\n\\nFor expected-rejection fixtures, any response containing an OAuth `error` is accepted before its transport envelope is validated. Consequently, `chatgpt-unregistered-redirect` can pass when the server redirects to the unregistered drifted URI or returns a mismatched state with `error=invalid_request`, and the unsupported-grant case can pass with an HTTP 200 JSON error. Validate the phase-appropriate status and, for authorization redirects, the callback destination and state before assessing the error code.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6hi7n2\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-11T16:10:35Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 314,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r3991101834\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Scrub acquired credentials from inspect snapshots**\\n\\nWhen the new authenticated `inspect` option is used against a server that reflects the opaque API key or bearer token in initialization metadata or inventory (for example, a tool description), `McpFnInspector.snapshot()` only performs credential-pattern redaction and the raw acquired value remains in stdout and `--output`. The target-suite path explicitly applies `redactTargetCredentials`, but this inspect path does not, so the option advertised as producing a redacted snapshot can leak its credential.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6hvRyg\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/client/src/client.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-12T10:15:58Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 1188,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r3995915243\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Retain handles whose credential cleanup fails**\\n\\nWhen an authenticated target's protocol closes remotely, or an in-progress open is aborted, the cli…4046 tokens truncated…diagnosti\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iDJPq\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-14T09:10:49Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 385,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4003708821\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Revoke the provider-owned credential object**\\n\\nWhen a provider associates lifecycle state with the object returned by `acquire()`—for example through a `WeakMap`, a class instance, or non-enumerable properties—this spread creates a different plain object and later passes that clone to `revoke()` and `dispose()`. Such a valid provider can no longer locate or release the acquired credential, leaving cleanup permanently failed. Fresh evidence beyond the prior mutable-header concern is that the new snapshot is also used as the lifecycle callback argument; keep `acquired` for provider callbacks and use a separate header snapshot for transport and redaction.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iD65I\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-14T09:52:31Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 39,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4004012216\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Redact decoded Basic credentials**\\n\\nWhen a custom credential uses HTTP Basic authentication, this registers only the full header and its Base64 token. A server that decodes the header and reflects the username or password in an error, tool result, or diagnostic therefore exposes those credential components in reports and inspector artifacts. The new generic scheme extraction covers custom schemes but omits Basic's decoded components; decode valid Basic tokens and register both components as secrets.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iD65P\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/conformance.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-14T09:52:32Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 424,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4004012227\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Sanitize conformance setup failures before rethrowing**\\n\\nWhen a programmatic credential provider returns an invalid header value, such as one containing a newline, proxy setup throws a `Headers` validation error that includes the raw value; after cleanup, this line rethrows that error unchanged to the caller. This leaks the credential through ordinary error logging despite authenticated conformance's redaction contract. Redact setup/close failures while the immutable credential snapshot is still available before storing or rethrowing them.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iD65W\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-14T09:52:32Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 232,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4004012235\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Scrub scenario errors before their size truncation**\\n\\nFor an authenticated target whose server reflects the credential near the `scenarioRun.maxErrorBytes` boundary, `runScenarios()` applies `truncateError()` before returning these results. That leaves only a credential prefix, so the final exact-value target scrub cannot recognize it and the JSON/JUnit report leaks the prefix. Fresh evidence after the target scrubber ordering fix is that scenario results arrive here already truncated; apply target-aware scrubbing before scenario error truncation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iG9eR\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-14T12:39:03Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 582,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4005212061\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Reject forbidden API-key headers during CLI parsing**\\n\\nWhen `inspect` or `test-target` receives a syntactically valid but prohibited header such as `--api-key-header host` or `content-length`, this check accepts the configuration and defers rejection to target opening. `test-target` then emits a failed runtime report and exit 1 (and `inspect` likewise classifies the client failure as runtime), although the CLI documents malformed configuration as exit 2; validate the header against the credential-header policy here before constructing the target.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iXUYB\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-15T03:47:11Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 261,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4011736872\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Honor the configured authorization-code fixture**\\n\\nWhen a caller sets `fixture.token.code` to exercise an invalid, expired, or independently authored authorization code, the runner ignores it and always submits the code returned by the authorization redirect. Such a negative token-exchange fixture can therefore pass while never testing its configured input; use the token-request fixture's `code` when supplied, or remove the public field so it cannot silently misconfigure an experiment.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6ify-K\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/inspector/tests/authenticated-artifacts.test.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-15T11:33:34Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 246,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4015100997\",\n        \"body\": \"\u003c!-- cubic:v=0645f387-8083-48da-aee7-d3979d8e8672 --\u003e\\n\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=ef4f688d-c951-5e37-a081-804532482b41 --\u003e\\n\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":6} --\u003e\\nP2: The custom redactor in this test substitutes only substrings equal to \\\"opaque-property-key\\\" in the serialized JSON, so a stored value of \\\"value\\\" (which contains no secret) is left untouched. After exportScenario redacts the operation arguments and structuredContent, the result is { \\\"${MCPFN_SECRET}\\\": \\\"value\\\" }, not { \\\"${MCPFN_SECRET}\\\": \\\"${MCPFN_SECRET}\\\" }. The two toEqual assertions on the value therefore fail, so this test breaks the @mcpfn/inspector suite (or, if the suite is green, is not exercising the behavior it claims). The point of the test is key redaction, so assert the unchanged value.\\n\\n\u003cdetails\u003e\\n\u003csummary\u003ePrompt for AI agents\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6i7PnT\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-16T12:25:35Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 449,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4025972715\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Require no-store headers on successful token responses**\\n\\nWhen a hosted authorization server returns a valid-looking 200 JSON token set but omits `Cache-Control: no-store` or `Pragma: no-cache`, this validator accepts both the exchange and refresh response. RFC 6749 §5.1 requires those headers for responses containing tokens, so the hosted regression can report an insecure, nonconforming provider as passed; validate both cache directives before accepting the token set.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jtJst\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-18T10:25:30Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 521,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4045892488\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Mark truncated conformance reports incomplete**\\n\\nWhen `--max-report-bytes` is smaller than an otherwise successful conformance result, this replaces the captured streams with `[TRUNCATED]` but leaves `ok: true` and `exitCode: 0`, and the CLI consequently exits successfully. The resulting machine artifact silently omits evidence without any truncation or incompleteness field; record the truncation in the report and make the artifact non-passing, as the other bounded report paths do.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jtKNB\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/cli/src/bin.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-18T10:25:59Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 31,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4045895485\",\n        \"body\": \"\u003c!-- cubic:v=1751549d-12ec-4215-87aa-bdb7a88c835b --\u003e\\n\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=a8ca27b3-ecd1-5754-a86a-a9042c91c442 --\u003e\\n\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\u003e\\nP2: When a target or conformance command emits a report and cleanup retry fails, `runCli` has already queued non-awaited stdout output. This forced exit can terminate before buffered report bytes reach CI or a pipe; flush stdout before exiting, or make CLI output writes awaitable.\\n\\n\u003cdetails\u003e\\n\u003csummary\u003ePrompt for AI agents\u003c/summary\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/cli/src/bin.ts, line 26:\\n\\n\u003ccomment\u003eWhen a target or conformance command emits a report and cleanup retry fails, `runCli` has already queued non-awaited stdout output. This forced exit can terminate before buffered report \"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jvE9Q\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-18T12:19:10Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 532,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4046644273\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Report OAuth revocation failures in the correct phase**\\n\\nWhen transport shutdown succeeds but an OAuth credential provider's `revoke()` rejects, this hard-coded event reports `transport-close` even though the lease identifies the failure as `token-revocation`. Diagnostic consumers and suite timelines consequently attribute an authorization-server cleanup failure to transport/preflight cleanup; distinguish handle-close failures from release failures and use `lease.cleanupPhase()` after the transport has closed.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jvkZ0\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-18T12:46:14Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 37,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4046835594\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Parse structured cookie credentials before redaction**\\n\\nWhen a custom credential uses a structured header such as `Cookie: session=opaque-secret`, only the entire header value is registered as secret; a server response that reflects the cookie value alone (for example, `{ \\\"user\\\": \\\"opaque-secret\\\" }`) therefore passes through client events, JSON/JUnit reports, and inspector artifacts unchanged. Parse recognized structured credential headers such as `Cookie`, or reject them when their credential components cannot be registered safely.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jvkZ9\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-18T12:46:14Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 414,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4046835604\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Classify report-write failures as runtime failures**\\n\\nWhen a `test-target` run succeeds but writing `--output` fails (for example, due to permissions or a full filesystem), this plain filesystem error reaches the outer handler and is classified as usage exit code 2 because it is not one of the recognized runtime error classes. This occurs after argument parsing and target execution, and the analogous `inspect` path explicitly wraps output failures as runtime failures, so this path should likewise return the documented test/runtime exit code 1.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jwTTI\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-18T13:25:27Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 293,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4047120637\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Classify conformance output failures as test failures**\\n\\nWhen `conformance --report` cannot write its file, or an injected stdout/stderr sink rejects, this call supplies no `failureMessage`, so `preserveCleanupOwner()` rethrows the raw I/O error and the outer handler returns usage exit code 2. These failures occur after valid argument parsing and conformance execution, while the documented code 2 is reserved for invalid configuration/source/usage; wrap this path as an `McpFnClientError` so operational report-output failures return code 1.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jyW3y\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/inspector/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-18T15:03:35Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 251,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4047930609\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Validate top-level scenario keys before export**\\n\\nWhen an active target credential equals a top-level scenario key such as `name`, this mapping redacts only the corresponding value and copies the key verbatim. Consequently, `exportScenario()` returns an artifact containing the exact credential even though nested argument keys are scrubbed; validate the fixed scenario keys with the target redactor or fail the export on a structural collision.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jyW37\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-18T15:03:35Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 460,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4047930620\",\n        \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Reject parameterized cache-prevention directives**\\n\\nFresh evidence after adding the token-response header checks is that `hasHeaderDirective()` accepts malformed values such as `Cache-Control: no-store=false` and `Pragma: no-cache=false` by discarding everything after `=`. Those directives do not satisfy the required `no-store`/`no-cache` response values, yet the hosted regression reports the token exchange as passed; require these argument-free directives to have no parameter.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jyasF\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-18T15:06:27Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 390,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4047954117\",\n        \"body\": \"**[P1] Preserve the retained cleanup owner on this failure path**\\n\\nThis immediate throw bypasses the `retainedCleanup` handoff below, so when structural collision and credential/transport cleanup fail together, callers receive no `retryCleanup()` capability and cannot complete release. Preserve access to the pending cleanup owner while still failing without serializing the credential-colliding report.\\n\\n\u003cdetails\u003e\u003csummary\u003eTechnical details\u003c/summary\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Keep cleanup retryable when report structure is unsafe\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts:285-307` — captures failed close/revocation ownership in `retainedCleanup`.\\n- `mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts:389-394` — throws the structural-collision error before ownership is transferred.\\n- `mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts:407` — the\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jybjm\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"currentCount\": 1,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-18T15:07:07Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"line\": 390,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4047959467\",\n        \"body\": \"\u003c!-- cubic:v=cb20f140-b9f3-4dd8-a1f8-e7e83edc5da8 --\u003e\\n\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=47c61d9f-3ebe-5e12-b906-aab16497065f --\u003e\\n\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\u003e\\nP1: When final report redaction collides with a credential after `client.close()` failed, this branch discards the retryable cleanup owner. Preserve the cleanup error and retry handle before surfacing the structural-serialization failure.\\n\\n\u003cdetails\u003e\\n\u003csummary\u003ePrompt for AI agents\u003c/summary\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts, line 390:\\n\\n\u003ccomment\u003eWhen final report redaction collides with a credential after `client.close()` failed, this branch discards the retryable cleanup owner. Preserve the cleanup error and retry handle before surfacing the structural-serializat\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"}],"latest_token_usage_record":{"response_id":"resp_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae5d7156a487d0b42d8328aa2596c0","root_turn_id":"01a0b91a-027b-7173-bd75-a52040008bc7","session_id":"01a0b3f5-d570-7a72-b668-401efd539e3b","thread_id":"01a0b3f5-d570-7a72-b668-401efd539e3b","thread_token_usage":{"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":76163968,"input_tokens":78211442,"output_tokens":312012,"reasoning_output_tokens":117432,"total_tokens":78523454},"turn_id":"01a0b91a-027b-7173-bd75-a52040008bc7","turn_token_usage":{"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":2386304,"input_tokens":2439937,"output_tokens":8767,"reasoning_output_tokens":2539,"total_tokens":2448704},"usage":{"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":219392,"input_tokens":231191,"output_tokens":2768,"reasoning_output_tokens":0,"total_tokens":233959}},"message":"","previous_window_id":"01a0b501-0796-7581-bd08-a71c7296628d","replacement_history":[{"content":[{"text":"Use `$use-skillplane` to retrieve and execute the exact hosted workflow `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.2.0`, revision 4, digest `sha256:8781c1c12fe9d5902337d6cf21bfbac49dd3a94c7eadd46bf2622db350444022`, for https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170.\n\nThis is one run of a recurring convergence workflow. Obey the hosted skill's absolute single-round boundary: fetch the complete review surfaces once, assess the exact PR head, make at most one complete fix batch, create at most one commit, push at most once, verify local/remote/PR heads once, report, and stop. Never refetch reviews after pushing, poll CI, wait for reviewers, merge the PR, resolve threads, dismiss reviews, or begin another round in this run.\n\nExecution requirements:\n\n- Work only in `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170` on branch `codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910` for PR 170. Confirm the branch, full Git state, remote, PR head, and the `thyaravind` GitHub account before edits. Use `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other` for every `gh` command and the existing `origin` remote for pushes.\n- Retrieve the pinned hosted version through Skillplane on every run and verify its semantic version, revision, and digest before acting. If it is unavailable or differs, do not mutate the repo; report the drift and disable this automation.\n- Reuse `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170/.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md` as the compact persistent handoff. Create it if absent. Never stage or commit the ledger. Record skill identity/version/digest, round number, snapshot/head SHA, stable defect-family IDs, deduplicated valid root causes, affected contracts, dispositions, first-seen and last-attempted rounds, attempted repairs, regressions, verification evidence, required-check snapshot, convergence trend, and clean-streak state.\n- Because the user requested convergence, perform the hosted workflow's broader subsystem assessment immediately on the first scheduled run before selecting a patch. State the shared invariant, producers/consumers, failure boundaries, coordinated repair, and verification criteria in the ledger. On later reset triggers, switch the ledger mode to assessment and reassess before further mutation. Do not publish another symptom patch if a complete repair cannot be established.\n- Count root causes rather than comments. Preserve older valid blockers and deferred findings. Never infer convergence from missing history, an outdated hunk, resolved thread count, test count, or one clean snapshot.\n\nConvergence and stopping rules:\n\n1. Reset the clean streak whenever the complete snapshot has an Actionable defect, a valid Not Attempted code defect, a new defect, a recurring family, a fix-induced regression, a changed PR head between assessments, or any required CI/reviewer check is pending or failing in the single allowed immediate check snapshot.\n2. A clean assessment requires: no code change or push in that round; zero Actionable root causes; zero valid Not Attempted code root causes; no unassessed review items; no recurring/deferred blocker; the PR head stayed stable; and all required CI/reviewer checks are terminal and successful in the one allowed immediate snapshot.\n3. Declare convergence only after two consecutive clean scheduled assessments at the same PR head. Then update the ledger, disable automation `4442e7f3-60f4-4125-a8e4-c818ac40fc82` with `orca automations edit 4442e7f3-60f4-4125-a8e4-c818ac40fc82 --disabled --json`, verify with `orca automations show 4442e7f3-60f4-4125-a8e4-c818ac40fc82 --json`, report convergence, and stop.\n4. If PR 170 is merged or closed, record the terminal state, disable and verify this automation, report that the schedule stopped, and stop without mutation.\n5. If a reset-trigger assessment cannot establish a complete coordinated repair, or an external dependency blocks further progress, record the blocker, disable and verify this automation so it cannot repeat unsafe mutations, report the blocker, and stop.\n\nEnd every nonterminal run with the hosted workflow's explicit result buckets and: `One review round is complete. No post-push refetch or additional review loop was performed.`","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0b3f5-e602-7a40-a467-fefd21cfcf81","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789725632.002675,"turn_id":"01a0b3f5-d608-7651-9c53-83ca31180f35"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Use `$use-skillplane` to retrieve and execute the exact hosted workflow `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.2.0`, revision 4, digest `sha256:8781c1c12fe9d5902337d6cf21bfbac49dd3a94c7eadd46bf2622db350444022`, for https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170.\n\nThis is one run of a recurring converg