ility inventory remains 36 findings under `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY`. The captured Sonar analysis check is successful, but individual analyzer details were not substituted for the GitHub review snapshot or declared fixed.\n- Unassessed: 0 captured GitHub threads, review bodies, issue comments, or inline comments.\n\n## Round 7 required-check snapshot\n\n- One snapshot only: all 18 contexts were terminal: 14 successful, 1 neutral, and 3 skipped. There were no pending or failed contexts; `reviewDecision` was empty. CodeRabbit, Cubic, Pullfrog, CodeQL, SonarCloud Code Analysis, GitGuardian, and the applicable security checks were successful. No check polling is permitted.\n\n## Round 7 convergence\n\n- Trend: stalled across scheduled convergence. Four selected roots are repaired locally, but cleanup-phase and credential-boundary families recurred again and the 36-finding analyzer family remains deferred.\n- Valid blocking root causes before / after: 4 selected code root causes plus 1 deferred analyzer family / 1 deferred analyzer family.\n- New defects: unsafe cleanup cause exposure, pre-handle phase loss, structured Cookie component leakage, and target-suite output misclassification.\n- Recurring families: cleanup-phase classification and credential-boundary redaction recurred; the reset-trigger assessment repaired their shared lease/target/client boundaries before mutation.\n- Fix-induced regressions: none found by focused regressions, affected-package typechecks/builds, whole-batch diff review, or the final Node 22 release gate.\n- Oldest deferred blocker: `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY` from round 1, last observed at 36 findings. It remains Not Attempted and prevents a clean assessment despite terminal successful required checks.\n- Clean streak: `0` (reset by four actionable/new root causes, recurring families, this code-changing round, and the deferred analyzer family).\n- Head stability: the complete snapshot stayed at `a9fc7f4b1e6b549caf1a5f80498980167429482a`; the authorized round then advanced local, remote, and PR head together to `0e89647cb6a20681e546a22c1d2c58eabe74253e` in the one allowed comparison.\n\n## Round 7 verification evidence\n\n- Focused testing: all 43 `@mcpfn/client` tests, 226 `@mcpfn/testing` tests, and 50 `@mcpfn/cli` tests passed. New regressions prove public cleanup causes cannot expose raw provider errors, failed-open OAuth retries retain `token-revocation`, reflected Cookie components are redacted while ambiguous syntax fails closed, and target JSON/JUnit/stdout failures are safe runtime exit 1 outcomes.\n- Typechecks: `@mcpfn/client`, `@mcpfn/testing`, and `@mcpfn/cli` passed; client and testing packages were rebuilt before downstream consumer tests.\n- Release gate: the final `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed all package tests/typechecks/builds, Playwright, official conformance, mixed-entry redaction, examples, ESM/CJS imports, dry-run packs, packed-consumer installation, and round trips.\n- `git diff --check`: passed; the whole six-file code/test batch and affected lease/target/client/suite/CLI consumers were reviewed before staging.\n- Hosted CI/reviewer state will not be refetched or polled after this snapshot.\n\n## Round 7 termination\n\n- Result: nonterminal recurring run; automation remains enabled for a future separately scheduled assessment.\n- No post-push review refetch, CI poll, reviewer wait, thread resolution, review dismissal, merge, or second fix loop was performed.\n\n## Round 8 snapshot dispositions\n\n- Actionable at snapshot: 2 new unresolved GitHub threads, deduplicated to 2 root causes. Both are fixed in the reviewed local batch; threads remain unresolved and will not be refetched after push.\n- Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale): 83 older unresolved threads. The five round-7 findings are already repaired at the assessed head; 78 retain earlier current-code evidence. Outdated status was not used as proof.\n- Invalid / Accepted Risk: 1 older GitHub finding remains invalid based on observed key-redaction behavior; no accepted risks.\n- Not Attempted: the preserved Sonar maintainability/reliability inventory remains 36 findings under `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY`. The captured Sonar analysis check is successful, but individual analyzer details were not substituted for the GitHub review snapshot or declared fixed.\n- Unassessed: 0 captured GitHub threads, review bodies, issue comments, or inline comments.\n\n## Round 8 required-check snapshot\n\n- One snapshot only: 18 contexts comprised 12 successful, 1 in progress (`Analyze (swift)`), 2 neutral, and 3 skipped. CodeRabbit, GitGuardian, SonarCloud, Cubic, Pullfrog, and applicable completed security checks were successful; `reviewDecision` was empty. No check polling is permitted.\n\n## Round 8 convergence\n\n- Trend: stalled across scheduled convergence. Both selected roots are repaired locally, but credential-boundary and CLI runtime-output families recurred, one hosted check was pending in the only allowed snapshot, and the 36-finding analyzer family remains deferred.\n- Valid blocking root causes before / after: 2 selected code root causes plus 1 deferred analyzer family / 1 deferred analyzer family.\n- New defects: raw custom-target kind reconstruction after redaction and conformance output/persistence usage-error classification.\n- Recurring families: credential-boundary structural safety and CLI runtime-output classification recurred; the reset-trigger assessment reused their shared client structural validator and cleanup-aware output boundary before mutation.\n- Fix-induced regressions: the first full gate exposed changed incomplete-reason wording in three existing structural-projection regressions. The batch now preserves both the established credential-redaction and safe-serialization semantics; 119 focused testing regressions and the final complete gate pass.\n- Oldest deferred blocker: `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY` from round 1, last observed at 36 findings. It remains Not Attempted and prevents a clean assessment.\n- Clean streak: `0` (reset by two actionable/new root causes, recurring families, this code-changing round, one pending hosted check, and the deferred analyzer family).\n- Head stability: the complete snapshot stayed at `0e89647cb6a20681e546a22c1d2c58eabe74253e`; the authorized round then advanced local, remote, and PR head together to `dfaeef0d1a4b25cc2ae9e10ccde0481b255637ad` in the one allowed comparison.\n\n## Round 8 verification evidence\n\n- Focused testing: 119 target-suite/remote-target regressions and 15 conformance-cleanup regressions passed. New assertions prove a custom target kind that conflicts with its redactor cannot enter JSON/JUnit artifacts and conformance report/stdout/stderr failures return exit 1 with fixed safe text.\n- Typechecks/builds: `@mcpfn/testing` and `@mcpfn/cli` passed under Node 22 before the complete gate.\n- Release gate: the final `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed all package tests/typechecks/builds, Playwright, official conformance, mixed-entry redaction, examples, ESM/CJS imports, dry-run packs, packed-consumer installation, and round trips.\n- `git diff --check`: passed; the whole four-file code/test batch and affected suite/CLI consumers were reviewed before staging.\n- Hosted CI/reviewer state will not be refetched or polled after this snapshot.\n\n## Round 8 termination\n\n- Result: nonterminal recurring run; automation remains enabled for a future separately scheduled assessment.\n- No post-push review refetch, CI poll, reviewer wait, thread resolution, review dismissal, merge, or second fix loop was performed.\n\n## Round 1 termination\n\n- Result: nonterminal recurring run; automation remains enabled for a future separately scheduled assessment.\n- No post-push review refetch, CI poll, reviewer wait, thread resolution, review dismissal, merge, or second fix loop was performed.\n\n## Historical handoff retained\n\n- Earlier bounded remediation produced `1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f` for credential redaction, cleanup-phase tracking, cleanup-path tests, and safe CLI handling.\n- At that round's one allowed immediate comparison, the remote branch matched the new commit while the PR API still reported the prior head `8b23aaa087b60844c63459a1c625a23dc954ba03`; this round must establish current live state independently.\n\n## Round 9 snapshot dispositions\n\n- Actionable at snapshot: 4 new unresolved GitHub threads, deduplicated to 4 root causes. All four are fixed in the reviewed local batch; threads remain unresolved and review surfaces will not be refetched after push.\n- Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale): 85 older unresolved threads. The two round-8 findings are already repaired at the assessed head; 83 retain earlier current-code evidence. Outdated status was not used as proof.\n- Invalid / Accepted Risk: 1 older GitHub finding remains invalid based on observed key-redaction behavior; no accepted risks.\n- Not Attempted: the preserved Sonar maintainability/reliability inventory remains 36 findings under `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY`. The captured Sonar analysis check is successful, but individual analyzer details were not substituted for the GitHub review snapshot or declared fixed.\n- Unassessed: 0 captured GitHub threads, review bodies, issue comments, raw inline comments, or nested thread comments.\n\n## Round 9 required-check snapshot\n\n- One snapshot only: all 18 contexts were terminal: 14 successful, 1 neutral, and 3 skipped. There were no pending or failed contexts; `reviewDecision` was empty. No check polling is permitted.\n\n## Round 9 convergence\n\n- Trend: stalled across scheduled convergence. Four selected roots are repaired locally, but credential-boundary and CLI runtime-output families recurred and the 36-finding analyzer family remains deferred.\n- Valid blocking root causes before / after: 4 selected code root causes plus 1 deferred analyzer family / 1 deferred analyzer family.\n- New defects: false credential-failure taxonomy for hostile descriptors, classified runtime failure replacement by persistent stderr rejection, fixed-key credential leakage, and unvalidated event/diagnostic target descriptors.\n- Recurring families: credential-boundary structural safety and CLI runtime-output classification recurred; the reset-trigger assessment repaired shared producer boundaries before mutation.\n- Fix-induced regressions: none remain. The first focused testing run exposed two incorrect new test expectations; the expectations were corrected to distinguish recoverable discriminator-value omission from unrecoverable fixed-key collision, after which all focused suites and the complete release gate passed.\n- Oldest deferred blocker: `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY` from round 1, last observed at 36 findings. It remains Not Attempted and prevents a clean assessment despite terminal successful required checks.\n- Clean streak: `0` (reset by four actionable/new root causes, recurring families, this code-changing round, and the deferred analyzer family).\n- Head stability: the complete snapshot stayed at `dfaeef0d1a4b25cc2ae9e10ccde0481b255637ad`; the authorized round then advanced local, remote, and PR head together to `cf76637ada4ba0263e36f30c23a278826c48dd0a` in the one allowed comparison.\n\n## Round 9 verification evidence\n\n- Focused testing: all 41 `@mcpfn/client` tests, 121 target-suite/remote-target `@mcpfn/testing` tests, and 15 conformance-cleanup `@mcpfn/cli` tests passed (177 total).\n- Typechecks: `@mcpfn/client`, `@mcpfn/testing`, and `@mcpfn/cli` passed under Node 22.\n- Release gate: `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed every reported package test/typecheck/build, Playwright, official conformance, mixed-entry redaction, examples, ESM/CJS imports, dry-run packs, packed-consumer installation, and round trips.\n- `git diff --check`: passed; the whole seven-file code/test batch and affected producer/consumer boundaries were reviewed before staging.\n- Hosted CI/reviewer state will not be refetched or polled after this snapshot.\n\n## Round 9 termination\n\n- Result: nonterminal recurring run; the four selected code roots are fixed and pushed, but the preserved deferred analyzer family prevents a clean assessment.\n- Automation remains disabled from the earlier retrieval-discovery stop and was not silently re-enabled during this manual retry.\n- No post-push review refetch, CI poll, reviewer wait, thread resolution, review dismissal, merge, or second fix loop will be performed.\nimport {\n  McpFnRedactionLimitError,\n  McpFnStructuralCredentialCollisionError,\n  beginTargetCredentialRedaction,\n  redactTargetCredentials,\n} from \"./remote-target.js\";\nimport type { Implementation, ServerCapabilities } from \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/types.js\";\nimport {\n  McpFnClientError,\n  type McpFnDiagnosticEvent,\n  type McpFnTarget,\n  type McpFnTargetDescriptor,\n} from \"@mcpfn/client\";\nimport type { McpFnManifest } from \"@mcpfn/core\";\n\nimport { assertManifestContract, McpFnAssertionError, stableJson } from \"./assertions.js\";\nimport {\n  McpFnTestClient,\n  McpFnTestClientCleanupError,\n  type McpFnTestClientOptions,\n} from \"./client.js\";\nimport {\n  MCPFN_REPORT_SCHEMA_VERSION,\n  MCPFN_TESTING_VERSION,\n  normalizeMcpFnReportFailure,\n  type McpFnReportFailure,\n} from \"./reports.js\";\nimport {\n  runScenarios,\n  type McpFnScenario,\n  type McpFnScenarioResult,\n} from \"./scenarios.js\";\n\nexport interface RunMcpFnTargetSuiteOptions {\n  target: McpFnTarget;\n  scenarios?: McpFnScenario[];\n  manifest?: McpFnManifest;\n  expectedToolNames?: readonly string[];\n  clientInfo?: Implementation;\n  client?: McpFnTestClientOptions;\n  scenarioRun?: NonNullable<Parameters<typeof runScenarios>[2]>;\n  /** Aggregate JSON size cap. Defaults to 1 MiB. */\n  maxReportBytes?: number;\n  /** Diagnostic timeline count cap. Defaults to 500. */\n  maxTimelineEvents?: number;\n}\n\nexport interface McpFnTargetSuiteReport {\n  formatVersion: 1;\n  kind: \"mcpfn.target-suite-report\";\n  status: \"complete\" | \"incomplete\";\n  runtime: {\n    node: string;\n    scenarioFormatVersion: 1;\n    reportSchemaVersion: string;\n    packages: { testing: string };\n  };\n  ok: boolean;\n  target: McpFnTargetDescriptor;\n  server?: Implementation;\n  capabilities?: ServerCapabilities;\n  manifestChecked: boolean;\n  manifestHash?: string;\n  total: number;\n  passed: number;\n  failed: number;\n  incomplete: number;\n  droppedResults: number;\n  droppedObservedEvents: number;\n  redactionOmittedObservedEvents?: number;\n  incompleteReason?: string;\n  failure?: McpFnReportFailure;\n  timeline: McpFnDiagnosticEvent[];\n  droppedTimelineEvents: number;\n  results: McpFnScenarioResult[];\n}\n\nconst suiteCleanupOwners = new WeakMap<McpFnTargetSuiteCleanupError, { close: () => Promise<void>; pending?: Promise<void> }>();\n\n/** Final cleanup failed. The bounded report is a snapshot; retain this error to retry. */\nexport class McpFnTargetSuiteCleanupError extends Error {\n  constructor(readonly report: McpFnTargetSuiteReport, close: () => Promise<void>) {\n    super(\"Target suite cleanup failed; retain this error and retryCleanup()\");\n    this.name = \"McpFnTargetSuiteCleanupError\";\n    suiteCleanupOwners.set(this, { close });\n  }\n\n  retryCleanup(): Promise<void> {\n    const owner = suiteCleanupOwners.get(this);\n    if (!owner) return Promise.resolve();\n    if (owner.pending) return owner.pending;\n    const pending = Promise.resolve().then(owner.close).then(\n      () => { suiteCleanupOwners.delete(this); },\n      () => { throw this; },\n    ).finally(() => { owner.pending = undefined; });\n    owner.pending = pending;\n    return pending;\n  }\n}\n\n/** Runs local, stdio, HTTP, or custom targets through the production session engine. */\nexport async function runMcpFnTargetSuite(\n  options: RunMcpFnTargetSuiteOptions,\n): Promise<McpFnTargetSuiteReport> {\n  const finishRedaction = beginTargetCredentialRedaction(options.target);\n  try { return await runTargetSuite(options); }\n  finally { finishRedaction(); }\n}\n\n/** Apply the target-owned scrubber before the bounded generic artifact pass. */\nfunction redactSuiteArtifact<T>(target: McpFnTarget, value: T, options: { preserveKeys?: boolean } = {}): T {\n  const scrubbed = target.redact ? target.redact(value, options) : value;\n  return redactTargetCredentials(target, scrubbed, options);\n}\n\nasync function runTargetSuite(options: RunMcpFnTargetSuiteOptions): Promise<McpFnTargetSuiteReport> {\n  const timeline: McpFnDiagnosticEvent[] = [];\n  let droppedTimelineEvents = 0;\n  let timelineBytes = 0;\n  let timelineCountExceeded = false;\n  let timelineBytesExceeded = false;\n  let timelineSerializationFailed = false;\n  let timelineRedactionFailed = false;\n  let observedDiagnosticRedactionOmissions = 0;\n  let initialDiagnosticRedactionOmissions = 0;\n  const timelineSizes: number[] = [];\n  const maxTimelineEvents = options.maxTimelineEvents ?? 500;\n  if (!Number.isInteger(maxTimelineEvents) || maxTimelineEvents < 1) {\n    throw new Error(\"maxTimelineEvents must be a positive integer\");\n  }\n  const maxReportBytes = options.maxReportBytes ?? 1_048_576;\n  validateReportCap(maxReportBytes);\n  const consumerDiagnostic = options.client?.diagnostics;\n  let client: McpFnTestClient | undefined;\n  let manifestChecked = false;\n  let failure: McpFnReportFailure | undefined;\n  let cleanupFailure: McpFnReportFailure | undefined;\n  let retainedCleanup: (() => Promise<void>) | undefined;\n  let capturedTarget: McpFnTargetDescriptor = { kind: \"custom\" };\n  let capturedManifestHash: string | undefined;\nimport { readFile, writeFile } from \"node:fs/promises\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { InMemoryTaskStore } from \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/experimental/tasks/stores/in-memory.js\";\nimport { cac } from \"cac\";\nimport { diagnoseMcpAuthorization } from \"@mcpfn/auth\";\nimport {\n  stdioTarget,\n  streamableHttpTarget,\n  McpFnClientError,\n  type McpFnTarget,\n} from \"@mcpfn/client\";\nimport {\n  diffManifests,\n  validateManifest,\n  type McpFnManifest,\n} from \"@mcpfn/core\";\nimport { McpFnInspector } from \"@mcpfn/inspector\";\nimport {\n  McpFnTestClient,\n  McpFnTestClientCleanupError,\n  McpFnAssertionError,\n  McpFnConformanceCleanupError,\n  McpFnTargetSuiteCleanupError,\n  assertManifestContract,\n  authenticatedHttpTarget,\n  validateRemoteCredentialHeaders,\n  beginTargetCredentialRedaction,\n  redactTargetCredentials,\n  createMcpFnTargetSuiteJUnit,\n  runAuthenticatedOfficialConformance,\n  runOfficialConformance,\n  runMcpFnTargetSuite,\n  runScenarios,\n  createMcpFnScenarioReport,\n  type McpFnRemoteCredential,\n} from \"@mcpfn/testing\";\n\nimport { loadManifestSource, loadScenarios } from \"./load.js\";\n\nexport { loadManifestSource, loadScenarios };\n\nexport interface CliRunOptions {\n  cwd?: string;\n  stdout?: (text: string) => void | Promise<void>;\n  stderr?: (text: string) => void | Promise<void>;\n}\n\ndeclare const __MCPFN_CLI_VERSION__: string;\n\nexport const MCPFN_CLI_EXIT_SUCCESS = 0;\nexport const MCPFN_CLI_EXIT_TEST_FAILURE = 1;\nexport const MCPFN_CLI_EXIT_USAGE = 2;\nexport const MCPFN_CLI_VERSION = __MCPFN_CLI_VERSION__;\n\ninterface RemoteAuthCliOptions {\n  bearerTokenEnv?: string;\n  apiKeyEnv?: string;\n  apiKeyHeader?: string;\n}\n\nconst inspectorCleanupOwners = new WeakMap<\n  McpFnInspectorCleanupError,\n  { close: () => Promise<void>; pending?: Promise<void> }\n>();\n\n/** Inspector cleanup failed. Retain this error until its transport closes. */\nexport class McpFnInspectorCleanupError extends Error {\n  constructor(close: () => Promise<void>, cause: unknown) {\n    super(\n      \"Inspector cleanup failed; retain this error and retryCleanup()\",\n      { cause },\n    );\n    this.name = \"McpFnInspectorCleanupError\";\n    inspectorCleanupOwners.set(this, { close });\n  }\n\n  retryCleanup(): Promise<void> {\n    const owner = inspectorCleanupOwners.get(this);\n    if (!owner) return Promise.resolve();\n    if (owner.pending) return owner.pending;\n    const pending = Promise.resolve().then(owner.close).then(\n      () => { inspectorCleanupOwners.delete(this); },\n      () => { throw this; },\n    ).finally(() => { owner.pending = undefined; });\n    owner.pending = pending;\n    return pending;\n  }\n}\n\ntype CliCleanupError =\n  | McpFnTestClientCleanupError\n  | McpFnTargetSuiteCleanupError\n  | McpFnConformanceCleanupError\n  | McpFnInspectorCleanupError;\n\nfunction isCliCleanupError(error: unknown): error is CliCleanupError {\n  return error instanceof McpFnTestClientCleanupError ||\n    error instanceof McpFnTargetSuiteCleanupError ||\n    error instanceof McpFnConformanceCleanupError ||\n    error instanceof McpFnInspectorCleanupError;\n}\n\nasync function preserveCleanupOwner(\n  owner: CliCleanupError | undefined,\n  operation: () => Promise<void>,\n  failureMessage?: string,\n): Promise<void> {\n  try {\n    await operation();\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (owner) throw owner;\n    if (failureMessage) {\n      throw new McpFnClientError(\n        \"MCPFN_OPERATION_FAILED\",\n        failureMessage,\n        { phase: \"capability-operation\" },\n      );\n    }\n    throw error;\n  }\n}\n\nexport async function runCli(\n  argv = process.argv.slice(2),\n  runOptions: CliRunOptions = {},\n): Promise<number> {\n  const cwd = runOptions.cwd ?? process.cwd();\n  const stdout = runOptions.stdout ?? ((text: string) => writeProcessOutput(process.stdout, text));\n  const stderr = runOptions.stderr ?? ((text: string) => writeProcessOutput(process.stderr, text));\n  let exitCode = 0;\nimport { startAuthenticatedServer } from \"../../test-support/authenticated-server.js\";\nimport { afterEach, describe, expect, it, vi } from \"vitest\";\nimport { McpFnClient, customTarget } from \"@mcpfn/client\";\nimport { authenticatedHttpTarget } from \"@mcpfn/testing\";\nimport { McpFnInspector } from \"../src/index.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"authenticated programmatic artifacts\", () => {\n const closeCallbacks: Array<() => Promise<void>> = [];\n afterEach(async () => { await Promise.allSettled(closeCallbacks.splice(0).map(close => close())); });\n  it.each([\"opaque-programmatic-secret\", \"opaque.[*]+secret\", \"MCPFN_SECRET\", \"SECRET\", \"[REDACTED]\", \"REDACTED\"])(\"redacts programmatic inspector artifacts for %s\", async (secret) => {\n    const fixture = await startAuthenticatedServer(secret, true);\n    closeCallbacks.push(fixture.close);\n    const events: unknown[] = [];\n    const client = new McpFnClient({\n      target: authenticatedHttpTarget(fixture.url, { credential: { headers: { authorization: `Bearer ${secret}` } } }),\n      events: event => { events.push(event); },\n      diagnostics: event => { events.push(event); },\n    });\n    const inspector = new McpFnInspector(client);\n    closeCallbacks.push(() => client.close());\n    await inspector.connect();\n    const operation = { kind: \"tools.call\" as const, name: \"identity\", arguments: {} };\n    const result = await inspector.run(operation);\n    expect(JSON.stringify(result)).toContain(secret); // Protocol values retain application semantics.\n    const snapshot = await inspector.snapshot();\n    expect(JSON.stringify(snapshot)).not.toContain(secret);\n    const exported = inspector.exportScenario(\"reflection\", operation, result);\n    expect(JSON.stringify(exported)).not.toContain(secret);\n    expect(JSON.stringify(events)).toContain(\"echo\");\n    expect(JSON.stringify(events)).not.toContain(secret);\n    await client.close();\n    expect(JSON.stringify(inspector.timeline())).not.toContain(secret);\n  });\n\n  it(\"marks an event omission when its discriminator matches a credential\", async () => {\n    const secret = \"logging.message\";\n    const fixture = await startAuthenticatedServer(secret, true);\n    closeCallbacks.push(fixture.close);\n    const events: any[] = [];\n    const client = new McpFnClient({\n      target: authenticatedHttpTarget(fixture.url, { credential: { headers: { authorization: `Bearer ${secret}` } } }),\n      events: event => { events.push(event); },\n    });\n    const inspector = new McpFnInspector(client);\n    closeCallbacks.push(() => client.close());\n    await inspector.connect();\n    const operation = { kind: \"tools.call\" as const, name: \"identity\", arguments: {} };\n    const result = await inspector.run(operation);\n    const snapshot = await inspector.snapshot();\n    expect(snapshot.clientState).toBe(\"connected\");\n    expect(events.some(event => event.kind === \"logging.message\")).toBe(false);\n    expect(events.some(event => client.isRedactionOmission(event))).toBe(true);\n    expect(snapshot.timelineComplete).toBe(false);\n    expect(JSON.stringify(snapshot)).not.toContain(secret);\n    const exported = inspector.exportScenario(\"reflection\", operation, result);\n    expect(JSON.stringify(exported)).toContain(\"${MCPFN_SECRET}\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"fails closed when an authenticated credential matches clientState\", async () => {\n    const secret = \"connected\";\n    const fixture = await startAuthenticatedServer(secret, true);\n    closeCallbacks.push(fixture.close);\n    const client = new McpFnClient({\n      target: authenticatedHttpTarget(fixture.url, {\n        credential: { headers: { authorization: `Bearer ${secret}` } },\n      }),\n    });\n    const inspector = new McpFnInspector(client);\n    closeCallbacks.push(() => client.close());\n    await inspector.connect();\n    const error = await inspector.snapshot().then(\n      () => { throw new Error(\"Expected structural collision\"); },\n      failure => failure as Error,\n    );\n    expect(error.message).toBe(\"MCP artifact structure conflicts with credential redaction\");\n    expect(error.message).not.toContain(secret);\n  });\n\n  it(\"keeps oversized diagnostic payloads from breaking a tool operation\", async () => {\n    const secret = \"oversized-secret\";\n    const fixture = await startAuthenticatedServer(secret, true, \"x\".repeat(300_000) + secret);\n    closeCallbacks.push(fixture.close);\n    const events: any[] = [];\n    const client = new McpFnClient({\n      target: authenticatedHttpTarget(fixture.url, { credential: { headers: { authorization: `Bearer ${secret}` } } }),\n      events: event => { events.push(event); },\n    });\n    closeCallbacks.push(() => client.close());\n    await client.connect();\n    const result = await client.tools.call(\"identity\", {});\n    expect(JSON.stringify(result)).toContain(secret);\n    expect(events.some(event => event.payload?.omitted === true)).toBe(true);\n    expect(JSON.stringify(events)).not.toContain(secret);\n  });\n\n});\n\nit(\"redacts client-event payloads in payload mode and records fallbacks as omissions\", async () => {\n  const events: any[] = [];\n  let throwOnPayload = false;\n  const target = customTarget({\n    kind: \"custom\",\n    open: async () => { throw new Error(\"unused\"); },\n    redact: <T>(value: T, options): T => {\n      if (throwOnPayload && value && typeof value === \"object\" && \"status\" in value) {\n        throw new Error(\"payload redaction unavailable\");\n      }\n      if (options?.preserveKeys !== false) return value;\n      return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(value).replaceAll(\"passed\", \"[REDACTED]\")) as T;\n    },\n  });\n  const client = new McpFnClient({ target, events: event => { events.push(event); } });\n  const inspector = new McpFnInspector(client);\n  const emitEvent = (client as unknown as {\n    emitEvent(kind: \"logging.message\", payload: unknown): Promise<void>;\n  }).emitEvent.bind(client);\n  await emitEvent(\"logging.message\", { status: \"passed\" });\n  expect(events[0].kind).toBe(\"logging.message\");\n  expect(events[0].payload.status).toBe(\"[REDACTED]\");\n  throwOnPayload = true;\n  await emitEvent(\"logging.message\", { status: \"passed\" });\n  expect(events[1].payload).toMatchObject({ omitted: true });\n  expect(client.isRedactionOmission(events[1])).toBe(true);\n  const snapshot = await inspector.snapshot();\n  expect(snapshot.timelineComplete).toBe(false);\n  expect(snapshot.droppedEvents).toBe(1);\n});\n\nit(\"reconstructs diagnostic discriminators around payload redaction\", async () => {\n  const observed: any[] = [];\nmcpfn/testing/tests/host-authorization.test.ts:14:  \"cache-control\": \"no-store\",\nmcpfn/testing/tests/host-authorization.test.ts:15:  pragma: \"no-cache\",\nmcpfn/testing/tests/host-authorization.test.ts:245:  [\"token-exchange\", \"cache-control\"],\nmcpfn/testing/tests/host-authorization.test.ts:246:  [\"token-exchange\", \"pragma\"],\nmcpfn/testing/tests/host-authorization.test.ts:247:  [\"token-refresh\", \"cache-control\"],\nmcpfn/testing/tests/host-authorization.test.ts:248:  [\"token-refresh\", \"pragma\"],\nmcpfn/testing/tests/suite.test.ts:310:  const first = error.retryCleanup();\nmcpfn/testing/tests/suite.test.ts:311:  expect(error.retryCleanup()).toBe(first);\nmcpfn/testing/tests/suite.test.ts:314:  await Promise.all([error.retryCleanup(), error.retryCleanup()]);\nmcpfn/testing/tests/suite.test.ts:316:  await error.retryCleanup();\nmcpfn/cli/tests/cli.test.ts:317:      await expect(failure.retryCleanup()).resolves.toBeUndefined();\nmcpfn/cli/tests/inspect-redaction.test.ts:79:    await expect(failure.retryCleanup()).resolves.toBeUndefined();\nmcpfn/testing/tests/authenticated-output.test.ts:55:  await (failure as McpFnConformanceCleanupError).retryCleanup();\nmcpfn/testing/tests/authenticated-output.test.ts:136:  await error.retryCleanup();\nmcpfn/cli/tests/conformance-cleanup.test.ts:118:    await expect(failure.retryCleanup()).resolves.toBeUndefined();\nmcpfn/cli/tests/conformance-cleanup.test.ts:165:      await expect(failure.retryCle