sts{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events\",\"type\":\"Organization\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"name\":\"coderabbitai\",\"description\":\"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\\r\\n\\r\\n## Features\\r\\n\\r\\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \\r\\n\\r\\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \\r\\n\\r\\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \\r\\n\\r\\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\",\"external_url\":\"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai\",\"created_at\":\"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-31T23:59:54Z\",\"permissions\":{\"actions\":\"read\",\"checks\":\"write\",\"contents\":\"write\",\"discussions\":\"read\",\"issues\":\"write\",\"members\":\"read\",\"merge_queues\":\"read\",\"metadata\":\"read\",\"pull_requests\":\"write\",\"statuses\":\"write\"},\"events\":[\"issues\",\"issue_comment\",\"label\",\"merge_group\",\"organization\",\"pull_request\",\"pull_request_review\",\"pull_request_review_comment\",\"pull_request_review_thread\",\"release\",\"repository\"]},\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5621014110\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5621014110\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5621014110,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABTwneXg\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"sourcery-ai[bot]\",\"id\":58596630,\"node_id\":\"MDM6Qm90NTg1OTY2MzA=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/48477?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai%5Bbot%5D\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/sourcery-ai\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-10T15:17:19Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-10T15:17:19Z\",\"body\":\"<!-- Generated by sourcery-ai[bot]: start review_guide -->\\n\\n## Reviewer's Guide\\n\\nThis PR adds a transport-neutral, authenticated external MCP testing platform: credential-safe Streamable HTTP targets and conformance proxying, provider-shaped OAuth fixtures, structured bounded reports, expanded CLI controls, and workspace/packed/published release verification with adoption documentation.\\n\\n#### Sequence diagram for authenticated external MCP target lifecycle\\n\\n```mermaid\\nsequenceDiagram\\n    participant Suite as McpFnTargetSuite\\n    participant Target as authenticatedHttpTarget\\n    participant Provider as McpFnRemoteCredentialProvider\\n    participant Client as McpFnClient\\n    participant Server as ExternalMCPServer\\n\\n    Suite->>Target: open(targetContext)\\n    Target->>Provider: acquire(context)\\n    Provider-->>Target: McpFnRemoteCredential\\n    Target->>Target: validateRemoteCredentialHeaders()\\n    Target->>Client: streamableHttpTarget(url, requestInit)\\n    Client->>Server: MCP requests with credential headers\\n    Server-->>Client: MCP responses\\n    Suite->>Target: close()\\n    Target->>Client: close()\\n    Target->>Provider: revoke(credential, context)\\n    Target->>Provider: dispose(credential, context)\\n```\\n\\n#### Sequence diagram for authenticated official conformance proxy\\n\\n```mermaid\\nsequenceDiagram\\n    participant CLI as McpFnCLI\\n    participant Conformance as runAuthenticatedOfficialConformance\\n    participant Provider as CredentialProvider\\n    participant Proxy as LoopbackAuthProxy\\n    participant Runner as OfficialConformanceRunner\\n    participant Server as ProtectedMCPServer\\n\\n    CLI->>Conformance: runAuthenticatedOfficialConformance()\\n    Conformance->>Provider: acquireRemoteCredential()\\n    Provider-->>Conformance: credential headers\\n    Conformance->>Proxy: createAuthenticatedConformanceProxy()\\n    Conformance->>Runner: runOfficialConformance(proxy.url)\\n    Runner->>Proxy: MCP requests\\n    Proxy->>Server: forward requests with injected headers\\n    Server-->>Proxy: MCP responses\\n    Proxy-->>Runner: MCP responses\\n    Runner-->>Conformance: exit code and output\\n    Conformance->>Proxy: close()\\n    Conformance->>Provider: release()\\n```\\n\\n#### Flow diagram for bounded McpFn test reporting\\n\\n```mermaid\\nflowchart LR\\n    Target[MCP target] --> Suite[runMcpFnTargetSuite]\\n    Suite --> Checks[Manifest and visibility checks]\\n    Checks --> Scenarios[runScenarios]\\n    Scenarios --> Failure[normalizeMcpFnReportFailure]\\n    Scenarios --> Report[Target-suite report]\\n    Failure --> Report\\n    Report --> JSON[Bounded redacted JSON]\\n    Report --> JUnit[createMcpFnTargetSuiteJUnit]\\n    JSON --> Artifacts[CI or consumer artifacts]\\n    JUnit --> Artifacts\\n```\\n\\n#### Flow diagram for hosted authorization regression fixtures\\n\\n```mermaid\\nflowchart LR\\n    Fixtures[createHostedAuthorizationFixtures] --> Registration[Client registration]\\n    Registration --> Authorization[Authorization code and S256 PKCE request]\\n    Authorization --> Exchange[Token exchange]\\n    Exchange --> Refresh[Refresh token flow]\\n    Fixtures --> Drift[Redirect drift case]\\n    Fixtures --> Grants[Advertised and unsupported grant cases]\\n    Drift --> Results[runHostedAuthorizationRegression]\\n    Refresh --> Results\\n    Grants --> Results\\n    Results --> Report[Layered authorization results]\\n```\\n\\n### File-Level Changes\\n\\n| Change | Details | Files |\\n| ------ | ------- | ----- |\\n| Added transport-neutral authenticated external-server testing with explicit credential lifecycle management and redirect-safe HTTP handling. | <ul><li>Introduced URL-plus-credential targets for Streamable HTTP servers, including bounded header validation and provider acquire/revoke/dispose semantics.</li><li>Prevented credential forwarding on redirects and excluded secret material from target descriptors and reports.</li><li>Added an official-SDK-only authenticated external server fixture and regression scenarios.</li><li>Added packed, workspace, and published-consumer verification for external targets.</li></ul> | `mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts`<br/>`mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts`<br/>`mcpfn/testing/tests/remote-target.test.ts`<br/>`mcpfn/examples/external-http-server.mjs`<br/>`mcpfn/examples/external-scenarios.mjs`<br/>`scripts/test-mcpfn-external-server.mjs`<br/>`scripts/test-mcpfn-registry-install.mjs`<br/>`scripts/gate-mcpfn-release.mjs` |\\n| Extended official conformance execution to support authenticated loopback proxying while isolating credentials from the upstream runner. | <ul><li>Added credential-backed authenticated conformance proxying with fixed loopback/upstream path validation and idempotent cleanup.</li><li>Sanitized child environments and redacted captured stdout/stderr and failure details.</li><li>Added structured conformance reports with stable exit behavior and upstream-conformance failure classification.</li></ul> | `mcpfn/testing/src/conformance.ts`<br/>`mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts`<br/>`mcpfn/testing/tests/testing.test.ts`<br/>`mcpfn/cli/tests/cli.test.ts` |\\n| Added hosted authorization fixtures and regression coverage for provider-shaped OAuth interoperability. | <ul><li>Added independent ChatGPT-, Claude-, and DCR-shaped registration and authorization inputs.</li><li>Covered authorization code, S256 PKCE, refresh, extensible advertised grants, redirect drift, incompatible registrations, and unsupported token grants.</li><li>Added structured authorization phases and failure classification.</li></ul> | `mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts`<br/>`mcpfn/testing/tests/host-authorization.test.ts`<br/>`mcpfn/testing/src/index.ts` |\\n| Standardized bounded, redacted, versioned test artifacts and exposed new CLI target-validation controls. | <ul><li>Added JSON/JUnit report serializers with report-schema, package-version, and Node-runtime provenance.</li><li>Added post-serialization size bounds, XML-safe output, redaction, and machine-readable failure layers.</li><li>Extended test-target, inspect, and conformance with environment-backed bearer/API-key options, manifest checks, visible-tool checks, JUnit output, and report caps.</li><li>Updated report and compatibility documentation for schema evolution and rollback expectations.</li></ul> | `mcpfn/testing/src/reports.ts`<br/>`mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts`<br/>`mcpfn/testing/tests/reports.test.ts`<br/>`mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts`<br/>`mcpfn/README.md`<br/>`mcpfn/TESTING.md`<br/>`mcpfn/ADR-0001-COMPATIBILITY.md`<br/>`mcpfn/ARCHITECTURE.md`<br/>`mcpfn/REQUIREMENTS.md`<br/>`mcpfn/TEST_VECTORS.md`<br/>`mcpfn/cli/README.md` |\\n| Completed release, CI, packaging, and adoption support for the new testing surface. | <ul><li>Uploaded McpFn release-gate artifacts in CI and added exact published-package consumer verification to tag publishing.</li><li>Bumped @mcpfn/testing and @mcpfn/cli versions and updated dependency pins.</li><li>Documented third-party server adoption, explicit package upgrades, evidence boundaries, and official conformance pinning.</li></ul> | `.github/workflows/ci.yml`<br/>`.github/workflows/publish-tag.yml`<br/>`mcpfn/testing/package.json`<br/>`mcpfn/cli/package.json`<br/>`package-lock.json`<br/>`mcpfn/ADOPTION.md`<br/>`mcpfn/MIGRATION.md`<br/>`mcpfn/testing/README.md` |\\n\\n---\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Tips and commands</summary>\\n\\n#### Interacting with Sourcery\\n\\n- **Trigger a new review:** Comment `@sourcery-ai review` on the pull request.\\n- **Continue discussions:** Reply directly to Sourcery's review comments.\\n- **Generate a GitHub issue from a review comment:** Ask Sourcery to create an\\n  issue from a review comment by replying to it. You can also reply to a\\n  review comment with `@sourcery-ai issue` to create an issue from it.\\n- **Generate a pull request title:** Write `@sourcery-ai` anywhere in the pull\\n  request title to generate a title at any time. You can also comment\\n  `@sourcery-ai title` on the pull request to (re-)generate the title at any time.\\n- **Generate a pull request summary:** Write `@sourcery-ai summary` anywhere in\\n  the pull request body to generate a PR summary at any time exactly where you\\n  want it. You can also comment `@sourcery-ai summary` on the pull request to\\n  (re-)generate the summary at any time.\\n- **Generate reviewer's guide:** Comment `@sourcery-ai guide` on the pull\\n  request to (re-)generate the reviewer's guide at any time.\\n- **Resolve all Sourcery comments:** Comment `@sourcery-ai resolve` on the\\n  pull request to resolve all Sourcery comments. Useful if you've already\\n  addressed all the comments and don't want to see them anymore.\\n- **Dismiss all Sourcery reviews:** Comment `@sourcery-ai dismiss` on the pull\\n  request to dismiss all existing Sourcery reviews. Especially useful if you\\n  want to start fresh with a new review - don't forget to comment\\n  `@sourcery-ai review` to trigger a new review!\\n\\n#### Customizing Your Experience\\n\\nAccess your [dashboard](https://app.sourcery.ai) to:\\n- Enable or disable review features such as the Sourcery-generated pull request\\n  summary, the reviewer's guide, and others.\\n- Change the review language.\\n- Add, remove or edit custom review instructions.\\n- Adjust other review settings.\\n\\n#### Getting Help\\n\\n- [Contact our support team](mailto:support@sourcery.ai) for questions or feedback.\\n- Visit our [documentation](https://docs.sourcery.ai) for detailed guides and information.\\n- Keep in touch with the Sourcery team by following us on [X/Twitter](https://x.com/SourceryAI), [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/company/sourcery-ai/) or [GitHub](https://github.com/sourcery-ai).\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<!-- Generated by sourcery-ai[bot]: end review_guide -->\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5621014110/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":{\"id\":48477,\"client_id\":\"Iv1.25d1242251bb3f02\",\"slug\":\"sourcery-ai\",\"node_id\":\"MDM6QXBwNDg0Nzc=\",\"owner\":{\"login\":\"sourcery-ai\",\"id\":36609879,\"node_id\":\"REDACTED\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36609879?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/sourcery-ai\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sourcery-ai/received_events\",\"type\":\"Organization\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"name\":\"Sourcery AI\",\"description\":\"## Instant AI code reviews\\r\\n\\r\\n- Speed up your code review process\\r\\n- Improve your code quality and ensure high quality code\\r\\n- Spend less time on reviews\\r\\n- Accelerate development velocity\",\"external_url\":\"https://sourcery.ai\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/sourcery-ai\",\"created_at\":\"2019-12-06T13:02:12Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-02-25T16:07:55Z\",\"permissions\":{\"actions\":\"write\",\"checks\":\"write\",\"contents\":\"write\",\"emails\":\"read\",\"issues\":\"write\",\"members\":\"read\",\"metadata\":\"read\",\"pull_requests\":\"write\",\"statuses\":\"write\",\"workflows\":\"write\"},\"events\":[\"check_suite\",\"issues\",\"issue_comment\",\"member\",\"membership\",\"organization\",\"pull_request\",\"pull_request_review\",\"pull_request_review_comment\",\"push\",\"repository\"]},\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5621036284\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5621036284\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5621036284,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABTwo0_A\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"socket-security[bot]\",\"id\":95510084,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOBbFeRA\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/156372?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/socket-security%5Bbot%5D\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/socket-security\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/socket-security%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/socket-security%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/socket-security%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/socket-security%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/socket-security%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/socket-security%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/socket-security%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/socket-security%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/socket-security%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-10T15:18:52Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-15T14:02:27Z\",\"body\":\"**Review the following changes in direct dependencies.** Learn more about [Socket for GitHub](https://socket.dev?utm_medium=gh).\\n\\n<table>\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th>Diff</th>\\n<th width=\\\"200px\\\">Package</th>\\n<th align=\\\"left\\\" width=\\\"100px\\\">Supply Chain<br/>Security</th>\\n<th align=\\\"left\\\" width=\\\"100px\\\">Vulnerability</th>\\n<th align=\\\"left\\\" width=\\\"100px\\\">Quality</th>\\n<th align=\\\"left\\\" width=\\\"100px\\\">Maintenance</th>\\n<th align=\\\"left\\\" width=\\\"100px\\\">License</th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody>\\n<tr><td align=\\\"center\\\"><a href=\\\"https://socket.dev/dashboard/org/21n/diff-scan/b67024f3-63ca-474d-b4c6-9e0573d5fac8?tab=dependencies&dependency_item_key=101946348222\\\"><img src=\\\"https://github-app-statics.socket.dev/diff-added.svg\\\" title=\\\"Added\\\" alt=\\\"Added\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\"></a></td><td><a href=\\\"https://socket.dev/dashboard/org/21n/diff-scan/b67024f3-63ca-474d-b4c6-9e0573d5fac8?tab=dependencies&dependency_item_key=101946348222\\\">npm/​@​mcpfn/​client@​0.0.4</a></td><td align=\\\"left\\\" title=\\\"Not analyzed\\\">N/A</td><td align=\\\"left\\\" title=\\\"Not analyzed\\\">N/A</td><td align=\\\"left\\\" title=\\\"Not analyzed\\\">N/A</td><td align=\\\"left\\\" title=\\\"Not analyzed\\\">N/A</td><td align=\\\"left\\\" title=\\\"Not analyzed\\\">N/A</td></tr>\\n<tr><td align=\\\"center\\\"><a href=\\\"https://socket.dev/dashboard/org/21n/diff-scan/b67024f3-63ca-474d-b4c6-9e0573d5fac8?tab=dependencies&dependency_item_key=101946349828\\\"><img src=\\\"https://github-app-statics.socket.dev/diff-updated.svg\\\" title=\\\"Updated\\\" alt=\\\"Updated\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\"></a></td><td><a href=\\\"https://socket.dev/dashboard/org/21n/diff-scan/b67024f3-63ca-474d-b4c6-9e0573d5fac8?tab=dependencies&dependency_item_key=101946349828\\\">npm/​@​mcpfn/​inspector@​0.0.3 ⏵ 0.0.4</a></td><td align=\\\"left\\\" title=\\\"Not analyzed\\\">N/A</td><td align=\\\"left\\\" title=\\\"Not analyzed\\\">N/A</td><td align=\\\"left\\\" title=\\\"Not analyzed\\\">N/A</td><td align=\\\"left\\\" title=\\\"Not analyzed\\\">N/A</td><td align=\\\"left\\\" title=\\\"Not analyzed\\\">N/A</td></tr>\\n<tr><td align=\\\"center\\\"><a href=\\\"https://socket.dev/dashboard/org/21n/diff-scan/b67024f3-63ca-474d-b4c6-9e0573d5fac8?tab=dependencies&dependency_item_key=101945750064\\\"><img src=\\\"https://github-app-statics.socket.dev/diff-updated.svg\\\" title=\\\"Updated\\\" alt=\\\"Updated\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\"></a></td><td><a href=\\\"https://socket.dev/dashboard/org/21n/diff-scan/b67024f3-63ca-474d-b4c6-9e0573d5fac8?tab=dependencies&dependency_item_key=101945750064\\\">npm/​@​mcpfn/​testing@​0.0.4 ⏵ 0.0.5</a></td><td align=\\\"left\\\" title=\\\"Not analyzed\\\">N/A</td><td align=\\\"left\\\" title=\\\"Not analyzed\\\">N/A</td><td align=\\\"left\\\" title=\\\"Not analyzed\\\">N/A</td><td align=\\\"left\\\" title=\\\"Not analyzed\\\">N/A</td><td align=\\\"left\\\" title=\\\"Not analyzed\\\">N/A</td></tr>\\n</tbody>\\n</table>\\n\\n[View full report](https://socket.dev/dashboard/org/21n/diff-scan/b67024f3-63ca-474d-b4c6-9e0573d5fac8?tab=dependencies)\\n\\n<!-- overview-comment -->\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5621036284/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":{\"id\":156372,\"client_id\":\"Iv1.0dc8bfb0ebf2ec17\",\"slug\":\"socket-security\",\"node_id\":\"A_kwHOBCHXrM4AAmLU\",\"owner\":{\"login\":\"SocketDev\",\"id\":69326764,\"node_id\":\"REDACTED\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69326764?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SocketDev\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/SocketDev\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SocketDev/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SocketDev/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SocketDev/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SocketDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SocketDev/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SocketDev/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SocketDev/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SocketDev/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SocketDev/received_events\",\"type\":\"Organization\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"name\":\"Socket Security\",\"description\":\"### Socket protects your app from malicious dependencies lurking in your open source supply chain.\\r\\n\\r\\nOpen source code makes up 90% of most codebases. It is critical to manage it effectively to reduce your security risk.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Detect and block open source supply chain attacks\\r\\n\\r\\nSecurity teams depend on Socket to prevent malicious open source dependencies from infiltrating their apps.\\r\\n\\r\\nSocket dramatically improves your open source security posture by _detecting and blocking the attacks you don't expect_ – malware, install scripts, hidden code, typo-squatting, and more – which aren't caught by traditional vulnerability scanners.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Block malware** – Block emerging malware threats\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Block typo-squatting** – Block malicious packages that differ in name by only a few characters, and recommend the correct package\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Detect hidden code** – Detect obfuscated, minified, or hidden code\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Detect privileged API usage** – Report when a dependency update introduces new risky API usage – filesystem, network, child_process, eval()\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Detect suspicious updates** – Sudden inclusion of privileged APIs in patch or minor releases\\r\\n\\r\\nSocket currently [supports 80+ detections](https://socket.dev/alerts) in 5 categories: supply chain risk, quality, maintenance, known vulnerabilities, and license problems.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Take charge of your dependency health\\r\\n\\r\\nSocket improves security outcomes and reduces work for security teams by **surfacing actionable security information directly inline in GitHub** so developers are empowered to make better decisions.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Five minute deployment** – The easiest security product you'll ever deploy in your organization. Just install a GitHub app and you're done.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Provide security feedback directly on PRs** – Empower developers to solve security issues before they're deployed into production.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Automated security** – Spend security team resources auditing the highest-impact dependencies, instead of all or nothing.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Socket detects what vulnerability scanners can’t\\r\\n\\r\\nIt's no longer sufficient to scan for known vulnerabilities (CVEs) and stop there. And yet, that's what the leading \\\"supply chain security\\\" products do, leaving you vulnerable.\\r\\n\\r\\nIt can take weeks or months for a CVE to be discovered, reported, and detected by tools. But in today's culture of fast development, a malicious dependency can be updated, merged, and running in production in days or even sometimes hours.\\r\\n\\r\\nDefenders need a new approach to address emerging threats from malicious dependencies:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Maintainer intentionally added malware** – Rogue maintainer sabotaged his own open source package with 100M downloads/month, affecting companies such as Amazon AWS\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Package hijacked and poisoned w/ cryptominers and password-stealing malware** – Deliberate malware introduced into multiple packages with 30M downloads/month each\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Package hijacked to add backdoor targeting a specific organization** – Obfuscated malware added to a dependency which targeted a single company, went undetected for over a week, and made it into their production build\\r\\n\\r\\n- **NPM package manager allowed anyone to publish new versions of any package** – Attackers could publish new versions of any NPM package without authorization _for multiple years_\\r\\n\\r\\nUsing third-party dependencies without proper vetting leaves you open to hacking, breaches, and assorted security misfortune.\",\"external_url\":\"https://socket.dev\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/socket-security\",\"created_at\":\"2021-12-04T00:33:05Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-07-02T15:17:38Z\",\"permissions\":{\"checks\":\"write\",\"contents\":\"write\",\"emails\":\"read\",\"issues\":\"read\",\"members\":\"read\",\"merge_queues\":\"read\",\"metadata\":\"read\",\"pull_requests\":\"write\"},\"events\":[\"check_run\",\"check_suite\",\"issue_comment\",\"member\",\"merge_group\",\"merge_queue_entry\",\"organization\",\"public\",\"pull_request\",\"push\",\"repository\"]},\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5621037480\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5621037480\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5621037480,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABTwo5qA\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"qodo-code-review[bot]\",\"id\":151058649,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-10T15:18:58Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-10T15:18:58Z\",\"body\":\"<h3>PR Summary by Qodo</h3>\\n\\nEnable transport-neutral authenticated MCP conformance testing\\n\\n<code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code>🧪 Tests</code> <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code>⚙️ Configuration changes</code> <code>🕐 40+ Minutes</code>\\n\\n<img src=\\\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\\\" height=\\\"10%\\\" alt=\\\"Grey Divider\\\">\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>AI Description</summary>\\n\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n<br/>\\n\\n><pre>\\n>• Test authenticated third-party MCP servers without requiring the McpFn server runtime.\\n>• Produce bounded, redacted reports with actionable failure and runtime provenance.\\n>• Verify external, packed, and published consumers through fixtures and release gates.\\n></pre>\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Diagram</summary>\\n\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n```mermaid\\ngraph TD\\n  CLI[\\\"McpFn CLI\\\"] --> TEST[\\\"Testing package\\\"] --> TARGET[\\\"Auth HTTP target\\\"] --> SERVER[\\\"External MCP server\\\"]\\n  TEST --> SUITE[\\\"Regression suite\\\"] --> REPORTS[\\\"JSON / JUnit\\\"]\\n  TEST --> PROXY[\\\"Auth proxy\\\"] --> CONF[\\\"Official conformance\\\"]\\n```\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>High-Level Assessment</summary>\\n\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n>The following are alternative approaches to this PR:\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><b>1. Implement a separate testing transport client</b></summary>\\n\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n- ➕ Could isolate testing behavior from production client changes.\\n- ➕ Might expose test-specific hooks more directly.\\n- ➖ Would duplicate MCP session and transport semantics.\\n- ➖ Creates protocol drift between production and conformance paths.\\n- ➖ Requires independently maintaining authorization and lifecycle behavior.\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><b>2. Add authentication directly to the upstream runner</b></summary>\\n\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n- ➕ Could remove the local loopback proxy.\\n- ➕ May eventually provide a standardized conformance authentication interface.\\n- ➖ Depends on upstream API and release timing.\\n- ➖ Risks exposing credentials through child arguments or environment.\\n- ➖ Does not solve regression-target credential lifecycle ownership.\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n>**Recommendation:** Keep the PR’s approach: reuse the production @mcpfn/client session engine for regression targets and retain the narrow loopback proxy for the unmodified official runner. This minimizes protocol duplication, keeps credentials outside upstream process inputs, and provides explicit acquire/revoke/dispose ownership.\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary> Files changed (35) <code> +2957 / -337 </code> </summary>\\n\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Enhancement (7) <code> +1137 / -68 </code></summary>\\n\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>index.ts<code>Add authenticated targets and bounded CLI reports</code> <code>+159/-8</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n>Add authenticated targets and bounded CLI reports\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>• Extends conformance, inspect, and test-target with environment-backed credentials. It also adds manifest and visible-tool checks, JUnit output, bounded reports, and stable runtime-failure JSON.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n><a href='https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-97edce1081d52ca886871984f7718ef98ee57660b3529ba1b1e947231869e036'>mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts</a>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>conformance.ts<code>Secure authenticated official conformance execution</code> <code>+111/-24</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n>Secure authenticated official conformance execution\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>• Adds credential leases, header validation, sanitized child environments, idempotent proxy closure, redacted output, and structured failures.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n><a href='https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-e5be1f3f8b7c02817cf6f33a698bd0963f06dba4b5f14fccb0d1dcb26e4a705f'>mcpfn/testing/src/conformance.ts</a>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>host-authorization.ts<code>Add hosted authorization regression harness</code> <code>+364/-0</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n>Add hosted authorization regression harness\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>• Introduces independent ChatGPT-, Claude-, and DCR-shaped fixtures covering S256 PKCE, refresh, redirect drift, extension grants, and unsupported grants.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n><a href='https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-5531f2e268697d158da6f6535506e0aa8f66b538e3ebfc3413aa18751a4253b7'>mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts</a>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>index.ts<code>Export transport-neutral testing APIs</code> <code>+3/-0</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n>Export transport-neutral testing APIs\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>• Publishes hosted authorization, authenticated remote target, and machine-report modules from the package root.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n><a href='https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-208b57220bac62d337da05cfd32912ec737ecb13a7002ab56b8c930b9ec19658'>mcpfn/testing/src/index.ts</a>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>remote-target.ts<code>Implement authenticated remote HTTP targets</code> <code>+224/-0</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n>Implement authenticated remote HTTP targets\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>• Adds bounded credential headers, acquire/revoke/dispose leases, redirect rejection, URL validation, and production-client transport delegation.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n><a href='https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-bc0703ad428f9c64202cfff108abc55f815ad2346a72462a934c3af463ca1e63'>mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts</a>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>reports.ts<code>Add structured failures and JUnit serialization</code> <code>+208/-0</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n>Add structured failures and JUnit serialization\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>• Classifies failures by system layer and emits redacted, XML-safe, size-bounded JUnit with package and runtime provenance.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n><a href='https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-0bbc1dc4407f267ffcc7413973d6ce25b0ad9c2f95c66d0ee5a74122d6bfe4a9'>mcpfn/testing/src/reports.ts</a>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>suite.ts<code>Return stable reports for target failures</code> <code>+68/-36</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n>Return stable reports for target failures\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>• Captures connection and initialization failures instead of throwing, adds report provenance, and includes failure details in size bounding.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n><a href='https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-41d6906f5331a3459a18e0497a36b13f5665ee149b573f35f1e6d39dd2f4ba5b'>mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts</a>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Tests (6) <code> +667 / -4 </code></summary>\\n\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>cli.test.ts<code>Test authenticated CLI target execution</code> <code>+78/-4</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n>Test authenticated CLI target execution\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>• Verifies structured connection failures, environment-backed API keys, JSON and JUnit output, report bounds, and empty-secret validation.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n><a href='https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-8821b187bc79acaa53a2b2e441a3215d60382ceb79e325db49cf3d84378872cd'>mcpfn/cli/tests/cli.test.ts</a>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>host-authorization.test.ts<code>Verify hosted authorization compatibility matrix</code> <code>+77/-0</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n>Verify hosted authorization compatibility matrix\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>• Exercises all provider-shaped fixtures and confirms redirect drift and unsupported grants fail at their intended phases.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n><a href='https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-0dc72fab92555976b2b9858fb5621c9de77855b28d382f0c6330de84567d97bf'