 same testing package version constant used by production bundles into Vitest.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n><a href='https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-181433c1d1ad6e3346373ee669cd3f46fdeb38a8ddb7bf67d269d9713b6d4feb'>mcpfn/testing/vitest.config.ts</a>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>package-lock.json<code>Synchronize McpFn package dependency graph</code> <code>+601/-249</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n>Synchronize McpFn package dependency graph\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>• Records testing and CLI version bumps, the runtime authentication dependency, and regenerated workspace dependency placement.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n><a href='https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-053150b640a7ce75eff69d1a22cae7f0f94ad64ce9a855db544dda0929316519'>package-lock.json</a>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>gate-mcpfn-release.mjs<code>Gate public exports and external server behavior</code> <code>+8/-0</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n>Gate public exports and external server behavior\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>• Checks packed-consumer exports and runs the authenticated official-SDK fixture during the release gate.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n><a href='https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-ac47695e6cdf4da7f9fac66b31c7bbb86f475880d60e7748dba903d741562edd'>scripts/gate-mcpfn-release.mjs</a>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>test-mcpfn-registry-install.mjs<code>Verify exact registry releases in clean consumers</code> <code>+158/-0</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n>Verify exact registry releases in clean consumers\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>• Retries registry installation and exercises published testing or CLI packages against the external authenticated fixture.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n><a href='https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-09b3986f6b604324d01aeeb45b2057f9704c931a47fe4bd23dceba2518dbad68'>scripts/test-mcpfn-registry-install.mjs</a>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n\\n</details>\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5621037480/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":{\"id\":484649,\"client_id\":\"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057\",\"slug\":\"qodo-code-review\",\"node_id\":\"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up\",\"owner\":{\"login\":\"qodo-ai\",\"id\":183290039,\"node_id\":\"O_kgDOCuzItw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/qodo-ai\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events\",\"type\":\"Organization\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"name\":\"Qodo Code Review\",\"description\":\"### The AI Code Review Platform\\r\\n\\r\\n## Get Started\\r\\nSimply sign into Github and click the \\\"Configure\\\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Overview\\r\\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\\r\\n\\r\\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\\r\\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\\r\\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\\r\\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\\r\\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\\r\\n- Build production software where reliability matters\\r\\n\\r\\n## Qodo Capabilities\\r\\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\\r\\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\\r\\n  - No manual trigger required\\r\\n\\r\\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\\r\\n  - Understands cross-file changes\\r\\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\\r\\n\\r\\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\\r\\n  - Concrete code fixes\\r\\n  - Clear explanations\\r\\n  - Prioritized feedback\\r\\n\\r\\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\\r\\n  - Identifies risky patterns\\r\\n  - Reduces attack surface area\",\"external_url\":\"https://www.qodo.ai/\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review\",\"created_at\":\"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z\",\"permissions\":{\"actions\":\"read\",\"checks\":\"read\",\"contents\":\"write\",\"discussions\":\"write\",\"issues\":\"write\",\"metadata\":\"read\",\"pull_requests\":\"write\"},\"events\":[\"check_run\",\"check_suite\",\"discussion_comment\",\"issue_comment\",\"pull_request\",\"pull_request_review_comment\",\"push\"]},\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5621086631\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5621086631\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5621086631,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABTwr5pw\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"qodo-code-review[bot]\",\"id\":151058649,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-10T15:22:29Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-16T15:29:59Z\",\"body\":\"<h3>Code Review by Qodo</h3>\\n\\n<code>🐞 Bugs (0)</code>  <code>📘 Rule violations (0)</code>  <code>📜 Skill insights (0)</code>\\n\\n<img src=\\\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\\\" height=\\\"10%\\\" alt=\\\"Grey Divider\\\">\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n<img src=\\\"https://img.shields.io/badge/High-634FD1?style=flat-square\\\" height=\\\"20px\\\" alt=\\\"Action required\\\">\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>  1.  <s>Filtered servers skip inventory checks</s> <code>✓ Resolved</code> <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>≡ Correctness</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n> <details open>\\n><summary>Description</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n><b><i>test-target</i></b> forwards <b><i>expectedToolNames</i></b> even when no <b><i>--manifest</i></b> was supplied, but\\n><b><i>runMcpFnTargetSuite</i></b> consumes those names only inside its manifest branch. Request-filtered servers\\n>invoked with <b><i>--visible-tools</i></b> alone therefore run scenarios and can return success even when their\\n>live tool inventory contains hidden or missing tools.\\n></pre>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Code</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><code>[mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts[R281-284]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-97edce1081d52ca886871984f7718ef98ee57660b3529ba1b1e947231869e036R281-R284)</code>\\n>\\n>```diff\\n>+        expectedToolNames: options.visibleTools\\n>+          ?.split(\\\",\\\")\\n>+          .map((name) => name.trim())\\n>+          .filter(Boolean),\\n>```\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The CLI parses and forwards the supplied names, but the suite only passes them to the assertion that\\n>compares inventory after confirming a manifest exists. With no manifest, execution proceeds directly\\n>to scenarios.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts[281-285]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts/#L281-L285)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts[104-114]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts/#L104-L114)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/assertions.ts[39-52]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/assertions.ts/#L39-L52)</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n>```\\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\\n>\\n>## Issue description\\n>`--visible-tools` is silently ignored by `test-target` unless callers also pass `--manifest`, so the advertised live-inventory check does not run for manifest-free remote targets.\\n>\\n>## Fix Focus Areas\\n>- mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts[281-285]\\n>- mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts[104-109]\\n>\\n>## Recommended Fix\\n>Make the target-suite path validate the live `tools/list` names whenever `expectedToolNames` is supplied, independently of manifest validation. Retain the existing manifest contract checks when a manifest is present, and add coverage for `test-target --visible-tools` without `--manifest`.\\n>```\\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n<hr/>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>  2.  <s>Cleanup failures suppress suite reports</s> <code>✓ Resolved</code> <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>☼ Reliability</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n> <details open>\\n><summary>Description</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n><b><i>runMcpFnTargetSuite</i></b> awaits <b><i>client.close()</i></b> in a <b><i>finally</i></b> block outside the error-normalization\\n>path, so a close rejection escapes instead of becoming a report failure. This occurs when a target\\n>transport close or remote credential revoke/dispose rejects, preventing CLI callers from producing\\n>the promised JSON and JUnit artifacts.\\n></pre>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Code</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><code>[mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts[122]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-41d6906f5331a3459a18e0497a36b13f5665ee149b573f35f1e6d39dd2f4ba5bR122-R122)</code>\\n>\\n>```diff\\n>+    await client?.close();\\n>```\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The suite catches connection and scenario errors at lines 119-120 but performs close afterward at\\n>line 122, where any rejection bypasses report construction beginning at line 124.\\n><b><i>McpFnTestClient.close()</i></b> delegates directly to the session close, and authenticated remote-target\\n>cleanup awaits both transport shutdown and provider-controlled revoke/dispose hooks, all of which\\n>can reject.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts[119-134]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts/#L119-L134)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/client.ts[145-148]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/client.ts/#L145-L148)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts[202-223]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts/#L202-L223)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts[277-301]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts/#L277-L301)</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n>```\\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\\n>\\n>## Issue description\\n>`runMcpFnTargetSuite` lets errors from `client.close()` escape its structured failure handling, so transport or credential cleanup failures prevent report generation.\\n>\\n>## Fix Focus Areas\\n>- mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts[119-124]\\n>- mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts[202-223]\\n>\\n>## Recommended Fix\\n>Catch and normalize errors from `client.close()` before constructing the report. Preserve an existing execution failure when both execution and cleanup fail, while recording cleanup failure details so the returned report remains incomplete and unsuccessful.\\n>```\\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n<hr/>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>  3.  <s>JUnit reports hide incomplete tests</s> <code>✓ Resolved</code> <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>≡ Correctness</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n> <details open>\\n><summary>Description</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n><b><i>createMcpFnTargetSuiteJUnit</i></b> emits a <b><i>&lt;failure&gt;</i></b> element for every scenario whose status is not\\n><b><i>passed</i></b>, but calculates the testsuite <b><i>failures</i></b> attribute from <b><i>safe.failed</i></b> only. Whenever a\\n>suite contains an <b><i>incomplete</i></b> scenario, CI consumers that rely on the aggregate JUnit attribute\\n>undercount the failed test cases despite the serialized testcase containing a failure element.\\n></pre>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Code</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><code>[mcpfn/testing/src/reports.ts[117]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-0bbc1dc4407f267ffcc7413973d6ce25b0ad9c2f95c66d0ee5a74122d6bfe4a9R117-R117)</code>\\n>\\n>```diff\\n>+  const failures = safe.failed + (safe.failure ? 1 : 0);\\n>```\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The serializer explicitly creates a failure element for any result other than <b><i>passed</i></b>, including\\n>one with the <b><i>incomplete</i></b> failure type, but its aggregate uses only the separately tracked <b><i>failed</i></b>\\n>total. The suite report tracks <b><i>failed</i></b> and <b><i>incomplete</i></b> independently, so incomplete results are\\n>valid and reachable.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/reports.ts[97-118]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/reports.ts/#L97-L118)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/reports.ts[131-150]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/reports.ts/#L131-L150)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts[124-156]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts/#L124-L156)</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n>```\\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\\n>\\n>Issue description\\n>`createMcpFnTargetSuiteJUnit` writes `<failure>` nodes for both failed and incomplete scenarios, while the testsuite-level `failures` count excludes incomplete scenarios.\\n>\\n>Fix Focus Areas\\n>- mcpfn/testing/src/reports.ts[97-118]\\n>- mcpfn/testing/tests/reports.test.ts[39-57]\\n>\\n>Recommended Fix\\n>Compute the `failures` attribute from every testcase that receives a `<failure>` node, including incomplete scenarios and the suite-level failure case. Add a regression test with at least one incomplete scenario and assert that the testsuite `failures` value matches the number of serialized failure elements.\\n>```\\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n<hr/>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<details><summary><ins><strong>View high (2)</strong></ins></summary><br/>\\n<details>\\n<summary>  4.  <s>Authorization failures pass regression tests</s> <code>✓ Resolved</code> <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>≡ Correctness</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n> <details open>\\n><summary>Description</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n><b><i>runHostedCase</i></b> catches exceptions, extracts no error code from ordinary <b><i>Error</i></b> values, and passes\\n>that undefined code to <b><i>assessHostedCase</i></b>. A network failure, malformed successful response, or\\n>non-OAuth HTTP error during an expected allowed case is consequently classified as allowed and\\n>returned with <b><i>status: &quot;passed&quot;</i></b>.\\n></pre>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Code</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><code>[mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[R301-304]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-5531f2e268697d158da6f6535506e0aa8f66b538e3ebfc3413aa18751a4253b7R301-R304)</code>\\n>\\n>```diff\\n>+    const safe = redactOAuthValue(error) as Record<string, unknown>;\\n>+    const code = typeof safe.code === \\\"string\\\" ? safe.code : undefined;\\n>+    const message = typeof safe.message === \\\"string\\\" ? safe.message : String(safe);\\n>+    return assessHostedCase(fixture, phase, undefined, code, message);\\n>```\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The catch path supplies an undefined <b><i>errorCode</i></b> for normal thrown errors, while the assessor\\n>defines any absent error code as <b><i>allowed</i></b>; the expected allowed fixtures therefore pass even when\\n>the request flow threw.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[300-304]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts/#L300-L304)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[315-332]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts/#L315-L332)</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n>```\\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\\n>\\n>Issue description\\n>`runHostedCase` currently sends caught errors without an OAuth error code into `assessHostedCase`, whose outcome logic treats a missing code as an allowed result. This allows failed requests and invalid non-OAuth responses to make expected-success fixtures pass.\\n>Fix Focus Areas\\n>- mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[300-304]\\n>- mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[315-319]\\n>Recommended Fix\\n>Represent caught exceptions as an explicit failed outcome rather than deriving their outcome from an absent OAuth error code. Update `assessHostedCase` or add a dedicated failure-result path so any exception always produces `status: \\\"failed\\\"`, while preserving the redacted error message.\\n>```\\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n<hr/>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>  5.  <s>Reports can expose query secrets</s> <code>✓ Resolved</code> <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛨ Security</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n> <details open>\\n><summary>Description</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n><b><i>authenticatedHttpTarget</i></b> stores <b><i>targetUrl.toString()</i></b> directly in its descriptor, retaining the\\n>URL query string. A target URL containing an API key or token in its query is returned by\\n><b><i>describe()</i></b> and reaches the target-suite report despite the credential-exclusion guarantee.\\n></pre>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Code</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><code>[mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts[R108-110]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-bc0703ad428f9c64202cfff108abc55f815ad2346a72462a934c3af463ca1e63R108-R110)</code>\\n>\\n>```diff\\n>+    descriptor: {\\n>+      url: targetUrl.toString(),\\n>+      authenticated: true,\\n>```\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The new target normalizes but does not remove query parameters before placing the full URL in its\\n>descriptor. Target-suite reports serialize that descriptor, while the underlying standard HTTP\\n>target explicitly removes the query string before exposing its own descriptor.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts[102-110]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts/#L102-L110)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts[156-166]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts/#L156-L166)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts[144-147]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts/#L144-L147)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/client/src/targets.ts[85-93]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/client/src/targets.ts/#L85-L93)</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n>```\\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\\n>\\n>## Issue description\\n>The authenticated target exposes query parameters through its descriptor, which can serialize query-based credentials into reports.\\n>\\n>## Fix Focus Areas\\n>- mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts[102-110]\\n>- mcpfn/client/src/targets.ts[85-93]\\n>\\n>## Recommended Fix\\n>Keep `targetUrl` unchanged for transport requests, but create a separate descriptor URL and clear its `search`, `hash`, `username`, and `password` before assigning `descriptor.url`. Mirror the sanitization used by `streamableHttpTarget`.\\n>```\\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n<hr/>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n</details>\\n<br/>\\n\\n<img src=\\\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Medium-634FD1?style=flat-square\\\" height=\\\"20px\\\" alt=\\\"Remediation recommended\\\">\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>  6.  <s>Resource-bound refreshes fail regression</s> <code>✓ Resolved</code> <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>≡ Correctness</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n> <details open>\\n><summary>Description</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The refresh request contains only the grant type, client ID, and refresh token even though the\\n>fixture defines and uses a resource indicator during authorization and code exchange. Targets that\\n>enable <b><i>requireRefreshResource</i></b> reject these expected-success refresh fixtures with\\n><b><i>invalid_target</i></b>, leaving that supported profile untestable through this harness.\\n></pre>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Code</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><code>[mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[R283-287]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-5531f2e268697d158da6f6535506e0aa8f66b538e3ebfc3413aa18751a4253b7R283-R287)</code>\\n>\\n>```diff\\n>+            body: new URLSearchParams({\\n>+              grant_type: \\\"refresh_token\\\",\\n>+              client_id: fixture.authorization.clientId,\\n>+              refresh_token: tokenSet.refresh_token,\\n>+            }),\\n>```\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The fixture carries the same resource through authorization and code exchange, but not refresh. The\\n>hosted authorization handler parses refresh resources and rejects their absence whenever its\\n>explicitly supported <b><i>requireRefreshResource</i></b> capability is enabled.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[253-257]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts/#L253-L257)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[277-289]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts/#L277-L289)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/auth/src/hosted-authorization.ts[868-901]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/auth/src/hosted-authorization.ts/#L868-L901)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/auth/src/hosted-authorization.ts[1132-1145]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/auth/src/hosted-authorization.ts/#L1132-L1145)</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n>```\\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\\n>\\n>Issue description\\n>The refresh branch omits the fixture resource indicator despite using that indicator for the preceding authorization and authorization-code exchange. Resource-bound authorization servers that require it on refresh reject the fixture's expected-success flow.\\n>Fix Focus Areas\\n>- mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[277-289]\\n>- mcpfn/auth/src/hosted-authorization.ts[886-898]\\n>Recommended Fix\\n>Add `resource: fixture.authorization.resource` to the refresh `URLSearchParams`. Add a regression test using an authorization target configured with `requireRefreshResource: true` to ensure the hosted fixture remains valid.\\n>```\\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n<hr/>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>  7.  <s>Startup failures omit the server&#x27;s diagnostics</s> <code>✓ Resolved</code> <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>◔ Observability</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n> <details open>\\n><summary>Description</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n><b><i>waitForUrl(server, serverStderr)</i></b> passes the current string value rather than a live stderr reader,\\n>so its timeout and exit errors always interpolate the value captured immediately after spawn. Any\\n>diagnostics emitted while the fixture is asynchronously binding or failing are excluded from the\\n>release-gate failure output.\\n></pre>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Code</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><code>[scripts/test-mcpfn-external-server.mjs[36]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-57a08d76dc807d69adcf29156bb25cd9522dfd81332dbf98b797496fb904ea7eR36-R36)</code>\\n>\\n>```diff\\n>+  const url = await waitForUrl(server, serverStderr);\\n>```\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The stderr handler updates <b><i>serverStderr</i></b> asynchronously, but the value is passed by value before\\n>the wait begins and only that parameter is used in later error messages.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n> <code>[scripts/test-mcpfn-external-server.mjs[31-36]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/scripts/test-mcpfn-external-server.mjs/#L31-L36)</code>\\n> <code>[scripts/test-mcpfn-external-server.mjs[113-131]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/scripts/test-mcpfn-external-server.mjs/#L113-L131)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/examples/external-http-server.mjs[53-61]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/examples/external-http-server.mjs/#L53-L61)</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n>```\\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\\n>\\n>Issue description\\n>`waitForUrl` receives a stale stderr snapshot, so fixture startup errors omit diagnostics written after the process starts.\\n>\\n>Fix Focus Areas\\n>- scripts/test-mcpfn-external-server.mjs[31-36]\\n>- scripts/test-mcpfn-external-server.mjs[113-130]\\n>\\n>Recommended Fix\\n>Pass a callback or mutable diagnostic object into `waitForUrl` and read the latest accumulated stderr when constructing timeout and exit errors. Also clean up the readline interface and listeners on every settlement path.\\n>```\\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n<hr/>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>  8.  <s>Timed-out registry checks leave servers running</s> <code>✓ Resolved</code> <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>☼ Reliability</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n> <details open>\\n><summary>Description</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The generated consumer verifiers only call <b><i>server.kill(&quot;SIGTERM&quot;)</i></b> from <b><i>finally</i></b> and neither await\\n>the fixture exit nor arrange cleanup when their parent is terminated. When the outer 30-second\\n><b><i>spawnSync</i></b> timeout kills a verifier, its <b><i>finally</i></b> is bypassed and the independently spawned HTTP\\n>fixture can remain listening on the release runner.\\n></pre>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Code</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><code>[scripts/test-mcpfn-registry-install.mjs[R123-125]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-09b3986f6b604324d01aeeb45b2057f9704c931a47fe4bd23dceba2518dbad68R123-R125)</code>\\n>\\n>```diff\\n>+} finally {\\n>+  server.kill(\\\"SIGTERM\\\");\\n>+}\\n>```\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The outer verification process has a hard timeout, while each generated verifier launches a separate\\n>fixture process and only sends SIGTERM during normal <b><i>finally</i></b> execution. The fixture itself\\n>performs asynchronous shutdown after SIGTERM, making an awaited exit necessary even on the normal\\n>cleanup path.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n> <code>[scripts/test-mcpfn-registry-install.mjs[48-57]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/scripts/test-mcpfn-registry-install.mjs/#L48-L57)</code>\\n> <code>[scripts/test-mcpfn-registry-install.mjs[103-125]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/scripts/test-mcpfn-registry-install.mjs/#L103-L125)</code>\\n> <code>[scripts/test-mcpfn-registry-install.mjs[137-156]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/scripts/test-mcpfn-registry-install.mjs/#L137-L156)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/examples/external-http-server.mjs[162-168]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/examples/external-http-server.mjs/#L162-L168)</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n>```\\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\\n>\\n>Issue description\\n>The generated published-consumer verifier does not reliably terminate its fixture server when verification times out or is terminated.\\n>\\n>Fix Focus Areas\\n>- scripts/test-mcpfn-registry-install.mjs[48-57]\\n>- scripts/test-mcpfn-registry-install.mjs[103-125]\\n>- scripts/test-mcpfn-registry-install.mjs[137-156]\\n>\\n>Recommended Fix\\n>Run verification with child-process lifecycle management that can terminate descendants on timeout. In both generated verifiers, await fixture exit after SIGTERM and escalate to SIGKILL after a bounded grace period; add signal handling so termination also invokes that cleanup.\\n>```\\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n<hr/>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<details><summary><ins><strong>View medium (6)</strong></ins></summary><br/>\\n<details>\\n<summary>  9.  <s>Conformance reports lack provenance</s> <code>✓ Resolved</code> <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⚙ Maintainability</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n> <details open>\\n><summary>Description</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The <b><i>conformance</i></b> command passes <b><i>OfficialConformanceResult</i></b> directly to <b><i>serializeBoundedReport</i></b>,\\n>but that result contains no testing-package, report-schema, or Node-runtime metadata. Whenever a\\n>user writes <b><i>--report</i></b>, the bounded JSON contains only conformance result fields, so it cannot\\n>identify the producing package or runtime as the new architecture text promises.\\n></pre>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Code</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><code>[mcpfn/ARCHITECTURE.md[R67-69]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-de4b32cd4932bd6068364ed72e2579f79f0900f5ca316d2531470b4b9bd42cbeR67-R69)</code>\\n>\\n>```diff\\n>+scenario, or upstream conformance. JSON and JUnit serializers apply redaction\\n>+and aggregate bounds after serialization and include the testing package, report\\n>+schema, and Node runtime versions.\\n>```\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The added architecture text makes an unqualified claim about JSON serializers immediately after\\n>discussing upstream conformance failures. The CLI writes conformance results directly, while the\\n>conformance result interface and construction omit the claimed provenance fields; target-suite and\\n>JUnit reports are separately shown to contain them.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/ARCHITECTURE.md[65-69]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/ARCHITECTURE.md/#L65-L69)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts[203-216]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts/#L203-L216)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/conformance.ts[41-50]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/conformance.ts/#L41-L50)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/conformance.ts[295-304]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/conformance.ts/#L295-L304)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts[38-47]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts/#L38-L47)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/reports.ts[139-145]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/reports.ts/#L139-L145)</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n>```\\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\\n>\\n>## Issue description\\n>The architecture documentation states that JSON and JUnit serializers include testing-package, report-schema, and Node-runtime versions. That is true for target-suite JSON/JUnit artifacts, but the official conformance `--report` JSON serializes `OfficialConformanceResult`, which has none of those fields.\\n>\\n>## Fix Focus Areas\\n>- mcpfn/ARCHITECTURE.md[65-69]\\n>\\n>## Recommended Fix\\n>Qualify the statement as applying to target-suite JSON and JUnit reports, or explicitly distinguish the official conformance report format and its smaller field set.\\n>```\\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n<hr/>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>  10.  <s>Missing codes pass authorization tests</s> <code>✓ Resolved</code> <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>≡ Correctness</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n> <details open>\\n><summary>Description</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The authorization-code exchange substitutes <b><i>fixture.token.code</i></b> when the authorization response has\\n>no <b><i>code</i></b> parameter in its redirect. A target that returns a malformed redirect or even a\\n>non-redirect successful authorization response can still receive the canned code and have the\\n>expected-success fixture marked passed.\\n></pre>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Code</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><code>[mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[R253-256]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-5531f2e268697d158da6f6535506e0aa8f66b538e3ebfc3413aa18751a4253b7R253-R256)</code>\\n>\\n>```diff\\n>+      if (fixture.token.grantType === \\\"authorization_code\\\") {\\n>+        tokenBody.set(\\\"code\\\", redirectCode(authorizationResponse) ?? fixture.token.code ?? \\\"code\\\");\\n>+        tokenBody.set(\\\"redirect_uri\\\", fixture.authorization.redirectUri);\\n>+        tokenBody.set(\\\"code_verifier\\\", fixture.authorization.codeVerifier);\\n>```\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The runner accepts any HTTP-success authorization response and then uses the fixture&#x27;s static code\\n>whenever <b><i>redirectCode</i></b> is absent. The token handler only requires that a <b><i>code</i></b> form value exists,\\n>so it cannot distinguish the fabricated value from one issued by the authorization endpoint.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[244-256]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts/#L244-L256)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[350-353]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts/#L350-L353)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/auth/src/hosted-authorization.ts[839-849]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/auth/src/hosted-authorization.ts/#L839-L849)</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n>```\\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\\n>\\n>Issue description\\n>The authorization-code flow falls back to a fixture-owned code when the authorization response does not contain a `code` parameter. This makes the regression harness validate a fabricated token exchange instead of validating that the authorization endpoint issued a code.\\n>Fix Focus Areas\\n>- mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[244-256]\\n>- mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[350-353]\\n>Recommended Fix\\n>Require a redirect authorization response containing a non-empty `code` before making the token request. Remove the fixture-code fallback for authorization-code grants and return a failed result when the response is not a valid successful authorization redirect.\\n>```\\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n<hr/>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>  11.  <s>Invalid report caps still contact servers</s> <code>✓ Resolved</code> <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>☼ Reliability</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n> <details open>\\n><summary>Description</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n><b><i>conformance</i></b> invokes the authenticated or normal official runner before parsing\\n><b><i>--max-report-bytes</i></b>, and only parses that option inside the <b><i>--report</i></b> branch. An invalid cap with\\n><b><i>--report</i></b> consequently performs the conformance run before returning a usage error, while an\\n>invalid cap without <b><i>--report</i></b> is silently ignored.\\n></pre>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Code</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><code>[mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts[R211-215]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-97edce1081d52ca886871984f7718ef98ee57660b3529ba1b1e947231869e036R211-R215)</code>\\n>\\n>```diff\\n>+      if (options.report) {\\n>+        const maxBytes = parseCliReportCap(options.maxReportBytes);\\n>+        await writeFile(\\n>+          path.resolve(cwd, options.report),\\n>+          serializeBoundedReport(result, maxBytes),\\n>```\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The runner call is made at lines 203-208, whereas the cap parser is reached only later in the\\n>conditional report-writing block. The downstream runner spawns the official conformance child\\n>process, so this ordering begins execution before configuration validation.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts[203-215]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts/#L203-L215)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/conformance.ts[238-258]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/conformance.ts/#L238-L258)</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n>```\\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\\n>\\n>## Issue description\\n>The conformance command validates `--max-report-bytes` only after starting the official conformance runner and only when `--report` is set, allowing malformed local configuration to trigger remote test traffic.\\n>\\n>## Fix Focus Areas\\n>- mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts[188-208]\\n>- mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts[211-215]\\n>\\n>## Recommended Fix\\n>Parse and validate `options.maxReportBytes` before invoking either conformance runner. Reject `--max-report-bytes` without `--report` or consistently validate it as an otherwise unused option, then reuse the prevalidated value when serializing the report.\\n>```\\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n<hr/>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>  12.  <s>Unauthorized payload reads can pass the gate</s> <code>✓ Resolved</code> <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⚙ Maintainability</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n> <details open>\\n><summary>Description</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The oversized unauthenticated request check only asserts that <b><i>fetch</i></b> eventually receives HTTP 401\\n>after submitting the entire string body. A fixture regression that consumes the body before\\n>performing the credential check still returns 401 and therefore passes this gate, despite violating\\n>the intended early-rejection behavior.\\n></pre>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Code</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><code>[scripts/test-mcpfn-external-server.mjs[R92-97]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-57a08d76dc807d69adcf29156bb25cd9522dfd81332dbf98b797496fb904ea7eR92-R97)</code>\\n>\\n>```diff\\n>+  const rejectedBeforeBody = await fetch(url, {\\n>+    method: \\\"POST\\\",\\n>+    headers: { \\\"content-type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" },\\n>+    body: \\\"x\\\".repeat(1_048_577),\\n>+  });\\n>+  assert.equal(rejectedBeforeBody.status, 401);\\n>```\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The harness supplies a complete 1 MiB body and checks only the final status code. Although the\\n>fixture currently authenticates before its body-size and body-read paths, that ordering is not\\n>distinguished by this assertion from an implementation that reads the request first and then returns\\n>the same 401.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n> <code>[scripts/test-mcpfn-external-server.mjs[92-97]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/scripts/test-mcpfn-external-server.mjs/#L92-L97)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/examples/external-http-server.mjs[20-35]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/examples/external-http-server.mjs/#L20-L35)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/examples/external-http-server.mjs[119-128]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/examples/external-http-server.mjs/#L119-L128)</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n>```\\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\\n>\\n>Issue description\\n>The external-server regression check proves only the final status code and cannot detect whether an unauthorized request body was consumed before authentication failed.\\n>\\n>Fix Focus Areas\\n>- scripts/test-mcpfn-external-server.mjs[92-97]\\n>- mcpfn/examples/external-http-server.mjs[20-32]\\n>\\n>Recommended Fix\\n>Use a deliberately slow or indefinitely paused streaming request body and assert that the 401 response arrives before the stream is released. Alternatively expose fixture-only byte-consumption instrumentation and assert it remains zero for unauthorized requests.\\n>```\\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n<hr/>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>  13.  <s>The report example cannot run as shown</s> <code>✓ Resolved</code> <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⚙ Maintainability</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n> <details open>\\n><summary>Description</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The new README snippet calls <b><i>writeArtifact(...)</i></b> without defining it or importing it from any\\n>module. Consumers copying the documented JUnit-output flow receive an unresolved-name error before\\n>an artifact is written.\\n></pre>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Code</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><code>[mcpfn/testing/README.md[84]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-b1cbefcf4e5e8fd565490091d63750e593c9f97e8c75bb2026aabd9fb6c684c9R84-R84)</code>\\n>\\n>```diff\\n>+await writeArtifact(\\\"mcpfn-report.xml\\\", createMcpFnTargetSuiteJUnit(report));\\n>```\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The snippet imports only three testing APIs, then invokes a fourth undeclared name. The package root\\n>exports the reports API used to create JUnit, but contains no artifact-writing export.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/README.md[68-84]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/README.md/#L68-L84)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/index.ts[2-10]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/index.ts/#L2-L10)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/reports.ts[84-91]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/reports.ts/#L84-L91)</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n>```\\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\\n>\\n>## Issue description\\n>The JUnit README example invokes `writeArtifact`, but the snippet neither imports nor defines that function and the package does not export it.\\n>\\n>## Fix Focus Areas\\n>- mcpfn/testing/README.md[68-84]\\n>- mcpfn/testing/src/index.ts[2-10]\\n>\\n>## Recommended Fix\\n>Make the example self-contained by importing a concrete writer such as `writeFile` from `node:fs/promises` and using it to write the JUnit string, or add and document an exported `writeArtifact` helper if that is intended as package API.\\n>```\\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n<hr/>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>  14.  <s>Insecure callbacks pass regression tests</s> <code>✓ Resolved</code> <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛨ Security</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n> <details open>\\n><summary>Description</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n><b><i>runHostedCase</i></b> extracts a code from the authorization <b><i>Location</i></b> header without checking that the\\n>redirect URI and returned state match <b><i>fixture.authorization</i></b>. A server that sends an authorization\\n>code to a different callback, or drops or changes state, is exchanged and reported as a successful\\n>hosted authorization flow.\\n></pre>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Code</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><code>[mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[R253-256]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-5531f2e268697d158da6f6535506e0aa8f66b538e3ebfc3413aa18751a4253b7R253-R256)</code>\\n>\\n>```diff\\n>+      if (fixture.token.grantType === \\\"authorization_code\\\") {\\n>+        tokenBody.set(\\\"code\\\", redirectCode(authorizationResponse) ?? fixture.token.code ?? \\\"code\\\");\\n>+        tokenBody.set(\\\"redirect_uri\\\", fixture.authorization.redirectUri);\\n>+        tokenBody.set(\\\"code_verifier\\\", fixture.authorization.codeVerifier);\\n>```\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>The runner provides a state and requested redirect URI but only extracts <b><i>code</i></b> from the response\\n>location. The authorization implementation itself explicitly treats redirect matching and state\\n>reflection as required authorization-flow properties, demonstrating that these are meaningful\\n>callback invariants.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[227-256]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts/#L227-L256)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[350-353]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts/#L350-L353)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/auth/src/hosted-authorization.ts[695-730]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/auth/src/hosted-authorization.ts/#L695-L730)</code>\\n> <code>[mcpfn/auth/src/hosted-authorization.ts[740-762]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f/mcpfn/auth/src/hosted-authorization.ts/#L740-L762)</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n> <details>\\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\\n><br/>\\n>\\n>```\\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\\n>\\n>Issue description\\n>The hosted authorization runner trusts any `Location` header with a code and does not verify that it targets the requested callback or reflects the supplied state. This permits unsafe authorization callback behavior to be certified by the regression suite.\\n>Fix Focus Areas\\n>- mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[237-256]\\n>- mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[350-353]\\n>Recommended Fix\\n>Parse the successful authorization redirect and require its origin, path, and relevant query behavior to match the fixture redirect URI, then require its `state` parameter to exactly equal the fixture state before extracting the code. Return a failed result for a mismatch.\\n>```\\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\\n></details>\\n\\n<hr/>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<img src=\\\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\\\" height=\\\"10%\\\" alt=\\\"Grey Divider\\\">\\n\\n\\n<!-- qodo-context:start -->\\n<details><summary><strong>Context sources</strong></summary>\\n\\n<div>&#x26A0;&#xFE0F; Tickets: not configured — ticket URL found in PR but could not be fetched — check ticket provider credentials</div>\\n<div>Review mode: <code>🧠 Deep</code>: This is a high-density, security-sensitive cross-cutting change spanning authenticated transport, OAuth/PKCE and redirect handling, CLI behavior, reporting, fixtures, CI, packaging, and registry consumers, creating multiple independent paths where subtle defects are easy to miss.</div>\\n<!-- qodo-context:end -->\\n</details>\\n\\n<img src=\\\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\\\" height=\\\"10%\\\" alt=\\\"Grey Divider\\\">\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- qodo-daily-tip:start -->\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>Tip of the day</strong></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n<pre>💡 Did you know, you can group findings by type and pick your Finding display, from Minimal to Full</pre>\\n\\n<a href=\\\"https://docs.qodo.ai/tips-and-tricks\\\">More tips ↗</a> | <a href=\\\"https://app.qodo.ai/configurations?tab=display-preferences\\\">Customize Qodo ↗</a> | <a href=\\\"https://docs.qodo.ai\\\">Qodo docs ↗</a>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<img src=\\\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\\\" height=\\\"10%\\\" alt=\\\"Grey Divider\\\">\\n<!-- qodo-daily-tip:end -->\\n\\n\\n<!-- https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f -->\\n\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.qodo.ai\\\"><img src=\\\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\\\" width=\\\"80\\\" alt=\\\"Qodo Logo\\\"></a>\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5621086631/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":{\"id\":484649,\"client_id\":\"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057\",\"slug\":\"qodo-code-review\",\"node_id\":\"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up\",\"owner\":{\"login\":\"qodo-ai\",\"id\":183290039,\"node_id\":\"O_kgDOCuzItw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/qodo-ai\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events\",\"type\":\"Organization\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"name\":\"Qodo Code Review\",\"description\":\"### The AI Code Review Platform\\r\\n\\r\\n## Get Started\\r\\nSimply sign into Github and click the \\\"Configure\\\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Overview\\r\\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\\r\\n\\r\\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\\r\\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\\r\\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\\r\\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\\r\\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\\r\\n- Build production software where reliability matters\\r\\n\\r\\n## Qodo Capabilities\\r\\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\\r\\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\\r\\n  - No manual trigger required\\r\\n\\r\\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\\r\\n  - Understands cross-file changes\\r\\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\\r\\n\\r\\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\\r\\n  - Concrete code fixes\\r\\n  - Clear explanations\\r\\n  - Prioritized feedback\\r\\n\\r\\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\\r\\n  - Identifies risky patterns\\r\\n  - Reduces attack surface area\",\"external_url\":\"https://www.qodo.ai/\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review\",\"created_at\":\"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z\",\"permissions\":{\"actions\":\"read\",\"checks\":\"read\",\"contents\":\"write\",\"discussions\":\"write\",\"issues\":\"write\",\"metadata\":\"read\",\"pull_requests\":\"write\"},\"events\":[\"check_run\",\"check_suite\",\"discussion_comment\",\"issue_comment\",\"pull_request\",\"pull_request_review_comment\",\"push\"]},\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5634298556\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5634298556\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5634298556,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABT9SSvA\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T12:15:55Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-11T12:15:55Z\",\"body\":\"MCP-1 consolidation: retaining #170 as the final merge candidate. It covers the authenticated target contract, shared client engine, credential lifecycle, official-suite proxy, hosted authorization matrix, bounded reports, CLI, and independent consumer gates. #165 and #168 are narrower CLI-oriented alternatives; #150 has useful hosted-role-3 coverage, now adapted into this PR using its existing fixture contract.\\n\\nFixed false-green hosted flows (exceptions, absent callbacks/codes, wrong state/destination, malformed token success), refused token-request redirects, and preserved the resource indicator on refresh. Fixed standalone visible-tool checks, cleanup-failure reporting, credential query leakage, remote plaintext credentials, case-insensitive runner environment filtering, incomplete/truncated JUnit cases, invalid XML characters, and HTTP 401/403 failure-layer attribution. Hardened report-option preflight, fixture diagnostics, header-only unauthenticated rejection, registry verifier process-tree cleanup, retry-safe CI artifact names, and documentation.\\n\\nValidation: 47 testing-package tests and 12 CLI tests pass; both typechecks and builds pass. The official-SDK-only external fixture passes authenticated scenarios, anonymous rejection, and JSON/JUnit artifacts. A bounded timeout probe confirms verifier descendants are removed. No new worktrees or dependency installs. Registry publication/installation against a newly released version and fresh upstream conformance/CI are not claimed.\\n\\nOne review suggestion was not applied: changing the incompatible-registration fixture to `unauthorized_client`. The actual hosted resolver rejects that incompatible stored registration before request validation and returns `invalid_client`; the live harness confirms this. Compatible extensible-grant fixtures remain successful.\\n\\nClosing #150, #165, and #168 as superseded. No merge performed.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5634298556/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5637249912\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5637249912\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5637249912,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUAGbeA\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"pullfrog[bot]\",\"id\":226033991,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDODXkBRw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1768019?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/pullfrog\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T16:07:20Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-11T16:07:20Z\",\"body\":\"**Run failed.** [View the logs →](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/34619962179)\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [Rerun failed job ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/34619962179?action=rerun) ｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/34619962179) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5637249912/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":{\"id\":1768019,\"client_id\":\"Iv23liBAcNaTdIrYHsOs\",\"slug\":\"pullfrog\",\"node_id\":\"A_kwHODU150s4AGvpT\",\"owner\":{\"login\":\"pullfrog\",\"id\":223181266,\"node_id\":\"O_kgDODU150g\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223181266?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/pullfrog\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/received_events\",\"type\":\"Organization\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"name\":\"Pullfrog\",\"description\":\"<p>\\r\\n  <picture>\\r\\n    <source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full.png\\\">\\r\\n    <img alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\" src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full.png\\\" height=\\\"24\\\">\\r\\n  </picture>\\r\\n</p>\\r\\n\\r\\nThe agent-powered GitHub bot that does it all. One agent, infinite workflows — review PRs, triage issues, plan features, autofix CI, and ship code. All inside GitHub. Open source and powered by GitHub Actions.\\r\\n\\r\\n- 💬 **Tag `@pullfrog` anywhere** — No new UI to learn. Mention `@pullfrog` in any issue, PR, or review comment and it pulls in the surrounding context to figure out what to do.\\r\\n- ⚙️ **Configurable automations** — Auto-review new PRs, auto-respond to human reviews, triage and label issues, draft plans from issues, autofix CI failures, autofix merge conflicts. Toggle each per repo with a custom prompt.\\r\\n- 🔁 **Iterates on its own PRs** — When CI fails on a PR Pullfrog opened, it reads the logs and pushes a fix. When you leave a review, it responds like a human colleague — pushing follow-up commits and replying inline.\\r\\n- 🧠 **Bring your own model** — Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Mistral, DeepSeek, OpenRouter — any provider. Stay state-of-the-art by switching models with a single config change. Or use [Pullfrog Router](https://pullfrog.com) and pay raw provider cost with no markup.\\r\\n- 🛠️ **Batteries-included tooling** — Purpose-built MCP server for git and GitHub operations. Isolated bash subprocess with no access to your secrets. Built-in headless browser for E2E tests, screenshots, and UI iteration. Custom MCPs, skills, and hooks supported per repo.\\r\\n- 👥 **GitHub-native permissions** — Org and repo permissions are enforced by GitHub itself. Signed-in users only see repos they can already see on GitHub. Only org admins can change settings.\\r\\n- ⚡ **Powered by GitHub Actions** — Runs entirely in your repo's Actions. Your secrets, your runners, your audit log. GitHub-related operations use a short-lived installation token that auto-revokes when the run ends.\\r\\n- 🆓 **Free tier + free for OSS** — 30 free runs per month on any account, no card required. $0.07/run after that. Free forever for qualifying open source projects.\\r\\n\\r\\n[Get started at pullfrog.com →](https://pullfrog.com)\",\"external_url\":\"https://pullfrog.com\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/pullfrog\",\"created_at\":\"2025-08-12T06:29:40Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-25T17:54:13Z\",\"permissions\":{\"actions\":\"write\",\"checks\":\"write\",\"contents\":\"write\",\"discussions\":\"read\",\"emails\":\"read\",\"issues\":\"write\",\"metadata\":\"read\",\"pull_requests\":\"write\",\"secrets\":\"write\",\"workflows\":\"write\"},\"events\":[\"check_suite\",\"create\",\"delete\",\"discussion\",\"discussion_comment\",\"issues\",\"issue_comment\",\"label\",\"public\",\"pull_request\",\"pull_request_review\",\"pull_request_review_comment\",\"pull_request_review_thread\",\"push\",\"release\",\"repository\",\"repository_dispatch\",\"workflow_dispatch\",\"workflow_run\"]},\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5643804080\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5643804080\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5643804080,\"node_id\":\"IC_kw