/sup>\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5643989131/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":{\"id\":1768019,\"client_id\":\"Iv23liBAcNaTdIrYHsOs\",\"slug\":\"pullfrog\",\"node_id\":\"A_kwHODU150s4AGvpT\",\"owner\":{\"login\":\"pullfrog\",\"id\":223181266,\"node_id\":\"O_kgDODU150g\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223181266?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/pullfrog\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/received_events\",\"type\":\"Organization\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"name\":\"Pullfrog\",\"description\":\"<p>\\r\\n  <picture>\\r\\n    <source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full.png\\\">\\r\\n    <img alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\" src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full.png\\\" height=\\\"24\\\">\\r\\n  </picture>\\r\\n</p>\\r\\n\\r\\nThe agent-powered GitHub bot that does it all. One agent, infinite workflows — review PRs, triage issues, plan features, autofix CI, and ship code. All inside GitHub. Open source and powered by GitHub Actions.\\r\\n\\r\\n- 💬 **Tag `@pullfrog` anywhere** — No new UI to learn. Mention `@pullfrog` in any issue, PR, or review comment and it pulls in the surrounding context to figure out what to do.\\r\\n- ⚙️ **Configurable automations** — Auto-review new PRs, auto-respond to human reviews, triage and label issues, draft plans from issues, autofix CI failures, autofix merge conflicts. Toggle each per repo with a custom prompt.\\r\\n- 🔁 **Iterates on its own PRs** — When CI fails on a PR Pullfrog opened, it reads the logs and pushes a fix. When you leave a review, it responds like a human colleague — pushing follow-up commits and replying inline.\\r\\n- 🧠 **Bring your own model** — Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Mistral, DeepSeek, OpenRouter — any provider. Stay state-of-the-art by switching models with a single config change. Or use [Pullfrog Router](https://pullfrog.com) and pay raw provider cost with no markup.\\r\\n- 🛠️ **Batteries-included tooling** — Purpose-built MCP server for git and GitHub operations. Isolated bash subprocess with no access to your secrets. Built-in headless browser for E2E tests, screenshots, and UI iteration. Custom MCPs, skills, and hooks supported per repo.\\r\\n- 👥 **GitHub-native permissions** — Org and repo permissions are enforced by GitHub itself. Signed-in users only see repos they can already see on GitHub. Only org admins can change settings.\\r\\n- ⚡ **Powered by GitHub Actions** — Runs entirely in your repo's Actions. Your secrets, your runners, your audit log. GitHub-related operations use a short-lived installation token that auto-revokes when the run ends.\\r\\n- 🆓 **Free tier + free for OSS** — 30 free runs per month on any account, no card required. $0.07/run after that. Free forever for qualifying open source projects.\\r\\n\\r\\n[Get started at pullfrog.com →](https://pullfrog.com)\",\"external_url\":\"https://pullfrog.com\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/pullfrog\",\"created_at\":\"2025-08-12T06:29:40Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-25T17:54:13Z\",\"permis