:\"\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5187468241\",\"pull_request_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"_links\":{\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5187468241\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\"}},\"submitted_at\":\"2026-09-12T18:14:06Z\",\"commit_id\":\"5a32dbf9772ccb9a65ff07c78196944d4be375b5\"},{\"id\":5187469208,\"node_id\":\"PRR_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABNTJ_mA\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\"id\":191113872,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOC2QqkA\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1082092?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/cubic-dev-ai\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"<!-- cubic:review-summary:start -->\\n**1 issue found across 8 files (changes from recent commits).**\\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:end -->\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents (unresolved issues)</summary>\\n\\n```text\\n\\nCheck if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately.\\n\\n\\n<file name=\\\"mcpfn/client/package.json\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"mcpfn/client/package.json:3\\\">\\nP2: Bumping @mcpfn/client to 0.0.4 leaves @mcpfn/inspector's dependency on \\\"@mcpfn/client\\\": \\\"0.0.3\\\" unsatisfied by the workspace (which is now 0.0.4). With npm workspaces an exact pin is not matched by the higher workspace version, so npm installs a separate copy of the old published client from the registry instead of linking the local 0.0.4 code — exactly the split the lockfile already shows for @mcpfn/testing: mcpfn/inspector/node_modules/@mcpfn/testing and mcpfn/datafn/node_modules/@mcpfn/testing are nested registry installs of testing 0.0.4 (resolved to registry.npmjs.org) while the workspace testing is 0.0.5. Inspector then builds/tests against the pre-fix client 0.0.3, silently missing this PR's cleanup/redaction fixes. Bump the dependent workspace packages in lockstep: @mcpfn/inspector to @mcpfn/client 0.0.4 (and @mcpfn/testing 0.0.5), and @mcpfn/datafn to @mcpfn/testing 0.0.5.</violation>\\n</file>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/170/ai_pr_review_github_delivery_8e15f2fd5a1248858e7638acb22ba3ef3724177455fc366abf927ca39c89a39f?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F170)</sub>\\n\\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_github_delivery_8e15f2fd5a1248858e7638acb22ba3ef3724177455fc366abf927ca39c89a39f:5a32dbf9772ccb9a65ff07c78196944d4be375b5:4e2c1d2d-c516-5a44-9510-21b8f7b1be54 -->\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-funct