21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\"}},\"submitted_at\":\"2026-09-14T05:52:17Z\",\"commit_id\":\"2ed3223dfea1a8a89f6bfb08ac931f0ffafdf276\"},{\"id\":5194301321,\"node_id\":\"PRR_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABNZq_iQ\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"pullfrog[bot]\",\"id\":226033991,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDODXkBRw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1768019?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/pullfrog\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> The Unix process-group fix closes the prior overflow hang there, but the new Windows branch can still leave authenticated conformance pending indefinitely when `taskkill` fails.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `36c4a3a1`, covering the shutdown and conformance process-tree hardening in `2ed3223d`.\\n\\n- **Hardened pending-open shutdown** — Made strict close fail retryably while a target open still owns cleanup work and allowed reconnect only after that work settles.\\n- **Supervised conformance overflow** — Spawned the Unix wrapper in a detached process group and added Windows tree-kill handling for captured output above 256 KiB.\\n- **Added executable regressions** — Covered retryable pending-open close behavior and a pipe-owning descendant that must terminate on Unix overflow.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 2ed3223;\\nif commits have landed on codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\\n\\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\\n- Files reviewed: 47\\n- Commits reviewed: 21\\n- Base: dev (dac6abf)\\n- Head: codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910 (2ed3223)\\n- Reviewed commits:\\n  - 2ed3223d — fix(mcpfn): enforce pending shutdown and terminate runner trees\\n  - 36c4a3a1 — fix(mcpfn): bound conformance capture and order deferred cleanup\\n  - 45affe39 — fix(mcpfn): preserve permanent shutdown and compact report bounds\\n  - 4bb10b48 — fix(mcpfn): classify cleanup errors and reject invalid-client redirects\\n  - bebdc22a — fix(mcpfn): preserve shutdown credentials and redact before truncation\\n  - 16b86310 — fix(mcpfn): bound credentials and clean up before diagnostics\\n  - b9ec3a7d — fix(mcpfn): preserve credential cleanup and conformance report integrity\\n  - 10d5eac2 — fix(mcpfn): retain conformance cleanup and validate OAuth report evidence\\n  - 3ffdf24b — fix(mcpfn): gate reconnect on credential cleanup and redact before truncation\\n  - a93ef9c5 — fix(mcpfn): use explicit inventory ordering and Windows cleanup executable\\n  - 933c96a0 — ci: run JavaScript tests on required Node 22 runtime\\n  - 76a5a16c — Merge branch 'dev' into codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910\\n  - f78a72ae — fix(mcpfn): retain failed credential cleanup and redact inspect errors\\n  - b6ac854c — fix(mcpfn): align client dependents and regenerate workspace lock\\n  - 5a32dbf9 — fix(mcpfn): serialize retained cleanup and reject authorization JSON errors\\n  - c4b1fe5e — fix(mcpfn): retain cleanup ownership and bound typed report redaction\\n  - dd1ac078 — fix(mcpfn): preserve redacted reports and retry credential cleanup\\n  - 9f42334f — fix(mcpfn): redact authenticated outputs and preserve cleanup ownership\\n  - 1e7d9eb0 — fix(mcpfn): protect credential artifacts and validate rejection envelopes\\n  - a7c0dea4 — fix(mcpfn): prevent false conformance success and preserve lifecycle evidence\\n  - f796d70a — feat(mcpfn): add transport-neutral conformance testing\\n- Prior pullfrog review: 36c4a3a1 (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5194136567)\\n-->\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [Fix all ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/170?action=fix&review_id=5194301321) ｜ [Fix 👍s ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/170?action=fix-approved&review_id=5194301321) ｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/34810638576/job/103871119469) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5194301321\",\"pull_request_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"_links\":{\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5194301321\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\"}},\"submitted_at\":\"2026-09-14T05:53:36Z\",\"commit_id\":\"2ed3223dfea1a8a89f6bfb08ac931f0ffafdf276\"},{\"id\":5194584124,\"node_id\":\"PRR_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABNZ8QPA\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\",\"id\":199175422,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOC98s_g\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1144995?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/2f98827f7d4f641ac5f64f34f41c28cb26e10416/mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts#L233\\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bound custom target kinds when shrinking reports**\\n\\nWhen a custom target supplies a long `kind` and the caller selects the supported 1024-byte cap, the initial OAuth redaction retains up to 2,048 characters and this fallback copies that value into the minimum report unchanged. The report therefore still exceeds the cap and `enforceReportCap()` throws, so `test-target` produces no bounded artifact and classifies the error as CLI usage. After the new failure-message compaction, this independently unbounded descriptor field still needs to be truncated or replaced.\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5194584124\",\"pull_request_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"_links\":{\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5194584124\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\"}},\"submitted_at\":\"2026-09-14T06:32:01Z\",\"commit_id\":\"2f98827f7d4f641ac5f64f34f41c28cb26e10416\"},{\"id\":5194594394,\"node_id\":\"PRR_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABNZ84Wg\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"coderabbitai[bot]\",\"id\":136622811,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscripti