:{\"href\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5196359698\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\"}},\"submitted_at\":\"2026-09-14T10:03:27Z\",\"commit_id\":\"30f398b6fe5b44a8c7c422d456bbf2644fd8eab3\"},{\"id\":5196410471,\"node_id\":\"PRR_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABNbruZw\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"pullfrog[bot]\",\"id\":226033991,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDODXkBRw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1768019?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/pullfrog\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"> ℹ️ No new issues found in this delta; the existing Windows descendant-cleanup thread remains open.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior review at `25ed30dc`:\\n- **Preserved provider lifecycle identity**: transport and redaction continue to use the bounded immutable snapshot, while `revoke` and `dispose` now receive the original provider-issued object.\\n- **Sanitized failed opens**: error messages are redacted while the acquired credential snapshot is still registered, before cleanup removes its scope.\\n- **Restored minimum-runtime coverage**: the general JavaScript CI lane now runs on both Node 20 and Node 22.\\n- **Expanded regressions**: tests cover provider object identity, malformed credential cleanup, authenticated artifact redaction, and the shared authenticated server fixture.\\n\\nLocal focused tests could not start because dependency bootstrap failed and `vitest` was unavailable; `git diff --check origin/dev...HEAD` passed and the worktree remained clean.\\n\\n<!-- pullfrog-review-meta:v1\\nmode: incremental\\nbase: dac6abf87d57c36f010bc6360e60086ae0eeeca6\\nhead: 30f398b6fe5b44a8c7c422d456bbf2644fd8eab3\\nhead_ref: codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910\\nfiles_reviewed: 53\\ncommits_reviewed: 26\\nreviewed_commits:\\n  - 30f398b6fe5b44a8c7c422d456bbf2644fd8eab3 fix(mcpfn): preserve provider identity and sanitize failed opens\\n  - 25ed30dce78a9d30f52d3f857f0edfb3f4fa9223 fix(mcpfn): harden conformance cleanup and redaction\\n  - e90cd535b622e313ccebd8d8cfa3fd03d047613f docs: document McpFn conformance and inspector rollout\\n  - a38c20fbb0cdd05cd89c3a7f2e2a10caf184f93e refactor(mcpfn): generalize transport hooks\\n  - f5611abc3b0dc4c2dbe1204b172817a186a51901 fix(mcpfn): bound cleanup and redact failures\\n  - 5e45470804f57af5a5d6c9fb722392789f43dca1 fix(mcpfn): harden conformance cleanup and exports\\n  - d8700e7900d54f2b2e9fcde936b74e8c99b68587 test(mcpfn): cover external conformance consumers\\n  - 2d3eea87b7185aadd4de7ecb10de43ff04532964 fix(mcpfn): harden release gate and inspector flows\\n  - 595913db22d4b7a69646e069d44911c36a251b9a fix(mcpfn): preserve events and surface conformance limits\\n  - e385403a4f4760b92ef8d543a27a9c4cb58a6254 fix(mcpfn): harden remote targets and conformance\\n  - 63fc268aff410e7f439450057412ec078584ac1b fix(mcpfn): harden conformance and remote auth\\n  - c147f5f93410dc9ee369bd643c48591728ad174c fix(mcpfn): preserve conformance case identity\\n  - 2eefc534af68c0eacccaf79dcfd770305c785e2f fix(mcpfn): harden conformance runner\\n  - 092154f889fd028b24328ade5619b734fab68fa7 fix(mcpfn): preserve structured params and cleanup\\n  - f7522a5670168dd1c356b5b2f2652a77fe24a160 fix(mcpfn): redact authenticated observability artifacts\\n  - d191e94dbe04d18ae3c87e9b303b6d967f29182f test(mcpfn): cover programmatic inspector redaction\\n  - 22804de1b936335495d9d38a24f59f510c18bf2 fix(mcpfn): harden auth and conformance flows\\n  - 0aa66805026108872bf80e36e8cd013100c1f8ea test(mcpfn): cover authenticated observability\\n  - 73bf0c363239fd0da22dc04a25272f84911aad18 fix(mcpfn): harden authenticated remote targets\\n  - 76a1eb03a134baf2a540a1cd33ca416564dcab93 Merge branch 'dev' into codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910\\n  - 1643085739694223c536b6bf6eb6870c82dbe981 fix(mcpfn): harden remote conformance boundaries\\n  - 7268dfb83b226489023ab29d181977f94aa7d929 fix(mcpfn): harden transport adapter\\n  - 6a17a61da5bc263992097a1638695295295a7de8 fix(mcpfn): enforce handshake before remote calls\\n  - 1142e603e6e90ce69b07338fc4af799a4fe43c98 fix(mcpfn): tighten handshake error boundaries\\n  - 1908b3b7db95cb7fd109005027857761aaf58c0c fix(mcpfn): tighten transport and conformance contracts\\n  - f79672f367958be3e1f09b65f68600d76e2d8105 feat(mcpfn): add transport-neutral client and conformance\\nprior_review: https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5196019923\\n-->\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [Fix it ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/170?action=fix&review_id=5196410471) ｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/34829899399/job/103930517504) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5196410471\",\"pull_request_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"_links\":{\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5196410471\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\"}},\"submitted_at\":\"2026-09-14T10:09:44Z\",\"commit_id\":\"30f398b6fe5b44a8c7c422d456bbf2644fd8eab3\"},{\"id\":5196722731,\"node_id\":\"PRR_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABNb-yKw\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\",\"id\":199175422,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOC98s_g\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1144995?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1195831fd338370c8a927d89835cc2f24843eb7d/mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts#L156-L158\\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Serialize default test reports within the one-MiB cap**\\n\\nWhen `mcpfn test` produces enough results to approach the documented default one-MiB limit, `createMcpFnScenarioReport()` enforces that limit against compact JSON, but this branch emits pretty-printed JSON without measuring it. Formatting overhead can therefore make stdout and `--output` exceed the default cap even though the report builder considers the artifact bounded; use the same compact serialization as the capped path or account for pretty-printing when enforcing the default.\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5196722731\",\"pull_request_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"_links\":{\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5196722731\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\"}},\"submitted_at\":\"2026-09-14T10:49:25Z\",\"commit_id\":\"1195831fd338370c8a927d89835cc2f24843eb7d\"},{\"id\":5196737926,\"node_id\":\"PRR_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABNb_thg\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"pullfrog[bot]\",\"id\":226033991,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDODXkBRw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1768019?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/pullfrog\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"> ℹ️ No new issues found in this delta; the existing Windows descendant-cleanup disposition remains unchanged.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `30f398b6`, covering the security and regression hardening in `1195831f`:\\n\\n- **Sanitized conformance failures** — Redacted authenticated setup and proxy-close exceptions while the immutable credential snapshot is still available, before release.\\n- **Expanded credential matching** — Recognized decoded Basic-auth user, password, and pair values in exact-value redaction.\\n- **Hardened scenario artifacts** — Routed scenario failure and incomplete reasons through the active target credential redactor before byte truncation.\\n- **Stabilized authenticated regressions** — Streamed fixture responses safely and made the malformed-header inspector test prove no outbound request occurs.\\n\\nThe McpFn release gate and Node 18 CommonJS check pass. Local focused tests could not start because the known out-of-sync root lockfile left `vitest` unavailable; `git diff --check` passed and the worktree is clean.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 1195831f;\\nif commits have landed on codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\\n\\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\\n- Files reviewed: 54\\n- Commits reviewed: 27\\n- Base: dev (354cada)\\n- Head: codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910 (1195831f)\\n- Reviewed commits:\\n  - 1195831f — fix(mcpfn): close authenticated report redaction gaps\\n- Prior pullfrog review: 30f398b6 (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5196410471)\\n-->\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [Fix it ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/170?action=fix&review_id=5196737926) ｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/34834513175/job/103945177190) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5196737926\",\"pull_request_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"_links\":{\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5196737926\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\"}},\"submitted_at\":\"2026-09-14T10:50:52Z\",\"commit_id\":