commit through `8d45c838`. The default one-MiB scenario-report cap is applied before report construction, compact serialization is used for the emitted JSON, and reserving one byte for the trailing newline keeps the final UTF-8 output within the configured limit. The added regression creates an oversized report and checks both incomplete-report fallback behavior and the exact final-output bound.\\n\\n**Key areas reviewed:** CLI option defaulting, report-size accounting, JSON serialization, trailing-newline handling, and regression coverage.\\n\\n**Verification:** `git diff --check` passed and the McpFn release-gate CI job passed. Local targeted tests could not start because root `npm ci` failed under Node 24 and left no Vitest executable.\\n\\n**Context:** The full PR adds transport-neutral authenticated McpFn testing and conformance support, bounded/redacted evidence, hosted authorization fixtures, CLI integrations, release checks, and subsequent credential-lifecycle and report-hardening fixes. All prior Pullfrog-originated review threads are resolved.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Review metadata:**\\n- Base: `dev` (`354cada`)\\n- Head: `codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910` (`8d45c838`)\\n- Files reviewed: 2\\n- Commits reviewed: 1\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [Fix it ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/170?action=fix&review_id=5197116582) ｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/34838142566/job/103956620276) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-fu