tps://github.com/apps/pullfrog\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"> [!CAUTION]\\n> The prior P1 serialized-output finding remains only partially fixed, and the new key-substitution path can silently alter scenarios.\\n\\n`mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts:191` limits the new serialization check to `role === \\\"payload\\\"`. Preserved envelopes therefore still bypass the boundary check: with credential `foo\\\":\\\"bar`, `redactRemoteCredential(credential, { target: { kind: \\\"custom\\\", foo: \\\"bar\\\" } }, { preserveKeys: true })` returns an object whose compact JSON contains the credential across the nested key/value separator. The final serialized artifact, or every enclosing role, must be checked without corrupting protected structural literals.\\n\\nThe mixed ESM/CommonJS omission-provenance finding is addressed by the client-instance method and mixed-entry release-gate probe; that prior thread has been resolved. `git diff --check` passes, as do the remote McpFn release gate, Node 18 CommonJS, and Node 20 compatibility checks. Local Vitest remained unavailable because root `npm ci` fails on missing Turbo platform lock records.\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -