functions/pull/170/files#diff-57a08d76dc807d69adcf29156bb25cd9522dfd81332dbf98b797496fb904ea7e'>scripts/test-mcpfn-external-server.mjs</a>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Documentation (10) <code> +160 / -11 </code></summary>\\n\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>ADOPTION.md<code>Document third-party server adoption</code> <code>+14/-0</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n>Document third-party server adoption\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>• Explains how non-McpFn servers adopt the testing platform and safely upgrade or roll back package pins.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n><a href='https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-271acfcc6f912c38fb3a35539400521d0363827c1c23e8a2c6663a71d7791d62'>mcpfn/ADOPTION.md</a>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>ADR-0001-COMPATIBILITY.md<code>Define report and conformance compatibility policy</code> <code>+12/-0</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n>Define report and conformance compatibility policy\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>• Establishes report-schema versioning, provenance requirements, conformance pinning, and consumer rollback boundaries.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n><a href='https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-e60deb902ccb17b5ce91e203b0d2d9e4eacc32863253641018698bdda0c8bee5'>mcpfn/ADR-0001-COMPATIBILITY.md</a>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>ARCHITECTURE.md<code>Describe authenticated target and reporting architecture</code> <code>+13/-0</code></summary>\\n\\n<br/>\\n\\n>Describe authenticated target and reporting architecture\\n>\\n><pre>\\n>• Documents credential lifecycle ownership, redirect protection, production-client delegation, failure layers, and artifact provenance.\\n></pre>\\n>\\n><a href='https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170/files#diff-de4b32cd4932bd6068364ed72e2579f79f0900f5ca316d2531470b4b9bd42cbe'>mcpfn/ARCHITECTURE.md</a>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>MIGRATION.md<code>Add non-McpFn regression adoption path</code> <code>+10/-0</code></s