tps://github.com/pullfrog\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog/received_events\",\"type\":\"Organization\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"name\":\"Pullfrog\",\"description\":\"<p>\\r\\n  <picture>\\r\\n    <source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full.png\\\">\\r\\n    <img alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\" src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full.png\\\" height=\\\"24\\\">\\r\\n  </picture>\\r\\n</p>\\r\\n\\r\\nThe agent-powered GitHub bot that does it all. One agent, infinite workflows — review PRs, triage issues, plan features, autofix CI, and ship code. All inside GitHub. Open source and powered by GitHub Actions.\\r\\n\\r\\n- 💬 **Tag `@pullfrog` anywhere** — No new UI to learn. Mention `@pullfrog` in any issue, PR, or review comment and it pulls in the surrounding context to figure out what to do.\\r\\n- ⚙️ **Configurable automations** — Auto-review new PRs, auto-respond to human reviews, triage and label issues, draft plans from issues, autofix CI failures, autofix merge conflicts. Toggle each per repo with a custom prompt.\\r\\n- 🔁 **Iterates on its own PRs** — When CI fails on a PR Pullfrog opened, it reads the logs and pushes a fix. When you leave a review, it responds like a human colleague — pushing follow-up commits and replying inline.\\r\\n- 🧠 **Bring your own model** — Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Mistral, DeepSeek, OpenRouter — any provider. Stay state-of-the-art by switching models with a single config change. Or use [Pullfrog Router](https://pullfrog.com) and pay raw provider cost with no markup.\\r\\n- 🛠️ **Batteries-included tooling** — Purpose-built MCP server for git and GitHub operations. Isolated bash subprocess with no access to your secrets. Built-in headless browser for E2E tests, screenshots, and UI iteration. Custom MCPs, skills, and hooks supported per repo.\\r\\n- 👥 **GitHub-native permissions** — Org and repo permissions are enforced by GitHub itself. Signed-in users only see repos they can already see on GitHub. Only org admins can change settings.\\r\\n- ⚡ **Powered by GitHub Actions** — Runs entirely in your repo's Actions. Your secrets, your runners, your audit log. GitHub-related operations use a short-lived installation token that auto-revokes when the run ends.\\r\\n- 🆓 **Free tier + free for OSS** — 30 free runs per month on any account, no card required. $0.07/run after that. Free forever for qualifying open source projects.\\r\\n\\r\\n[Get started at pullfrog.com →](https://pullfrog.com)\",\"external_url\":\"https://pullfrog.com\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/pullfrog\",\"created_at\":\"2025-08-12T06:29:40Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-25T17:54:13Z\",\"permissions\":{\"actions\":\"write\",\"checks\":\"write\",\"contents\":\"write\",\"discussions\":\"read\",\"emails\":\"read\",\"issues\":\"write\",\"metadata\":\"read\",\"pull_requests\":\"write\",\"secrets\":\"write\",\"workflows\":\"write\"},\"events\":[\"check_suite\",\"create\",\"delete\",\"discussion\",\"discussion_comment\",\"issues\",\"issue_comment\",\"label\",\"public\",\"pull_request\",\"pull_request_review\",\"pull_request_review_comment\",\"pull_request_review_thread\",\"push\",\"release\",\"repository\",\"repository_dispatch\",\"workflow_dispatch\",\"workflow_run\"]},\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5659245722\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5659245722\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5659245722,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUVE8mg\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T05:00:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T05:00:11Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 36c4a3a1c834710c461582ba1eebdd41c2e4a9f6.\\n\\nFixed: reset the permanent-close latch when reopening; defer target-owned cleanup until pending opens finish without blocking close on an uncooperative open; preserve the preexisting test environment variable; bound captured conformance output to 262144 bytes while streaming, terminate excessive output, and emit only a generic failure so truncated credentials cannot escape. Updated lifecycle regressions to require one deferred cleanup rather than premature duplicate cleanup.\\n\\nSkipped: the request to reject every token-endpoint invalid_client HTTP 401 without an Authorization request header contradicts RFC 6749 section 5.2, which permits 401 to indicate supported authentication schemes, including when authentication was omitted. Existing behavior is retained. Source: https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6749#section-5.2\\n\\nVerification: 30 client tests, 106 testing tests and the CLI suite passed; client/testing builds and testing typecheck passed. New checks cover close/reopen/remote-close, non-idempotent deferred cleanup and capture overflow. Pullfrog failed on the initial head; merge requires fresh review. The Node-version coverage disposition remains unchanged.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5659245722/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5659558760\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5659558760\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5659558760,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUVYDaA\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T05:43:01Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T05:43:01Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 2ed3223dfea1a8a89f6bfb08ac931f0ffafdf276.\\n\\nFixed: strict close now fails retryably while an open still owns resources; reconnect clears permanent-close intent; target-wide cleanup excludes live successful handles and retains only failed releases. Conformance overflow now terminates the POSIX process group or invokes Windows taskkill /T, rather than killing only the npx wrapper.\\n\\nVerification: 30 client tests and 107 testing tests passed, plus a real POSIX wrapper/descendant regression proving overflow settles after terminating inherited pipes. Client build and testing typecheck passed. Windows tree termination is implemented but was not executed on this macOS host. Existing tests now require a retryable close failure while cleanup is pending, and verify one client's cleanup preserves another live lease. Fresh review required; no merge this round.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5659558760/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5659917108\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5659917108\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5659917108,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUVt7NA\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T06:25:48Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T06:25:48Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 2f98827f7d4f641ac5f64f34f41c28cb26e10416.\\n\\nFixed: credential revocation/disposal now use a fresh non-aborted cleanup signal on each release attempt, so cancelling acquisition does not permanently poison cleanup retries. Conformance overflow uses an absolute Windows system taskkill path, observes command failure, bounds the tree-kill attempt, falls back to killing the wrapper, closes capture streams and settles the failed report even if no close event arrives.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): previous pending-open, independent-handle and POSIX process-tree findings retain their fixes.\\n\\nVerification: 112 testing tests and testing typecheck passed, including successful/failed/unresponsive Windows command simulations, cancelled-signal cleanup retries, and the actual POSIX overflowing child-process fixture. Native Windows execution was not available. Failed OS termination remains best effort and never yields a passing conformance report.\\n\\nNot Attempted: the new Sonar aggregate failure and existing release/runtime completeness limitations still require disposition before merge. Fresh review/CI is required for this push.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5659917108/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5660431079\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5660431079\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5660431079,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUWNS5w\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T07:18:50Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T07:18:50Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 1d1d1b93303af6f022cfd6f1dbf2293dc2b1aaa5.\\n\\nFixed: preserve locally authored report-schema and official-suite version fields when a credential happens to match their text. Windows cleanup now hides taskkill's console. Cleanup exhaustion retains a redacted failed conformance result on McpFnConformanceCleanupError, and the CLI writes that result through its normal bounded --report path.\\n\\nReview disposition: retained the public throwing/retryCleanup contract instead of silently returning and discarding the retained cleanup handle. The completed result is still available for reporting, and successful cleanup behavior is unchanged.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): Pullfrog confirmed the preceding Windows bounded termination fix; previous cancellation and independent-handle fixes remain covered.\\n\\nVerification: 114 testing tests, 18 existing CLI tests and the new CLI cleanup-report regression passed. Testing/CLI typechecks and testing build passed. Native Windows execution remains unverified locally.\\n\\nNot Attempted: release/completeness limitations still need final disposition. Fresh CI and current-head review required; no merge this round.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5660431079/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5660932781\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5660932781\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5660932781,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUWr6rQ\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T08:07:48Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T08:07:48Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed bd07bfc46855fca3cc244927a4c8517b2cc0984b.\\n\\nFixed: preserved the original upstream conformance stderr/failure/exit code when credential cleanup also fails, recording cleanupFailure separately. Added a target-owned redaction hook used by client events/diagnostics and inspector snapshots/exports; exact credentials are scrubbed before generic truncation. Added a real authenticated HTTP regression with reflected descriptions, logging data and tool results. Normal protocol return values remain unmodified; documentation explains exporting while the credential lease is active.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): earlier cleanup retry, bounded process termination and structural version findings retain their previous fixes. Two fresh review findings are addressed by this batch.\\n\\nNot Attempted: aggregate Sonar reliability gate requires separate issue-level diagnosis; native Windows execution was not performed. No merge in this run after pushing.\\n\\nVerification: 115 testing tests, client and inspector suites, 19 CLI tests passed; client/testing typechecks and client/inspector/testing builds passed. git diff --check passed. New dev base contains merged #153; this PR remains deferred for integration/readiness assessment and fresh current-head reviews.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5660932781/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5661571117\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5661571117\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5661571117,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUXS4LQ\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T09:04:34Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T09:04:34Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 25ed30dce78a9d30f52d3f857f0edfb3f4fa9223.\\n\\nFixed:\\n- Snapshot acquired credential headers so provider mutation cannot expose the original credential in reports or revoke the wrong token.\\n- Keep diagnostic redaction failures from rejecting protocol operations; emit a bounded omission event.\\n- Redact credentials in one pass so scenario markers survive token collisions; preserve typed client event and inspector state fields.\\n- Move the programmatic inspector regression into its downstream package, removing the testing-to-inspector build cycle.\\n- Address SonarQube S1143 by retaining operation errors, performing cleanup, then throwing outside finally.\\n\\nVerification: 115 testing tests and 12 inspector tests passed. Full Node 22 `npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed, including package typechecks/tests/builds, Playwright, official conformance, authenticated external-server checks, and packed consumer imports/round trips. Added mutable-header, regex-token, marker/event-collision and oversized notification regressions.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): duplicate redaction-limit reports share the same fix.\\nNot Attempted: older Node 20 runtime coverage and Windows descendant-process cleanup remain unresolved; this Node 22 macOS validation does not establish those guarantees. Fresh hosted Sonar analysis is required to confirm its gate.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5661571117/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5662106541\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5662106541\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5662106541,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUXzjrQ\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T09:48:19Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T09:48:19Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 30f398b6fe5b44a8c7c422d456bbf2644fd8eab3.\\n\\nFixed:\\n- Preserve the provider-issued credential identity for revoke/dispose callbacks while using detached headers for transport and redaction. WeakMap-backed lifecycle regression added.\\n- Sanitize target-open errors before releasing the lease, preventing malformed multiline credentials from leaking to direct client diagnostics after cleanup. Uninspectable credentials produce a generic safe error.\\n- Share the authenticated HTTP test fixture between testing and inspector without reversing production dependencies; removes the 84-line duplication identified through SonarQube MCP.\\n- Restore the general JavaScript CI lane as a Node 20/22 matrix, retaining changed-package build/test/typecheck/lint coverage for both runtimes.\\n\\nVerification: full Node 22 release gate passed all 84 steps; testing 115 and inspector 13 tests passed, including existing Windows taskkill success/failure/timeout tests. Node 20 @mdfn/core build and 26 tests passed. Hosted matrix and Sonar analysis are pending.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): the Windows tree-kill finding is already handled by conformance-process.ts (absolute SystemRoot executable, observed completion, 2.5-second fallback) and conformance.ts explicitly settles the failed report even without child close. Existing Windows branch unit tests pass; native Windows process-tree behavior was not run on this macOS host. The previous summary incorrectly listed the code fix as still outstanding.\\nNot Attempted: no fresh hosted review or gate result for this pushed head; no merge this run.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5662106541/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5662701541\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5662701541\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5662701541,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUYX35Q\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T10:42:24Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T10:42:24Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 1195831fd338370c8a927d89835cc2f24843eb7d.\\n\\nFixed:\\n- Register decoded Basic username/password values for credential redaction, including passwords containing colons.\\n- Sanitize authenticated conformance setup/close failures before credential release; preserve provider identity for cleanup callbacks.\\n- Redact scenario errors before truncating, preventing partial credential leaks in JSON/JUnit.\\n- Stream the shared authenticated HTTP fixture with backpressure instead of buffering SSE until close.\\n- Merge current dev while retaining the Node 20/22 CI matrix; inspected the base merge and combined lockfile.\\n\\nVerification: all 84 steps of the Node 22 MCP release gate passed, including package builds/typechecks, tests, Playwright and packed consumers. The focused redaction suites passed 40 tests. The malformed-header inspector regression now explicitly asserts that no fetch occurs.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): the malformed-header fixture does not contact port 1; header validation rejects before transport creation. The older Windows cleanup issue is already fixed, as Pullfrog itself acknowledged in its thread; the release gate covers Windows branch unit regressions, but this macOS run does not establish native Windows behavior.\\n\\nNot Attempted: fresh hosted CI/review coverage for this push; no merge this run. Sonar before this push passed with 0.5% duplication.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5662701541/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5663183022\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5663183022\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5663183022,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUY1Qrg\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T11:25:32Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T11:25:32Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 8d45c83808ef16474b0c5eca12bbdaf418629890.\\n\\nFixed: the default local test report now uses compact JSON, reserves one byte for the trailing newline, and enforces the same one-MiB cap on stdout and --output. Added default/explicit-limit regression coverage against exact emitted bytes and file parity.\\n\\nVerification: CLI tests and build passed after rebuilding the MCP workspace dependencies for this exact branch. Initial validation used stale built exports from #171; rebuilding resolved those failures. The default-cap fixture was reduced to the supported 1000-scenario limit.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): previous redaction and Windows cleanup dispositions remain unchanged; no new inline findings.\\nNot Attempted: Node 20 hosted CI remains a merge blocker. Its failure is a truncated generated UIFN core autocomplete.mjs parsed by the Svelte catalog (expected closing brace, got EOF), not an MCP test failure. Build scripts were inspected; the cause is not yet established, so no unsupported workflow bypass or runtime removal was made. New-head CI/reviews pending, no merge this run.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5663183022/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5663934108\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5663934108\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5663934108,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUZjGnA\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T12:29:48Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T12:29:48Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 167afb7abd5b0d428c46ba3bb2fe3f2f91553501.\\n\\nFixed:\\n- Suite initialization/inventory failures now scrub registered credentials before bounded normalization, including non-enumerable Error causes. Added a boundary-crossing secret regression covering JSON and JUnit.\\n- Credential disposal now follows successful revocation, preserving provider state for revocation retries. Disposal failures still retry without repeating successful revocation.\\n- Diagnosed this head's Node 20 CI failure: six mocked-conformance tests reached the real Node 22 runtime guard. The fake-runner tests now explicitly model a supported runtime; an additional test proves the production guard still rejects Node 20 without spawning. The actual Node 20 job remains enabled.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): previous-round dispositions retained; overlapping reviewer reports deduplicated. Not Attempted: no merge while a new head awaits CI/review coverage.\\n\\nVerification: 44 affected tests passed on both Node 20 and Node 22; testing package build passed. This does not claim that the official conformance runner supports Node 20 or that hosted CI has passed.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5663934108/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5664551600\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5664551600\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5664551600,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUaIysA\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T13:14:51Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T13:14:51Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed a080b785d168ceb444465bd5ba9dd46f7e73050d.\\n\\nFixed:\\n- Suite failure normalization catches all failures while inspecting/redacting arbitrary errors, including oversized data and throwing proxy causes, and returns a fixed bounded incomplete report without copying the thrown value.\\n- CLI API-key options use the shared credential-header validator, classifying forbidden headers as usage errors (exit 2) without printing credentials.\\n- Authenticated conformance accepts the full literal IPv4 127/8 loopback range while retaining its loopback-only proxy listener; remote addresses remain rejected. This finding appeared in the review body, not an inline thread.\\n- Sonar MCP identified two CI security findings on on-demand npx installation. CI now invokes the lockfile-installed local Turbo binary directly for build/typecheck/test/lint, with no package download fallback.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): prior dispositions retained; redaction-limit and throwing-cause findings share one fail-closed fix. Not Attempted: Node 20 hosted CI now fails two DevFn exact-port diagnostic tests; the previous mocked-conformance runtime failures are gone. That CI blocker remains, and new-head review/CI is required before merging.\\n\\nVerification: 38 remote-target tests passed on Node 22 and Node 20, core/testing/CLI builds passed, all 23 CLI tests passed, CI planner tests passed. No Sonar suppression or Node 20 lane removal.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5664551600/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5665195046\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5665195046\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5665195046,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUawEJg\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T14:01:18Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T14:01:18Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed e664880b7ce715e0ee13fe7aa5e94938f888fbb0.\\n\\nStabilized credential ownership and reporting as one bounded task:\\n\\n- Failed initialization now drains retained target cleanup even when no client was returned. Regression proves transient revocation retries and disposal completes.\\n- Acquisition failures use a fixed safe error because no returned credential exists to identify opaque secrets. The provider contract explicitly owns rollback before acquisition returns.\\n- Final descriptor/redaction/serialization failures produce a safe incomplete report. Opaque secrets are scrubbed before generic truncation. Background diagnostic construction also fails safely instead of producing an unhandled rejection.\\n- Invalid RFC 6750 Bearer tokens are configuration errors (exit 2), without printing their contents.\\n- Diagnosed the unrelated DevFn failure: the general Node 20 matrix ran a CLI that requires Node 22. General JavaScript now runs on Node 22; a dedicated Node 20 job builds the McpFn client/testing/CLI dependency closure and runs their typechecks and tests. The official release gate remains on Node 22. No production runtime guard was weakened.\\n\\nVerification: 188 client/testing/CLI tests pass on Node 22 (30 + 130 + 28). The Node 20 compatibility command passed all 187 tests before the final acquisition change; its affected authenticated suites then passed 51/51 including that new regression. All 11 scoped dependency builds passed on both Node versions, scoped typechecks passed, the CI planner contract passed, and git diff --check passed. The hostile descriptor regression initially exposed two background unhandled rejections; those are fixed and absent from the final run.\\n\\nAddresses current review threads discussion_r4005596983, discussion_r4005596988 and discussion_r4005701040. Fresh CI/review is required before merge. The full release gate and post-publication registry installation were not rerun locally in this task. MCP-1 explicitly requires clean installation of released packages; release automation includes that check, but wiring is not proof of a completed registry release. Do not mark the Linear issue complete without that evidence.\\n\\nQueue: #170 readiness first, #171 after #170 merges, then #133 following its recorded loader replacement decision. No new worktrees or dependency installations.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5665195046/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5665667553\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5665667553\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5665667553,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUbM54Q\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T14:34:40Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T14:34:40Z\",\"body\":\"Readiness assessment for `e664880b7ce715e0ee13fe7aa5e94938f888fbb0`: **not mergeable yet**.\\n\\n- `dev` advanced to `2867c68f0` (PR #178 merged independently). A non-mutating `git merge-tree` confirms a conflict only in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`. The current head has no completed JavaScript or McpFn release-gate check in its check rollup; CodeQL success is not a substitute.\\n- Sonar MCP reports one open security finding, `githubactions:S6505`, on the new compatibility job's `npm ci` (line 164): lifecycle scripts are enabled. No repository `.npmrc` disables them. Resolve with an explicit install/rebuild policy, without a blanket suppression.\\n- Valid lifecycle finding: the suite's unconditional no-client `target.cleanup()` duplicates already-successful cleanup after an open failure. Preserve retry ownership in the session/test-client boundary, retry only retained failures, and keep the initialization-revocation regression. Add a non-idempotent custom cleanup regression.\\n- Valid CLI finding: post-connect inspect redaction failures are converted to plain Error and therefore usage exit 2. They should remain runtime exit 1, using a safe error boundary.\\n- The request to restore the general Node 20 matrix is not accepted as written: DevFn requires Node 22, and current dev itself uses a Node 22-only general job. Retain scoped McpFn Node 20 coverage when reconciling the workflow. Review broader package runtime coverage separately; do not reintroduce the known DevFn failure.\\n\\nFixed: none in this assessment. Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale): prior documented dispositions retained; the general Node 20 restoration suggestion conflicts with the verified runtime requirement. Not Attempted: the two valid runtime fixes, workflow conflict and install policy are queued as the next bounded stabilization task. Verification: exact head and clean worktree checked, all review-thread pages and review/comment bodies read, Sonar gate/security issues queried, and merge-tree inspected without modifying the checkout. No commit, push, merge or post-snapshot review loop. #171 and #133 remain queued.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5665667553/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5666150070\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5666150070\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5666150070,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUbqWtg\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T15:09:08Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T15:09:08Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 422c753d18ca9e3aebba6407da1b74e8af8f4a11.\\n\\nFixed:\\n- The suite now creates its test-client/session owner before connecting and always closes that owner. Failed initialization retains retryable cleanup, while a custom target whose failed open already cleaned successfully is not cleaned twice. Added a non-idempotent cleanup regression; the existing transient revocation test remains passing.\\n- Inspect errors after parsing (inventory, redaction, output, cleanup) retain runtime exit 1. Hostile thrown values use a fixed safe fallback. Oversized inventory and hostile-error regressions pass without exposing credentials.\\n- Reconciled dev at 2867c68f0d387776d10b4a753a14798fb5f49b67. Resolved the CI conflict preserving dev's test concurrency limit and general Node 22 job/name. Kept the dedicated McpFn Node 20 compatibility job.\\n- The new compatibility job installs with npm ci --ignore-scripts and explicitly rebuilds only the trusted esbuild package. This addresses Sonar S6505's unrestricted install-hook finding without suppression.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): the suggestion to restore general Node 20 coverage conflicts with DevFn's Node 22 requirement and current dev's general CI policy; scoped McpFn compatibility remains. Earlier documented dispositions are retained.\\n\\nNot Attempted: new-head hosted CI, Sonar reanalysis, full local release gate, or actual registry publication proof. These are not claimed by local unit-test results. #171 and #133 remain queued.\\n\\nVerification: all 191 client/testing/CLI tests passed on both Node 22 and Node 20 (30 + 131 + 30 each); 11 dependency-closure builds passed; testing/CLI typechecks, CI planner test, workflow YAML parsing and staged diff checks passed. Reused the existing worktree and dependencies; no new installs or worktrees. This is one merge commit incorporating current dev plus the reviewed fixes, with one normal push. Fresh CI and review must complete before merging the PR.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5666150070/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5666627510\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5666627510\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5666627510,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUcHftg\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T15:43:26Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T15:43:26Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 0c8948affe807ad5348586316e5713be09c83c74.\\n\\nFixed:\\n- Protocol shutdown now finishes before handle cleanup can revoke credentials or stop the peer. If protocol shutdown fails, both protocol and handle cleanup ownership remain retryable. Existing in-flight cleanup promises are retained across the await so late aborted handles are not closed twice. Added controlled asynchronous shutdown and failed-shutdown retry regressions; the existing late-handle concurrency regression also passes.\\n- Descriptor scrubbing uses the protected target role, preserving the canonical target kind when a short credential matches part of it. Other descriptor contents remain redacted.\\n- Hosted token-response validation rejects embedded whitespace, invalid characters and misplaced padding using the same Bearer grammar as the CLI.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): prior documented dispositions retained. The previous workflow conflict and install-hook Sonar failure are cleared on the fetched head: hosted McpFn release gate, Node 20 compatibility, Node 18 CommonJS and Sonar all passed. General JavaScript was still running at the one snapshot.\\n\\nNot Attempted: merge while current valid findings required fixes; new-head CI/review; registry publication proof. #171/#133 remain queued.\\n\\nVerification: Node 20 full client/testing/CLI run passed 197 tests (32 + 135 + 30). Node 22 client32 passed after the concurrency fix, testing135 and CLI30 passed in the preceding run. The first shutdown-order implementation exposed a late-aborted-handle timeout; retaining the in-flight cleanup promise fixed it, with no timeout increase or skipped tests. Dependency-closure build11, client/testing typechecks and diff checks passed. No installs or new worktrees. Fresh CI/reviews are required for the pushed commit.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5666627510/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5667095836\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5667095836\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5667095836,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUckFHA\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T16:17:35Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T16:17:35Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 4579aaf1d24400a1560b590c8bd8e0c8f4fd11f2.\\n\\nFixed: initialization-failure cleanup no longer suppresses a failed SDK shutdown or disposes its handle prematurely. It retains the protocol and handle owners, enters the closing state, and requires a successful close retry before another connection. Regressions cover transient and persistent shutdown failures with connect retries configured, asserting no second session and no premature handle cleanup.\\n\\nSkipped / invalid finding: the request to remove Bearer character validation rests on an incorrect claim that RFC 6750 imposes no charset constraint. Section 2.1 explicitly defines b64token and the Bearer Authorization syntax: https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc6750/#section-2.1 . This regex implements that grammar; it does not decode tokens, require JWTs, or require valid base64 encoding. Opaque tokens using the permitted alphabet remain accepted. Colon and embedded whitespace are not valid for this supported Bearer-header contract. No validation rollback.\\n\\nVerification: client34 tests pass on Node22 and Node20, target-suite/remote52 pass on Node22, client build/typecheck and diff checks pass. Before this fix, all functional hosted checks—including general JavaScript, McpFn release gate, Node20, Node18 and Sonar—passed on 0c8948af. That is meaningful progress but not evidence for the new commit.\\n\\nNot Attempted: merging with a valid lifecycle blocker; new-head CI/review or registry release verification. Fresh CI/review is needed after this one fix push. #171/#133 remain queued. No new worktrees or installations.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5667095836/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5667526041\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5667526041\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5667526041,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUc-VmQ\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T16:50:39Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T16:50:39Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 8d18e51818a5a36010f9346dbfe1979d2a8c095c.\\n\\nFixed: deduplicated Codex/Pullfrog findings into one initialization-cleanup ownership race. Initialization cleanup is now registered before detaching the protocol/handle, and explicit close waits for that in-flight cleanup. Rejected shutdown makes the concurrent close fail with retryable cleanup ownership retained; successful shutdown allows close to finish. The wait targets cleanup only, not an abort-ignoring target.open or the whole connect promise. Concurrent callers reuse the same cleanup promise.\\n\\nVerification: client36 tests pass on Node22 and Node20, including deferred shutdown success/rejection during concurrent permanent close and existing abort-ignoring/late-handle regressions. Remote/suite52 pass on Node22; client build and diff checks pass.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): previous dispositions retained. The fetched head has green general JavaScript, McpFn release gate, Node20/18 and Sonar checks. CodeRabbit is auto-paused; its green check is not fresh review evidence. Codex and Pullfrog both reviewed the current head and identified this same race.\\n\\nNot Attempted: merge while this valid finding needed remediation; new-head review/CI; registry release proof. One normal fix push, no additional worktrees or installs. #171 and #133 remain queued. Fresh CI and substantive review are required before merging.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5667526041/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5668154252\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5668154252\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5668154252,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUdkrjA\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T17:41:15Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T17:41:15Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 96edf052a966bffa6ed3c394b942323c05df25b8.\\n\\nFixed: Codex P1 percent-encoded credential reflection. Credential registration now retains URL-encoded and form-space variants of opaque header components (including decoded Basic components), with case-insensitive percent hex matching while preserving case-sensitive opaque text. The same registered variants flow through direct conformance redaction and retained target report scopes after cleanup.\\n\\nVerification: all 139 testing-package tests pass on Node22; 66 remote-target/report/suite tests pass on Node20. Testing typecheck, build and diff checks pass. Regressions cover API-key/Bearer fields, mixed-case escapes, payload keys and Error messages, scope retention after cleanup, and finalized suite JSON/JUnit cleanup errors.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): previous dispositions retained. Pullfrog reviewed the previous exact head and reported no new issues. Codex found this separate redaction gap. Snapshot functional CI passed; CodeRabbit remains auto-paused and skipped reviewers do not count as fresh coverage.\\n\\nNot Attempted: merging the new head before fresh CI/substantive review, registry publication proof, or changes to queued PRs. No additional worktrees or installs. If another lifecycle race appears, the agreed next action is coordinated shutdown/ownership consolidation with concurrency tests before another lifecycle push.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5668154252/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5668568971\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5668568971\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5668568971,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUd9_iw\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T18:15:02Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T18:15:02Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed b245fe637726679a32c8a4549c57b59d73af4047.\\n\\nFixed: completed the encoded-credential matching task. Use URLSearchParams serialization for the actual form encode set (including !, apostrophe, parentheses and tilde); retain literal versus derived pattern provenance so raw percent sequences remain case-sensitive. Generate derived patterns from retained raw credentials, including report scopes after release. Replace first-occurrence test replacements with replaceAll to address the two CodeQL annotations without suppressions.\\n\\nVerification: testing140 tests pass on Node22; remote/report/suite67 pass on Node20; testing typecheck/build and git diff check pass. New regressions prove actual form punctuation redaction and case-sensitive raw percent credentials alongside existing mixed-case encoded escapes and post-cleanup report scopes. Hosted CodeQL must revalidate the pushed head; local Vitest is not CodeQL proof.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): older dispositions retained. Deduplicated form-encoding findings from Pullfrog/Codex/Cubic and test-encoding findings from CodeQL/Pullfrog. Pullfrog could not run its tests due to its installation failure; local passing tests above are separate evidence.\\n\\nNot Attempted / deferred valid findings: suite artifacts bypass custom target.redact hooks (server metadata, failures and final report), and final suite close can discard retained cleanup ownership after a transient release failure. Both are confirmed against suite.ts and remain merge blockers, with their threads left open. Next defined task: coordinate suite redaction and cleanup ownership through finalization, with custom-target/failed-cleanup regression tests; do not add another isolated lifecycle retry patch. This follows the agreed ownership-stabilization approach.\\n\\nNo merge. One encoding-contract task completed, one normal push, no new worktrees or installs. #171 and #133 remain queued. Release/registry proof remains outstanding separately from code CI.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5668568971/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5668986373\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5668986373\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5668986373,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUeXeBQ\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T18:48:17Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T18:48:17Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 793fa12368bed341a44cb315838bf4e6873baeed.\\n\\nFixed: completed the custom-target artifact redaction task. Suite failures, diagnostics, descriptors and final reports now use a single helper that invokes the target-owned redact hook before the bounded credential/generic scrubber. This covers custom targets without authenticatedHttpTarget secret registration. Existing fail-closed boundaries omit report payloads when a custom redactor throws.\\n\\nVerification: testing143 tests pass on Node22; suite/remote/report70 pass on Node20; testing typecheck, build and diff check pass. Three new custom-target cases cover reflected server metadata/descriptors, inventory failure text, and a throwing secret-bearing redactor. The initial failure fixture lacked tools/list support; adding a real fixture tool exercised the intended inventory mismatch path and passed.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): no newly added inline findings this snapshot. The previous encoding fixes have green CodeQL and functional CI; Pullfrog reports no new incremental issues, but its local test install was blocked and is not counted as passing test evidence. Older dispositions retained.\\n\\nNot Attempted / deferred valid: final suite close still discards the retained client owner when cleanup rejects. That thread remains open and blocks merge. Next task must transfer persistent cleanup ownership explicitly (using the existing conformance cleanup-error contract as precedent), preserve the safe bounded report, serialize retry calls, and test transient/permanent shutdown plus credential release failures. No isolated unconditional retry was added in this redaction task.\\n\\nOne normal push; no merge, new worktrees or installs. #171 and #133 remain queued. Fresh new-head CI/review and the remaining cleanup ownership task are required before merge consideration; published-consumer proof remains a separate release-completion requirement.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5668986373/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5669487732\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5669487732\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5669487732,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUe2EdA\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T19:22:36Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T19:22:36Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 85fc0747394ff7e7e40d8f5deeba14463869ebef.\\n\\nFixed: suite finalization now explicitly transfers failed cleanup ownership to McpFnTargetSuiteCleanupError, following the conformance error precedent. The error carries the finalized bounded report and retains the original client in a WeakMap. retryCleanup shares concurrent calls, retains ownership on rejection (rethrowing the same safe error), and releases ownership only on success. It reuses the client's coordinated shutdown rather than bypassing it or adding a competing target-cleanup path. The CLI performs one retry and emits the failed snapshot/exit1. README documents the new rejection contract; ordinary successful cleanup still returns a report.\\n\\nVerification: testing146 and CLI30 tests pass on Node22; suite/remote63 pass on Node20. Testing build and testing/CLI typechecks pass; diff check passes. Regressions cover repeated failed custom handle shutdown, concurrent retries, successful release/no-op later retries, and transient credential revoke/dispose failures without duplicating successful release stages. Existing cleanup-report tests now explicitly catch the typed cleanup error. No raw cleanup exception is exposed through retry errors.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): previous dispositions retained. Snapshot hosted functional gates passed, but reviewers found additional valid redaction/report issues, so green CI is not merge readiness.\\n\\nNot Attempted / deferred: four snapshot findings remain open: duplicate custom-redactor processing of already-redacted diagnostics; custom redactors corrupt fixed report discriminators; JSON-string-escaped credential reflections; falsy adapter rejections in host-authorization. Next task should stabilize the report projection/redaction boundary, preserving structural fields and invoking custom redactors only on target-controlled payloads. Also guard null/undefined adapter failures. These are merge blockers and are not counted as resolved by the ownership work.\\n\\nOne bounded ownership task and normal push completed; no merge, new worktree or install. CLI cleanup retry is an attempt, not a guarantee that an external provider successfully releases resources. Fresh CI/review is required. #171 and #133 remain queued; registry release proof is separate.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5669487732/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5669972056\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5669972056\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5669972056,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUfToWA\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T19:57:48Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T19:57:48Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 00e661ce8afd7f0c2cf43f4056d2ae31b8f20344.\\n\\nFixed: completed the bounded report-projection task covering all six actionable snapshot findings. Suite finalization rebuilds its authored envelope and invokes custom hooks only on target-controlled payloads, preserving status/kind/counters and already-redacted failure/scenario/diagnostic content. Consumer diagnostics no longer run the custom hook a second time. Timeline retention now accounts for serialized bytes and evicts/drops during collection under maxReportBytes, not only after execution. Credential patterns include JSON-string escaping. Hosted adapter null/undefined/false/zero/empty-string failures produce failed cases and continue fixtures. Cleanup regression tests now fail explicitly if the operation resolves instead of transferring its error owner.\\n\\nVerification: testing155 tests pass on Node22; suite/remote/host-authorization108 pass on Node20; testing build/typecheck/diff checks pass. Added custom structural-secret collision tests, single custom diagnostic pass and byte-bound coverage, JSON-escaped secret coverage, five falsy adapter rejection fixtures, and strengthened the cleanup error assertions. Existing retry-ownership regressions continue passing.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): previous dispositions retained. Pullfrog reported no new cleanup-ownership problems in the previous head; Codex/Cubic identified timeline retention and assertion coverage. Previous four report findings were still valid and are included in this batch. Snapshot functional CI passed; skipped/paused reviewers are not treated as coverage.\\n\\nNot Attempted: new-head review/CI, merge or published-registry verification. No new worktrees or installs. All six currently actionable findings were addressed; convergence still requires a later fresh-head review rather than inference from local tests. #171 then #133 remain queued.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5669972056/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5670395294\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5670395294\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5670395294,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUftdng\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T20:31:37Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T20:31:37Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 96ab203f43330d133786cca58442b22f29db3ba1.\\n\\nFixed: three validated snapshot findings in artifact collection. Inspector recording uses generic redaction for already client-redacted events, and snapshot serialization keeps retained events outside the custom-hook pass as well. Map/Set redaction checks intrinsic collection size before materializing entries and uses intrinsic iterators so subclass overrides cannot bypass that bound. Suite timeline loss tracks byte/count causes separately and reports the limit actually exceeded.\\n\\nVerification: testing157 and inspector14 tests pass on Node22; focused suite/remote69 plus inspector14 pass on Node20. Testing/inspector builds and typechecks pass; diff checks pass. Added non-idempotent event-redactor recording/snapshot regression, oversized Map/Set tests with a spoofed public size, and byte-only timeline reason assertions. No extra installs/worktrees.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): prior dispositions retained. Pullfrog confirms the previous suite envelope issue is closed; its new finding was truncation reason accuracy. Codex identified the inspector event and collection allocation gaps addressed above. Previous-head functional CI is green; fresh pushed-head CI/review remains required.\\n\\nNot Attempted: merge or release publication verification. No valid deferred code finding from this snapshot remains; further review is needed to establish convergence. #171 and #133 remain queued in that order.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5670395294/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5670804442\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5670804442\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5670804442,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUgGb2g\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T21:05:59Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T21:05:59Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 9924c80725c6f7a13a63dbaa448b041e55c09296.\\n\\nFixed: authenticated conformance operational exceptions without a result now become safe typed runtime failures (exit1), rather than usage exit2. Explicit proxy input TypeErrors preserve usage classification. Added regression coverage for plain bind/close failures, credential-safe stderr, and input validation. Strengthened inspector event coverage with an explicit nonempty diagnostic assertion and moved the regression inside its existing describe group.\\n\\nVerification: CLI31 and inspector14 tests pass on Node22; the two conformance cleanup/runtime tests pass on Node20. CLI build plus CLI/inspector typechecks and diff check pass. General JavaScript hosted CI was still in progress at the single snapshot; release/compatibility gates passed. No post-push CI/review polling.\\n\\nInvalid finding: immutable target redactor output does NOT make inspector snapshot assignment throw in the reported path. McpFnClient.redact passes hook output through redactOAuthValue, which creates a fresh mutable object. A direct Node22 probe using target.redact = value => Object.freeze({...value}) yielded Object.isFrozen(result) === false and allowed timeline assignment. No speculative production change for this report. Previous dispositions retained.\\n\\nNot Attempted: merge or registry publication verification. All actionable findings from this snapshot addressed; new-head CI/review still required. No new worktrees or installs; #171 and #133 remain queued.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5670804442/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5671193355\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5671193355\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5671193355,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUgeLCw\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T21:41:22Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T21:41:22Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed f3667495eb67892198d81725d412c63e79c79353.\\n\\nFixed: moved shared authenticated conformance URL validation before credential acquisition and the operational sanitizer. Actual malformed URL/protocol/userinfo/fragment/nonloopback inputs now reach CLI usage exit2; runtime failures retain safe exit1. CLI regressions exercise the real library validation boundary, not just a mocked TypeError.\\n\\nFixed: requested replacement markers are checked against credential patterns and scrubbed before the outer generic redaction pass can reintroduce them. Inspector export tests cover credentials MCPFN_SECRET and SECRET; colliding placeholders are omitted instead of reproducing credentials. Existing normal placeholders remain unchanged.\\n\\nFixed: suite and inspector diagnostic serialization failures (including bigint) now increment dropped-event accounting, making reports incomplete instead of silently swallowing listener failures. Includes the additional Codex finding in its substantive review body, not only inline threads.\\n\\nVerification: Node22 client36, testing158, inspector17 and CLI36 tests pass; Node20 client36, focused testing30, inspector17 and conformanceCLI7 pass. Client/testing/inspector builds and client/testing/inspector/CLI typechecks pass; diff check passes. Invalid-URL cleanup fixture now expects no release because validation precedes acquisition. No new installs/worktrees.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): prior dispositions retained; duplicate configuration findings from Pullfrog/Cubic treated as one root cause. Previous-head functional checks passed. No known valid code finding deferred from this snapshot.\\n\\nNot Attempted: merge or registry publication verification. Fresh review and CI must validate the pushed head. #171 then #133 remain queued. One bounded report/validation-contract fix push; no post-push review loop.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5671193355/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5671537920\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5671537920\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5671537920,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUgzNAA\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T22:14:00Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T22:14:00Z\",\"body\":\"Readiness assessment for f3667495eb67892198d81725d412c63e79c79353: NOT READY.\\n\\nAll functional hosted checks in the snapshot passed, and Pullfrog found no new incremental issue (its local test install remained blocked). Codex identified a reproduced cleanup ordering bug. No code commit/push/merge in this assessment run.\\n\\nConfirmed: an abort-ignoring open returns a late handle; handle.close fails transiently; openTargetAttempt finally calls target.cleanup despite pendingCleanup retaining that handle. A direct Node22 production-client probe produced beforeRetry=[handle-close,target-cleanup], afterRetry=[handle-close,target-cleanup,handle-close], disposed=true, retry=failed. Target cleanup destroyed peer state required by the retry. This is another lifecycle ordering defect, triggering the user-approved coordinated-shutdown approach rather than another isolated conditional.\\n\\nNext implementation task: centralize ownership draining. Every explicit close, initialization-failure cleanup, failed open, and late aborted open must register ownership before detaching it and use one coordinated ordering policy: protocol shutdown -> owned handles -> target-wide cleanup. The coordinator must serialize concurrent drains, retain failed ownership, and forbid target cleanup while any pending/opening/protocol/handle owner needs its state. Do not await abort-ignoring open itself. Late owners arriving during a drain must trigger a later drain without self-await deadlocks. Retry remains explicit after shutdown failure; errors remain safe and typed. Reuse existing client session/cleanup-error contracts, no competing target-only retry path. Replace direct target cleanup calls at the boundaries with the coordinator; do not merely add pendingCleanup.size to this one finally block.\\n\\nRequired matrix: deferred open resolves/rejects after abort, late handle first-close fails then succeeds, target cleanup must not precede successful handle close; concurrent close and late arrival; initialization protocol close failure + retry; handle-close/target-cleanup failures separately; permanent-close escalation, idempotent successful release, and existing abort-ignoring tests. Validate client Node20/22 plus dependent suite/inspector cleanup tests.\\n\\nOther valid pending findings: conformance credential release exhaustion is mislabeled upstream-conformance (use provider/transport-close layer or OAuth token-revocation as appropriate); suite must check structuredClone compatibility before retaining function/symbol-bearing diagnostics; invalid-URL test must assert acquire never called. Keep these pending until addressed, with subsystem tests.\\n\\nInvalid Cubic marker-test finding: it conflates two different it.each blocks. MCPFN_SECRET/SECRET cases belong to the first programmatic-artifact test, which asserts absence of the secret. The guard secret===MCPFN is in the second test with cases logging.message/connected/MCPFN. Do not change the guard as requested; existing passing inspector17 tests cover both blocks.\\n\\nNo extra worktrees/install. #171/#133 remain queued. Current state and findings—not elapsed review rounds—prevent merge. Registry completion evidence remains separate.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5671537920/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5672005780\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5672005780\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5672005780,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUhPwlA\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T23:05:17Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T23:05:17Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 7ed88154bddf34c59a1fe4d1042610c45706b54c.\\n\\nFixed: consolidated production-client shutdown into one ownership drain. Explicit close, initialization cleanup, failed opens, and late aborted opens register retained protocols/handles before detaching them and share drainCleanup. The drain closes protocols before handles and target-wide state last; live sessions or pending opens prevent target cleanup. Failed ownership remains queued, and a latched failure prevents the late-open finally path from implicitly retrying or disposing peer state. Explicit close retries the same owners. The drain checks protocol ownership between handles so late arrivals respect ordering. This replaces the previous separate initialization/handle cleanup promise paths rather than adding a one-off finally guard.\\n\\nVerification: Node22 client39, testing158, inspector17 and CLI36 tests pass; Node20 client39 and focused suite/remote70 pass. Client build/typecheck and diff checks pass. Existing deferred initialization shutdown/concurrent close and abort-ignoring regressions remain green. New late-open success/handle-failure/target-failure cases assert exact cleanup ordering, concurrent explicit retry, no premature target disposal and no duplicate successful cleanup. Production protocol/handle/target shutdown calls now reside in the coordinated drain.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): no new findings beyond the prior snapshot. Retained invalid marker-test disposition: reviewer conflated separate it.each blocks. Previous-head hosted checks passed; new-head CI/review pending.\\n\\nNot Attempted / deferred valid: provider cleanup failure classification in conformance, structuredClone-incompatible diagnostic retention, and the missing acquisition spy assertion. Those threads remain open for the next bounded reporting task. No merge, new worktree or install. #171 then #133 remain queued; release registry proof is separate.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5672005780/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5672364544\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5672364544\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5672364544,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUhlqAA\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T23:39:14Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T23:39:14Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed a2315f70c222c5eff63fccf7b6ddf42a961bbdf2.\\n\\nFixed: inspector snapshots now redact descriptor payload, server metadata and inventories separately, then construct authored kind/state/count fields. Custom secrets matching custom, connected or mcpfn.inspector-snapshot cannot overwrite those discriminators.\\n\\nFixed: suite diagnostic retention checks structuredClone compatibility as well as JSON encoding; function/symbol diagnostics are dropped and accounted for before they can erase successful scenario results during finalization. Regression cases explicitly retain a passed scenario result.\\n\\nFixed: exhausted conformance credential cleanup is attributed to token-revocation/authorization-server for OAuth credentials or transport-close/mcpfn-preflight for other providers, preserving separate upstream results. Successful runner regressions verify that synthesized primary cleanup failures use the correct layer. Invalid-URL validation tests now spy on acquisition directly.\\n\\nVerification: testing162 and inspector20 tests pass on Node22, with the strengthened suite18 rerun passing after its final test edit. Focused testing42 and inspector20 pass on Node20. Testing/inspector builds and typechecks plus diff checks pass. No new installs/worktrees.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): previous dispositions retained. Pullfrog found no new cleanup-coordinator issue and ran the focused client lifecycle tests successfully. Codex's new inspector-envelope finding is addressed here together with the three already pending reporting findings. Snapshot hosted functional checks passed.\\n\\nNot Attempted: merge, new-head CI/review or registry publication verification. No valid code finding remains deferred from this snapshot. #171 then #133 remain queued; fresh current-head review is required to confirm convergence.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5672364544/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5672804023\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5672804023\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5672804023,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUiAetw\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-15T00:28:06Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-15T00:28:06Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed a57043bb8a45a56345706eab88c66c64e7873139.\\n\\nFixed: implicit and explicit replacement markers now follow the same credential-safety policy. The remote scrubber checks the default [REDACTED] marker; the client sanitizes the selected default or custom marker before its generic pass. Inspector events are retained as structured clones of the already-redacted client envelopes, avoiding generic re-redaction that could reintroduce the unsafe default marker. Default-marker and substring credentials are covered through live inspector artifacts and direct redaction. Also made fixture teardown run even if inspector.close rejects.\\n\\nVerification: Node22 client39/testing164/inspector22 pass; Node20 remote56/inspector22 pass. Client/testing/inspector builds, client/inspector typechecks and diff checks pass. The final fixture cleanup edit passed the authenticated-artifact test file again.\\n\\nHosted CI diagnosis: general JavaScript failed in inherited @superfunctions/admin dispatcher idempotency test, missing meta.idempotencyReplay on the assumed second concurrent caller (dispatcher.test.ts:1221). Dispatcher source and test are unchanged from integrated dev2867c68f; the focused test passes locally on Node22. This suggests an ordering-sensitive baseline failure but is not proof the hosted check passed. No admin code change or suppression; hosted CI remains a merge gate.\\n\\nNot Attempted / deferred: custom suite metadata must be scrubbed before target cleanup clears custom credential state; live client event discriminators need payload-only custom redaction; lossy JSON diagnostics (non-finite values and undefined semantics) require a deliberate fidelity policy. These remain review blockers; no merge. Next task is the live custom-redaction contract rather than more isolated serialization patches. Prior dispositions retained. No new worktrees or installs; #171/#133 queued.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5672804023/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5673101731\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5673101731\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5673101731,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUiSpow\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-15T01:06:24Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-15T01:06:24Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed e0550a2cc0715a37092ac72a32238800876d71ae.\\n\\nFixed: suite payload projection now happens while the session is connected, before target cleanup can erase custom credential state. Finalization serializes the captured safe values without invoking custom hooks after release. Cleanup diagnostics use a minimal target descriptor so retries cannot reread disposed custom state. Unavailable/unredactable payloads retain the fail-closed report path and cleanup-error ownership. Descriptor fixtures now verify capture before post-close behavior changes rather than requiring a post-close read.\\n\\nFixed: live client-event kind/format and target kind are constructed outside custom payload redaction. Inspector scenario exports likewise reconstruct formatVersion/kind/sideEffect and preserve top-level authored keys around redacted payload fields. Regressions cover logging.message recognition and tools.call/non-idempotent/none collisions.\\n\\nFixed: diagnostic serialization rejects undefined and non-finite numbers before retaining them; existing cloneability/JSON checks cover functions/symbols/bigint. These events increment drop accounting and mark reports incomplete while preserving passed scenario results. Full suite tests verify ordinary diagnostics remain complete.\\n\\nVerification: Node22 client39/testing168/inspector26/CLI36 pass; Node20 suite/remote78 and inspector26 pass. Client/testing/inspector builds and typechecks pass; diff check passes. The final cleanup-diagnostic adjustment passed client39 and suite22 again. New ephemeral-custom-credential regression proves report metadata is scrubbed before handle.close clears its secret state.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Stale): previous dispositions retained. Current snapshot functional CI is green, including general JavaScript after the prior inherited admin test failure. Pullfrog's remaining JSON-fidelity finding is addressed here; Codex scenario discriminator finding is addressed along with prior live-redaction findings.\\n\\nNot Attempted: merge, new-head CI/review or registry publication verification. All actionable snapshot findings addressed; fresh review still required. No new worktrees/install; #171 then #133 remain queued.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5673101731/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5674385881\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5674385881\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5674385881,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUjhB2Q\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-15T03:41:20Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-15T03:41:20Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 2c3ea3bb4080e343327a490de93b603f78e84511.\\n\\nFixed: reproduced four credential leaks in exported scenario payloads whose fields resemble diagnostic envelopes (clientState/status/kind/target.kind). Payload redaction now explicitly disables envelope exemptions through the target hook; authored scenario format/kind/sideEffect remain intact. Added and documented the optional preserveKeys hook setting. All four new regressions failed before the fix and pass afterward.\\n\\nSkipped (Invalid): Pullfrog PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iVk0e assumes Map reaches JSON.stringify unnormalized. Production client redaction converts Map and Set into explicit type/entries or type/values objects before suite admission. New real-client suite regressions verify exact persisted entries, complete status and zero drops; no production container rejection added. Earlier historical dispositions retained.\\n\\nNot Attempted: four remaining findings are deferred to the next bounded report-failure task: preserve original connection failure when manifest is supplied but execution never starts (PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iVj57); retain structural target kind on failed connections (PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iVlbx); count diagnostic-redaction fallback omissions in suite/inspector completeness (PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iVlb5); add hostile descriptor coverage at the live capture boundary (PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iVj6D). These remain open. No merge; #171/#133 remain queued. Published consumer verification remains outstanding.\\n\\nVerification: Node22 inspector30/client39/suite24; Node20 inspector30. Client build and client/inspector typechecks passed; diff check passed. Snapshot functional CI green. Graphite/Sourcery skipped and CodeRabbit paused are not passing review coverage. Pullfrog review ran but its local tests could not run. No new worktrees or installs. One bounded scenario-redaction task only; no post-push review loop.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5674385881/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5674637441\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5674637441\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5674637441,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUjwYgQ\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-15T04:15:05Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-15T04:15:05Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed f4f5f0aa6c42f26be120686b22c392ffb4f8a839.\\n\\nFixed: authenticated handle cleanup now follows transport shutdown -> credential release. A failed transport close retains the credential and redaction state for retry. Once transport shutdown succeeds, later revoke/dispose retries do not close the transport again. Concurrent handle closes share the existing in-flight promise. This brings the authenticated adapter into agreement with the central client cleanup coordinator; the coordinator architecture is unchanged. PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iXUX6 addressed.\\n\\nVerification: three regressions failed before the fix and pass afterward: failed transport shutdown retains provider state and orders the successful retry; failed revocation and failed disposal retry only their unfinished stage. Node22 testing173, Node20 suite/remote83 passed; testing build/typecheck and diff check passed. No network server or additional installation needed for the new transport-failure fixtures.\\n\\nSkipped (Invalid / Nonblocking): prior Map/Set evidence finding remains disproven and Pullfrog now agrees. Cubic PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iXTTU is a test-name preference, not a correctness problem: Map and Set names are distinct and identify the container type. No unrelated naming-only edit. Historical addressed/stale dispositions retained.\\n\\nNot Attempted: report-failure work remains pending (manifest masking connection errors, failed-target kind, diagnostic omission accounting and hostile live descriptor coverage). New PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iXUX_ confirms diagnostic whole-envelope custom redaction can corrupt phase/outcome; include it in that report task. PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iXUYB identifies ignored fixture.token.code; source confirms it is replaced with the redirect code, so evaluate fixture semantics and correct separately. No merge; JavaScript CI still running in the snapshot, other functional checks green. CodeRabbit paused and skipped reviewers are not counted as passing coverage. Pullfrog found no new issue in the preceding delta, but its local tests were blocked. #171 and #133 remain queued. No new worktrees/install or post-push review loop.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5674637441/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5674886729\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5674886729\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5674886729,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUj_mSQ\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-15T04:48:10Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-15T04:48:10Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed af4ddc996c39984db38e9e43c9a8f65c9b226435.\\n\\nFixed: preconnection suite failures now retain the known structural transport kind. Supplying an unchecked manifest no longer forces the generic serialization fallback when no execution payload exists, so normalized connection/authentication failure evidence survives. Arbitrary descriptor values remain deferred until credential-aware redaction is available; unknown custom kind strings use the safe custom fallback on preconnection failure.\\n\\nFixed (coverage): added live hostile-descriptor throw/proxy regressions proving safe incomplete artifacts, empty unsafe results/timeline, no credential leak, and successful cleanup. These complement the existing successful capture-before-post-cleanup-descriptor tests.\\n\\nAddressed: PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iVj57, PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iVlbx, PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iVj6D. Three connection-failure regressions failed before the fixes and pass afterward; two hostile-descriptor regressions verify the existing fallback.\\n\\nVerification: Node22 testing178; Node20 suite/remote88; testing build/typecheck and diff check passed. Snapshot functional CI green. Pullfrog found no new issue in the prior lease-order change; its local tests remained blocked. Paused/skipped reviewers are not counted as passing coverage.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Invalid): retain historical dispositions, including Map/Set normalization and nonblocking test-title preference.\\n\\nNot Attempted: diagnostic structural preservation and omission accounting remain one pending task (PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iXUX_, PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iVlb5). Separate hosted-fixture code override finding PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iXUYB remains pending. New PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iXsct is valid by source: credentialValues extracts a whitespace suffix from every header; constrain scheme-specific extraction rather than treating an API-key suffix as an independent credential. These findings remain open. No merge, registry-publication claim, other-PR change, worktree creation or install. One bounded suite-failure reporting task completed.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5674886729/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5675177248\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5675177248\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5675177248,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUkRVIA\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-15T05:21:53Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-15T05:21:53Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed a92257f07ca835c83f5896d293bff669d8c6e9a9.\\n\\nFixed: suite and inspector artifacts now count MCPFN_DIAGNOSTIC_REDACTION_FAILED as an omitted original diagnostic. They retain the safe replacement event as evidence, but mark timeline/report completeness false. Suite reports explain the redaction omission without inventing a transport-cleanup failure. Addresses PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iVlb5.\\n\\nVerification: both new regressions failed before and pass after: a custom provider loses redaction state after successful close, and an inspector target rejects diagnostic redaction while remaining usable. Tests verify incomplete artifacts, retained safe fallback, absent private error text, and no fabricated suite failure. Node22 testing179/inspector31; Node20 suite30/inspector31; both builds/typechecks and diff check pass. Snapshot functional CI green; prior Pullfrog review found no new issue. Paused/skipped reviewers are not counted as passing coverage.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Invalid): historical dispositions retained, including normalized Map/Set diagnostic evidence and nonblocking container-test naming.\\n\\nNot Attempted: reconstruct diagnostic phase/outcome outside custom redaction (PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iXUX_); restrict credential suffix extraction (PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iXsct); honor explicitly configured token code fixtures (PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iXUYB). New PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iYHEW is valid by source: variable discovery and substitution currently visit values only, so redacted property-key placeholders cannot replay correctly. Include keys with collision handling in a separate export/replay contract task. These four findings remain open. No merge or registry-publication claim. No new worktrees/install or other-PR changes. One bounded diagnostic omission-accounting task completed.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5675177248/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5675462421\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5675462421\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5675462421,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUkivFQ\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-15T05:56:00Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-15T05:56:00Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed e77a401fa1ef8a2a3a02641ec2023090d6810050.\\n\\nFixed: diagnostic omission accounting now uses client-owned object identity, not the public diagnostic code. The client tracks generated safe fallbacks in a WeakSet and exposes a live-event predicate used by suite and inspector before cloning/serialization. Already-safe generated fallbacks bypass further target redaction. Target-authored code collisions remain ordinary complete evidence. Addresses PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iYmUx.\\n\\nVerification: new suite/inspector code-collision regressions failed before and pass after; prior real redaction-omission tests remain passing. Node22 client39/testing180/inspector32; Node20 suite31/inspector32; client/testing/inspector builds and typechecks pass; diff check clean. Snapshot functional CI green. Paused/skipped reviewers and unavailable reviewer-local tests are not counted as passing coverage.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Invalid): PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iYppO describes the inverse of current source: validateOAuthRejection explicitly throws when the requested callback is absent from registered redirect URIs. A production built-package probe using chatgpt-unregistered-redirect and an error callback to that URI returned status=failed, phase=authorization-request, responseStatus=302, error=Rejected redirect URI must not receive a callback. No production change warranted. Historical Map/Set and naming dispositions retained.\\n\\nNot Attempted: four earlier valid tasks remain: diagnostic phase/outcome preservation (PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iXUX_), recognized-scheme credential extraction (PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iXsct), explicit token-code fixture behavior (PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iXUYB), and key-placeholder discovery/substitution (PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iYHEW). No merge, publication-completeness claim, other-PR changes, new worktree or install. One bounded diagnostic provenance task completed.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5675462421/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5675797833\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5675797833\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5675797833,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUk3NSQ\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-15T06:29:36Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-15T06:29:36Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed 37a072aeb5b3db53513d5381d4b85300100e0534.\\n\\nFixed: generated short redaction masks are checked against the full registered credential-variant set, using empty replacement if a mask would reproduce another credential. Covers abc plus *** and marker collisions. Addresses PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iZIHx.\\n\\nFixed: token suffix extraction now requires an Authorization or Proxy-Authorization header; opaque API-key values remain whole even when they contain spaces or look like a scheme. Preserved supported custom Authorization schemes (including Token) and Basic decoding. Restricting named schemes alone initially failed the existing custom-scheme security test, so header context supplies the correct boundary. Addresses PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iXsct.\\n\\nVerification: four new cases failed before the change; nine new cases cover collision-safe masks, opaque header values and case-insensitive authorization header handling. Node22 testing189/inspector32; Node20 remote68; testing build/typecheck and diff check pass. All existing custom-scheme/Basic credential tests remain passing. Snapshot general JavaScript CI pending; other functional checks green. Skipped/paused reviewers are not passing coverage.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Invalid): previous Map/Set and unregistered-callback findings remain disproven; prior nonblocking naming preference retained.\\n\\nNot Attempted: new PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iZFjD correctly identifies that module-local omission provenance is lost across mixed ESM/CJS client and inspector entrypoints. Next fix should expose the check on the supplied client instance, with a built-package mixed-entry regression. Three other pending tasks remain: diagnostic phase/outcome preservation, explicit token-code fixture behavior, and key-placeholder discovery/substitution. No merge, publication claim, other-PR changes, worktree creation or install. One bounded credential extraction/replacement task completed.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5675797833/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5676120271\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5676120271\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5676120271,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABUlK4zw\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"id\":52457571,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52457571?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/thyaravind\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/thyaravind/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-15T06:58:22Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-15T06:58:22Z\",\"body\":\"Pushed aa08ef72e54d822de9dbd5d95f9216ec6417e8a3.\\n\\nFixed: credential redaction now validates complete payload strings and dynamic keys after both opaque and generic redaction. If a final string contains a registered credential variant, the entire string is omitted instead of deleting a substring and potentially joining surrounding fragments into another secret. This final pass performs no further substitutions and preserves the existing authored-envelope exemptions. Addresses PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iZouO and PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iZrz7.\\n\\nVerification: regression cases cover adjacent masks, deletion joining surrounding text, a mask joining existing text, and generic marker output. Node22 testing193/inspector32; Node20 remote72; testing build/typecheck and diff check pass.\\n\\nCI diagnosis: general JavaScript failed packages/admin/src/dispatcher.test.ts:1221 (atomic idempotency test), expecting secondResult.meta.idempotencyReplay. Dispatcher, test and idempotency code are inherited from integrated dev, outside this remediation diff. Both dispatches await input fingerprinting before reservation; invocation order does not guarantee reservation order, whereas the test assumes the second invocation loses. Focused Node22 test passes locally. This is evidence of an ordering-sensitive assertion, not proof that the hosted job now passes. No unrelated admin edit or suppression was made. Log /tmp/sf-hb40-ci.log; local /tmp/sf-hb40-admin.log.\\n\\nSkipped (Already Fixed / Invalid): historical Map/Set and unregistered-callback findings remain disproven. Paused/skipped reviewers do not count as passing coverage.\\n\\nNot Attempted: mixed-entry omission provenance, diagnostic structural-field preservation, explicit token-code fixtures and property-key variable replay remain pending. Two newly fetched client-event findings also remain: explicit payload-mode redaction (PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iZrJG) and omitted-event provenance/completeness for inspector and scenario expectations (PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iZrJL). These belong in the pending client-event/diagnostic contract task. No merge or publication claim. No new worktrees/install/other-PR changes. One bounded final-redaction-output task completed, with separate CI diagnosis.\\n\\n\\nOne review-remediation pass completed. Fresh CI/reviews are pending; no merge or post-push review loop performed. Other PRs are handled separately.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5676120271/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/comments/5700136851\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5700136851\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170\",\"id\":5700136851,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABU8Evkw\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"sonarqubecloud[bot]\",\"id\":39514782,\"node_id\":\"MDM6Qm90Mzk1MTQ3ODI=\",\"avatar_url\":\"ht