tps://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"_links\":{\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5199832110\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\"}},\"submitted_at\":\"2026-09-14T15:47:18Z\",\"commit_id\":\"0c8948affe807ad5348586316e5713be09c83c74\"},{\"id\":5199879472,\"node_id\":\"PRR_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABNe_dMA\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\",\"id\":199175422,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOC98s_g\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1144995?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/0c8948affe807ad5348586316e5713be09c83c74/mcpfn/testing/src/conformance.ts#L132\\n**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Handle upstream response stream errors**\\n\\nWhen the protected upstream sends response headers and then resets or aborts the body stream, its `IncomingMessage` emits an `error`/`aborted` event that this bare `pipe()` does not handle. Because the proxy runs in the conformance caller process, such a malformed server response can become an uncaught exception, terminating the CLI instead of producing a failed conformance report and potentially bypassing credential cleanup; handle response-stream failures by ending or destroying the outgoing response safely.\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5199879472\",\"pull_request_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"_links\":{\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5199879472\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\"}},\"submitted_at\":\"2026-09-14T15:51:49Z\",\"commit_id\":\"0c8948affe807ad5348586316e5713be09c83c74\"},{\"id\":5199921285,\"node_id\":\"PRR_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABNfCAhQ\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"pullfrog[bot]\",\"id\":226033991,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDODXkBRw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1768019?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/pullfrog\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"> ✅ No new issues found.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `422c753d`, covering the shutdown, OAuth evidence, and structural-redaction hardening in `0c8948af`.\\n\\n- **Ordered shutdown ownership** — Closed the MCP protocol before transport handles and retained both owners when protocol shutdown requires a retry.\\n- **Tightened token evidence** — Validated hosted Bearer access tokens against the RFC 6750 token grammar and expanded malformed-token regressions.\\n- **Preserved descriptor structure** — Redacted target descriptors through their report role so credential collisions cannot corrupt `target.kind`.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 0c8948af;\\nif commits have landed on codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\\n\\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\\n- Files reviewed: 55\\n- Commits reviewed: 33\\n- Base: dev (2867c68f)\\n- Head: codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910 (0c8948af)\\n- Reviewed commits:\\n  - 0c8948af — fix(mcpfn): order shutdown and preserve credential contracts\\n  - 422c753d — merge dev and preserve session cleanup ownership\\n  - e664880b — fix(mcpfn): stabilize credential ownership and safe reporting\\n  - a080b785 — fix(mcpfn): fail closed on unsafe error inspection\\n  - 167afb7a — fix(mcpfn): preserve credential cleanup and failure redaction\\n  - 8d45c838 — fix(mcpfn): bound default CLI report serialization\\n  - 1195831f — fix(mcpfn): close authenticated report redaction gaps\\n  - 30f398b6 — fix(mcpfn): preserve provider identity and sanitize failed opens\\n  - 25ed30dc — fix(mcpfn): preserve credential lifecycle and diagnostic contracts\\n  - bd07bfc4 — fix(mcpfn): redact programmatic artifacts and retain conformance evidence\\n  - 1d1d1b93 — fix(mcpfn): retain failed cleanup reports and structural versions\\n  - 2f98827f — fix(mcpfn): isolate cleanup cancellation and bound Windows termination\\n  - 2ed3223d — fix(mcpfn): enforce pending shutdown and terminate runner trees\\n  - 36c4a3a1 — fix(mcpfn): bound conformance capture and order deferred cleanup\\n  - 45affe39 — fix(mcpfn): preserve permanent shutdown and compact report bounds\\n  - 4bb10b48 — fix(mcpfn): classify cleanup errors and reject invalid-client redirects\\n  - bebdc22a — fix(mcpfn): preserve shutdown credentials and redact before truncation\\n  - 16b86310 — fix(mcpfn): bound credentials and clean up before diagnostics\\n  - b9ec3a7d — fix(mcpfn): preserve credential cleanup and conformance report integrity\\n  - 10d5eac2 — fix(mcpfn): retain conformance cleanup and validate OAuth report evidence\\n  - 3ffdf24b — fix(mcpfn): gate reconnect on credential cleanup and redact before truncation\\n  - a93ef9c5 — fix(mcpfn): use explicit inventory ordering and Windows cleanup executable\\n  - 933c96a0 — ci: run JavaScript tests on required Node 22 runtime\\n  - 76a5a16c — Merge branch 'dev' into codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910\\n  - f78a72ae — fix(mcpfn): retain failed credential cleanup and redact inspect errors\\n  - b6ac854c — fix(mcpfn): align client dependents and regenerate workspace lock\\n  - 5a32dbf9 — fix(mcpfn): serialize retained cleanup and reject authorization JSON errors\\n  - c4b1fe5e — fix(mcpfn): retain cleanup ownership and bound typed report redaction\\n  - dd1ac078 — fix(mcpfn): preserve redacted reports and retry credential cleanup\\n  - 9f42334f — fix(mcpfn): redact authenticated outputs and preserve cleanup ownership\\n  - 1e7d9eb0 — fix(mcpfn): protect credential artifacts and validate rejection envelopes\\n  - a7c0dea4 — fix(mcpfn): prevent false conformance success and preserve lifecycle evidence\\n  - f796d70a — feat(mcpfn): add transport-neutral conformance testing\\n- Prior pullfrog review: 422c753d (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5199585062)\\n-->\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/34864035175/job/104043263148) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5199921285\",\"pull_request_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"_links\":{\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5199921285\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\"}},\"submitted_at\":\"2026-09-14T15:56:05Z\",\"commit_id\":\"0c8948affe807ad5348586316e5713be09c83c74\"},{\"id\":52