nctions/170?action=fix&review_id=5206691870) ｜ [Fix 👍s ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/170?action=fix-approved&review_id=5206691870) ｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/34939387720/job/104284342200) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5206691870\",\"pull_request_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"_links\":{\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5206691870\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\"}},\"submitted_at\":\"2026-09-15T07:08:43Z\",\"commit_id\":\"aa08ef72e54d822de9dbd5d95f9216ec6417e8a3\"},{\"id\":5209399308,\"node_id\":\"PRR_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABNoEgDA\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\",\"id\":199175422,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOC98s_g\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1144995?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/1e27fd69af0c741bf68edfdc4d1611d7b647f90e/mcpfn/inspector/src/index.ts#L429-L433\\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Track renamed keys when checking export bounds**\\n\\nWhen a target redactor changes a nested property key, such as replacing a key equal to an active credential with `${MCPFN_SECRET}`, indexing `redactedRecord` by the original key returns `undefined`. If that property's value was also truncated by the 2,048-character export limit, the bounds check misses the truncation and exports the scenario as complete even though replay no longer matches the recorded operation; compare entries using their transformed keys or otherwise retain the original-to-redacted key mapping.\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5209399308\",\"pull_request_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"_links\":{\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5209399308\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\"}},\"submitted_at\":\"2026-09-15T11:32:35Z\",\"commit_id\":\"1e27fd69af0c741bf68edfdc4d1611d7b647f90e\"},{\"id\":5209407629,\"node_id\":\"PRR_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABNoFAjQ\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\"id\":191113872,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOC2QqkA\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1082092?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/cubic-dev-ai\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"<!-- cubic:review-summary:start -->\\n**1 issue found** across 16 files (changes from recent commits).\\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:end -->\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents (unresolved issues)</summary>\\n\\n```text\\n\\nCheck if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately.\\n\\n\\n<file name=\\\"mcpfn/inspector/tests/authenticated-artifacts.test.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"mcpfn/inspector/tests/authenticated-artifacts.test.ts:220\\\">\\nP2: The custom redactor in this test substitutes only substrings equal to \\\"opaque-property-key\\\" in the serialized JSON, so a stored value of \\\"value\\\" (which contains no secret) is left untouched. After exportScenario redacts the operation arguments and structuredContent, the result is { \\\"${MCPFN_SECRET}\\\": \\\"value\\\" }, not { \\\"${MCPFN_SECRET}\\\": \\\"${MCPFN_SECRET}\\\" }. The two toEqual assertions on the value therefore fail, so this test breaks the @mcpfn/inspector suite (or, if the suite is green, is not exercising the behavior it claims). The point of the test is key redaction, so assert the unchanged value.</violation>\\n</file>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/170/ai_pr_review_github_delivery_5c7eafa1ab453f18486cdb1beb33f82af71ebe0cf2f1bf61f4c2457ce01254ea?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F170)</sub>\\n\\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_github_delivery_5c7eafa1ab453f18486cdb1beb33f82af71ebe0cf2f1bf61f4c2457ce01254ea:1e27fd69af0c741bf68edfdc4d1611d7b647f90e:ef4f688d-c951-5e37-a081-804532482b41 -->\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5209407629\",\"pull_request_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"_links\":{\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5209407629\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170\"}},\"submitted_at\":\"2026-09-15T11:33:33Z\",\"commit_id\":\"1e27fd69af0c741bf68edfdc4d1611d7b647f90e\"},{\"id\":5209484065,\"node_id\":\"PRR_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABNoJrIQ\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"pullfrog[bot]\",\"id\":226033991,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDODXkB