pe\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> Failed artifact writes can still strand cleanup ownership and leave the CLI process alive.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `1e45b794`, covering the cleanup and evidence hardening in `45785a27`.\\n\\n- **Preserved cleanup ownership** — Persisted failed conformance and target-suite snapshots before retrying their retained cleanup owners, and moved forced termination for all cleanup-error types to the executable boundary.\\n- **Closed artifact redaction gaps** — Passed payload-key redaction intent through inspector snapshots and expanded credential-collision coverage.\\n- **Enforced OAuth response safety** — Required successful token and refresh responses to carry both `Cache-Control: no-store` and `Pragma: no-cache`, with focused negative fixtures.\\n- **Hardened verification setup** — Restricted Python package setup to binary wheels and removed an unrelated client retry override from lifecycle coverage.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 45785a27;\\nif commits have landed on codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\\n\\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\\n- Files reviewed: 61\\n- Commits reviewed: 61\\n- Base: dev (76ea5821)\\n- Head: codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910 (45785a27)\\n- Reviewed commits:\\n  - 45785a27 — fix(mcpfn): preserve cleanup and evidence contracts\\n  - 1e45b794 — fix(mcpfn): preserve credential cleanup contracts\\n  - 8b23aaa0 — fix(mcpfn): close remaining redaction and cleanup gaps\\n  - bd2669ef — fix(mcpfn): bound cleanup failure handling\\n  - 451f20bd — fix(mcpfn): harden redaction key invariants\\n  - 0010a6c7 — fix(mcpfn): close review artifact invariants\\n  - 1e27fd69 — fix(mcpfn): close remaining review invariants\\n  