{"timestamp":"2026-09-19T10:06:03.778Z","ordinal":4632,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae5e69c79087d0a810f467ed33e28c","status":"completed","call_id":"call_qBrXfdVVVwvEwG8Ga2FSdLRP","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170/.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md\\n@@\\n ## Round 9 termination\\n@@\\n - No post-push review refetch, CI poll, reviewer wait, thread resolution, review dismissal, merge, or second fix loop will be performed.\\n+\\n+## Round 10 assessment\\n+\\n+- Hosted workflow: `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.2.0`, revision `4`, digest `sha256:8781c1c12fe9d5902337d6cf21bfbac49dd3a94c7eadd46bf2622db350444022` (published identity verified through Skillplane via Composio before repository mutation).\\n+- Mode: assessment reset. Round 10 is the next separately invoked single review round; the prior clean streak remains `0`.\\n+- Complete snapshot: captured once at `2026-09-19T10:01:05.850Z` against stable local/upstream/PR head `cf76637ada4ba0263e36f30c23a278826c48dd0a`. Seven thread pages were terminal, all nested comment pages were terminal, and start/end/page head checks matched. The snapshot contains 329 threads (92 unresolved: 39 current and 53 outdated-only), 224 reviews, 64 issue comments, 369 raw inline comments, and 18 check contexts.\\n+- Shared invariant: every emitted typed artifact must preserve credential-free authored keys and discriminators or fail closed; cleanup ownership must remain callable even when no safe artifact can be serialized; OAuth success evidence must accept only exact argument-free anti-cache directives; behavior-preserving maintainability work must keep these boundaries intact.\\n+- Producers and consumers: scenario creation plus inspector export feed replay artifacts; target/session close plus suite finalization feed direct callers and CLI JSON/JUnit/stdout; hosted OAuth response parsing feeds exchange and refresh case results; redaction, authorization, report, orchestration, CLI, and Node/Web adapters feed tests and required analysis.\\n+- Failure boundaries: fixed-key credential collisions cannot produce a typed scenario/report; structural report failure can coincide with a failed cleanup lease; parameterized cache directives do not prove anti-caching; broad analyzer refactors can regress credential redaction, lifecycle phases, bounded serialization, or exit classification.\\n+- Coordinated repair criteria: validate every possible top-level scenario export key before constructing output; retain structural-collision cleanup in a dedicated retryable error with no unsafe report and teach both library/CLI boundaries to preserve it; require exact `no-store` and `no-cache` tokens for both exchange and refresh; decompose only validated analyzer findings with unchanged observable contracts and focused regressions.\\n+- Verification criteria: focused inspector, hosted-authorization, target-suite, report, CLI, conformance, adapter, and redaction regressions; affected package typechecks/builds; complete Node 22 release gate; `git diff --check`; one local/upstream/PR head comparison after at most one push. Hosted review/check surfaces will not be fetched again this round.\\n+\\n+### Round 10 defect families\\n+\\n+| Stable family | Root cause / affected contract | Disposition | First seen | Last attempted | Repair / evidence state |\\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n+| `MCP170-SCENARIO-KEY-STRUCTURE` | Inspector validates scenario discriminator values but not authored top-level keys, allowing a key-equal credential to survive export | Actionable | round 10 | round 10 | Coordinated key-boundary repair selected; regression uses credential `name` |\\n+| `MCP170-OAUTH-CACHE-DIRECTIVE-PARAMS` | Hosted token validation discards directive parameters, so `no-store=false` and `no-cache=false` are accepted | Actionable | round 10 | round 10 | Exact directive-token repair selected for exchange and refresh |\\n+| `MCP170-STRUCTURAL-COLLISION-CLEANUP-OWNER` | Suite finalization throws a safe structural error before transferring an already-retained cleanup owner | Actionable; recurring cleanup-ownership family | round 10 | round 10 | Dedicated reportless retry-owner repair selected for direct and CLI consumers |\\n+| `MCP170-SONAR-REDACTION-DECOMPOSITION` | Redaction/credential helpers contain duplicated bounds, regex, and deeply nested traversal/lifecycle logic | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 11 findings grouped under shared credential/redaction contract |\\n+| `MCP170-SONAR-BASE64-REGEX` | Base64 token patterns use avoidable character-class forms | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 10 | round 10 | 2 findings grouped under token grammar preservation |\\n+| `MCP170-SONAR-SUITE-ORCHESTRATION` | Suite orchestration contains dense comparisons, fallbacks, and control flow | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 5 findings grouped under report/lifecycle behavior preservation |\\n+| `MCP170-SONAR-HOSTED-OAUTH` | Hosted OAuth assessment and rejection validation contain dense conditional construction | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 5 findings grouped under authorization evidence preservation |\\n+| `MCP170-SONAR-REPORT-JUNIT` | Failure normalization and JUnit mapping contain avoidable branching/spread/ternary complexity | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 3 findings grouped under stable report serialization |\\n+| `MCP170-SONAR-CLI` | CLI dispatch and portable-identifier regex trigger maintainability findings | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 10 | round 10 | 2 findings grouped under unchanged exit/output classification |\\n+| `MCP170-SONAR-NODE-WEB-HEADERS` | Two Node-to-Web header adapters duplicate nested ternary conversion | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 2 findings grouped under identical multi-value header semantics |\\n+| `MCP170-SONAR-INSPECTOR` | Secret-marker generation and export fallback selection contain avoidable constructs | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 2 findings grouped under replayable placeholder behavior |\\n+| `MCP170-SONAR-CONFORMANCE` | Official conformance completion mutates a parameter-derived exit code | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 1 finding; preserve incomplete/failure classification |\\n+| `MCP170-SONAR-CUSTOM-TARGET-TYPE` | Custom-target redactor field redundantly combines optional syntax with `undefined` | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 1 type-contract cleanup |\\n+| `MCP170-SONAR-THROW-THIS` | Four analyzer findings flag intentional retry-owner self-rejection in cleanup error classes | Invalid analyzer interpretation | round 10 | round 10 | Existing retry identity is required; suite occurrence is removed incidentally by shared helper, other owner classes remain valid intentional behavior |\\n+\\n+- Snapshot check state: all 18 contexts terminal; 14 successful, 1 neutral, and 3 skipped. Sonar Quality Gate passed and reported 38 new issues; `reviewDecision` was empty.\\n+- Convergence state: not clean. Three new review roots, the recurring cleanup-ownership family, and the now-assessed analyzer families reset the clean streak to `0` even though the snapshot head was stable and required checks were terminal.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b91a-027b-7173-bd75-a52040008bc7","create_time":1789812324.596089}}}
