{"timestamp":"2026-09-19T10:21:03.288Z","ordinal":5056,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae61f6357c87d0bf18a96ce334bbf1","status":"completed","call_id":"call_BYvbjKKO87x7iItB5rY8LP1S","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170/.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md\\n@@\\n-| `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY` | External analyzer inventory contains 36 additional maintainability/reliability findings | Not Attempted (non-gating broad refactor inventory); preserve for reassessment | round 1 | not attempted | None | Round 4 Sonar Quality Gate passed, but its summary increased from 35 to 36 open issues; individual analyzer details were not part of the captured GitHub review surfaces and require a separately coordinated behavior-preserving assessment |\\n+| `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY` | External analyzer inventory contains behavior-preserving maintainability/reliability findings | Assessed and attempted as coordinated subfamilies in round 10; hosted closure pending a later snapshot | round 1 | round 10 | Split 38 reported issues into 34 valid findings across ten contract-aligned repair families and 4 invalid retry-owner findings; the round-10 batch decomposes the valid families without changing external behavior | Round 10 local package suites and release gate passed; no post-push Sonar refetch is permitted this round |\\n@@\\n - Convergence state: not clean. Three new review roots, the recurring cleanup-ownership family, and the now-assessed analyzer families reset the clean streak to `0` even though the snapshot head was stable and required checks were terminal.\\n+\\n+## Round 10 snapshot dispositions\\n+\\n+- Actionable: 4 new unresolved GitHub threads, deduplicated to 3 root causes. `MCP170-SCENARIO-KEY-STRUCTURE`, `MCP170-OAUTH-CACHE-DIRECTIVE-PARAMS`, and `MCP170-STRUCTURAL-COLLISION-CLEANUP-OWNER` are repaired by `80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1`; the threads remain unresolved and were not refetched after push.\\n+- Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale): 87 older unresolved threads retain their prior current-code dispositions. The four round-9 roots are already repaired at the assessed head; outdated status alone was not used as evidence.\\n+- Invalid / Accepted Risk: the older property-key-redaction finding remains invalid based on observed payload-key behavior. The analyzer's retry-owner `throw this` family is invalid because object identity is the ownership token; the suite instance was removed incidentally by a shared retry helper, while the three remaining instances preserve required owner identity. No accepted risks.\\n+- Not Attempted: 0 valid code root causes. The 34 valid Sonar findings were attempted as ten coordinated subfamilies in this batch; their hosted analyzer disposition remains pending until a future separately scheduled snapshot because post-push refetch is forbidden.\\n+- Unassessed: 0 captured threads, review bodies, issue comments, raw inline comments, nested comments, or analyzer findings.\\n+\\n+## Round 10 verification evidence\\n+\\n+- Focused regressions: 28 inspector credential-artifact tests and 145 hosted-authorization/remote-target tests passed after the three review-root repairs. The broader testing/report/suite set passed 189 tests after decomposition, and the CLI reportless-owner regression passed with the target-suite cleanup suite.\\n+- Complete affected package suites: 45 `@mcpfn/client`, 234 `@mcpfn/testing`, 38 `@mcpfn/inspector`, and 54 `@mcpfn/cli` tests passed (371 total).\\n+- Typechecks: `@mcpfn/client`, `@mcpfn/testing`, `@mcpfn/inspector`, and `@mcpfn/cli` passed under Node 22; `@mcpfn/testing` rebuilt successfully before downstream CLI verification.\\n+- Release gate: `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed every reported package test/typecheck/build, Playwright, official conformance, mixed-entry redaction, examples, ESM/CJS imports, dry-run packs, packed-consumer installation, and round trips.\\n+- `git diff --check` and the staged diff check passed. The ledger remained untracked and was never staged or committed.\\n+- Required-check snapshot: the one pre-mutation snapshot contained 18 terminal contexts: 14 successful, 1 neutral, and 3 skipped; Sonar Quality Gate passed while reporting 38 new issues. No hosted checks were fetched after push.\\n+- Head verification (one comparison only): local head, `origin/codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910`, and PR 170 head all equal `80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1`; the PR remained open.\\n+\\n+## Round 10 convergence\\n+\\n+- Trend: improving but nonterminal. The deferred analyzer inventory is no longer Not Attempted, all three new review roots have coordinated repairs, and no local regression remains; hosted reviewers/analyzers have not yet assessed the new head.\\n+- Valid blocking root causes before / after: 3 new review roots plus 10 valid analyzer subfamilies / 0 deliberately deferred valid code roots, with hosted verification pending a future round.\\n+- New defects: top-level scenario key leakage, parameterized anti-cache directive acceptance, and cleanup-owner loss during structural report collision.\\n+- Recurring families: credential-boundary structural safety and cleanup ownership recurred; both were repaired at their shared producer/consumer boundaries.\\n+- Fix-induced regressions: none found by 371 complete affected-package tests, four typechecks, rebuilt package consumers, whole-batch diff review, or the Node 22 release gate.\\n+- Clean streak: `0` (reset by new/actionable roots, recurring families, this code-changing round, and the changed PR head after the assessment).\\n+- Head stability: the snapshot remained at `cf76637ada4ba0263e36f30c23a278826c48dd0a` during assessment; the single commit and push advanced local, remote, and PR head together to `80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1` in the one allowed comparison.\\n+\\n+## Round 10 termination\\n+\\n+- Result: nonterminal recurring run. A future separately scheduled clean assessment must verify the new head, review dispositions, and analyzer/check state; this code-changing round cannot count toward the clean streak.\\n+- Automation `4442e7f3-60f4-4125-a8e4-c818ac40fc82` remains disabled from the earlier retrieval-discovery stop and was not silently re-enabled during this manual round.\\n+- No post-push review refetch, CI poll, reviewer wait, thread resolution, review dismissal, merge, or second fix loop was performed.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b91a-027b-7173-bd75-a52040008bc7","create_time":1789813226.113671}}}
