ot payload. If a credential\\n+    // collides with one of them, no replayable typed artifact can be emitted.\\n+    for (const key of [\\n+      ...Object.keys(scenario),\\n+      \\\"status\\\",\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4052873779\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 4052880086,\n      \"user\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-19T10:25:56Z\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n      \"line\": 325,\n      \"originalLine\": 325,\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Validate fallback report structure with the target redactor**\\n\\nWhen a custom target fails before reaching `connected`, this early return bypasses `client.preserveArtifactStructure()` and the target-owned redactor. For example, a target whose opaque credential is `incomplete` can fail during `open()`, after which the suite serializes `status: \\\"incomplete\\\"`; the final `redactTargetCredentials()` pass knows only credentials registered by `authenticatedHttpTarget`, so the custom credential remains exposed. Fresh evidence beyond the earlier target-kind issue is this non-connected fallback branch, which skips validation for every fixed report discriminator; validate those structural values while the custom hook is still available or fail the artifact.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4052880086\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 4052884967,\n      \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-19T10:27:34Z\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"originalLine\": 390,\n      \"body\": \"Addressed in 80ba026 by retaining the cleanup owner in `McpFnTargetSuiteArtifactCleanupError` and adding combined collision/retry coverage.\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_