h issue separately.\\n\\n\\n<file name=\\\"mcpfn/inspector/src/index.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"mcpfn/inspector/src/index.ts:243\\\">\\nP2: When a credential equals `status`, `incompleteReason`, or `variables`, complete exports fail even when those optional fields are not emitted. Validate optional structural keys only when the corresponding field is actually added.</violation>\\n</file>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/170/ai_pr_review_github_delivery_7077910b94aa69d2232c9a2206ecafa319e57507329bbf281a6bc27c357e5db8?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F170)</sub>\\n\\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_github_delivery_7077910b94aa69d2232c9a2206ecafa319e57507329bbf281a6bc27c357e5db8:80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1:3f2b0c8e-464a-550e-ac0b-0b595abbdda1 -->\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5255342068\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 5255348648,\n      \"user\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-09-19T10:25:56Z\",\n      \"commitId\": \"80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1\",\n      \"body\": \"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `80ba026172`\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5255348648\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 5255354305,\n      \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-09-19T10:27:34Z\",\n      \"commitId\": \"80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1\",\n      \"body\": \"\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5255354305\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 5255359562,\n      \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-09-19T10:29:21Z\",\n      \"commitId\": \"80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1\",\n      \"body\": \"> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> The suite refactor can bypass cleanup after a target session is already live.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `cf76637a`, covering the behavioral delta in `80ba0261`.\\n\\n- **Preserved structural-collision cleanup** — Added a reportless cleanup-owner error and CLI handling so unsafe artifacts remain omitted while cleanup stays retryable.\\n- **Refactored suite execution** — Extracted diagnostic collection, connected execution, artifact projection, and client close handling.\\n- **Refactored hosted authorization** — Split authorization, token exchange, refresh, and rejection-envelope validation into phase-specific helpers.\\n- **Hardened artifact boundaries** — Preserved inspector schema keys, tightened cache-directive checks, and extracted bounded credential-redaction helpers.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 80ba0261;\\nif commits have landed on codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\\n\\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\\n- Files reviewed: 61\\n- Commits reviewed: 70\\n- Base: dev (2867c68f)\\n- Head: codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910 (80ba0261)\\n- Reviewed commits:\\n  - 80ba0261 — fix(mcpfn): close review and analyzer findings (incremental delta; full PR context reviewed through this commit)\\n- Prior pullfrog review: cf76637a (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5249315211)\\n-->\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [Fix all ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/170?action=fix&review_id=5255359562) ｜ [Fix 👍s ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/170?action=fix-approved&review_id=5255359562) ｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/35437126199/job/105881585044) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5255359562\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"newIssues\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 5741021520,\n      \"user\": \"sonarqubecloud[bot]\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-19T10:23:43Z\",\n      \"body\": \"## [![Quality Gate Passed](https://sonarsource.github.io/sonarcloud-github-static-resources/v2/checks/QualityGateBadge/qg-passed-20px.png 'Quality Gate Passed')](https://sonarcloud.io/dashboard?id=21nCo_super-functions&pullRequest=170) **Quality Gate passed**  \\nIssues  \\n![](https://sonarsource.github.io/sonarcloud-github-static-resources/v2/common/passed-16px.png '') [11 New issues](https://sonarcloud.io/project/issues?id=21nCo_super-functions&pullRequest=170&issueStatuses=OPEN,CONFIRMED&sinceLeakPeriod=true)  \\n![](https://sonarsource.github.io/sonarcloud-github-static-resources/v2/common/accepted-16px.png '') [0 Accepted issues](https://sonarcloud.io/project/issues?id=21nCo_super-functions&pullRequest=170&issueStatuses=ACCEPTED)\\n\\nMeasures  \\n![](https://sonarsource.github.io/sonarcloud-github-static-resources/v2/common/passed-16px.png '') [0 Security Hotspots](https://sonarcloud.io/project/security_hotspots?id=21nCo_super-functions&pullRequest=170&issueStatuses=OPEN,CONFIRMED&sinceLeakPeriod=true)  \\n![](https://sonarsource.github.io/sonarcloud-github-static-resources/v2/common/passed-16px.png '') [0.0% Coverage on New Code](https://sonarcloud.io/component_measures?id=21nCo_super-functions&pullRequest=170&metric=new_coverage&view=list)  \\n![](https://sonarsource.github.io/sonarcloud-github-static-resources/v2/common/passed-16px.png '') [2.7% Duplication on New Code](https://sonarcloud.io/component_measures?id=21nCo_super-functions&pullRequest=170&metric=new_duplicated_lines_density&view=list)  \\n  \\n<!-- sqra-placement-anchor -->\\n[See analysis details on SonarQube Cloud](https://sonarcloud.io/dashboard?id=21nCo_super-functions&pullRequest=170)\\n\\n\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5741021520\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"newInline\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 4052873779,\n      \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-19T10:23:38Z\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/inspector/src/index.ts\",\n      \"line\": 243,\n      \"originalLine\": 243,\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=a052d67b-f905-485e-8b31-06c93082dca8 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=3f2b0c8e-464a-550e-ac0b-0b595abbdda1 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: When a credential equals `status`, `incompleteReason`, or `variables`, complete exports fail even when those optional fields are not emitted. Validate optional structural keys only when the corresponding field is actually added.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/inspector/src/index.ts, line 243:\\n\\n<comment>When a credential equals `status`, `incompleteReason`, or `variables`, complete exports fail even when those optional fields are not emitted. Validate optional structural keys only when the corresponding field is actually added.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -238,6 +238,16 @@ export class McpFnInspector {\\n     const scenario = createMcpFnScenario(name, operation, result);\\n+    // Top-level scenario keys are authored schema, not payload. If a credential\\n+    // collides with one of them, no replayable typed artifact can be emitted.\\n+    for (const key of [\\n+      ...Object.keys(scenario),\\n+      \\\"status\\\",\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4052873779\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 4052880086,\n      \"user\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-19T10:25:56Z\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n      \"line\": 325,\n      \"originalLine\": 325,\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Validate fallback report structure with the target redactor**\\n\\nWhen a custom target fails before reaching `connected`, this early return bypasses `client.preserveArtifactStructure()` and the target-owned redactor. For example, a target whose opaque credential is `incomplete` can fail during `open()`, after which the suite serializes `status: \\\"incomplete\\\"`; the final `redactTargetCredentials()` pass knows only credentials registered by `authenticatedHttpTarget`, so the custom credential remains exposed. Fresh evidence beyond the earlier target-kind issue is this non-connected fallback branch, which skips validation for every fixed report discriminator; validate those structural values while the custom hook is still available or fail the artifact.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4052880086\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 4052884967,\n      \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-19T10:27:34Z\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"originalLine\": 390,\n      \"body\": \"Addressed in 80ba026 by retaining the cleanup owner in `McpFnTargetSuiteArtifactCleanupError` and adding combined collision/retry coverage.\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/35437126199/job/105881585044) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4052884967\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 4052889913,\n      \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-19T10:29:20Z\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n      \"line\": 317,\n      \"originalLine\": 317,\n      \"body\": \"**[P1] Keep fallback projection inside the guarded cleanup path**\\n\\nConstructing `fallback` reads the arbitrary `target.kind` before this function enters its `try`. If that getter/proxy throws after the client has connected, `runTargetSuite()` exits before `closeSuiteClient()` and can leave the transport or credential owner live; guard this read and add a post-open throwing-kind regression.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Preserve cleanup when target metadata access throws\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts:304-317` — `initialTargetDescriptor()` reads `target.kind` while `fallback` is created outside the projection guard.\\n- `mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts:433-435` — projection runs after connection but before the only `closeSuiteClient()` call.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Arbitrary target metadata access must not escape after connection without attempting client cleanup.\\n- A safe incomplete report should be produced when possible, while any failed cleanup remains retryable.\\n````\\n\\n</details>\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4052889913\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9","create_time":1789819942.907422}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
