ews or checks again afterward.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae61e49f0c87d08c35378b0677f657","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1789813214.913956,"turn_id":"01a0b91a-027b-7173-bd75-a52040008bc7"},"phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_gsfQNKJArbrFUPxw3tnWczs8","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae61e52cd487d09e6e410fe94c39bc","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git rev-parse HEAD\\ngit ls-remote origin refs/heads/codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910\\nGH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh pr view 170 --repo 21nCo/super-functions --json headRefOid,headRefName,state,url\\ngit status --short --branch\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":12000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789813214.913956,"turn_id":"01a0b91a-027b-7173-bd75-a52040008bc7"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_gsfQNKJArbrFUPxw3tnWczs8","id":"ctco_01a0b92e-7767-7270-b076-650e9fa0eeb0","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789813225.319943,"turn_id":"01a0b91a-027b-7173-bd75-a52040008bc7"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.8 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1\n80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1\trefs/heads/codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910\n{\"headRefName\":\"codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910\",\"headRefOid\":\"80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1\",\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170\"}\n## codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910...origin/codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910\n?? .conduct/\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae61eb132087d09d1f46b974f32c54","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b91a-027b-7173-bd75-a52040008bc7"},"summary":[{"text":"**Updating ledger with verification and dispositions**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Clarifying disposition counts and automation status**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Updating defect family table and verifying test results**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae61f5d23887d0a24590ae7732fbec","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b91a-027b-7173-bd75-a52040008bc7"},"summary":[{"text":"**Applying patch to codebase**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_BYvbjKKO87x7iItB5rY8LP1S","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae61f6357c87d0bf18a96ce334bbf1","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170/.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md\\n@@\\n-| `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY` | External analyzer inventory contains 36 additional maintainability/reliability findings | Not Attempted (non-gating broad refactor inventory); preserve for reassessment | round 1 | not attempted | None | Round 4 Sonar Quality Gate passed, but its summary increased from 35 to 36 open issues; individual analyzer details were not part of the captured GitHub review surfaces and require a separately coordinated behavior-preserving assessment |\\n+| `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY` | External analyzer inventory contains behavior-preserving maintainability/reliability findings | Assessed and attempted as coordinated subfamilies in round 10; hosted closure pending a later snapshot | round 1 | round 10 | Split 38 reported issues into 34 valid findings across ten contract-aligned repair families and 4 invalid retry-owner findings; the round-10 batch decomposes the valid families without changing external behavior | Round 10 local package suites and release gate passed; no post-push Sonar refetch is permitted this round |\\n@@\\n - Convergence state: not clean. Three new review roots, the recurring cleanup-ownership family, and the now-assessed analyzer families reset the clean streak to `0` even though the snapshot head was stable and required checks were terminal.\\n+\\n+## Round 10 snapshot dispositions\\n+\\n+- Actionable: 4 new unresolved GitHub threads, deduplicated to 3 root causes. `MCP170-SCENARIO-KEY-STRUCTURE`, `MCP170-OAUTH-CACHE-DIRECTIVE-PARAMS`, and `MCP170-STRUCTURAL-COLLISION-CLEANUP-OWNER` are repaired by `80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1`; the threads remain unresolved and were not refetched after push.\\n+- Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale): 87 older unresolved threads retain their prior current-code dispositions. The four round-9 roots are already repaired at the assessed head; outdated status alone was not used as evidence.\\n+- Invalid / Accepted Risk: the older property-key-redaction finding remains invalid based on observed payload-key behavior. The analyzer's retry-owner `throw this` family is invalid because object identity is the ownership token; the suite instance was removed incidentally by a shared retry helper, while the three remaining instances preserve required owner identity. No accepted risks.\\n+- Not Attempted: 0 valid code root causes. The 34 valid Sonar findings were attempted as ten coordinated subfamilies in this batch; their hosted analyzer disposition remains pending until a future separately scheduled snapshot because post-push refetch is forbidden.\\n+- Unassessed: 0 captured threads, review bodies, issue comments, raw inline comments, nested comments, or analyzer findings.\\n+\\n+## Round 10 verification evidence\\n+\\n+- Focused regressions: 28 inspector credential-artifact tests and 145 hosted-authorization/remote-target tests passed after the three review-root repairs. The broader testing/report/suite set passed 189 tests after decomposition, and the CLI reportless-owner regression passed with the target-suite cleanup suite.\\n+- Complete affected package suites: 45 `@mcpfn/client`, 234 `@mcpfn/testing`, 38 `@mcpfn/inspector`, and 54 `@mcpfn/cli` tests passed (371 total).\\n+- Typechecks: `@mcpfn/client`, `@mcpfn/testing`, `@mcpfn/inspector`, and `@mcpfn/cli` passed under Node 22; `@mcpfn/testing` rebuilt successfully before downstream CLI verification.\\n+- Release gate: `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed every reported package test/typecheck/build, Playwright, official conformance, mixed-entry redaction, examples, ESM/CJS imports, dry-run packs, packed-consumer installation, and round trips.\\n+- `git diff --check` and the staged diff check passed. The ledger remained untracked and was never staged or committed.\\n+- Required-check snapshot: the one pre-mutation snapshot contained 18 terminal contexts: 14 successful, 1 neutral, and 3 skipped; Sonar Quality Gate passed while reporting 38 new issues. No hosted checks were fetched after push.\\n+- Head verification (one comparison only): local head, `origin/codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910`, and PR 170 head all equal `80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1`; the PR remained open.\\n+\\n+## Round 10 convergence\\n+\\n+- Trend: improving but nonterminal. The deferred analyzer inventory is no longer Not Attempted, all three new review roots have coordinated repairs, and no local regression remains; hosted reviewers/analyzers have not yet assessed the new head.\\n+- Valid blocking root causes before / after: 3 new review roots plus 10 valid analyzer subfamilies / 0 deliberately deferred valid code roots, with hosted verification pending a future round.\\n+- New defects: top-level scenario key leakage, parameterized anti-cache directive acceptance, and cleanup-owner loss during structural report collision.\\n+- Recurring families: credential-boundary structural safety and cleanup ownership recurred; both were repaired at their shared producer/consumer boundaries.\\n+- Fix-induced regressions: none found by 371 complete affected-package tests, four typechecks, rebuilt package consumers, whole-batch diff review, or the Node 22 release gate.\\n+- Clean streak: `0` (reset by new/actionable roots, recurring families, this code-changing round, and the changed PR head after the assessment).\\n+- Head stability: the snapshot remained at `cf76637ada4ba0263e36f30c23a278826c48dd0a` during assessment; the single commit and push advanced local, remote, and PR head together to `80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1` in the one allowed comparison.\\n+\\n+## Round 10 termination\\n+\\n+- Result: nonterminal recurring run. A future separately scheduled clean assessment must verify the new head, review dispositions, and analyzer/check state; this code-changing round cannot count toward the clean streak.\\n+- Automation `4442e7f3-60f4-4125-a8e4-c818ac40fc82` remains disabled from the earlier retrieval-discovery stop and was not silently re-enabled during this manual round.\\n+- No post-push review refetch, CI poll, reviewer wait, thread resolution, review dismissal, merge, or second fix loop was performed.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789813226.113671,"turn_id":"01a0b91a-027b-7173-bd75-a52040008bc7"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_BYvbjKKO87x7iItB5rY8LP1S","id":"ctco_01a0b92f-0e0f-7573-8c2e-e482f2b33e2f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789813263.887653,"turn_id":"01a0b91a-027b-7173-bd75-a52040008bc7"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.5 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae6211d24487d082beb18d119bae9c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b91a-027b-7173-bd75-a52040008bc7"},"summary":[{"text":"**Verifying git status and memory citations**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Finalizing report buckets and termination sentence**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Including push confirmation and head matching**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"Completed and pushed round 10 as commit `80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1`. Local, remote, and [PR 170](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170) heads match.\n\nResult buckets:\n\n- Actionable: 4 threads → 3 root causes, all repaired.\n- Skipped: 87 older findings retained their existing dispositions.\n- Invalid / Accepted Risk: prior invalid key-redaction finding plus four invalid retry-owner analyzer findings; no accepted risks.\n- Not Attempted: 0 valid code root causes. All 34 valid Sonar findings received coordinated repairs.\n- Unassessed: 0.\n- Verification: 371 affected-package tests, four typechecks, `git diff --check`, and the complete Node 22 release gate passed.\n- Convergence: nonterminal, clean streak `0`. This code-changing round cannot be clean; the next separately scheduled assessment must evaluate the new head.\n- Automation remains disabled and was not silently re-enabled.\n\nOne review round is complete. No post-push refetch or additional review loop was performed.\n\n\u003coai-mem-citation\u003e\n\u003ccitation_entries\u003e\nMEMORY.md:309-347|note=[PR 170 bounded workflow and live verification requirements]\n\u003c/citation_entries\u003e\n\u003crollout_ids\u003e\n01a0a522-f7e4-7422-a0fb-002c30b622cc\n01a0aa3d-a004-7df3-b812-85a576729d2d\n01a0a496-fa30-7f70-ac42-1e7080963f28\n\u003c/rollout_ids\u003e\n\u003c/oai-mem-citation\u003e","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae621a530887d08f93b36373ba377d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1789813264.615866,"turn_id":"01a0b91a-027b-7173-bd75-a52040008bc7"},"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"what's next","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0b992-0a25-7df2-b3b5-c2b48a8c0525","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789819750.949395,"turn_id":"01a0b992-00c3-7a93-91f5-56dd7dab8b34"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7b6cc82087d0ac2864abca8b6e59","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b992-00c3-7a93-91f5-56dd7dab8b34"},"summary":[{"text":"**Clarifying current state and next steps**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Outlining next retrieval and assessment steps**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"Next is a fresh, read-only convergence assessment of head `80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1`.\n\nIt should:\n\n- Retrieve and verify the pinned Skillplane workflow again.\n- Fetch one complete review/check snapshot.\n- Confirm the 3 review roots and 34 valid Sonar findings are cleared.\n- Make no changes or push if clean.\n- Record clean streak `1/2`.\n\nThe automation is currently disabled, so this requires either another manual invocation or explicit authorization to re-enable automation `4442e7f3-60f4-4125-a8e4-c818ac40fc82`.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7b7072f087d0b2295c5bed0c124d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1789819753.597801,"turn_id":"01a0b992-00c3-7a93-91f5-56dd7dab8b34"},"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"proceed","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0b992-a13c-7c10-a938-ada655598277","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789819789.628867,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7b8f706c87d0a7f35e5f1662f898","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"summary":[{"text":"**Planning strict single-round skill use**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Starting commentary and memory search**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"I’m starting the next bounded convergence assessment. I’ll use the hosted Skillplane workflow through the Composio CLI, the 21nCo GitHub account rules for the single PR snapshot, and Orca only if the two-clean-round stopping rule requires changing the automation. This round will stop after one snapshot and one head comparison.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7b931be087d09c644ac930bd82f5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1789819790.478953,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_XA7vsyBJsImND41j04vgQ5P0","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7b94b28c87d0aa6291e6ade059d3","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,260p' /Users/serro/.agents/skills/skillplane/SKILL.md\\nsed -n '1,320p' /Users/serro/.agents/skills/composio-cli/SKILL.md\\nsed -n '1,260p' /Users/serro/.agents/skills/using-21nco-github/SKILL.md\\nsed -n '1,280p' /Users/serro/.agents/skills/orca-cli/SKILL.md\\nrg -n \\\"PR #170|pr-refetch-fix|convergence|automation 4442e7f3|80ba026\\\" /Users/serro/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":50000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789819790.478953,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_XA7vsyBJsImND41j04vgQ5P0","id":"ctco_01a0b992-cda8-75d3-883e-53c9d60aff54","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789819801.000396,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.4 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"---\nname: use-skillplane\ndescription: Use skillplane to resolve skill\n---\n\n# Skillplane\n\nSkillplane is user's hosted skills platform. Retrieve user's skill using the slug or skill name provided and use that to execute the requested task.\n\nNOTE: Always retrieve and read the hosted skill first before working on the task. If the skill is not found, return an error message indicating the skill could not be located.\n\n## Using skillplane\nTry these in this order to communicate with user's Skillplane for skill retrieval, creation, amend etc.\n1. Direct Skillplane MCP if available and authenticated\n2. Direct Skillplane CLI if available and authenticated\n3. Via Composio CLI if available and authenticated\n4. Via Rex CLI if available and authenticated\n\n## Using tools mentioned in skillplane skills\nWhen executing a skill retrieved from Skillplane, use the tools referenced within the skill's definition to complete the task. Example tools: Linear, Notion, etc. Tool/Integrations resolution order:\n1. Direct integrations or MCP if available and authenticated\n2. Via Orca CLI if available and authenticated\n3. Via Composio CLI if available and authenticated\n4. Via Rex CLI if available and authenticated\n---\nname: composio-cli\ndescription: Help users operate the published Composio CLI to find the right tool, connect accounts, inspect schemas, execute tools, subscribe to trigger events with `composio listen`, script workflows with `composio run`, and call authenticated app APIs with `composio proxy`. Use when the user asks how to do something with `composio`, wants to run a known tool slug, needs to discover a slug with `composio search`, fix a missing connection with `composio link`, inspect tool inputs with `--get-schema` or `--dry-run`, troubleshoot top-level CLI flows, or explicitly needs `composio dev` guidance.\n---\n\n\u003c!-- AUTO-GENERATED: edit skills-src/composio-cli/index.ts and rebuild --\u003e\n\u003c!-- release-channel: stable --\u003e\n\n# Composio CLI\n\n## Default Workflow\n\n1. Start with `composio execute \u003cslug\u003e` whenever the slug is known.\n2. If several independent tool calls must happen at once, use `composio execute -p/--parallel` with repeated `\u003cslug\u003e -d \u003cjson\u003e` groups.\n3. If `execute` says the toolkit is not connected, run `composio link \u003ctoolkit\u003e` and retry.\n4. If the arguments are unclear, run `composio execute \u003cslug\u003e --get-schema` or `--dry-run` before guessing.\n5. Reach for `composio search \"\u003ctask\u003e\"` only when the slug is unknown. `search` accepts one or more queries, so batch related discovery work into a single command when useful.\n\n## `execute` - Run A Tool\n\nUse `execute` when the tool slug is already known.\n\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_GET_THE_AUTHENTICATED_USER -d '{}'\n```\n\nInspect required inputs without executing:\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE --get-schema\n```\n\nPreview safely:\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE --skip-connection-check --dry-run -d '{ owner: \"acme\", repo: \"app\", title: \"Bug report\", body: \"Steps to reproduce...\" }'\n```\n\nPass data from a file or stdin:\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE -d @issue.json\ncat issue.json | composio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE -d -\n```\n\nUpload a local file:\n```bash\ncomposio execute SLACK_UPLOAD_OR_CREATE_A_FILE_IN_SLACK \\\n  --file ./image.png \\\n  -d '{ channels: \"C123\" }'\n```\n\nRun independent tool calls in parallel:\n```bash\ncomposio execute --parallel \\\n  GMAIL_SEND_EMAIL -d '{ recipient_email: \"a@b.com\", subject: \"Hi\" }' \\\n  GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE -d '{ owner: \"acme\", repo: \"app\", title: \"Bug\" }'\n```\n\nKey flags:\n- `--get-schema`: Inspect required arguments without executing the tool.\n- `--dry-run`: Preview the request shape without performing the action.\n- `--file`: Inject a local file path into a tool that exposes exactly one uploadable file argument.\n- `--parallel`: Execute multiple independent tool calls in the same invocation.\n- `--account`: Select which connected account to use by alias, word_id, or account id when multiple accounts exist for the same toolkit.\n\n- `--file` only works when the tool exposes a single uploadable file input. Otherwise use explicit `-d` JSON.\n\n## `search` - Find The Slug\n\nUse `search` only when the tool slug is not already known.\n\n```bash\ncomposio search \"create a github issue\"\ncomposio search \"send an email\" --toolkits gmail\ncomposio search \"send an email\" \"create a github issue\"\ncomposio search \"my emails\" \"my github issues\" --toolkits gmail,github\n```\n\n- Batch related discovery work into one `search` invocation, then move back to `execute` once the correct slugs are known.\n\n## `link` - Connect An Account\n\nUse `link` when `execute` reports that a toolkit is not connected, or when the user explicitly wants to authorize an account.\n\n```bash\ncomposio link gmail\ncomposio link googlecalendar --no-browser\n```\n\nKey flags:\n- `--alias`: Assign an alias to the connected account. Required when creating an additional account for the same toolkit.\n\n- Retry the original `execute` command after linking succeeds.\n\n## `proxy` - Raw API Access\n\nUse `proxy` when a toolkit supports a raw API operation that is easier than finding a dedicated tool slug.\n\n```bash\ncomposio proxy https://api.github.com/user --toolkit github --account work --method GET \u003c/dev/null\n```\n\nKey flags:\n- `--account`: Select which connected account to use by alias, word_id, or account id.\n\n## `run` - Scripting, LLMs, and Programmatic Workflows\n\nFor programmatic calls, loops, output plumbing, or anything beyond a single tool call, prefer `composio run`.\n\n`composio run` executes an inline ESM JavaScript/TypeScript snippet with authenticated `execute()`, `search()`, `proxy()`, and the experimental `experimental_subAgent()` helper pre-injected. No SDK setup required.\n\nChain multiple tools:\n```bash\ncomposio run '\n  const me = await execute(\"GITHUB_GET_THE_AUTHENTICATED_USER\");\n  const emails = await execute(\"GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS\", { max_results: 1 });\n  console.log({ login: me.data.login, fetchedEmails: !!emails.data });\n'\n```\n\nFan out with Promise.all:\n```bash\ncomposio run '\n  const [me, emails] = await Promise.all([\n    execute(\"GITHUB_GET_THE_AUTHENTICATED_USER\"),\n    execute(\"GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS\", { max_results: 5 }),\n  ]);\n  console.log({ login: me.data.login, emailCount: emails.data.messages?.length });\n'\n```\n\nFeed tool output into an LLM and get structured JSON back:\n```bash\ncomposio run --logs-off '\n  const emails = await execute(\"GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS\", { max_results: 5 });\n  const brief = await experimental_subAgent(\n    `Summarize these emails and count them.\\n\\n${emails.prompt()}`,\n    { schema: z.object({ summary: z.string(), count: z.number() }) }\n  );\n  console.log(brief.structuredOutput);\n'\n```\n\n- Use top-level `execute --parallel` instead when the user only needs a few independent tool calls and does not need script logic.\n\n## Auth\n\n```bash\ncomposio whoami   # check current session\ncomposio login    # authenticate if whoami fails\n```\n\n## Escalate Only When Needed\n\nIf the user is stuck on top-level commands or needs fallback inspection commands, load [references/troubleshooting.md](references/troubleshooting.md).\n\nIf the user explicitly asks about developer projects, auth configs, connected accounts, triggers, logs, orgs, or projects, load [references/composio-dev.md](references/composio-dev.md). `composio dev` is not the default end-user path.\n---\nname: using-21nco-github\ndescription: Uses the thyaravind GitHub account for repositories under dev/n or with a 21nCo origin. Use for any GitHub CLI, pull request, issue, release, or repository operation in those repositories.\n---\n\n# Using 21nCo GitHub\n\nFor any repository whose path is under `dev/n` or whose Git remote belongs to `21nCo`:\n\n- Run every `gh` command with `GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other`.\n- Verify `GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other gh auth status` reports `thyaravind` as the active account before making changes.\n- Never use the default GitHub account or silently fall back to another account.\n- Use the existing `21nCo` remote for pushes. If `thyaravind` lacks permission, stop and report the denial instead of creating a fork or alternate remote.\n---\nname: orca-cli\ndescription: \u003e-\n  Operate Orca-managed worktrees, folder contexts, terminals, repos, automations, artifacts,\n  skill sharing, worktree comments, and Orca's embedded browser through the `orca` CLI. Use\n  when the user says \"$orca-cli\", \"Orca worktree\", \"child worktree\", \"spawn codex/claude in a\n  worktree\", \"read/wait/send Orca terminal\", \"handoff\" / \"handover\" / \"give this to another\n  agent\", \"Orca browser\", \"orca artifacts\", or \"share skills\". Prefer it over raw git\n  worktree, ad hoc PTYs, or Computer Use when Orca state is involved. Use Computer Use only\n  for external windows or desktop UI that needs OS-level control, and Playwright or CDP for\n  external pages.\n---\n\n# Orca CLI\n\nThis discovery stub loads the version-matched guide from the Orca executable used for this session.\n\n## Resolve the CLI for this session\n\nChoose the executable once and reuse it for every later command:\n\n- If the `ORCA_CLI_COMMAND` environment variable is set, use its value. Orca exports this\n  for managed WSL sessions.\n- Otherwise, in a dev checkout whose session exposes `ORCA_DEV_REPO_ROOT`, use `orca-dev`.\n- Otherwise, on Linux outside an Orca-managed terminal, use `orca-ide`. Never run bare\n  `orca` there — outside Orca's terminals it normally resolves to the\n  GNOME Orca screen reader (`/usr/bin/orca`) and starts speech on the user's machine.\n- Otherwise, use `orca`.\n\nBelow, `ORCA` is a placeholder for the executable you resolved. Substitute it before\nrunning anything; do not create a shell variable or run `ORCA` literally. This works the\nsame way in POSIX shells, PowerShell, and cmd.exe.\n\nIf the selected executable cannot run, report its exact error and stop. Do not fall through\nto another executable, which could silently target a different Orca build.\n\n## Load the version-matched guide before running Orca commands\n\n```text\nORCA skills get orca-cli\n```\n\nPrefer `--json`. Use the selected executable's `--help` for commands or flags the guide does\nnot cover. If a command reports that Orca is not running, start it with `ORCA open --json`\nand retry. If `skills get` is unknown, explain that updating Orca restores the guide; use\n`--help` for read-only discovery and do not guess unsupported commands.\n68:- git worktree list --porcelain, gh pr list, GH_CONFIG_DIR, 21nCo/super-functions, 21nCo/superfunctions, docs/http-decode-params, sfns-4-rex-upstream, prunable-worktree, PR #188, PR #179, PR #170\n78:- At the September 17 snapshot, `superfunctions-dev`/`docs/http-decode-params` matched clean PR #188; SFNS-4/`sfns-4-rex-upstream` matched dirty PR #179; `/private/tmp/pr170-refetch-fix.h2yq4m` was missing and prunable, associated with PR #170. [Task 1]\n221:- SFNS-4, PR #179, pr-refetch-fix, reviewThreads, adapterNamespace, Retry-After, tenantId, SecFn readJson, e200f50d, 511c02a\n309:# Task Group: September 15 Superfunctions PR #170 bounded remediation and dirty-dev reconciliation\n310:scope: Use for live hosted `pr-refetch-fix` work on McpFn PR #170, or scoped publication/reconciliation from a dirty, stale Superfunctions dev checkout.\n313:## Task 1: Harden PR #170 redaction/export invariants in a bounded hosted round, success\n323:- PR #170, pr-refetch-fix, reviewThreads, GH_CONFIG_DIR, gate:mcpfn-release, McpFnRemoteCredentialLease, cleanupPhase, redaction, 8b23aaa, 1e45b794\n337:- when the user invokes `use-skillplane PR #170 pr-refetch-fix` -\u003e retrieve the exact live hosted workflow; make one snapshot/fix/verify/commit/push pass, verify the required head once, then stop without refetching reviews, polling CI, or merging. [Task 1]\n343:- Use `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other` for GitHub commands. Page every GraphQL `reviewThreads` cursor: PR #170’s first 100-thread result had `hasNextPage: true`; only a three-page, 284-thread snapshot was complete. [Task 1]\n605:- PR #23, reviewThreads(first:100), GH_CONFIG_DIR, pr-refetch-fix, projections, SQLite writer lock, SkillEditor, CompositionPanel, SonarQube, 7715373, 83058246\n778:- splane, PR #174, PR #177, SFNS-3, OAuth invalid_grant, Composio CLI, 21n/pr-quality-analysis@1.0.0, pr-refetch-fix, gate:reviewfn-release, package-lock, d4de3791\n1043:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-10T14-20-26-2rMD-mcp1_transport_neutral_conformance_pr_170.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/10/rollout-2026-09-10T19-50-26-01a08bb0-f9fe-7951-aed1-965679939fc3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-10T15:17:36+00:00, thread_id=01a08bb0-f9fe-7951-aed1-965679939fc3, PR #170 local release gate passed; hosted CI queued)\n1544:# Task Group: September 8-15 Superfunctions PR quality, issue-grounded review, and PR #170 convergence\n1545:scope: Use for broad read-only Superfunctions PR review, comparative findings/quality reporting, follow-up assessment, and root-cause remediation convergence across DataFn/UIFN/McpFn.\n1548:## Task 1: Review requested live Superfunctions PRs and diagnose remediation convergence, partial\n1552:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-07T09-15-30-XKOk-pr_review_remediation_convergence_and_skill_amendment.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T14-45-31-01a07b26-bb2c-7b32-95a4-8fb6b484fad0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T07:43:24+00:00, thread_id=01a07b26-bb2c-7b32-95a4-8fb6b484fad0, complete comparative report was not delivered; PR #170 symptom-patching convergence failure documented)\n1556:- GH_CONFIG_DIR, gh pr list, PR #144, PR #145, PR #149, PR #150, PR #151, PR #152, PR #153, PR #155, PR #170, reviewThreads, Sonar, convergence, root-cause\n1568:## Task 3: Evaluate PR #170 and all subsequent fixes, partial\n1576:- PR #170, MCP-1, transport-neutral conformance, aa08ef72e, reviewThreads(first:100), isOutdated, JUnit, --visible-tools, redaction, ESM/CJS, GH_CONFIG_DIR\n1581:- when the user asks to evaluate “PR #170 and all subsequent PR fixes” -\u003e assess both history and exact current head, enumerate all commits/review surfaces/checks, and finish the requested verdict before pursuing unrelated PR material. [Task 3]\n1582:- when remediation repeatedly finds adjacent variants, the user asked to “strive for convergence and broader look” -\u003e reset to the shared invariant/subsystem rather than publish another one-example symptom patch. [Task 1]\n1592:- For PR #170, paginate `pullRequest.reviewThreads(first:100,after:$endCursor)` and separate `isOutdated` from current unresolved threads; snapshot base/head OIDs, commits, local exact-head source, and hosted checks independently. The captured head `aa08ef72e` was open/mergeable but `UNSTABLE`, with 34 current unresolved threads and 10 pending checks; do not call it merge-ready from focused tests or resolved threads. [Task 3]\n2037:- splane, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1, PR #133, DocsFn, GH_CONFIG_DIR, release-gate, OAuth, authorization-server issuer, @next/swc-darwin-arm64, SvelteKit\n2053:- for `pr-refetch-fix` -\u003e perform one snapshot/fix/verify/commit/push round; do not refetch reviews or poll CI afterward. [Task 1]\n2103:- splane, pr-refetch-fix, PR #139, applyOmit, applyOmitToArrayValue, nested arrays, userId, datafn/server/src/execution/query/select.ts, ff833823\n2127:- when the user invokes `splane` -\u003e resolve the exact hosted Skillplane workflow live; this rollout used `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1` rather than local instructions. [Task 1]\n2204:- splane, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1, PR #569, OAuth refresh credentials, authorization server issuer, codex mcp logout skillplane, codex mcp login skillplane, sslmode, sslrootcert, resolveClientIp, 400ee32b\n2224:- 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1, PR #569, reviewThreads, 49d13ae6, merge-async, gh-other, 9971f77, SonarCloud, CircleCI, Vercel\n2236:- A `pr-refetch-fix` invocation is one review snapshot, narrow fixes, proportionate verification, at most one commit/push, and one head comparison; preserve a divergent local PR branch under a backup ref and use a clean exact-head worktree. PR #569 fixed duplicate `sslmode`/`sslrootcert` values with `URL.searchParams.getAll(...)`, and supplied Node AuthFn `resolveClientIp` preferring `cf-connecting-ip`, then first `x-forwarded-for`. [Task 1]\n2269:- splane pr refetch fix, PR #570, reviewThreads, GraphQL, df11df18, merge-async, direct_merge, f849c684, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1\n2359:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-29T14-45-30-EDVy-ski_13_multi_region_review_fixes.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/29/rollout-2026-08-29T20-15-30-01a04dfb-9d6e-7000-a3ce-3006e2ed565c.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-01T15:20:17+00:00, thread_id=01a04dfb-9d6e-7000-a3ce-3006e2ed565c, 31 intended files pushed once; full integration retained unrelated attribution failures and PR-head convergence was unverified)\n2393:- Full integration retained two caller-attribution expectation failures (`Authenticated OAuth client`/`unknown` versus `Codex`/`gpt-5.6`); treat them as outside the SKI-13 delta unless another fix round is authorized. After pushing, local/remote matched `a52f368` but the immediate PR API still showed `cbac7dd`; do not claim PR-head convergence without a permitted later check. [Task 1]\n2529:- splane pr-review-fix, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1, PR #567, PR #568, 69723719, 9c576dc, 41e1efbb, reviewThreads, legacy-product-keys, svelte-check\n3333:- splane pr-review-fix, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1, PR #3, SKI-1, d398cba6, reviewThreads, outdated, repeatable-read, applicationCommit\n3364:- `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1` uses unresolved GraphQL threads plus review bodies, issue comments, and inline comments as one snapshot; after an authorized push, verify heads once and do not refetch/poll. An unresolved thread can be historical: inspect `outdated`, current code/commit, and addressed markers. [Task 1]\n3425:- PR #116, SFNS-2, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1, reviewThreads, nodeType, undefined versus null, authfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt, MCPFn, UIFn, d27cceb2\n4094:- Green package build/typecheck/test/pack gates are not release proof when browser, IME, clipboard, accessibility, SSR/hydration, corpus, fuzzing, convergence, and migration matrices are absent. [Task 2]\n4519:- when the user invokes `pr-refetch-fix`, check unresolved GraphQL review threads first, then review bodies, issue comments, and inline comments; do not filter by timestamps only. [Task 3]\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7b9afb8c87d0a4611f0f94e809b5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"summary":[{"text":"**Planning skill retrieval via Composio**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7b9cd1d487d0a75f1f782f365e56","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"summary":[{"text":"**Planning skill retrieval and search**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"The Skillplane resolver requires live retrieval before any repository action. I’m resolving the exact published revision through Composio now; if the version, revision, or digest drifts, I’ll stop without touching the worktree.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7b9ebbf887d084bddb34f005f642","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1789819801.671706,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_e2kSElVJv48WPeJPhppT4Qo4","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7b9f738c87d0a7462a430c6c8a32","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"composio search \\\"Skillplane retrieve a hosted skill by slug semantic version revision digest\\\" --toolkits skillplane\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":20000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789819801.671706,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_e2kSElVJv48WPeJPhppT4Qo4","id":"ctco_01a0b992-fe76-7902-a99a-29876569721e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789819813.494596,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.6 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"💥  effects/ToolRouterSessionCreateError  • Failed to create a Tool Router session.\nCaused by: 400 {\"error\":{\"message\":\"Invalid toolkit slugs: skillplane. Please provide valid toolkit slugs.\",\"code\":4305,\"slug\":\"ToolRouterV2_InvalidToolkitSlugs\",\"status\":400,\"request_id\":\"3bd29926-00ac-4fba-b9e7-34d642122a4f\",\"suggested_fix\":\"\"}} \r\n\r\n◯\r\n╰─ composio-cli\r\n   ~ 1622ms\r\n     name: @composio/cli\r\n     filename: src/bin.ts\n\nUSAGE\n  composio search \u003cquery...\u003e [--toolkits text] [--limit integer] [--human]\n\nDESCRIPTION\n  Find tools by use case. Defaults to JSON output; use --human for formatted output.\n\nARGUMENTS\n  \u003cquery...\u003e              One or more semantic use-case queries (e.g. \"send an email\", \"create github issue\")\n\nOPTIONS\n  --toolkits \u003ctext\u003e       Filter by toolkit slugs, comma-separated\n  --limit \u003cinteger\u003e       Maximum number of results (1-1000)\n  --human                 Show formatted human-readable search output\n\nEXAMPLES\n  # Find tools for a use case\n  composio search \"send an email\"\n  composio search \"send an email\" \"create github issue\"\n  composio search \"my emails\" \"my github issues\" --toolkits gmail,github\n  composio search \"create issue\" --toolkits github\n  composio search \"send an email\" --human\n  \n  # Cross-app workflow discovery\n  composio search \"post a message to a slack channel\"\n  composio search \"add a row to google sheet\"\n  \n  # Narrow results to a specific toolkit\n  composio search \"list calendar events\" --toolkits google_calendar --limit 5\n\nSEE ALSO\n  composio execute \u003cslug\u003e -d '{ ... }'    Run a tool from the results\n  composio tools info \u003cslug\u003e               Inspect a tool's full schema\n  composio link \u003ctoolkit\u003e                  Connect an account if execute tells you to\n\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7ba9010087d0a9c6ac6ae85df8c1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_pcro4EPZ8v9fu13Gv28s9fQr","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7ba97f2887d0aeb699ecaa1bd271","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"composio search \\\"Skillplane retrieve a hosted skill by slug semantic version revision digest\\\" --limit 10\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":20000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789819814.257111,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_pcro4EPZ8v9fu13Gv28s9fQr","id":"ctco_01a0b993-24e4-7222-a5b1-274d7098c2ad","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789819823.332572,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.6 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"index\": 1,\n      \"use_case\": \"Skillplane retrieve a hosted skill by slug semantic version revision digest\",\n      \"execution_guidance\": \"Found 5 tools for this query. Look at the schemas to know how to use them.\",\n      \"primary_tool_slugs\": [\n        \"CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILL_RETRIEVE\",\n        \"CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILL_ASSET_RETRIEVE\",\n        \"CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILL_VERSIONS_DIFF\",\n        \"CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILLS_SEARCH\",\n        \"CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILL_CREATE\"\n      ],\n      \"related_tool_slugs\": [],\n      \"toolkits\": [\n        \"custom_skillplane\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tool_schemas\": {\n    \"primary\": {\n      \"CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILL_RETRIEVE\": \"~/.composio/tool_definitions/CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILL_RETRIEVE.json\",\n      \"CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILL_ASSET_RETRIEVE\": \"~/.composio/tool_definitions/CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILL_ASSET_RETRIEVE.json\",\n      \"CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILL_VERSIONS_DIFF\": \"~/.composio/tool_definitions/CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILL_VERSIONS_DIFF.json\",\n      \"CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILLS_SEARCH\": \"~/.composio/tool_definitions/CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILLS_SEARCH.json\",\n      \"CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILL_CREATE\": \"~/.composio/tool_definitions/CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILL_CREATE.json\"\n    },\n    \"related_tools_path_format\": \"~/.composio/tool_definitions/\u003cTOOL_SLUG\u003e.json\"\n  },\n  \"connected_toolkits\": [\n    \"custom_skillplane\"\n  ],\n  \"next_steps\": {\n    \"guidance\": \"You can directly proceed with these steps without waiting for the user to ask. Link accounts first if needed, then execute tools.\",\n    \"steps\": [\n      {\n        \"action\": \"Link a user account\",\n        \"command\": \"composio link custom_skillplane\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"action\": \"Execute a tool\",\n        \"command\": \"composio execute \\\"CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILL_RETRIEVE\\\" -d '{\\\"skill\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"caller\\\":{},\\\"context\\\":{},\\\"version\\\":{\\\"selector\\\":\\\"current\\\"}}'\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7bb22aac87d09f34dbeaae67b87e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"summary":[{"text":"**Requesting schema with get-schema**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_T5WZoEzi3Shwihkh26PZ0vUD","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7bb2ce4087d089d716e16110fd70","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"composio execute CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILL_RETRIEVE --get-schema\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":30000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789819823.945818,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_T5WZoEzi3Shwihkh26PZ0vUD","id":"ctco_01a0b993-5c83-7d61-8981-95c99813d8b4","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789819837.571326,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 9.7 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\n  \"slug\": \"CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILL_RETRIEVE\",\n  \"version\": null,\n  \"schemaPath\": \"/Users/serro/.composio/tool_definitions/CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILL_RETRIEVE.json\",\n  \"inputSchema\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n    \"required\": [\n      \"skill\",\n      \"caller\"\n    ],\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"skill\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"required\": [\n              \"id\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"id\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\",\n                \"maxLength\": 200,\n                \"minLength\": 1\n              }\n            },\n            \"additionalProperties\": false\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"required\": [\n              \"workspaceSlug\",\n              \"skillSlug\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"skillSlug\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\",\n                \"pattern\": \"^[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$\",\n                \"maxLength\": 120,\n                \"minLength\": 1\n              },\n              \"workspaceSlug\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\",\n                \"pattern\": \"^[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$\",\n                \"maxLength\": 120,\n                \"minLength\": 1\n              }\n            },\n            \"additionalProperties\": false\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"caller\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\n          \"agentId\",\n          \"agentName\",\n          \"modelProvider\",\n          \"modelName\",\n          \"modelVersion\",\n          \"clientName\",\n          \"clientVersion\",\n          \"runId\",\n          \"sessionId\",\n          \"conversationId\"\n        ],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"runId\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"maxLength\": 200,\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          },\n          \"agentId\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"maxLength\": 160,\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          },\n          \"agentName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"maxLength\": 120,\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          },\n          \"modelName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"maxLength\": 160,\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          },\n          \"sessionId\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"maxLength\": 200,\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          },\n          \"clientName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"maxLength\": 160,\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          },\n          \"modelVersion\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"maxLength\": 120,\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          },\n          \"clientVersion\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"maxLength\": 120,\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          },\n          \"modelProvider\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"maxLength\": 120,\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          },\n          \"conversationId\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"maxLength\": 200,\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          }\n        },\n        \"additionalProperties\": false\n      },\n      \"context\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\n          \"selector\"\n        ],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"selector\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"id\"\n                ],\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"id\": {\n                    \"type\": \"string\",\n                    \"maxLength\": 200,\n                    \"minLength\": 1\n                  }\n                },\n                \"additionalProperties\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"slug\"\n                ],\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"slug\": {\n                    \"type\": \"string\",\n                    \"pattern\": \"^[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$\",\n                    \"maxLength\": 120,\n                    \"minLength\": 1\n                  }\n                },\n                \"additionalProperties\": false\n              }\n            ]\n          },\n          \"knowledge\": {\n            \"oneOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"selector\"\n                ],\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"selector\": {\n                    \"type\": \"string\",\n                    \"const\": \"current\"\n                  }\n                },\n                \"additionalProperties\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"selector\",\n                  \"revisionId\"\n                ],\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"selector\": {\n                    \"type\": \"string\",\n                    \"const\": \"revisionId\"\n                  },\n                  \"revisionId\": {\n                    \"type\": \"string\",\n                    \"maxLength\": 200,\n                    \"minLength\": 1\n                  }\n                },\n                \"additionalProperties\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"selector\",\n                  \"revision\"\n                ],\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"revision\": {\n                    \"type\": \"integer\",\n                    \"maximum\": 9007199254740991,\n                    \"exclusiveMinimum\": 0\n                  },\n                  \"selector\": {\n                    \"type\": \"string\",\n                    \"const\": \"revision\"\n                  }\n                },\n                \"additionalProperties\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"default\": {\n              \"selector\": \"current\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"includeNotes\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\",\n            \"default\": false\n          }\n        },\n        \"additionalProperties\": false\n      },\n      \"version\": {\n        \"oneOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"required\": [\n              \"selector\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"selector\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\",\n                \"const\": \"current\"\n              }\n            },\n            \"additionalProperties\": false\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"required\": [\n              \"selector\",\n              \"versionId\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"selector\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\",\n                \"const\": \"versionId\"\n              },\n              \"versionId\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\",\n                \"maxLength\": 200,\n                \"minLength\": 1\n              }\n            },\n            \"additionalProperties\": false\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"required\": [\n              \"selector\",\n              \"semanticVersion\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"selector\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\",\n                \"const\": \"semanticVersion\"\n              },\n              \"semanticVersion\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\",\n                \"pattern\": \"^(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)(?:-[0-9A-Za-z.-]+)?(?:\\\\+[0-9A-Za-z.-]+)?$\",\n                \"maxLength\": 160,\n                \"minLength\": 1\n              }\n            },\n            \"additionalProperties\": false\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"required\": [\n              \"selector\",\n              \"revision\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"revision\": {\n                \"type\": \"integer\",\n                \"maximum\": 9007199254740991,\n                \"exclusiveMinimum\": 0\n              },\n              \"selector\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\",\n                \"const\": \"revision\"\n              }\n            },\n            \"additionalProperties\": false\n          }\n        ],\n        \"default\": {\n          \"selector\": \"current\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"additionalProperties\": false\n  }\n}\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7bc225d087d0b4b1dac3879d5c17","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"summary":[{"text":"**Planning execution with unique run IDs**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_jLiFO4HCDc0mTPTnPYQvs1RY","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7bc42b1887d0a360ca0f0415aa02","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"composio execute CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILL_RETRIEVE -d '{\\\"skill\\\":{\\\"workspaceSlug\\\":\\\"21n\\\",\\\"skillSlug\\\":\\\"pr-refetch-fix\\\"},\\\"version\\\":{\\\"selector\\\":\\\"semanticVersion\\\",\\\"semanticVersion\\\":\\\"1.2.0\\\"},\\\"caller\\\":{\\\"agentId\\\":\\\"codex-root\\\",\\\"agentName\\\":\\\"Codex\\\",\\\"modelProvider\\\":\\\"OpenAI\\\",\\\"modelName\\\":\\\"GPT-5\\\",\\\"modelVersion\\\":\\\"2026-09-19\\\",\\\"clientName\\\":\\\"Codex Desktop\\\",\\\"clientVersion\\\":\\\"1\\\",\\\"runId\\\":\\\"pr170-round11-20260919\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"pr170-convergence\\\",\\\"conversationId\\\":\\\"pr170-convergence\\\"}}'\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170\",\"yield_time_ms\":30000,\"max_output_tokens\":50000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789819838.394949,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_jLiFO4HCDc0mTPTnPYQvs1RY","id":"ctco_01a0b993-bcb3-7e50-a68d-f9c28d4dfd2e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789819862.195453,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 14.9 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\n  \"successful\": true,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"context\": null,\n    \"files\": [\n      {\n        \"byteSize\": 17699,\n        \"mediaType\": \"text/markdown; charset=utf-8\",\n        \"path\": \"SKILL.md\",\n        \"sha256\": \"735dafee62d04e1be09123929a0a325972ca4312e1072fd55f4c9ca35e3002c8\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"byteSize\": 655,\n        \"mediaType\": \"application/json\",\n        \"path\": \"skill.json\",\n        \"sha256\": \"615c75037c206c8414bf58724fa02c777e91c9e9d8b10f8642a4f7509f5156a8\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"instructions\": \"---\\nname: pr-refetch-fix\\ndescription: \\\"Run exactly one bounded GitHub PR review-remediation pass: fetch all pending review surfaces, validate findings against the exact PR worktree, fix current valid issues, verify, push one reviewed fix commit to the PR, report, and stop without any post-push refetch, CI wait, or reviewer loop.\\\"\\n---\\n\\n# PR Refetch Fix\\n\\nRefetch the current GitHub pull-request review queue, fix the findings that remain valid against the exact PR worktree, verify the affected code, push the fixes to the PR once, report, and stop.\\n\\n## Absolute single-round boundary\\n\\nThis skill performs exactly one bounded round per invocation. The bound limits feedback collection and publication, not the completeness of analysis. One round does not mean one comment, one example, or one file. Related defects belong to one complete repair of their shared contract.\\n\\nOne round is:\\n\\n1. identify the PR, authentication context, exact head branch, and dedicated worktree\\n2. fetch the current review surfaces once\\n3. classify the fetched findings against the current worktree\\n4. trace each valid root cause across affected paths and fix the complete scoped behavior\\n5. run proportionate local verification\\n6. when fixes were made, create one reviewed commit and push it to the PR head branch\\n7. report the result and stop\\n\\nAfter step 7, the invocation is complete.\\n\\nDo not:\\n\\n- refetch review feedback after the push\\n- wait for reviewers or bots to analyze the new commit\\n- poll CI until completion\\n- begin another fetch/fix/test/push cycle\\n- keep working because new feedback arrives asynchronously\\n- interpret \\\"latest\\\", \\\"complete\\\", or \\\"fix pending findings\\\" as permission for an open-ended loop\\n\\nA second round requires a new, explicit user invocation or previously granted recurring authorization. Recurring authorization does not waive the convergence safeguards below. If CI or reviewer checks are still running, report them as pending and stop. If no actionable findings are present, report that and stop. If the round is blocked, report the blocker and stop rather than monitoring for a state change.\\n\\n## Convergence across repeated runs\\n\\nBefore selecting work, read the prior remediation ledger for this PR. Record the hosted skill identity, version and digest actually used. For recurring workflows, pin the reviewed hosted version in the workflow configuration when authorized; compare local copies with that version and report drift. Do not silently substitute a weaker local copy. A deliberate version upgrade must be recorded. Amending this skill alone does not update running automations.\\n\\nKeep a compact, persistent task handoff for recurring work; reuse an existing artifact rather than creating one per round. For a single invocation, task context is sufficient. Track snapshot/head SHAs, stable defect-family identifiers, deduplicated valid defects, affected contracts, first-seen and last-attempted rounds, attempted repairs, introduced regressions, dispositions and behavioral evidence. Preserve deferred findings across runs. If history is unavailable, mark the trend unknown and inspect available review/commit history; never infer convergence from missing data.\\n\\nUse these default reset triggers unless the user explicitly chooses different thresholds:\\n\\n- The same defect family reappears after two remediation rounds, including newly exposed sibling variants.\\n- The number of remaining valid blocking root causes fails to decrease across three consecutive assessed rounds.\\n- The user requests convergence, a broader assessment, or a stop to symptom patching: perform the broader assessment immediately rather than waiting for a numeric trigger.\\n\\nCount root causes, not comments. Do not reset counters by renaming a family, resolving duplicate threads, accepting risk, or narrowing the reported scope. These thresholds trigger reassessment; they are never merge or risk-acceptance thresholds.\\n\\nWhen triggered, stop routine incremental patch selection. Reassess the affected subsystem against the linked issue and relevant architecture, define the shared invariant, map producers/consumers and failure boundaries, and select a coordinated repair. Continue authorized analysis and implementation; this is not an automatic permission request or an excuse to stop working. If the assessment cannot establish a complete repair, report the unresolved design question or external dependency and do not publish another symptom patch as a completed fix.\\n\\nFor recurring automation, suspend routine mutation runs when the reset triggers and switch to this assessment. If authorized scheduler controls are available, persist that mode or pause the mutation schedule; otherwise record the reset-required state in the handoff and notify the user. Do not claim the scheduler is paused without confirmation. Resume routine remediation only after recording the revised contract, coordinated plan and verification criteria. Never automatically resume an automation explicitly paused by the user.\\n\\nDo not continually displace older blockers with the newest bot comment. Related pending findings must be handled together or explicitly leave that contract incomplete. Deferrals require a concrete reason and a next action; convenience, cadence and a desired small commit are not sufficient reasons to split a necessary repair.\\n\\n## Core review rule\\n\\nUse current unresolved review threads as the primary queue. Timestamp filtering is secondary.\\n\\nThe workflow must prevent these failure modes:\\n\\n- querying only inline comments after a guessed cutoff\\n- missing findings in review threads, review bodies, or issue comments\\n- ignoring an older unresolved thread that is still valid on the current head\\n- treating every unresolved bot comment as valid without inspecting current code\\n- fixing against the wrong branch or worktree\\n- starting an unbounded post-push review loop\\n\\n## 1. Identify the PR and authentication context\\n\\nPreserve the user's established GitHub authentication context for every GitHub command, for example:\\n\\n```bash\\nGH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other\\n```\\n\\nResolve the repository and PR number from the current branch, worktree, supplied PR URL, or explicit user input.\\n\\n## 2. Use only the PR's corresponding worktree\\n\\nBefore fetching comments or editing code:\\n\\n1. locate the PR's dedicated worktree\\n2. confirm its checked-out branch equals the PR head branch\\n3. inspect its existing tracked, staged, unstaged, and untracked state\\n4. preserve unrelated work and artifacts\\n\\nMinimum checks:\\n\\n```bash\\ngit branch --show-current\\ngit status --short\\ngit remote -v\\n```\\n\\nTreat that exact worktree as the source of truth for code, validation, staging, and commit decisions. Do not validate comments against a main checkout, base branch, sibling branch, or another PR's worktree.\\n\\nIf multiple PRs are requested, each PR is a separate round unless the user explicitly defines one bounded multi-PR round.\\n\\n## 3. Fetch the current review surfaces once\\n\\nStart with paginated GraphQL review threads. Fetch every page when more than 100 threads may exist.\\n\\n```bash\\nGH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other gh api graphql --paginate -f query='\\nquery($endCursor: String) {\\n  repository(owner: \\\"OWNER\\\", name: \\\"REPO\\\") {\\n    pullRequest(number: PR_NUMBER) {\\n      reviewThreads(first: 100, after: $endCursor) {\\n        nodes {\\n          id\\n          isResolved\\n          path\\n          comments(first: 20) {\\n            nodes {\\n              body\\n              author { login }\\n              createdAt\\n              outdated\\n              url\\n              diffHunk\\n              originalLine\\n              line\\n            }\\n            pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }\\n          }\\n        }\\n        pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n}'\\n```\\n\\nCheck every returned `pageInfo`, including nested comment connections. Do not assume `--paginate` traversed a nested GraphQL connection: explicitly follow its cursor if necessary. Complete every required connection. Record the head SHA and ensure it stays unchanged throughout collection; if it changes, discard the inconsistent snapshot and re-establish the exact head before editing.\\n\\nThen inspect the supplementary surfaces once:\\n\\n1. PR review bodies\\n2. PR issue comments\\n3. raw inline review comments when needed for metadata or export\\n\\n```bash\\nGH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other gh pr view PR_NUMBER --repo OWNER/REPO --json headRefOid,reviews,comments,updatedAt,url\\n```\\n\\n```bash\\nGH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other gh api --paginate repos/OWNER/REPO/pulls/PR_NUMBER/comments\\n```\\n\\nDo not replace unresolved-thread discovery with only `gh pr view --json comments`, only `pulls/\u003cn\u003e/comments`, or only a timestamp query.\\n\\n## 4. Use timestamps only as a secondary lens\\n\\nIf the user explicitly asks for findings since a push:\\n\\n1. resolve the exact pushed commit SHA\\n2. read its absolute UTC timestamp\\n3. use that timestamp only to describe which feedback arrived later\\n\\nStill include an older unresolved thread when it remains actionable on the current head.\\n\\n## 5. Classify root causes before editing\\n\\nKeep a compact working ledger keyed by root cause: thread IDs/URLs, snapshot SHA, affected paths, current-code evidence, status, and verification. Keep it in task context for a single pass; persist it in the reusable task handoff for recurring runs as described above.\\n\\nClassify every relevant finding as exactly one of:\\n\\n- `Actionable`: a current defect within scope that can be addressed in this round.\\n- `Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale)`: current-code evidence shows the behavior is fixed, superseded, or no longer applicable. An outdated hunk alone is not proof; trace its current implementation.\\n- `Invalid`: current-code or behavioral evidence disproves the reported defect. Record the evidence, not just disagreement with the reviewer.\\n- `Accepted Risk`: a verified defect explicitly accepted by the user or an identified authorized decision-maker. Record the decision, scope, impact and follow-up. The agent cannot use this label to clear unfinished work; accepted risks remain visible and do not count as fixes.\\n- `Not Attempted`: a blocked current defect, out-of-scope concern, or external/non-code gate. Distinguish these reasons. A valid blocked defect remains unresolved; do not count it as clean.\\n\\nDeduplicate comments reporting the same root cause. An unchanged old comment is not evidence that its issue is fixed. Reuse prior verified evidence only when the relevant code and contract remain unchanged.\\n\\n## 6. Establish the affected contract\\n\\nFor each actionable root cause, before editing:\\n\\n1. State the behavior that must hold and the concrete failing case.\\n2. Trace its producers, consumers, callers, and sibling implementations in the PR worktree. Inspect equivalent entrypoints such as CLI versus batch operations, gateway versus worker execution, and normal versus retry/recovery paths when relevant.\\n3. Identify where the invariant is enforced and what the proposed change could break. For stateful changes, consider ownership, fencing, ordering, partial failure, and cleanup where they affect this contract.\\n4. Record which paths need changes, which already satisfy the contract, and the behavioral evidence needed to verify the fix.\\n5. Make assumptions and exclusions explicit. For security or serialization, identify the protected data, threat model, final consumer-visible boundary and permitted structural output. Resolve contradictory or impossible guarantees before implementation. A substring match, for example, needs analysis of data provenance and the promised artifact contract before being classified as disclosure.\\n\\nThe unit of remediation is the root cause and its affected contract, not the commented line. A directly related defect discovered during this inspection belongs to the same scoped batch even when no reviewer named that line. Record its connection to the snapshot finding. Unrelated discoveries remain out of scope.\\n\\n## 7. Implement the smallest complete repair\\n\\nRepair every applicable path identified above. Prefer a shared enforcement point when it simplifies correctness; do not introduce an abstraction solely to satisfy this procedure.\\n\\nPreserve unrelated dirty work and exclude unrelated untracked and `.conduct/` artifacts. Do not expand into repository-wide cleanup or redesign. If a complete repair requires expanded authority or an unavailable dependency, explain the remaining defect and classify it as blocked rather than presenting a symptom patch as complete.\\n\\n## 8. Verify behavior and review the fix batch\\n\\nFor each root cause, demonstrate the previously failing behavior and its corrected outcome with focused regression coverage where practical. Confirm the test would fail on the old behavior, by running it against the old code when safe or by explaining the distinguishing assertion. Do not claim a reproduced failure when it was only reasoned through.\\n\\nUse evidence appropriate to the contract. Verify consumer-visible outcomes at the relevant boundaries: serialized artifacts, cleanup recovery, supported package entrypoints, or export/replay. Exercise combinations and composition where failures arise from interacting inputs; use property-based or generated cases when justified, without requiring them for every small fix. A regression matrix must test the stated invariant, not merely enumerate examples from bot comments.\\n\\nUse evidence appropriate to the contract:\\n\\n- For SQL, claims, locks, and transactions, prove resulting state and relevant concurrency behavior using a real disposable database when feasible. SQL-text assertions alone do not establish correctness.\\n- For retry/recovery, cover the relevant interrupted state and the evidence needed to declare success.\\n- For configuration propagation, verify both the executing component's configuration and required secret wiring without deploying.\\n- Tests that mutate fixtures must restore prior values and row existence or use isolated disposable fixtures.\\n\\nIf behavioral verification is unavailable, report the gap explicitly. Test counts, mocks that mirror the implementation, and typechecks are not substitutes for proof of the failing behavior.\\n\\nAfter editing, review the entire fix diff together with its callers and affected contract before staging. Check for missed sibling paths, newly broken consumers, error/cleanup regressions, and interactions between fixes. Re-run checks when justified by subsequent changes or unresolved concerns. Complete local repair and verification within this single pre-push batch.\\n\\nRun focused tests first, then proportionate typecheck, lint, test, and build gates. Distinguish change-caused failures, baseline/environment limits, local proof, and external state.\\n\\nDo not wait for external CI in this skill. A single immediate check snapshot is allowed for reporting; no polling. Skipped, failed, or absent reviewers do not prove coverage.\\n\\n## 9. Commit and push the fixes exactly once\\n\\nInvoking this skill authorizes one reviewed commit and one normal push of the fixes produced by this round to the PR head branch. Do not leave completed fixes only in the local worktree. If the fetched snapshot contains no actionable findings and no changes were made, do not create an empty commit or push.\\n\\nBefore committing:\\n\\n1. review the exact staged allowlist\\n2. run `git diff --cached --check`\\n3. confirm unrelated artifacts are excluded\\n4. confirm the root-cause ledger identifies evidence for every claimed fix and lists remaining valid defects\\n5. confirm no reset trigger remains unaddressed and no claimed complete repair leaves a known affected path deferred\\n\\nCreate exactly one commit for the reviewed fix batch and push it once to the PR head branch. Do not force-push. Verify the local, remote, and PR head SHAs once after pushing.\\n\\nDo not refetch review feedback after the push. Do not wait for the pushed commit to receive new reviews.\\n\\n## 10. Reconcile the queue\\n\\nSeparate remaining code defects from open GitHub thread count. Report how many snapshot threads are fixed/already fixed, still valid, blocked, or unassessed, distinguishing thread counts from deduplicated root causes.\\n\\nThis skill does not by itself authorize posting replies, resolving threads, or dismissing reviews. If separately authorized by the user, resolve only snapshot threads whose full concern is covered by current-code evidence and the verified PR head; use captured IDs and mutation responses without refetching feedback. Never resolve a valid blocked finding or dismiss a review merely to reduce the count. Otherwise report fixed threads as eligible for resolution while leaving their GitHub state unchanged.\\n\\n## 11. Report and terminate\\n\\nReport with these explicit buckets:\\n\\n- `Fixed`\\n- `Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale)`\\n- `Not Attempted`\\n- `Verification`\\n- `Invalid / Accepted Risk` when applicable\\n- `Convergence`: valid blocking root causes before/after, newly discovered defects, fix-induced regressions, recurring families, oldest deferred blockers and verification gaps. Distinguish assessed from unassessed items. Use improving, stalled, regressing or unknown with evidence; more tests, commits or resolved threads alone do not establish progress.\\n\\nFor each fixed root cause, summarize affected paths and behavioral evidence. Include unverified contracts and valid blocked defects; a completed round does not establish merge readiness.\\n\\nInclude the exact pushed commit SHA and PR URL. If no changes were needed, say explicitly that no commit or push was created. State any pending CI or reviewer checks without waiting for them.\\n\\nEnd with a clear termination statement such as:\\n\\n\u003e One review round is complete. No post-push refetch or additional review loop was performed.\\n\\nThen stop.\\n\",\n    \"requestId\": \"mcp:03b0f6c9-a781-436e-ab70-eab8b3cdc6f0\",\n    \"skill\": {\n      \"description\": \"Run exactly one bounded GitHub PR review-remediation pass: fetch all pending review surfaces, validate findings against the exact PR worktree, fix only current valid issues, verify, optionally commit and push once when authorized, report, and stop without any post-push refetch, CI wait, or reviewer loop.\",\n      \"id\": \"skill:3ba0f6dd-212c-4933-9feb-cf87481a0466\",\n      \"name\": \"PR Refetch Fix\",\n      \"slug\": \"pr-refetch-fix\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"code-review\",\n        \"github\",\n        \"pull-request\",\n        \"remediation\",\n        \"single-pass\"\n      ],\n      \"visibility\": \"workspace\",\n      \"workspaceId\": \"workspace:cf0aa9c5-76c8-4a89-8a9b-66c70676c298\",\n      \"workspaceSlug\": \"21n\"\n    },\n    \"version\": {\n      \"byteSize\": 7678,\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-15T07:41:54.717Z\",\n      \"digest\": \"sha256:8781c1c12fe9d5902337d6cf21bfbac49dd3a94c7eadd46bf2622db350444022\",\n      \"id\": \"skill-version:e741e530-df30-485d-9253-affc90d6ac56\",\n      \"manifest\": {\n        \"byteSize\": 7678,\n        \"digest\": \"sha256:8781c1c12fe9d5902337d6cf21bfbac49dd3a94c7eadd46bf2622db350444022\",\n        \"expandedByteSize\": 18354,\n        \"fileCount\": 2,\n        \"files\": [\n          {\n            \"byteSize\": 17699,\n            \"mediaType\": \"text/markdown; charset=utf-8\",\n            \"path\": \"SKILL.md\",\n            \"sha256\": \"735dafee62d04e1be09123929a0a325972ca4312e1072fd55f4c9ca35e3002c8\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"byteSize\": 655,\n            \"mediaType\": \"application/json\",\n            \"path\": \"skill.json\",\n            \"sha256\": \"615c75037c206c8414bf58724fa02c777e91c9e9d8b10f8642a4f7509f5156a8\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"formatVersion\": 1\n      },\n      \"publishedAt\": \"2026-09-15T07:52:37.513Z\",\n      \"revision\": 4,\n      \"semanticVersion\": \"1.2.0\",\n      \"state\": \"published\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"logId\": \"log_cogL92UYF7UO\"\n}\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7bd8d19c87d086ea1bde040151af","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"summary":[{"text":"**Confirming GitHub auth and branch status**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Planning prechecks and ledger reading**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_IZ4cEAy8E4Tl1lBW1BPUeKRh","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7bdd099c87d0b87e9c19890127ce","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git branch --show-current\\ngit status --short --branch\\ngit status --porcelain=v2\\ngit remote -v\\nGH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh auth status\\nGH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api user --jq .login\\ntail -n 180 .conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":30000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789819863.027228,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_IZ4cEAy8E4Tl1lBW1BPUeKRh","id":"ctco_01a0b993-e406-70e3-a171-e19dfbdea335","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789819872.26261,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.6 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910\n## codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910...origin/codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910\n?? .conduct/\n? .conduct/\norigin\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.git (fetch)\norigin\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.git (push)\nsf-next\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.next.git (fetch)\nsf-next\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.next.git (push)\ngithub.com\n  ✓ Logged in to github.com account thyaravind (keyring)\n  - Active account: true\n  - Git operations protocol: https\n  - Token: gho_************************************\n  - Token scopes: 'gist', 'read:org', 'repo', 'workflow'\nthyaravind\n- Not Attempted: the preserved Sonar maintainability/reliability inventory remains 36 findings under `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY`. The captured Sonar analysis check is successful, but individual analyzer details were not substituted for the GitHub review snapshot or declared fixed.\n- Unassessed: 0 captured GitHub threads, review bodies, issue comments, or inline comments.\n\n## Round 7 required-check snapshot\n\n- One snapshot only: all 18 contexts were terminal: 14 successful, 1 neutral, and 3 skipped. There were no pending or failed contexts; `reviewDecision` was empty. CodeRabbit, Cubic, Pullfrog, CodeQL, SonarCloud Code Analysis, GitGuardian, and the applicable security checks were successful. No check polling is permitted.\n\n## Round 7 convergence\n\n- Trend: stalled across scheduled convergence. Four selected roots are repaired locally, but cleanup-phase and credential-boundary families recurred again and the 36-finding analyzer family remains deferred.\n- Valid blocking root causes before / after: 4 selected code root causes plus 1 deferred analyzer family / 1 deferred analyzer family.\n- New defects: unsafe cleanup cause exposure, pre-handle phase loss, structured Cookie component leakage, and target-suite output misclassification.\n- Recurring families: cleanup-phase classification and credential-boundary redaction recurred; the reset-trigger assessment repaired their shared lease/target/client boundaries before mutation.\n- Fix-induced regressions: none found by focused regressions, affected-package typechecks/builds, whole-batch diff review, or the final Node 22 release gate.\n- Oldest deferred blocker: `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY` from round 1, last observed at 36 findings. It remains Not Attempted and prevents a clean assessment despite terminal successful required checks.\n- Clean streak: `0` (reset by four actionable/new root causes, recurring families, this code-changing round, and the deferred analyzer family).\n- Head stability: the complete snapshot stayed at `a9fc7f4b1e6b549caf1a5f80498980167429482a`; the authorized round then advanced local, remote, and PR head together to `0e89647cb6a20681e546a22c1d2c58eabe74253e` in the one allowed comparison.\n\n## Round 7 verification evidence\n\n- Focused testing: all 43 `@mcpfn/client` tests, 226 `@mcpfn/testing` tests, and 50 `@mcpfn/cli` tests passed. New regressions prove public cleanup causes cannot expose raw provider errors, failed-open OAuth retries retain `token-revocation`, reflected Cookie components are redacted while ambiguous syntax fails closed, and target JSON/JUnit/stdout failures are safe runtime exit 1 outcomes.\n- Typechecks: `@mcpfn/client`, `@mcpfn/testing`, and `@mcpfn/cli` passed; client and testing packages were rebuilt before downstream consumer tests.\n- Release gate: the final `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed all package tests/typechecks/builds, Playwright, official conformance, mixed-entry redaction, examples, ESM/CJS imports, dry-run packs, packed-consumer installation, and round trips.\n- `git diff --check`: passed; the whole six-file code/test batch and affected lease/target/client/suite/CLI consumers were reviewed before staging.\n- Hosted CI/reviewer state will not be refetched or polled after this snapshot.\n\n## Round 7 termination\n\n- Result: nonterminal recurring run; automation remains enabled for a future separately scheduled assessment.\n- No post-push review refetch, CI poll, reviewer wait, thread resolution, review dismissal, merge, or second fix loop was performed.\n\n## Round 8 snapshot dispositions\n\n- Actionable at snapshot: 2 new unresolved GitHub threads, deduplicated to 2 root causes. Both are fixed in the reviewed local batch; threads remain unresolved and will not be refetched after push.\n- Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale): 83 older unresolved threads. The five round-7 findings are already repaired at the assessed head; 78 retain earlier current-code evidence. Outdated status was not used as proof.\n- Invalid / Accepted Risk: 1 older GitHub finding remains invalid based on observed key-redaction behavior; no accepted risks.\n- Not Attempted: the preserved Sonar maintainability/reliability inventory remains 36 findings under `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY`. The captured Sonar analysis check is successful, but individual analyzer details were not substituted for the GitHub review snapshot or declared fixed.\n- Unassessed: 0 captured GitHub threads, review bodies, issue comments, or inline comments.\n\n## Round 8 required-check snapshot\n\n- One snapshot only: 18 contexts comprised 12 successful, 1 in progress (`Analyze (swift)`), 2 neutral, and 3 skipped. CodeRabbit, GitGuardian, SonarCloud, Cubic, Pullfrog, and applicable completed security checks were successful; `reviewDecision` was empty. No check polling is permitted.\n\n## Round 8 convergence\n\n- Trend: stalled across scheduled convergence. Both selected roots are repaired locally, but credential-boundary and CLI runtime-output families recurred, one hosted check was pending in the only allowed snapshot, and the 36-finding analyzer family remains deferred.\n- Valid blocking root causes before / after: 2 selected code root causes plus 1 deferred analyzer family / 1 deferred analyzer family.\n- New defects: raw custom-target kind reconstruction after redaction and conformance output/persistence usage-error classification.\n- Recurring families: credential-boundary structural safety and CLI runtime-output classification recurred; the reset-trigger assessment reused their shared client structural validator and cleanup-aware output boundary before mutation.\n- Fix-induced regressions: the first full gate exposed changed incomplete-reason wording in three existing structural-projection regressions. The batch now preserves both the established credential-redaction and safe-serialization semantics; 119 focused testing regressions and the final complete gate pass.\n- Oldest deferred blocker: `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY` from round 1, last observed at 36 findings. It remains Not Attempted and prevents a clean assessment.\n- Clean streak: `0` (reset by two actionable/new root causes, recurring families, this code-changing round, one pending hosted check, and the deferred analyzer family).\n- Head stability: the complete snapshot stayed at `0e89647cb6a20681e546a22c1d2c58eabe74253e`; the authorized round then advanced local, remote, and PR head together to `dfaeef0d1a4b25cc2ae9e10ccde0481b255637ad` in the one allowed comparison.\n\n## Round 8 verification evidence\n\n- Focused testing: 119 target-suite/remote-target regressions and 15 conformance-cleanup regressions passed. New assertions prove a custom target kind that conflicts with its redactor cannot enter JSON/JUnit artifacts and conformance report/stdout/stderr failures return exit 1 with fixed safe text.\n- Typechecks/builds: `@mcpfn/testing` and `@mcpfn/cli` passed under Node 22 before the complete gate.\n- Release gate: the final `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed all package tests/typechecks/builds, Playwright, official conformance, mixed-entry redaction, examples, ESM/CJS imports, dry-run packs, packed-consumer installation, and round trips.\n- `git diff --check`: passed; the whole four-file code/test batch and affected suite/CLI consumers were reviewed before staging.\n- Hosted CI/reviewer state will not be refetched or polled after this snapshot.\n\n## Round 8 termination\n\n- Result: nonterminal recurring run; automation remains enabled for a future separately scheduled assessment.\n- No post-push review refetch, CI poll, reviewer wait, thread resolution, review dismissal, merge, or second fix loop was performed.\n\n## Round 1 termination\n\n- Result: nonterminal recurring run; automation remains enabled for a future separately scheduled assessment.\n- No post-push review refetch, CI poll, reviewer wait, thread resolution, review dismissal, merge, or second fix loop was performed.\n\n## Historical handoff retained\n\n- Earlier bounded remediation produced `1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f` for credential redaction, cleanup-phase tracking, cleanup-path tests, and safe CLI handling.\n- At that round's one allowed immediate comparison, the remote branch matched the new commit while the PR API still reported the prior head `8b23aaa087b60844c63459a1c625a23dc954ba03`; this round must establish current live state independently.\n\n## Round 9 snapshot dispositions\n\n- Actionable at snapshot: 4 new unresolved GitHub threads, deduplicated to 4 root causes. All four are fixed in the reviewed local batch; threads remain unresolved and review surfaces will not be refetched after push.\n- Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale): 85 older unresolved threads. The two round-8 findings are already repaired at the assessed head; 83 retain earlier current-code evidence. Outdated status was not used as proof.\n- Invalid / Accepted Risk: 1 older GitHub finding remains invalid based on observed key-redaction behavior; no accepted risks.\n- Not Attempted: the preserved Sonar maintainability/reliability inventory remains 36 findings under `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY`. The captured Sonar analysis check is successful, but individual analyzer details were not substituted for the GitHub review snapshot or declared fixed.\n- Unassessed: 0 captured GitHub threads, review bodies, issue comments, raw inline comments, or nested thread comments.\n\n## Round 9 required-check snapshot\n\n- One snapshot only: all 18 contexts were terminal: 14 successful, 1 neutral, and 3 skipped. There were no pending or failed contexts; `reviewDecision` was empty. No check polling is permitted.\n\n## Round 9 convergence\n\n- Trend: stalled across scheduled convergence. Four selected roots are repaired locally, but credential-boundary and CLI runtime-output families recurred and the 36-finding analyzer family remains deferred.\n- Valid blocking root causes before / after: 4 selected code root causes plus 1 deferred analyzer family / 1 deferred analyzer family.\n- New defects: false credential-failure taxonomy for hostile descriptors, classified runtime failure replacement by persistent stderr rejection, fixed-key credential leakage, and unvalidated event/diagnostic target descriptors.\n- Recurring families: credential-boundary structural safety and CLI runtime-output classification recurred; the reset-trigger assessment repaired shared producer boundaries before mutation.\n- Fix-induced regressions: none remain. The first focused testing run exposed two incorrect new test expectations; the expectations were corrected to distinguish recoverable discriminator-value omission from unrecoverable fixed-key collision, after which all focused suites and the complete release gate passed.\n- Oldest deferred blocker: `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY` from round 1, last observed at 36 findings. It remains Not Attempted and prevents a clean assessment despite terminal successful required checks.\n- Clean streak: `0` (reset by four actionable/new root causes, recurring families, this code-changing round, and the deferred analyzer family).\n- Head stability: the complete snapshot stayed at `dfaeef0d1a4b25cc2ae9e10ccde0481b255637ad`; the authorized round then advanced local, remote, and PR head together to `cf76637ada4ba0263e36f30c23a278826c48dd0a` in the one allowed comparison.\n\n## Round 9 verification evidence\n\n- Focused testing: all 41 `@mcpfn/client` tests, 121 target-suite/remote-target `@mcpfn/testing` tests, and 15 conformance-cleanup `@mcpfn/cli` tests passed (177 total).\n- Typechecks: `@mcpfn/client`, `@mcpfn/testing`, and `@mcpfn/cli` passed under Node 22.\n- Release gate: `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed every reported package test/typecheck/build, Playwright, official conformance, mixed-entry redaction, examples, ESM/CJS imports, dry-run packs, packed-consumer installation, and round trips.\n- `git diff --check`: passed; the whole seven-file code/test batch and affected producer/consumer boundaries were reviewed before staging.\n- Hosted CI/reviewer state will not be refetched or polled after this snapshot.\n\n## Round 9 termination\n\n- Result: nonterminal recurring run; the four selected code roots are fixed and pushed, but the preserved deferred analyzer family prevents a clean assessment.\n- Automation remains disabled from the earlier retrieval-discovery stop and was not silently re-enabled during this manual retry.\n- No post-push review refetch, CI poll, reviewer wait, thread resolution, review dismissal, merge, or second fix loop will be performed.\n\n## Round 10 assessment\n\n- Hosted workflow: `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.2.0`, revision `4`, digest `sha256:8781c1c12fe9d5902337d6cf21bfbac49dd3a94c7eadd46bf2622db350444022` (published identity verified through Skillplane via Composio before repository mutation).\n- Mode: assessment reset. Round 10 is the next separately invoked single review round; the prior clean streak remains `0`.\n- Complete snapshot: captured once at `2026-09-19T10:01:05.850Z` against stable local/upstream/PR head `cf76637ada4ba0263e36f30c23a278826c48dd0a`. Seven thread pages were terminal, all nested comment pages were terminal, and start/end/page head checks matched. The snapshot contains 329 threads (92 unresolved: 39 current and 53 outdated-only), 224 reviews, 64 issue comments, 369 raw inline comments, and 18 check contexts.\n- Shared invariant: every emitted typed artifact must preserve credential-free authored keys and discriminators or fail closed; cleanup ownership must remain callable even when no safe artifact can be serialized; OAuth success evidence must accept only exact argument-free anti-cache directives; behavior-preserving maintainability work must keep these boundaries intact.\n- Producers and consumers: scenario creation plus inspector export feed replay artifacts; target/session close plus suite finalization feed direct callers and CLI JSON/JUnit/stdout; hosted OAuth response parsing feeds exchange and refresh case results; redaction, authorization, report, orchestration, CLI, and Node/Web adapters feed tests and required analysis.\n- Failure boundaries: fixed-key credential collisions cannot produce a typed scenario/report; structural report failure can coincide with a failed cleanup lease; parameterized cache directives do not prove anti-caching; broad analyzer refactors can regress credential redaction, lifecycle phases, bounded serialization, or exit classification.\n- Coordinated repair criteria: validate every possible top-level scenario export key before constructing output; retain structural-collision cleanup in a dedicated retryable error with no unsafe report and teach both library/CLI boundaries to preserve it; require exact `no-store` and `no-cache` tokens for both exchange and refresh; decompose only validated analyzer findings with unchanged observable contracts and focused regressions.\n- Verification criteria: focused inspector, hosted-authorization, target-suite, report, CLI, conformance, adapter, and redaction regressions; affected package typechecks/builds; complete Node 22 release gate; `git diff --check`; one local/upstream/PR head comparison after at most one push. Hosted review/check surfaces will not be fetched again this round.\n\n### Round 10 defect families\n\n| Stable family | Root cause / affected contract | Disposition | First seen | Last attempted | Repair / evidence state |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `MCP170-SCENARIO-KEY-STRUCTURE` | Inspector validates scenario discriminator values but not authored top-level keys, allowing a key-equal credential to survive export | Actionable | round 10 | round 10 | Coordinated key-boundary repair selected; regression uses credential `name` |\n| `MCP170-OAUTH-CACHE-DIRECTIVE-PARAMS` | Hosted token validation discards directive parameters, so `no-store=false` and `no-cache=false` are accepted | Actionable | round 10 | round 10 | Exact directive-token repair selected for exchange and refresh |\n| `MCP170-STRUCTURAL-COLLISION-CLEANUP-OWNER` | Suite finalization throws a safe structural error before transferring an already-retained cleanup owner | Actionable; recurring cleanup-ownership family | round 10 | round 10 | Dedicated reportless retry-owner repair selected for direct and CLI consumers |\n| `MCP170-SONAR-REDACTION-DECOMPOSITION` | Redaction/credential helpers contain duplicated bounds, regex, and deeply nested traversal/lifecycle logic | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 11 findings grouped under shared credential/redaction contract |\n| `MCP170-SONAR-BASE64-REGEX` | Base64 token patterns use avoidable character-class forms | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 10 | round 10 | 2 findings grouped under token grammar preservation |\n| `MCP170-SONAR-SUITE-ORCHESTRATION` | Suite orchestration contains dense comparisons, fallbacks, and control flow | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 5 findings grouped under report/lifecycle behavior preservation |\n| `MCP170-SONAR-HOSTED-OAUTH` | Hosted OAuth assessment and rejection validation contain dense conditional construction | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 5 findings grouped under authorization evidence preservation |\n| `MCP170-SONAR-REPORT-JUNIT` | Failure normalization and JUnit mapping contain avoidable branching/spread/ternary complexity | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 3 findings grouped under stable report serialization |\n| `MCP170-SONAR-CLI` | CLI dispatch and portable-identifier regex trigger maintainability findings | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 10 | round 10 | 2 findings grouped under unchanged exit/output classification |\n| `MCP170-SONAR-NODE-WEB-HEADERS` | Two Node-to-Web header adapters duplicate nested ternary conversion | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 2 findings grouped under identical multi-value header semantics |\n| `MCP170-SONAR-INSPECTOR` | Secret-marker generation and export fallback selection contain avoidable constructs | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 2 findings grouped under replayable placeholder behavior |\n| `MCP170-SONAR-CONFORMANCE` | Official conformance completion mutates a parameter-derived exit code | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 1 finding; preserve incomplete/failure classification |\n| `MCP170-SONAR-CUSTOM-TARGET-TYPE` | Custom-target redactor field redundantly combines optional syntax with `undefined` | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 1 type-contract cleanup |\n| `MCP170-SONAR-THROW-THIS` | Four analyzer findings flag intentional retry-owner self-rejection in cleanup error classes | Invalid analyzer interpretation | round 10 | round 10 | Existing retry identity is required; suite occurrence is removed incidentally by shared helper, other owner classes remain valid intentional behavior |\n\n- Snapshot check state: all 18 contexts terminal; 14 successful, 1 neutral, and 3 skipped. Sonar Quality Gate passed and reported 38 new issues; `reviewDecision` was empty.\n- Convergence state: not clean. Three new review roots, the recurring cleanup-ownership family, and the now-assessed analyzer families reset the clean streak to `0` even though the snapshot head was stable and required checks were terminal.\n\n## Round 10 snapshot dispositions\n\n- Actionable: 4 new unresolved GitHub threads, deduplicated to 3 root causes. `MCP170-SCENARIO-KEY-STRUCTURE`, `MCP170-OAUTH-CACHE-DIRECTIVE-PARAMS`, and `MCP170-STRUCTURAL-COLLISION-CLEANUP-OWNER` are repaired by `80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1`; the threads remain unresolved and were not refetched after push.\n- Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale): 87 older unresolved threads retain their prior current-code dispositions. The four round-9 roots are already repaired at the assessed head; outdated status alone was not used as evidence.\n- Invalid / Accepted Risk: the older property-key-redaction finding remains invalid based on observed payload-key behavior. The analyzer's retry-owner `throw this` family is invalid because object identity is the ownership token; the suite instance was removed incidentally by a shared retry helper, while the three remaining instances preserve required owner identity. No accepted risks.\n- Not Attempted: 0 valid code root causes. The 34 valid Sonar findings were attempted as ten coordinated subfamilies in this batch; their hosted analyzer disposition remains pending until a future separately scheduled snapshot because post-push refetch is forbidden.\n- Unassessed: 0 captured threads, review bodies, issue comments, raw inline comments, nested comments, or analyzer findings.\n\n## Round 10 verification evidence\n\n- Focused regressions: 28 inspector credential-artifact tests and 145 hosted-authorization/remote-target tests passed after the three review-root repairs. The broader testing/report/suite set passed 189 tests after decomposition, and the CLI reportless-owner regression passed with the target-suite cleanup suite.\n- Complete affected package suites: 45 `@mcpfn/client`, 234 `@mcpfn/testing`, 38 `@mcpfn/inspector`, and 54 `@mcpfn/cli` tests passed (371 total).\n- Typechecks: `@mcpfn/client`, `@mcpfn/testing`, `@mcpfn/inspector`, and `@mcpfn/cli` passed under Node 22; `@mcpfn/testing` rebuilt successfully before downstream CLI verification.\n- Release gate: `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed every reported package test/typecheck/build, Playwright, official conformance, mixed-entry redaction, examples, ESM/CJS imports, dry-run packs, packed-consumer installation, and round trips.\n- `git diff --check` and the staged diff check passed. The ledger remained untracked and was never staged or committed.\n- Required-check snapshot: the one pre-mutation snapshot contained 18 terminal contexts: 14 successful, 1 neutral, and 3 skipped; Sonar Quality Gate passed while reporting 38 new issues. No hosted checks were fetched after push.\n- Head verification (one comparison only): local head, `origin/codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910`, and PR 170 head all equal `80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1`; the PR remained open.\n\n## Round 10 convergence\n\n- Trend: improving but nonterminal. The deferred analyzer inventory is no longer Not Attempted, all three new review roots have coordinated repairs, and no local regression remains; hosted reviewers/analyzers have not yet assessed the new head.\n- Valid blocking root causes before / after: 3 new review roots plus 10 valid analyzer subfamilies / 0 deliberately deferred valid code roots, with hosted verification pending a future round.\n- New defects: top-level scenario key leakage, parameterized anti-cache directive acceptance, and cleanup-owner loss during structural report collision.\n- Recurring families: credential-boundary structural safety and cleanup ownership recurred; both were repaired at their shared producer/consumer boundaries.\n- Fix-induced regressions: none found by 371 complete affected-package tests, four typechecks, rebuilt package consumers, whole-batch diff review, or the Node 22 release gate.\n- Clean streak: `0` (reset by new/actionable roots, recurring families, this code-changing round, and the changed PR head after the assessment).\n- Head stability: the snapshot remained at `cf76637ada4ba0263e36f30c23a278826c48dd0a` during assessment; the single commit and push advanced local, remote, and PR head together to `80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1` in the one allowed comparison.\n\n## Round 10 termination\n\n- Result: nonterminal recurring run. A future separately scheduled clean assessment must verify the new head, review dispositions, and analyzer/check state; this code-changing round cannot count toward the clean streak.\n- Automation `4442e7f3-60f4-4125-a8e4-c818ac40fc82` remains disabled from the earlier retrieval-discovery stop and was not silently re-enabled during this manual round.\n- No post-push review refetch, CI poll, reviewer wait, thread resolution, review dismissal, merge, or second fix loop was performed.\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7be41be087d0877b6aa16d242179","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"summary":[{"text":"**Planning robust GraphQL pagination script**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Designing file-less pagination with gh api**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Assessing shell variable capacity for JSON data**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7bef354087d099e8f4eaff1720dc","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"summary":[{"text":"**Planning data fetching and orchestration**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Designing efficient GitHub API pagination**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Confirming PR view data snapshot strategy**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7bf9426487d08a00432045ff287b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"summary":[{"text":"**Planning PR snapshot creation**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Designing unresolved review thread summarization**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Executing snapshot capture with jq extraction**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"The pinned hosted workflow matches exactly: `1.2.0`, revision `4`, published digest `sha256:8781c1c12fe9d5902337d6cf21bfbac49dd3a94c7eadd46bf2622db350444022`. The worktree is on the required branch, only `.conduct/` is untracked, `origin` is correct, and `thyaravind` is active. I’m taking the one complete review/check snapshot now.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7c045e0087d09e396baeca5e57c7","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1789819872.898685,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_oBcJCHysR06zfjpWfwRda5ps","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7c05921487d082c9684e13526ac4","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"snapshot_dir=$(mktemp -d /tmp/pr170-round11.XXXXXX)\\nGH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh pr view 170 --repo 21nCo/super-functions --json headRefOid,headRefName,state,mergeStateStatus,reviewDecision,statusCheckRollup,updatedAt,url \u003e \\\"$snapshot_dir/pr-start.json\\\"\\nGH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api graphql --paginate --slurp -f query='query($endCursor: String) { repository(owner: \\\"21nCo\\\", name: \\\"super-functions\\\") { pullRequest(number: 170) { headRefOid reviewThreads(first: 50, after: $endCursor) { nodes { id isResolved path comments(first: 100) { nodes { id body author { login } createdAt outdated url diffHunk originalLine line } pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor } } } pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor } } } } }' \u003e \\\"$snapshot_dir/threads.json\\\"\\nGH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api --paginate --slurp 'repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170/reviews?per_page=100' \u003e \\\"$snapshot_dir/reviews.json\\\"\\nGH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api --paginate --slurp 'repos/21nCo/super-functions/issues/170/comments?per_page=100' \u003e \\\"$snapshot_dir/issue-comments.json\\\"\\nGH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api --paginate --slurp 'repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/170/comments?per_page=100' \u003e \\\"$snapshot_dir/inline-comments.json\\\"\\nGH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh pr view 170 --repo 21nCo/super-functions --json headRefOid,state \u003e \\\"$snapshot_dir/pr-end.json\\\"\\nnode -e '\\nconst fs=require(\\\"fs\\\"); const d=process.argv[1];\\nconst start=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(d+\\\"/pr-start.json\\\",\\\"utf8\\\"));\\nconst end=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(d+\\\"/pr-end.json\\\",\\\"utf8\\\"));\\nconst pages=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(d+\\\"/threads.json\\\",\\\"utf8\\\"));\\nconst threads=pages.flatMap(p=\u003ep.data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes);\\nconst reviews=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(d+\\\"/reviews.json\\\",\\\"utf8\\\")).flat();\\nconst issues=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(d+\\\"/issue-comments.json\\\",\\\"utf8\\\")).flat();\\nconst inline=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(d+\\\"/inline-comments.json\\\",\\\"utf8\\\")).flat();\\nconst unresolved=threads.filter(t=\u003e!t.isResolved);\\nconst current=unresolved.filter(t=\u003et.comments.nodes.some(c=\u003e!c.outdated));\\nconst nested=threads.filter(t=\u003et.comments.pageInfo.hasNextPage);\\nconst checks=start.statusCheckRollup.map(c=\u003e({name:c.name||c.context,status:c.status||c.state,conclusion:c.conclusion||c.state}));\\nconst newThreads=unresolved.filter(t=\u003et.comments.nodes.some(c=\u003ec.createdAt\u003e\\\"2026-09-19T10:01:05Z\\\"));\\nconst newReviews=reviews.filter(x=\u003e(x.submitted_at||\\\"\\\")\u003e\\\"2026-09-19T10:01:05Z\\\");\\nconst newIssues=issues.filter(x=\u003ex.created_at\u003e\\\"2026-09-19T10:01:05Z\\\");\\nconst newInline=inline.filter(x=\u003ex.created_at\u003e\\\"2026-09-19T10:01:05Z\\\");\\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({snapshotDir:d,startHead:start.headRefOid,endHead:end.headRefOid,state:start.state,endState:end.state,mergeStateStatus:start.mergeStateStatus,reviewDecision:start.reviewDecision,pageHeads:[...new Set(pages.map(p=\u003ep.data.repository.pullRequest.headRefOid))],threadPages:pages.length,threads:threads.length,unresolved:unresolved.length,current:current.length,outdatedOnly:unresolved.length-current.length,nestedExtra:nested.length,reviews:reviews.length,issueComments:issues.length,inlineComments:inline.length,checks,newCounts:{threads:newThreads.length,reviews:newReviews.length,issueComments:newIssues.length,inlineComments:newInline.length},newThreads:newThreads.map(t=\u003e({id:t.id,path:t.path,comments:t.comments.nodes.filter(c=\u003ec.createdAt\u003e\\\"2026-09-19T10:01:05Z\\\").map(c=\u003e({id:c.id,author:c.author?.login,createdAt:c.createdAt,outdated:c.outdated,line:c.line,originalLine:c.originalLine,url:c.url,body:c.body}))})),newReviews:newReviews.map(x=\u003e({id:x.id,user:x.user?.login,state:x.state,submittedAt:x.submitted_at,commitId:x.commit_id,body:x.body,htmlUrl:x.html_url})),newIssues:newIssues.map(x=\u003e({id:x.id,user:x.user?.login,createdAt:x.created_at,body:x.body,htmlUrl:x.html_url})),newInline:newInline.map(x=\u003e({id:x.id,user:x.user?.login,createdAt:x.created_at,path:x.path,line:x.line,originalLine:x.original_line,body:x.body,htmlUrl:x.html_url}))},null,2));\\n' \\\"$snapshot_dir\\\"\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170\",\"yield_time_ms\":30000,\"max_output_tokens\":50000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789819872.898685,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_oBcJCHysR06zfjpWfwRda5ps","id":"ctco_01a0b994-f7fb-7fd2-8ce3-badc8f1bb1b4","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789819942.907422,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 14.9 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\n  \"snapshotDir\": \"/tmp/pr170-round11.2MJNpH\",\n  \"startHead\": \"80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1\",\n  \"endHead\": \"80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1\",\n  \"state\": \"OPEN\",\n  \"endState\": \"OPEN\",\n  \"mergeStateStatus\": \"DIRTY\",\n  \"reviewDecision\": \"\",\n  \"pageHeads\": [\n    \"80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1\"\n  ],\n  \"threadPages\": 1,\n  \"threads\": 50,\n  \"unresolved\": 5,\n  \"current\": 2,\n  \"outdatedOnly\": 3,\n  \"nestedExtra\": 0,\n  \"reviews\": 228,\n  \"issueComments\": 64,\n  \"inlineComments\": 373,\n  \"checks\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Analyze (javascript-typescript)\",\n      \"status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"SUCCESS\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Analyze (actions)\",\n      \"status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"SUCCESS\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Analyze (python)\",\n      \"status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"SUCCESS\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Analyze (javascript-typescript)\",\n      \"status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"SUCCESS\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Analyze (python)\",\n      \"status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"SUCCESS\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Analyze (rust)\",\n      \"status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"SUCCESS\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Analyze (swift)\",\n      \"status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"SUCCESS\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Socket Security: Pull Request Alerts\",\n      \"status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"NEUTRAL\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Graphite / AI Reviews\",\n      \"status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"SKIPPED\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Sourcery review\",\n      \"status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"SKIPPED\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"[code]smith\",\n      \"status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"SKIPPED\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"CodeQL\",\n      \"status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"SUCCESS\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"CodeRabbit\",\n      \"status\": \"SUCCESS\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"SUCCESS\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"GitGuardian Security Checks\",\n      \"status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"SUCCESS\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Socket Security: Project Report\",\n      \"status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"SUCCESS\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"SonarCloud Code Analysis\",\n      \"status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"SUCCESS\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"cubic · AI code reviewer\",\n      \"status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"SUCCESS\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"SUCCESS\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"newCounts\": {\n    \"threads\": 0,\n    \"reviews\": 4,\n    \"issueComments\": 1,\n    \"inlineComments\": 4\n  },\n  \"newThreads\": [],\n  \"newReviews\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 5255342068,\n      \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-09-19T10:23:38Z\",\n      \"commitId\": \"80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1\",\n      \"body\": \"\u003c!-- cubic:review-summary:start --\u003e\\n**1 issue found across 15 files (changes from recent commits).**\\n\u003c!-- cubic:review-summary:end --\u003e\\n\\n\u003cdetails\u003e\\n\u003csummary\u003ePrompt for AI agents (unresolved issues)\u003c/summary\u003e\\n\\n```text\\n\\nCheck if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately.\\n\\n\\n\u003cfile name=\\\"mcpfn/inspector/src/index.ts\\\"\u003e\\n\\n\u003cviolation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"mcpfn/inspector/src/index.ts:243\\\"\u003e\\nP2: When a credential equals `status`, `incompleteReason`, or `variables`, complete exports fail even when those optional fields are not emitted. Validate optional structural keys only when the corresponding field is actually added.\u003c/violation\u003e\\n\u003c/file\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\u003c/details\u003e\\n\\n\u003csub\u003e**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github\u0026utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/170/ai_pr_review_github_delivery_7077910b94aa69d2232c9a2206ecafa319e57507329bbf281a6bc27c357e5db8?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F170)\u003c/sub\u003e\\n\\n\u003c!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_github_delivery_7077910b94aa69d2232c9a2206ecafa319e57507329bbf281a6bc27c357e5db8:80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1:3f2b0c8e-464a-550e-ac0b-0b595abbdda1 --\u003e\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5255342068\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 5255348648,\n      \"user\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-09-19T10:25:56Z\",\n      \"commitId\": \"80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1\",\n      \"body\": \"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `80ba026172`\\n    \\n\\n\u003cdetails\u003e \u003csummary\u003eℹ️ About Codex in GitHub\u003c/summary\u003e\\n\u003cbr/\u003e\\n\\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n\u003c/details\u003e\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5255348648\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 5255354305,\n      \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-09-19T10:27:34Z\",\n      \"commitId\": \"80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1\",\n      \"body\": \"\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5255354305\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 5255359562,\n      \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-09-19T10:29:21Z\",\n      \"commitId\": \"80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1\",\n      \"body\": \"\u003e [!IMPORTANT]\\n\u003e The suite refactor can bypass cleanup after a target session is already live.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `cf76637a`, covering the behavioral delta in `80ba0261`.\\n\\n- **Preserved structural-collision cleanup** — Added a reportless cleanup-owner error and CLI handling so unsafe artifacts remain omitted while cleanup stays retryable.\\n- **Refactored suite execution** — Extracted diagnostic collection, connected execution, artifact projection, and client close handling.\\n- **Refactored hosted authorization** — Split authorization, token exchange, refresh, and rejection-envelope validation into phase-specific helpers.\\n- **Hardened artifact boundaries** — Preserved inspector schema keys, tightened cache-directive checks, and extracted bounded credential-redaction helpers.\\n\\n\u003c!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 80ba0261;\\nif commits have landed on codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\\n\\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\\n- Files reviewed: 61\\n- Commits reviewed: 70\\n- Base: dev (2867c68f)\\n- Head: codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910 (80ba0261)\\n- Reviewed commits:\\n  - 80ba0261 — fix(mcpfn): close review and analyzer findings (incremental delta; full PR context reviewed through this commit)\\n- Prior pullfrog review: cf76637a (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5249315211)\\n--\u003e\\n\\n\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\u003e\\n\u003csup\u003e\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\u003e\u003cpicture\u003e\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\u003e\u003c/picture\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;｜ [Fix all ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/170?action=fix\u0026review_id=5255359562) ｜ [Fix 👍s ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/170?action=fix-approved\u0026review_id=5255359562) ｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/35437126199/job/105881585044) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\u003c/sup\u003e\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5255359562\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"newIssues\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 5741021520,\n      \"user\": \"sonarqubecloud[bot]\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-19T10:23:43Z\",\n      \"body\": \"## [![Quality Gate Passed](https://sonarsource.github.io/sonarcloud-github-static-resources/v2/checks/QualityGateBadge/qg-passed-20px.png 'Quality Gate Passed')](https://sonarcloud.io/dashboard?id=21nCo_super-functions\u0026pullRequest=170) **Quality Gate passed**  \\nIssues  \\n![](https://sonarsource.github.io/sonarcloud-github-static-resources/v2/common/passed-16px.png '') [11 New issues](https://sonarcloud.io/project/issues?id=21nCo_super-functions\u0026pullRequest=170\u0026issueStatuses=OPEN,CONFIRMED\u0026sinceLeakPeriod=true)  \\n![](https://sonarsource.github.io/sonarcloud-github-static-resources/v2/common/accepted-16px.png '') [0 Accepted issues](https://sonarcloud.io/project/issues?id=21nCo_super-functions\u0026pullRequest=170\u0026issueStatuses=ACCEPTED)\\n\\nMeasures  \\n![](https://sonarsource.github.io/sonarcloud-github-static-resources/v2/common/passed-16px.png '') [0 Security Hotspots](https://sonarcloud.io/project/security_hotspots?id=21nCo_super-functions\u0026pullRequest=170\u0026issueStatuses=OPEN,CONFIRMED\u0026sinceLeakPeriod=true)  \\n![](https://sonarsource.github.io/sonarcloud-github-static-resources/v2/common/passed-16px.png '') [0.0% Coverage on New Code](https://sonarcloud.io/component_measures?id=21nCo_super-functions\u0026pullRequest=170\u0026metric=new_coverage\u0026view=list)  \\n![](https://sonarsource.github.io/sonarcloud-github-static-resources/v2/common/passed-16px.png '') [2.7% Duplication on New Code](https://sonarcloud.io/component_measures?id=21nCo_super-functions\u0026pullRequest=170\u0026metric=new_duplicated_lines_density\u0026view=list)  \\n  \\n\u003c!-- sqra-placement-anchor --\u003e\\n[See analysis details on SonarQube Cloud](https://sonarcloud.io/dashboard?id=21nCo_super-functions\u0026pullRequest=170)\\n\\n\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#issuecomment-5741021520\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"newInline\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 4052873779,\n      \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-19T10:23:38Z\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/inspector/src/index.ts\",\n      \"line\": 243,\n      \"originalLine\": 243,\n      \"body\": \"\u003c!-- cubic:v=a052d67b-f905-485e-8b31-06c93082dca8 --\u003e\\n\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=3f2b0c8e-464a-550e-ac0b-0b595abbdda1 --\u003e\\n\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\u003e\\nP2: When a credential equals `status`, `incompleteReason`, or `variables`, complete exports fail even when those optional fields are not emitted. Validate optional structural keys only when the corresponding field is actually added.\\n\\n\u003cdetails\u003e\\n\u003csummary\u003ePrompt for AI agents\u003c/summary\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/inspector/src/index.ts, line 243:\\n\\n\u003ccomment\u003eWhen a credential equals `status`, `incompleteReason`, or `variables`, complete exports fail even when those optional fields are not emitted. Validate optional structural keys only when the corresponding field is actually added.\u003c/comment\u003e\\n\\n\u003cfile context\u003e\\n@@ -238,6 +238,16 @@ export class McpFnInspector {\\n     const scenario = createMcpFnScenario(name, operation, result);\\n+    // Top-level scenario keys are authored schema, not payload. If a credential\\n+    // collides with one of them, no replayable typed artifact can be emitted.\\n+    for (const key of [\\n+      ...Object.keys(scenario),\\n+      \\\"status\\\",\\n\u003c/file context\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\u003c/details\u003e\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4052873779\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 4052880086,\n      \"user\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-19T10:25:56Z\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n      \"line\": 325,\n      \"originalLine\": 325,\n      \"body\": \"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Validate fallback report structure with the target redactor**\\n\\nWhen a custom target fails before reaching `connected`, this early return bypasses `client.preserveArtifactStructure()` and the target-owned redactor. For example, a target whose opaque credential is `incomplete` can fail during `open()`, after which the suite serializes `status: \\\"incomplete\\\"`; the final `redactTargetCredentials()` pass knows only credentials registered by `authenticatedHttpTarget`, so the custom credential remains exposed. Fresh evidence beyond the earlier target-kind issue is this non-connected fallback branch, which skips validation for every fixed report discriminator; validate those structural values while the custom hook is still available or fail the artifact.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4052880086\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 4052884967,\n      \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-19T10:27:34Z\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"originalLine\": 390,\n      \"body\": \"Addressed in 80ba026 by retaining the cleanup owner in `McpFnTargetSuiteArtifactCleanupError` and adding combined collision/retry coverage.\\n\\n\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\u003e\\n\u003csup\u003e\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\u003e\u003cpicture\u003e\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\u003e\u003c/picture\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/35437126199/job/105881585044) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\u003c/sup\u003e\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4052884967\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 4052889913,\n      \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-19T10:29:20Z\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n      \"line\": 317,\n      \"originalLine\": 317,\n      \"body\": \"**[P1] Keep fallback projection inside the guarded cleanup path**\\n\\nConstructing `fallback` reads the arbitrary `target.kind` before this function enters its `try`. If that getter/proxy throws after the client has connected, `runTargetSuite()` exits before `closeSuiteClient()` and can leave the transport or credential owner live; guard this read and add a post-open throwing-kind regression.\\n\\n\u003cdetails\u003e\u003csummary\u003eTechnical details\u003c/summary\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Preserve cleanup when target metadata access throws\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts:304-317` — `initialTargetDescriptor()` reads `target.kind` while `fallback` is created outside the projection guard.\\n- `mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts:433-435` — projection runs after connection but before the only `closeSuiteClient()` call.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Arbitrary target metadata access must not escape after connection without attempting client cleanup.\\n- A safe incomplete report should be produced when possible, while any failed cleanup remains retryable.\\n````\\n\\n\u003c/details\u003e\",\n      \"htmlUrl\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4052889913\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7c29e81c87d0b28e4675fe143c08","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"summary":[{"text":"**Investigating incomplete pagination with pageInfo**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Planning manual cursor-based pagination loop**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Designing jq command to merge paginated files**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7c35a60887d0ac50f17f179992a3","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"summary":[{"text":"**Improving head consistency verification after paging**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Updating PR end head with gh command**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"The first GraphQL response exposed a pagination-tool quirk: only page 1 was returned even though the thread connection is larger. I’m completing the same snapshot from its returned cursor—without refetching page 1 or any supplementary surface—then I’ll assess the newly reported roots against head `80ba02617`.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7c38b9cc87d0806dbe1f5f865229","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1789819943.856327,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_jZfazId4ehiQJf7ehdC4YYnu","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aae7c39cb9c87d09606a09a2a6337ec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"snapshot_dir=/tmp/pr170-round11.2MJNpH\\ncursor=$(jq -r '.[-1].data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.pageInfo.endCursor // empty' \\\"$snapshot_dir/threads.json\\\")\\nhas_next=$(jq -r '.[-1].data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.pageInfo.hasNextPage' \\\"$snapshot_dir/threads.json\\\")\\npage=2\\nwhile [ \\\"$has_next\\\" = \\\"true\\\" ]; do\\n  GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api graphql -f query='query($endCursor: String) { repository(owner: \\\"21nCo\\\", name: \\\"super-functions\\\") { pullRequest(number: 170) { headRefOid reviewThreads(first: 50, after: $endCursor) { nodes { id isResolved path comments(first: 100) { nodes { id body author { login } createdAt outdated url diffHunk originalLine line } pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor } } } pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor } } } } }' -F endCursor=\\\"$cursor\\\" \u003e \\\"$snapshot_dir/thread-page-$page.json\\\"\\n  cursor=$(jq -r '.data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.pageInfo.endCursor // empty' \\\"$snapshot_dir/thread-page-$page.json\\\")\\n  has_next=$(jq -r '.data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.pageInfo.hasNextPage' \\\"$snapshot_dir/thread-page-$page.json\\\")\\n  page=$((page + 1))\\ndone\\njq -s '.[0] + .[1:]' \\\"$snapshot_dir/threads.json\\\" \\\"$snapshot_dir\\\"/thread-page-*.json \u003e \\\"$snapshot_dir/threads-complete.json\\\"\\nGH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh pr view 170 --repo 21nCo/super-functions --json headRefOid,state \u003e \\\"$snapshot_dir/pr-end.json\\\"\\nnode -e '\\nconst fs=require(\\\"fs\\\"); const d=process.argv[1];\\nconst start=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(d+\\\"/pr-start.json\\\",\\\"utf8\\\"));\\nconst end=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(d+\\\"/pr-end.json\\\",\\\"utf8\\\"));\\nconst pages=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(d+\\\"/threads-complete.json\\\",\\\"utf8\\\"));\\nconst threads=pages.flatMap(p=\u003ep.data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes);\\nconst unresolved=threads.filter(t=\u003e!t.isResolved);\\nconst current=unresolved.filter(t=\u003et.comments.nodes.some(c=\u003e!c.outdated));\\nconst nested=threads.filter(t=\u003et.comments.pageInfo.hasNextPage);\\nconst fresh=unresolved.filter(t=\u003et.comments.nodes.some(c=\u003ec.createdAt\u003e\\\"2026-09-19T10:01:05Z\\\"));\\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({snapshotDir:d,startHead:start.headRefOid,endHead:end.headRefOid,pageHeads:[...new Set(pages.map(p=\u003ep.data.repository.pullRequest.headRefOid))],threadPages:pages.length,threads:threads.length,unresolved:unresolved.length,current:current.length,outdatedOnly:unresolved.length-current.length,nestedExtra:nested.length,newUnresolved:fresh.map(t=\u003e({id:t.id,path:t.path,isResolved:t.isResolved,comments:t.comments.nodes.filter(c=\u003ec.createdAt\u003e\\\"2026-09-19T10:01:05Z\\\").map(c=\u003e({id:c.id,author:c.author?.login,createdAt:c.createdAt,outdated:c.outdated,line:c.line,originalLine:c.originalLine,url:c.url,body:c.body,diffHunk:c.diffHunk}))}))},null,2));\\n' \\\"$snapshot_dir\\\"\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170\",\"yield_time_ms\":30000,\"max_output_tokens\":40000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789819943.856327,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_jZfazId4ehiQJf7ehdC4YYnu","id":"ctco_01a0b995-eddd-7211-bd11-349d70eb89a0","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789820005.853315,"turn_id":"01a0b992-9248-7613-95d3-df05acb573b9"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 31.1 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"Post \"https://api.github.com/graphql\": dial tcp 20.207.73.85:443: connect: operation timed out\n{\n  \"snapshotDir\": \"/tmp/pr170-round11.2MJNpH\",\n  \"startHead\": \"80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1\",\n  \"endHead\": \"80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1\",\n  \"pageHeads\": [\n    \"80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1\"\n  ],\n  \"threadPages\": 6,\n  \"threads\": 300,\n  \"unresolved\": 