ring families, this code-changing round, and the deferred analyzer family).\n- Head stability: the complete snapshot stayed at `dfaeef0d1a4b25cc2ae9e10ccde0481b255637ad`; the authorized round then advanced local, remote, and PR head together to `cf76637ada4ba0263e36f30c23a278826c48dd0a` in the one allowed comparison.\n\n## Round 9 verification evidence\n\n- Focused testing: all 41 `@mcpfn/client` tests, 121 target-suite/remote-target `@mcpfn/testing` tests, and 15 conformance-cleanup `@mcpfn/cli` tests passed (177 total).\n- Typechecks: `@mcpfn/client`, `@mcpfn/testing`, and `@mcpfn/cli` passed under Node 22.\n- Release gate: `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed every reported package test/typecheck/build, Playwright, official conformance, mixed-entry redaction, examples, ESM/CJS imports, dry-run packs, packed-consumer installation, and round trips.\n- `git diff --check`: passed; the whole seven-file code/test batch and affected producer/consumer boundaries were reviewed before staging.\n- Hosted CI/reviewer state will not be refetched or polled after this snapshot.\n\n## Round 9 termination\n\n- Result: nonterminal recurring run; the four selected code roots are fixed and pushed, but the preserved deferred analyzer family prevents a clean assessment.\n- Automation remains disabled from the earlier retrieval-discovery stop and was not silently re-enabled during this manual retry.\n- No post-push review refetch, CI poll, reviewer wait, thread resolution, review dismissal, merge, or second fix loop will be performed.\n\n## Round 10 assessment\n\n- Hosted workflow: `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.2.0`, revision `4`, digest `sha256:8781c1c12fe9d5902337d6cf21bfbac49dd3a94c7eadd46bf2622db350444022` (published identity verified through Skillplane via Composio before repository mutation).\n- Mode: assessment reset. Round 10 is the next separately invoked single review round; the prior clean streak remains `0`.\n- Complete snapshot: captured onc