{"timestamp":"2026-09-21T08:39:22.647Z","ordinal":5631,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0b3f5-d570-7a72-b668-401efd539e3b","turn_id":"01a0c31e-6a96-7383-bda9-a191f2448a61","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-053b4504-6a81-4e8d-80dd-074289378ac2","process_id":"7369","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,240p' /Users/serro/.agents/skills/skillplane/SKILL.md\nsed -n '1,260p' /Users/serro/.agents/skills/composio-cli/SKILL.md\nsed -n '1,260p' /Users/serro/.agents/skills/using-21nco-github/SKILL.md\nrg -n \"PR #170|pr-refetch-fix|convergence|remediation ledger|Skillplane\" /Users/serro/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | head -n 80"],"cwd":"file:///Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,240p' /Users/serro/.agents/skills/skillplane/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":"/Users/serro/.agents/skills/skillplane/SKILL.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,260p' /Users/serro/.agents/skills/composio-cli/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":"/Users/serro/.agents/skills/composio-cli/SKILL.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,260p' /Users/serro/.agents/skills/using-21nco-github/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":"/Users/serro/.agents/skills/using-21nco-github/SKILL.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'PR #170|pr-refetch-fix|convergence|remediation ledger|Skillplane' /Users/serro/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md","query":"PR #170|pr-refetch-fix|convergence|remediation ledger|Skillplane","path":"MEMORY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"---\nname: use-skillplane\ndescription: Use skillplane to resolve skill\n---\n\n# Skillplane\n\nSkillplane is user's hosted skills platform. Retrieve user's skill using the slug or skill name provided and use that to execute the requested task.\n\nNOTE: Always retrieve and read the hosted skill first before working on the task. If the skill is not found, return an error message indicating the skill could not be located.\n\n## Using skillplane\nTry these in this order to communicate with user's Skillplane for skill retrieval, creation, amend etc.\n1. Direct Skillplane MCP if available and authenticated\n2. Direct Skillplane CLI if available and authenticated\n3. Via Composio CLI if available and authenticated\n4. Via Rex CLI if available and authenticated\n\n## Using tools mentioned in skillplane skills\nWhen executing a skill retrieved from Skillplane, use the tools referenced within the skill's definition to complete the task. Example tools: Linear, Notion, etc. Tool/Integrations resolution order:\n1. Direct integrations or MCP if available and authenticated\n2. Via Orca CLI if available and authenticated\n3. Via Composio CLI if available and authenticated\n4. Via Rex CLI if available and authenticated\n---\nname: composio-cli\ndescription: Help users operate the published Composio CLI to find the right tool, connect accounts, inspect schemas, execute tools, subscribe to trigger events with `composio listen`, script workflows with `composio run`, and call authenticated app APIs with `composio proxy`. Use when the user asks how to do something with `composio`, wants to run a known tool slug, needs to discover a slug with `composio search`, fix a missing connection with `composio link`, inspect tool inputs with `--get-schema` or `--dry-run`, troubleshoot top-level CLI flows, or explicitly needs `composio dev` guidance.\n---\n\n<!-- AUTO-GENERATED: edit skills-src/composio-cli/index.ts and rebuild -->\n<!-- release-channel: stable -->\n\n# Composio CLI\n\n## Default Workflow\n\n1. Start with `composio execute <slug>` whenever the slug is known.\n2. If several independent tool calls must happen at once, use `composio execute -p/--parallel` with repeated `<slug> -d <json>` groups.\n3. If `execute` says the toolkit is not connected, run `composio link <toolkit>` and retry.\n4. If the arguments are unclear, run `composio execute <slug> --get-schema` or `--dry-run` before guessing.\n5. Reach for `composio search \"<task>\"` only when the slug is unknown. `search` accepts one or more queries, so batch related discovery work into a single command when useful.\n\n## `execute` - Run A Tool\n\nUse `execute` when the tool slug is already known.\n\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_GET_THE_AUTHENTICATED_USER -d '{}'\n```\n\nInspect required inputs without executing:\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE --get-schema\n```\n\nPreview safely:\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE --skip-connection-check --dry-run -d '{ owner: \"acme\", repo: \"app\", title: \"Bug report\", body: \"Steps to reproduce...\" }'\n```\n\nPass data from a file or stdin:\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE -d @issue.json\ncat issue.json | composio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE -d -\n```\n\nUpload a local file:\n```bash\ncomposio execute SLACK_UPLOAD_OR_CREATE_A_FILE_IN_SLACK \\\n  --file ./image.png \\\n  -d '{ channels: \"C123\" }'\n```\n\nRun independent tool calls in parallel:\n```bash\ncomposio execute --parallel \\\n  GMAIL_SEND_EMAIL -d '{ recipient_email: \"a@b.com\", subject: \"Hi\" }' \\\n  GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE -d '{ owner: \"acme\", repo: \"app\", title: \"Bug\" }'\n```\n\nKey flags:\n- `--get-schema`: Inspect required arguments without executing the tool.\n- `--dry-run`: Preview the request shape without performing the action.\n- `--file`: Inject a local file path into a tool that exposes exactly one uploadable file argument.\n- `--parallel`: Execute multiple independent tool calls in the same invocation.\n- `--account`: Select which connected account to use by alias, word_id, or account id when multiple accounts exist for the same toolkit.\n\n- `--file` only works when the tool exposes a single uploadable file input. Otherwise use explicit `-d` JSON.\n\n## `search` - Find The Slug\n\nUse `search` only when the tool slug is not already known.\n\n```bash\ncomposio search \"create a github issue\"\ncomposio search \"send an email\" --toolkits gmail\ncomposio search \"send an email\" \"create a github issue\"\ncomposio search \"my emails\" \"my github issues\" --toolkits gmail,github\n```\n\n- Batch related discovery work into one `search` invocation, then move back to `execute` once the correct slugs are known.\n\n## `link` - Connect An Account\n\nUse `link` when `execute` reports that a toolkit is not connected, or when the user explicitly wants to authorize an account.\n\n```bash\ncomposio link gmail\ncomposio link googlecalendar --no-browser\n```\n\nKey flags:\n- `--alias`: Assign an alias to the connected account. Required when creating an additional account for the same toolkit.\n\n- Retry the original `execute` command after linking succeeds.\n\n## `proxy` - Raw API Access\n\nUse `proxy` when a toolkit supports a raw API operation that is easier than finding a dedicated tool slug.\n\n```bash\ncomposio proxy https://api.github.com/user --toolkit github --account work --method GET </dev/null\n```\n\nKey flags:\n- `--account`: Select which connected account to use by alias, word_id, or account id.\n\n## `run` - Scripting, LLMs, and Programmatic Workflows\n\nFor programmatic calls, loops, output plumbing, or anything beyond a single tool call, prefer `composio run`.\n\n`composio run` executes an inline ESM JavaScript/TypeScript snippet with authenticated `execute()`, `search()`, `proxy()`, and the experimental `experimental_subAgent()` helper pre-injected. No SDK setup required.\n\nChain multiple tools:\n```bash\ncomposio run '\n  const me = await execute(\"GITHUB_GET_THE_AUTHENTICATED_USER\");\n  const emails = await execute(\"GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS\", { max_results: 1 });\n  console.log({ login: me.data.login, fetchedEmails: !!emails.data });\n'\n```\n\nFan out with Promise.all:\n```bash\ncomposio run '\n  const [me, emails] = await Promise.all([\n    execute(\"GITHUB_GET_THE_AUTHENTICATED_USER\"),\n    execute(\"GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS\", { max_results: 5 }),\n  ]);\n  console.log({ login: me.data.login, emailCount: emails.data.messages?.length });\n'\n```\n\nFeed tool output into an LLM and get structured JSON back:\n```bash\ncomposio run --logs-off '\n  const emails = await execute(\"GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS\", { max_results: 5 });\n  const brief = await experimental_subAgent(\n    `Summarize these emails and count them.\\n\\n${emails.prompt()}`,\n    { schema: z.object({ summary: z.string(), count: z.number() }) }\n  );\n  console.log(brief.structuredOutput);\n'\n```\n\n- Use top-level `execute --parallel` instead when the user only needs a few independent tool calls and does not need script logic.\n\n## Auth\n\n```bash\ncomposio whoami   # check current session\ncomposio login    # authenticate if whoami fails\n```\n\n## Escalate Only When Needed\n\nIf the user is stuck on top-level commands or needs fallback inspection commands, load [references/troubleshooting.md](references/troubleshooting.md).\n\nIf the user explicitly asks about developer projects, auth configs, connected accounts, triggers, logs, orgs, or projects, load [references/composio-dev.md](references/composio-dev.md). `composio dev` is not the default end-user path.\n---\nname: using-21nco-github\ndescription: Uses the thyaravind GitHub account for repositories under dev/n or with a 21nCo origin. Use for any GitHub CLI, pull request, issue, release, or repository operation in those repositories.\n---\n\n# Using 21nCo GitHub\n\nFor any repository whose path is under `dev/n` or whose Git remote belongs to `21nCo`:\n\n- Run every `gh` command with `GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other`.\n- Verify `GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other gh auth status` reports `thyaravind` as the active account before making changes.\n- Never use the default GitHub account or silently fall back to another account.\n- Use the existing `21nCo` remote for pushes. If `thyaravind` lacks permission, stop and report the denial instead of creating a fork or alternate remote.\n148:- git worktree list --porcelain, gh pr list, GH_CONFIG_DIR, 21nCo/super-functions, 21nCo/superfunctions, docs/http-decode-params, sfns-4-rex-upstream, prunable-worktree, PR #188, PR #179, PR #170\n158:- At the September 17 snapshot, `superfunctions-dev`/`docs/http-decode-params` matched clean PR #188; SFNS-4/`sfns-4-rex-upstream` matched dirty PR #179; `/private/tmp/pr170-refetch-fix.h2yq4m` was missing and prunable, associated with PR #170. [Task 1]\n247:# Task Group: September 16 Skillplane PR #38 bounded DataFn date-cursor remediation\n248:scope: Use for the exact bounded `pr-review-fix` workflow or date-valued DataFn HTTP cursor pagination defects in Skillplane.\n301:- SFNS-4, PR #179, pr-refetch-fix, reviewThreads, adapterNamespace, Retry-After, tenantId, SecFn readJson, e200f50d, 511c02a\n320:# Task Group: September 16 Skillplane SKI-17 read-only review and Linear acceptance completeness\n321:scope: Use for strict read-only review of Skillplane DataFn upgrade work, especially when local code looks complete but acceptance criteria may require deployed-region verification.\n349:# Task Group: September 16 Skillplane Linear issue verification and published-contract blocker\n380:- When direct Skillplane/Linear MCP fails with `oauth_token_invalid_grant`, retrieve the hosted workflow via Composio and read the issue through `orca linear issue --current --full --json`; do not substitute cached instructions. [Task 1][Task 2]\n389:# Task Group: September 15 Superfunctions PR #170 bounded remediation and dirty-dev reconciliation\n390:scope: Use for live hosted `pr-refetch-fix` work on McpFn PR #170, or scoped publication/reconciliation from a dirty, stale Superfunctions dev checkout.\n393:## Task 1: Harden PR #170 redaction/export invariants in a bounded hosted round, success\n403:- PR #170, pr-refetch-fix, reviewThreads, GH_CONFIG_DIR, gate:mcpfn-release, McpFnRemoteCredentialLease, cleanupPhase, redaction, 8b23aaa, 1e45b794\n417:- when the user invokes `use-skillplane PR #170 pr-refetch-fix` -> retrieve the exact live hosted workflow; make one snapshot/fix/verify/commit/push pass, verify the required head once, then stop without refetching reviews, polling CI, or merging. [Task 1]\n423:- Use `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other` for GitHub commands. Page every GraphQL `reviewThreads` cursor: PR #170’s first 100-thread result had `hasNextPage: true`; only a three-page, 284-thread snapshot was complete. [Task 1]\n465:## Task 1: Diagnose Skillplane MCP visibility and Codex MCP removal, partial\n469:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/15/rollout-2026-09-15T13-28-31-01a0a413-1d4e-75b2-b09c-73af08420dc3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T08:05:33+00:00, thread_id=01a0a413-1d4e-75b2-b09c-73af08420dc3, configured Skillplane was not model-visible)\n490:- when the user asks to check Skillplane MCP tools -> distinguish enabled/configured registration from model-visible callable tools; use direct MCP first and Composio CLI fallback if unavailable. [Task 1][ad-hoc note]\n496:- `codex mcp list`/`get` only establish configuration; tool inventory establishes model visibility. If direct Skillplane MCP is unavailable, retrieve the live hosted workflow with the configured Composio fallback rather than cached local instructions. [Task 1][ad-hoc note]\n503:- Do not claim Skillplane access from a configured endpoint alone. `curl: (6) Could not resolve host: mcp.skillplane.dev` was sandbox-only evidence, and the escalation was aborted. [Task 1]\n673:# Task Group: September 13 Skillplane release, PR remediation, worktree sync, and reuse boundaries\n674:scope: Use for Skillplane tagged CLI publication, bounded live-review remediation, approved worktree cleanup, or deciding whether Superfunctions/CliFn is contract-compatible.\n685:- PR #23, reviewThreads(first:100), GH_CONFIG_DIR, pr-refetch-fix, projections, SQLite writer lock, SkillEditor, CompositionPanel, SonarQube, 7715373, 83058246\n719:- when the user says “splane pr review fix” -> use live direct Skillplane MCP when available, otherwise Composio; classify current findings, take one bounded review/fix/verify/push round, and stop without post-push polling. [Task 1]\n722:- when the user asks whether Skillplane can use Superfunctions or says “how about clifn?” -> inspect actual package contracts and preserve product-owned security/domain behavior rather than equating similar plumbing. [Task 4]\n730:- Prefer `@superfunctions/observability` and possibly `@superfunctions/http-hono` as narrow infrastructure candidates. Do not replace Skillplane search/storage/MCP/CLI security contracts: signed authorization-filtered cursors, immutable digest-verified bundles, Keychain/Secret Service credentials, `O_NOFOLLOW` filesystem safety, and transport-error redaction are product-owned. CliFn fits repeated scripts more than the local-runtime command graph. [Task 4]\n736:- Do not use CliFn credentials or generic runner errors as-is: its INI API-key store and thrown-message serialization conflict with Skillplane's secret-store and redaction requirements. [Task 4]\n791:# Task Group: September 13 Skillplane worktree cleanup and PR #21 synchronization\n792:scope: Use for evidence-backed Skillplane worktree inventory/removal or reconciling stale primary-checkout changes with a squash-merged PR.\n847:scope: Use for live hosted Skillplane PR-quality review, one bounded remediation round, or an explicitly authorized Superfunctions merge.\n858:- splane, PR #174, PR #177, SFNS-3, OAuth invalid_grant, Composio CLI, 21n/pr-quality-analysis@1.0.0, pr-refetch-fix, gate:reviewfn-release, package-lock, d4de3791\n862:- when direct Skillplane MCP fails with OAuth `invalid_grant` -> retrieve the exact hosted workflow through Composio CLI before declaring access blocked; do not substitute cached local instructions. [Task 1]\n906:# Task Group: September 12 Skillplane hosted PR quality analysis and publication\n907:scope: Use for `splane pr-quality-analysis` of open Skillplane PRs, exact-head probes, Notion publication, and review provenance.\n910:## Task 1: Review open Skillplane PRs #17, #20, and #21, success\n920:## Task 2: Remediate open Skillplane review findings in one bounded round, success\n938:- If direct Skillplane MCP is unavailable, discover Composio schemas once, retrieve the live skill with `CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILL_RETRIEVE`, and reuse the resolved tool shapes. Separate reviewer runtime from PR author/implementation provenance. [Task 1]\n948:# Task Group: September 12 Skillplane local-first runtime, native composition, and Linear document retrieval\n949:scope: Use for SKI-15/SKI-3 local-first and composition work, or when retrieving Skillplane Linear documents through Composio.\n973:## Task 3: Inventory and remove only requested safe Skillplane worktrees, success\n986:- when the user invokes `splane` or requests communication with Skillplane -> prefer the direct Skillplane MCP; if unavailable or unreachable, use Composio CLI to discover schemas and communicate through the intended connected account. Do not substitute a local cached skill merely because direct MCP is unavailable. [ad-hoc note]\n1123:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-10T14-20-26-2rMD-mcp1_transport_neutral_conformance_pr_170.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/10/rollout-2026-09-10T19-50-26-01a08bb0-f9fe-7951-aed1-965679939fc3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-10T15:17:36+00:00, thread_id=01a08bb0-f9fe-7951-aed1-965679939fc3, PR #170 local release gate passed; hosted CI queued)\n1206:# Task Group: September 11 Skillplane PR #14 exact-head remediation, conditional merge, and worktree cleanup\n1207:scope: Use for a bounded hosted PR remediation, conditional exact-head merge, and separately authorized removal of merged Skillplane worktrees.\n1666:# Task Group: September 8-15 Superfunctions PR quality, issue-grounded review, and PR #170 convergence\n1667:scope: Use for broad read-only Superfunctions PR review, comparative findings/quality reporting, follow-up assessment, and root-cause remediation convergence across DataFn/UIFN/McpFn.\n1670:## Task 1: Review requested live Superfunctions PRs and diagnose remediation convergence, partial\n1674:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T14-45-31-01a07b26-bb2c-7b32-95a4-8fb6b484fad0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T07:43:24+00:00, thread_id=01a07b26-bb2c-7b32-95a4-8fb6b484fad0, complete comparative report was not delivered; PR #170 symptom-patching convergence failure documented)\n1678:- GH_CONFIG_DIR, gh pr list, PR #144, PR #145, PR #149, PR #150, PR #151, PR #152, PR #153, PR #155, PR #170, reviewThreads, Sonar, convergence, root-cause\n1690:## Task 3: Evaluate PR #170 and all subsequent fixes, partial\n1698:- PR #170, MCP-1, transport-neutral conformance, aa08ef72e, reviewThreads(first:100), isOutdated, JUnit, --visible-tools, redaction, ESM/CJS, GH_CONFIG_DIR\n1703:- when the user asks to evaluate “PR #170 and all subsequent PR fixes” -> assess both history and exact current head, enumerate all commits/review surfaces/checks, and finish the requested verdict before pursuing unrelated PR material. [Task 3]\n1704:- when remediation repeatedly finds adjacent variants, the user asked to “strive for convergence and broader look” -> reset to the shared invariant/subsystem rather than publish another one-example symptom patch. [Task 1]\n1714:- For PR #170, paginate `pullRequest.reviewThreads(first:100,after:$endCursor)` and separate `isOutdated` from current unresolved threads; snapshot base/head OIDs, commits, local exact-head source, and hosted checks independently. The captured head `aa08ef72e` was open/mergeable but `UNSTABLE`, with 34 current unresolved threads and 10 pending checks; do not call it merge-ready from focused tests or resolved threads. [Task 3]\n1725:# Task Group: September 8-9 Skillplane PR #8 review-fix quality, migration hardening, and chronology\n1726:scope: Use for a bounded current-review remediation or a timestamped quality comparison of Skillplane PR #8 fixes; distinguish cumulative-head evidence from commit-specific proof.\n1880:# Task Group: September 3 Skillplane Factory MCP Unicode-regex schema compatibility\n1881:scope: Use to diagnose a client rejecting Skillplane's generic MCP tool catalog before tool invocation.\n1892:- Skillplane___skills_search, `^[\\\\p{L}\\\\p{N}._:-]+$`, Factory Droid, JSON Schema, Zod, `rg -F`, disabledTools, skills_list, skill_retrieve\n1901:- Literal `\\\\p{L}` searches can make ripgrep parse an invalid Unicode class; use `rg -F`. Do not misdiagnose this as Skillplane search or PR access failure. [Task 1]\n2159:- splane, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1, PR #133, DocsFn, GH_CONFIG_DIR, release-gate, OAuth, authorization-server issuer, @next/swc-darwin-arm64, SvelteKit\n2173:- when the user says `splane` -> retrieve the exact hosted Skillplane workflow live through MCP rather than substituting local instructions or memory. [Task 1]\n2175:- for `pr-refetch-fix` -> perform one snapshot/fix/verify/commit/push round; do not refetch reviews or poll CI afterward. [Task 1]\n2187:- Symptom: repeated Skillplane login prompts. Cause: refresh state lacks the authorization-server issuer. Fix: one `codex mcp logout skillplane`, then one `codex mcp login skillplane`. [Task 1]\n2225:- splane, pr-refetch-fix, PR #139, applyOmit, applyOmitToArrayValue, nested arrays, userId, datafn/server/src/execution/query/select.ts, ff833823\n2249:- when the user invokes `splane` -> resolve the exact hosted Skillplane workflow live; this rollout used `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1` rather than local instructions. [Task 1]\n2312:- A dirty checkout 83 commits behind `origin/dev` cannot establish current repository truth. Inspect live remote code and do not treat the private traversal or Skillplane duplicate helper as a shipped canonical API. [Task 1]\n2315:scope: Use for bounded PR #569 review/merge work, Skillplane OAuth recovery, or a read-only Nucleus worktree removal-safety classification.\n2318:## Task 1: Run one hosted Skillplane PR #569 review-fix round and diagnose OAuth churn, success\n2326:- splane, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1, PR #569, OAuth refresh credentials, authorization server issuer, codex mcp logout skillplane, codex mcp login skillplane, sslmode, sslrootcert, resolveClientIp, 400ee32b\n2346:- 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1, PR #569, reviewThreads, 49d13ae6, merge-async, gh-other, 9971f77, SonarCloud, CircleCI, Vercel\n2350:- when the user writes `splane` -> resolve the exact hosted Skillplane workflow live through MCP rather than using local instructions or memory. [Task 1]\n2353:- when hosted Skillplane OAuth failed, the user said “use local cached version of the skill” -> use that exact cached published workflow only after explicit authorization; a no-change round does not authorize edits or polling. [Task 3]\n2358:- A `pr-refetch-fix` invocation is one review snapshot, narrow fixes, proportionate verification, at most one commit/push, and one head comparison; preserve a divergent local PR branch under a backup ref and use a clean exact-head worktree. PR #569 fixed duplicate `sslmode`/`sslrootcert` values with `URL.searchParams.getAll(...)`, and supplied Node AuthFn `resolveClientIp` preferring `cf-connecting-ip`, then first `x-forwarded-for`. [Task 1]\n2359:- Stale Skillplane OAuth refresh state missing the authorization-server issuer, rather than normal expiry, caused repeated prompts. The durable reset is one `codex mcp logout skillplane` followed by one `codex mcp login skillplane`; desktop, CLI, and IDE share this MCP configuration. [Task 1]\n2391:- splane pr refetch fix, PR #570, reviewThreads, GraphQL, df11df18, merge-async, direct_merge, f849c684, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1\n2408:# Task Group: August 31 Skillplane MCP schema, OAuth compatibility, production release, and DevFn local-development fit\n2409:scope: Use for strict MCP `skills_list` failures, OAuth redirect compatibility, production-only Skillplane releases, durable local verification, or assessing DevFn local-development fit.\n2432:## Task 3: Push and deploy Skillplane to production only, success\n2442:## Task 4: Assess DevFn for Skillplane local development, uncertain\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: use-skillplane\ndescription: Use skillplane to resolve skill\n---\n\n# Skillplane\n\nSkillplane is user's hosted skills platform. Retrieve user's skill using the slug or skill name provided and use that to execute the requested task.\n\nNOTE: Always retrieve and read the hosted skill first before working on the task. If the skill is not found, return an error message indicating the skill could not be located.\n\n## Using skillplane\nTry these in this order to communicate with user's Skillplane for skill retrieval, creation, amend etc.\n1. Direct Skillplane MCP if available and authenticated\n2. Direct Skillplane CLI if available and authenticated\n3. Via Composio CLI if available and authenticated\n4. Via Rex CLI if available and authenticated\n\n## Using tools mentioned in skillplane skills\nWhen executing a skill retrieved from Skillplane, use the tools referenced within the skill's definition to complete the task. Example tools: Linear, Notion, etc. Tool/Integrations resolution order:\n1. Direct integrations or MCP if available and authenticated\n2. Via Orca CLI if available and authenticated\n3. Via Composio CLI if available and authenticated\n4. Via Rex CLI if available and authenticated\n---\nname: composio-cli\ndescription: Help users operate the published Composio CLI to find the right tool, connect accounts, inspect schemas, execute tools, subscribe to trigger events with `composio listen`, script workflows with `composio run`, and call authenticated app APIs with `composio proxy`. Use when the user asks how to do something with `composio`, wants to run a known tool slug, needs to discover a slug with `composio search`, fix a missing connection with `composio link`, inspect tool inputs with `--get-schema` or `--dry-run`, troubleshoot top-level CLI flows, or explicitly needs `composio dev` guidance.\n---\n\n<!-- AUTO-GENERATED: edit skills-src/composio-cli/index.ts and rebuild -->\n<!-- release-channel: stable -->\n\n# Composio CLI\n\n## Default Workflow\n\n1. Start with `composio execute <slug>` whenever the slug is known.\n2. If several independent tool calls must happen at once, use `composio execute -p/--parallel` with repeated `<slug> -d <json>` groups.\n3. If `execute` says the toolkit is not connected, run `composio link <toolkit>` and retry.\n4. If the arguments are unclear, run `composio execute <slug> --get-schema` or `--dry-run` before guessing.\n5. Reach for `composio search \"<task>\"` only when the slug is unknown. `search` accepts one or more queries, so batch related discovery work into a single command when useful.\n\n## `execute` - Run A Tool\n\nUse `execute` when the tool slug is already known.\n\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_GET_THE_AUTHENTICATED_USER -d '{}'\n```\n\nInspect required inputs without executing:\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE --get-schema\n```\n\nPreview safely:\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE --skip-connection-check --dry-run -d '{ owner: \"acme\", repo: \"app\", title: \"Bug report\", body: \"Steps to reproduce...\" }'\n```\n\nPass data from a file or stdin:\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE -d @issue.json\ncat issue.json | composio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE -d -\n```\n\nUpload a local file:\n```bash\ncomposio execute SLACK_UPLOAD_OR_CREATE_A_FILE_IN_SLACK \\\n  --file ./image.png \\\n  -d '{ channels: \"C123\" }'\n```\n\nRun independent tool calls in parallel:\n```bash\ncomposio execute --parallel \\\n  GMAIL_SEND_EMAIL -d '{ recipient_email: \"a@b.com\", subject: \"Hi\" }' \\\n  GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE -d '{ owner: \"acme\", repo: \"app\", title: \"Bug\" }'\n```\n\nKey flags:\n- `--get-schema`: Inspect required arguments without executing the tool.\n- `--dry-run`: Preview the request shape without performing the action.\n- `--file`: Inject a local file path into a tool that exposes exactly one uploadable file argument.\n- `--parallel`: Execute multiple independent tool calls in the same invocation.\n- `--account`: Select which connected account to use by alias, word_id, or account id when multiple accounts exist for the same toolkit.\n\n- `--file` only works when the tool exposes a single uploadable file input. Otherwise use explicit `-d` JSON.\n\n## `search` - Find The Slug\n\nUse `search` only when the tool slug is not already known.\n\n```bash\ncomposio search \"create a github issue\"\ncomposio search \"send an email\" --toolkits gmail\ncomposio search \"send an email\" \"create a github issue\"\ncomposio search \"my emails\" \"my github issues\" --toolkits gmail,github\n```\n\n- Batch related discovery work into one `search` invocation, then move back to `execute` once the correct slugs are known.\n\n## `link` - Connect An Account\n\nUse `link` when `execute` reports that a toolkit is not connected, or when the user explicitly wants to authorize an account.\n\n```bash\ncomposio link gmail\ncomposio link googlecalendar --no-browser\n```\n\nKey flags:\n- `--alias`: Assign an alias to the connected account. Required when creating an additional account for the same toolkit.\n\n- Retry the original `execute` command after linking succeeds.\n\n## `proxy` - Raw API Access\n\nUse `proxy` when a toolkit supports a raw API operation that is easier than finding a dedicated tool slug.\n\n```bash\ncomposio proxy https://api.github.com/user --toolkit github --account work --method GET </dev/null\n```\n\nKey flags:\n- `--account`: Select which connected account to use by alias, word_id, or account id.\n\n## `run` - Scripting, LLMs, and Programmatic Workflows\n\nFor programmatic calls, loops, output plumbing, or anything beyond a single tool call, prefer `composio run`.\n\n`composio run` executes an inline ESM JavaScript/TypeScript snippet with authenticated `execute()`, `search()`, `proxy()`, and the experimental `experimental_subAgent()` helper pre-injected. No SDK setup required.\n\nChain multiple tools:\n```bash\ncomposio run '\n  const me = await execute(\"GITHUB_GET_THE_AUTHENTICATED_USER\");\n  const emails = await execute(\"GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS\", { max_results: 1 });\n  console.log({ login: me.data.login, fetchedEmails: !!emails.data });\n'\n```\n\nFan out with Promise.all:\n```bash\ncomposio run '\n  const [me, emails] = await Promise.all([\n    execute(\"GITHUB_GET_THE_AUTHENTICATED_USER\"),\n    execute(\"GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS\", { max_results: 5 }),\n  ]);\n  console.log({ login: me.data.login, emailCount: emails.data.messages?.length });\n'\n```\n\nFeed tool output into an LLM and get structured JSON back:\n```bash\ncomposio run --logs-off '\n  const emails = await execute(\"GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS\", { max_results: 5 });\n  const brief = await experimental_subAgent(\n    `Summarize these emails and count them.\\n\\n${emails.prompt()}`,\n    { schema: z.object({ summary: z.string(), count: z.number() }) }\n  );\n  console.log(brief.structuredOutput);\n'\n```\n\n- Use top-level `execute --parallel` instead when the user only needs a few independent tool calls and does not need script logic.\n\n## Auth\n\n```bash\ncomposio whoami   # check current session\ncomposio login    # authenticate if whoami fails\n```\n\n## Escalate Only When Needed\n\nIf the user is stuck on top-level commands or needs fallback inspection commands, load [references/troubleshooting.md](references/troubleshooting.md).\n\nIf the user explicitly asks about developer projects, auth configs, connected accounts, triggers, logs, orgs, or projects, load [references/composio-dev.md](references/composio-dev.md). `composio dev` is not the default end-user path.\n---\nname: using-21nco-github\ndescription: Uses the thyaravind GitHub account for repositories under dev/n or with a 21nCo origin. Use for any GitHub CLI, pull request, issue, release, or repository operation in those repositories.\n---\n\n# Using 21nCo GitHub\n\nFor any repository whose path is under `dev/n` or whose Git remote belongs to `21nCo`:\n\n- Run every `gh` command with `GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other`.\n- Verify `GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other gh auth status` reports `thyaravind` as the active account before making changes.\n- Never use the default GitHub account or silently fall back to another account.\n- Use the existing `21nCo` remote for pushes. If `thyaravind` lacks permission, stop and report the denial instead of creating a fork or alternate remote.\n148:- git worktree list --porcelain, gh pr list, GH_CONFIG_DIR, 21nCo/super-functions, 21nCo/superfunctions, docs/http-decode-params, sfns-4-rex-upstream, prunable-worktree, PR #188, PR #179, PR #170\n158:- At the September 17 snapshot, `superfunctions-dev`/`docs/http-decode-params` matched clean PR #188; SFNS-4/`sfns-4-rex-upstream` matched dirty PR #179; `/private/tmp/pr170-refetch-fix.h2yq4m` was missing and prunable, associated with PR #170. [Task 1]\n247:# Task Group: September 16 Skillplane PR #38 bounded DataFn date-cursor remediation\n248:scope: Use for the exact bounded `pr-review-fix` workflow or date-valued DataFn HTTP cursor pagination defects in Skillplane.\n301:- SFNS-4, PR #179, pr-refetch-fix, reviewThreads, adapterNamespace, Retry-After, tenantId, SecFn readJson, e200f50d, 511c02a\n320:# Task Group: September 16 Skillplane SKI-17 read-only review and Linear acceptance completeness\n321:scope: Use for strict read-only review of Skillplane DataFn upgrade work, especially when local code looks complete but acceptance criteria may require deployed-region verification.\n349:# Task Group: September 16 Skillplane Linear issue verification and published-contract blocker\n380:- When direct Skillplane/Linear MCP fails with `oauth_token_invalid_grant`, retrieve the hosted workflow via Composio and read the issue through `orca linear issue --current --full --json`; do not substitute cached instructions. [Task 1][Task 2]\n389:# Task Group: September 15 Superfunctions PR #170 bounded remediation and dirty-dev reconciliation\n390:scope: Use for live hosted `pr-refetch-fix` work on McpFn PR #170, or scoped publication/reconciliation from a dirty, stale Superfunctions dev checkout.\n393:## Task 1: Harden PR #170 redaction/export invariants in a bounded hosted round, success\n403:- PR #170, pr-refetch-fix, reviewThreads, GH_CONFIG_DIR, gate:mcpfn-release, McpFnRemoteCredentialLease, cleanupPhase, redaction, 8b23aaa, 1e45b794\n417:- when the user invokes `use-skillplane PR #170 pr-refetch-fix` -> retrieve the exact live hosted workflow; make one snapshot/fix/verify/commit/push pass, verify the required head once, then stop without refetching reviews, polling CI, or merging. [Task 1]\n423:- Use `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other` for GitHub commands. Page every GraphQL `reviewThreads` cursor: PR #170’s first 100-thread result had `hasNextPage: true`; only a three-page, 284-thread snapshot was complete. [Task 1]\n465:## Task 1: Diagnose Skillplane MCP visibility and Codex MCP removal, partial\n469:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/15/rollout-2026-09-15T13-28-31-01a0a413-1d4e-75b2-b09c-73af08420dc3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T08:05:33+00:00, thread_id=01a0a413-1d4e-75b2-b09c-73af08420dc3, configured Skillplane was not model-visible)\n490:- when the user asks to check Skillplane MCP tools -> distinguish enabled/configured registration from model-visible callable tools; use direct MCP first and Composio CLI fallback if unavailable. [Task 1][ad-hoc note]\n496:- `codex mcp list`/`get` only establish configuration; tool inventory establishes model visibility. If direct Skillplane MCP is unavailable, retrieve the live hosted workflow with the configured Composio fallback rather than cached local instructions. [Task 1][ad-hoc note]\n503:- Do not claim Skillplane access from a configured endpoint alone. `curl: (6) Could not resolve host: mcp.skillplane.dev` was sandbox-only evidence, and the escalation was aborted. [Task 1]\n673:# Task Group: September 13 Skillplane release, PR remediation, worktree sync, and reuse boundaries\n674:scope: Use for Skillplane tagged CLI publication, bounded live-review remediation, approved worktree cleanup, or deciding whether Superfunctions/CliFn is contract-compatible.\n685:- PR #23, reviewThreads(first:100), GH_CONFIG_DIR, pr-refetch-fix, projections, SQLite writer lock, SkillEditor, CompositionPanel, SonarQube, 7715373, 83058246\n719:- when the user says “splane pr review fix” -> use live direct Skillplane MCP when available, otherwise Composio; classify current findings, take one bounded review/fix/verify/push round, and stop without post-push polling. [Task 1]\n722:- when the user asks whether Skillplane can use Superfunctions or says “how about clifn?” -> inspect actual package contracts and preserve product-owned security/domain behavior rather than equating similar plumbing. [Task 4]\n730:- Prefer `@superfunctions/observability` and possibly `@superfunctions/http-hono` as narrow infrastructure candidates. Do not replace Skillplane search/storage/MCP/CLI security contracts: signed authorization-filtered cursors, immutable digest-verified bundles, Keychain/Secret Service credentials, `O_NOFOLLOW` filesystem safety, and transport-error redaction are product-owned. CliFn fits repeated scripts more than the local-runtime command graph. [Task 4]\n736:- Do not use CliFn credentials or generic runner errors as-is: its INI API-key store and thrown-message serialization conflict with Skillplane's secret-store and redaction requirements. [Task 4]\n791:# Task Group: September 13 Skillplane worktree cleanup and PR #21 synchronization\n792:scope: Use for evidence-backed Skillplane worktree inventory/removal or reconciling stale primary-checkout changes with a squash-merged PR.\n847:scope: Use for live hosted Skillplane PR-quality review, one bounded remediation round, or an explicitly authorized Superfunctions merge.\n858:- splane, PR #174, PR #177, SFNS-3, OAuth invalid_grant, Composio CLI, 21n/pr-quality-analysis@1.0.0, pr-refetch-fix, gate:reviewfn-release, package-lock, d4de3791\n862:- when direct Skillplane MCP fails with OAuth `invalid_grant` -> retrieve the exact hosted workflow through Composio CLI before declaring access blocked; do not substitute cached local instructions. [Task 1]\n906:# Task Group: September 12 Skillplane hosted PR quality analysis and publication\n907:scope: Use for `splane pr-quality-analysis` of open Skillplane PRs, exact-head probes, Notion publication, and review provenance.\n910:## Task 1: Review open Skillplane PRs #17, #20, and #21, success\n920:## Task 2: Remediate open Skillplane review findings in one bounded round, success\n938:- If direct Skillplane MCP is unavailable, discover Composio schemas once, retrieve the live skill with `CUSTOM_SKILLPLANE_SKILL_RETRIEVE`, and reuse the resolved tool shapes. Separate reviewer runtime from PR author/implementation provenance. [Task 1]\n948:# Task Group: September 12 Skillplane local-first runtime, native composition, and Linear document retrieval\n949:scope: Use for SKI-15/SKI-3 local-first and composition work, or when retrieving Skillplane Linear documents through Composio.\n973:## Task 3: Inventory and remove only requested safe Skillplane worktrees, success\n986:- when the user invokes `splane` or requests communication with Skillplane -> prefer the direct Skillplane MCP; if unavailable or unreachable, use Composio CLI to discover schemas and communicate through the intended connected account. Do not substitute a local cached skill merely because direct MCP is unavailable. [ad-hoc note]\n1123:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-10T14-20-26-2rMD-mcp1_transport_neutral_conformance_pr_170.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/10/rollout-2026-09-10T19-50-26-01a08bb0-f9fe-7951-aed1-965679939fc3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-10T15:17:36+00:00, thread_id=01a08bb0-f9fe-7951-aed1-965679939fc3, PR #170 local release gate passed; hosted CI queued)\n1206:# Task Group: September 11 Skillplane PR #14 exact-head remediation, conditional merge, and worktree cleanup\n1207:scope: Use for a bounded hosted PR remediation, conditional exact-head merge, and separately authorized removal of merged Skillplane worktrees.\n1666:# Task Group: September 8-15 Superfunctions PR quality, issue-grounded review, and PR #170 convergence\n1667:scope: Use for broad read-only Superfunctions PR review, comparative findings/quality reporting, follow-up assessment, and root-cause remediation convergence across DataFn/UIFN/McpFn.\n1670:## Task 1: Review requested live Superfunctions PRs and diagnose remediation convergence, partial\n1674:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T14-45-31-01a07b26-bb2c-7b32-95a4-8fb6b484fad0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T07:43:24+00:00, thread_id=01a07b26-bb2c-7b32-95a4-8fb6b484fad0, complete comparative report was not delivered; PR #170 symptom-patching convergence failure documented)\n1678:- GH_CONFIG_DIR, gh pr list, PR #144, PR #145, PR #149, PR #150, PR #151, PR #152, PR #153, PR #155, PR #170, reviewThreads, Sonar, convergence, root-cause\n1690:## Task 3: Evaluate PR #170 and all subsequent fixes, partial\n1698:- PR #170, MCP-1, transport-neutral conformance, aa08ef72e, reviewThreads(first:100), isOutdated, JUnit, --visible-tools, redaction, ESM/CJS, GH_CONFIG_DIR\n1703:- when the user asks to evaluate “PR #170 and all subsequent PR fixes” -> assess both history and exact current head, enumerate all commits/review surfaces/checks, and finish the requested verdict before pursuing unrelated PR material. [Task 3]\n1704:- when remediation repeatedly finds adjacent variants, the user asked to “strive for convergence and broader look” -> reset to the shared invariant/subsystem rather than publish another one-example symptom patch. [Task 1]\n1714:- For PR #170, paginate `pullRequest.reviewThreads(first:100,after:$endCursor)` and separate `isOutdated` from current unresolved threads; snapshot base/head OIDs, commits, local exact-head source, and hosted checks independently. The captured head `aa08ef72e` was open/mergeable but `UNSTABLE`, with 34 current unresolved threads and 10 pending checks; do not call it merge-ready from focused tests or resolved threads. [Task 3]\n1725:# Task Group: September 8-9 Skillplane PR #8 review-fix quality, migration hardening, and chronology\n1726:scope: Use for a bounded current-review remediation or a timestamped quality comparison of Skillplane PR #8 fixes; distinguish cumulative-head evidence from commit-specific proof.\n1880:# Task Group: September 3 Skillplane Factory MCP Unicode-regex schema compatibility\n1881:scope: Use to diagnose a client rejecting Skillplane's generic MCP tool catalog before tool invocation.\n1892:- Skillplane___skills_search, `^[\\\\p{L}\\\\p{N}._:-]+$`, Factory Droid, JSON Schema, Zod, `rg -F`, disabledTools, skills_list, skill_retrieve\n1901:- Literal `\\\\p{L}` searches can make ripgrep parse an invalid Unicode class; use `rg -F`. Do not misdiagnose this as Skillplane search or PR access failure. [Task 1]\n2159:- splane, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1, PR #133, DocsFn, GH_CONFIG_DIR, release-gate, OAuth, authorization-server issuer, @next/swc-darwin-arm64, SvelteKit\n2173:- when the user says `splane` -> retrieve the exact hosted Skillplane workflow live through MCP rather than substituting local instructions or memory. [Task 1]\n2175:- for `pr-refetch-fix` -> perform one snapshot/fix/verify/commit/push round; do not refetch reviews or poll CI afterward. [Task 1]\n2187:- Symptom: repeated Skillplane login prompts. Cause: refresh state lacks the authorization-server issuer. Fix: one `codex mcp logout skillplane`, then one `codex mcp login skillplane`. [Task 1]\n2225:- splane, pr-refetch-fix, PR #139, applyOmit, applyOmitToArrayValue, nested arrays, userId, datafn/server/src/execution/query/select.ts, ff833823\n2249:- when the user invokes `splane` -> resolve the exact hosted Skillplane workflow live; this rollout used `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1` rather than local instructions. [Task 1]\n2312:- A dirty checkout 83 commits behind `origin/dev` cannot establish current repository truth. Inspect live remote code and do not treat the private traversal or Skillplane duplicate helper as a shipped canonical API. [Task 1]\n2315:scope: Use for bounded PR #569 review/merge work, Skillplane OAuth recovery, or a read-only Nucleus worktree removal-safety classification.\n2318:## Task 1: Run one hosted Skillplane PR #569 review-fix round and diagnose OAuth churn, success\n2326:- splane, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1, PR #569, OAuth refresh credentials, authorization server issuer, codex mcp logout skillplane, codex mcp login skillplane, sslmode, sslrootcert, resolveClientIp, 400ee32b\n2346:- 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1, PR #569, reviewThreads, 49d13ae6, merge-async, gh-other, 9971f77, SonarCloud, CircleCI, Vercel\n2350:- when the user writes `splane` -> resolve the exact hosted Skillplane workflow live through MCP rather than using local instructions or memory. [Task 1]\n2353:- when hosted Skillplane OAuth failed, the user said “use local cached version of the skill” -> use that exact cached published workflow only after explicit authorization; a no-change round does not authorize edits or polling. [Task 3]\n2358:- A `pr-refetch-fix` invocation is one review snapshot, narrow fixes, proportionate verification, at most one commit/push, and one head comparison; preserve a divergent local PR branch under a backup ref and use a clean exact-head worktree. PR #569 fixed duplicate `sslmode`/`sslrootcert` values with `URL.searchParams.getAll(...)`, and supplied Node AuthFn `resolveClientIp` preferring `cf-connecting-ip`, then first `x-forwarded-for`. [Task 1]\n2359:- Stale Skillplane OAuth refresh state missing the authorization-server issuer, rather than normal expiry, caused repeated prompts. The durable reset is one `codex mcp logout skillplane` followed by one `codex mcp login skillplane`; desktop, CLI, and IDE share this MCP configuration. [Task 1]\n2391:- splane pr refetch fix, PR #570, reviewThreads, GraphQL, df11df18, merge-async, direct_merge, f849c684, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1\n2408:# Task Group: August 31 Skillplane MCP schema, OAuth compatibility, production release, and DevFn local-development fit\n2409:scope: Use for strict MCP `skills_list` failures, OAuth redirect compatibility, production-only Skillplane releases, durable local verification, or assessing DevFn local-development fit.\n2432:## Task 3: Push and deploy Skillplane to production only, success\n2442:## Task 4: Assess DevFn for Skillplane local development, uncertain\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":16791},"formatted_output":"---\nname: use-skillplane\ndescription: Use skillplane to resolve skill\n---\n\n# Skillplane\n\nSkillplane is user's hosted skills platform. Retrieve user's skill using the slug or skill name provided and use that to execute the requested task.\n\nNOTE: Always retrieve and read the hosted skill first before working on the task. If the skill is not found, return an error message indicating the skill could not be located.\n\n## Using skillplane\nTry these in this order to communicate with user's Skillplane for skill retrieval, creation, amend etc.\n1. Direct Skillplane MCP if available and authenticated\n2. Direct Skillplane CLI if available and authenticated\n3. Via Composio CLI if available and authenticated\n4. Via Rex CLI if available and authenticated\n\n## Using tools mentioned in skillplane skills\nWhen executing a skill retrieved from Skillplane, use the tools referenced within the skill's definition to complete the task. Example tools: Linear, Notion, etc. Tool/Integrations resolution order:\n1. Direct integrations or MCP if available and authenticated\n2. Via Orca CLI if available and authenticated\n3. Via Composio CLI if available and authenticated\n4. Via Rex CLI if available and authenticated\n---\nname: composio-cli\ndescription: Help users operate the published Composio CLI to find the right tool, connect accounts, inspect schemas, execute tools, subscribe to trigger events with `composio listen`, script workflows with `composio run`, and call authenticated app APIs with `composio proxy`. Use when the user asks how to do something with `composio`, wants to run a known tool slug, needs to discover a slug with `composio search`, fix a missing connection with `composio link`, inspect tool inputs with `--get-schema` or `--dry-run`, troubleshoot top-level CLI flows, or explicitly needs `composio dev` guidance.\n---\n\n<!-- AUTO-GENERATED: edit skills-src/composio-cli/index.ts and rebuild -->\n<!-- release-channel: stable -->\n\n# Composio CLI\n\n## Default Workflow\n\n1. Start with `composio execute <slug>` whenever the slug is known.\n2. If several independent tool calls must happen at once, use `composio execute -p/--parallel` with repeated `<slug> -d <json>` groups.\n3. If `execute` says the toolkit is not connected, run `composio link <toolkit>` and retry.\n4. If the arguments are unclear, run `composio execute <slug> --get-schema` or `--dry-run` before guessing.\n5. Reach for `composio search \"<task>\"` only when the slug is unknown. `search` accepts one or more queries, so batch related discovery work into a single command when useful.\n\n## `execute` - Run A Tool\n\nUse `execute` when the tool slug is already known.\n\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_GET_THE_AUTHENTICATED_USER -d '{}'\n```\n\nInspect required inputs without executing:\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE --get-schema\n```\n\nPreview safely:\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE --skip-connection-check --dry-run -d '{ owner: \"acme\", repo: \"app\", title: \"Bug report\", body: \"Steps to reproduce...\" }'\n```\n\nPass data from a file or stdin:\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE -d @issue.json\ncat issue.json | composio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE -d -\n```\n\nUpload a local file:\n```bash\ncomposio execute SLACK_UPLOAD_OR_CREATE_A_FILE_IN_SLACK \\\n  --file ./image.png \\\n  -d '{ channels: \"C123\" }'\n```\n\nRun independent tool calls in parallel:\n```bash\ncomposio execute --parallel \\\n  GMAIL_SEND_EMAIL -d '{ recipient_email: \"a@b.com\", subject: \"Hi\" }' \\\n  GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE -d '{ owner: \"acme\", repo: \"app\", title: \"Bug\" }'\n```\n\nKey flags:\n- `--get-schema`: Inspect required arguments without executing the tool.\n- `--dry-run`: Preview the request shape without performing the action.\n- `--file`: Inject a local file path into a tool that exposes exactly one uploadable file argument.\n- `--parallel`: Execute multiple independent tool calls in the same invocation.\n- `--account`: Select which connected account to use by alias, word_id, or account id when multiple accounts exist for the same toolkit.\n\n- `--file` only works when the tool exposes a single uploadable file input. Otherwise use explicit `-d` JSON.\n\n## `search` - Find The Slug\n\nUse `search` only when the tool slug is not already known.\n\n```bash\ncomposio search \"create a github issue\"\ncomposio search \"send an email\" --toolkits gmail\ncomposio search \"send an email\" \"create a github issue\"\ncomposio search \"my emails\" \"my github issues\" --toolkits gmail,github\n```\n\n- Batch related discovery work into one `search` invocation, then move back to `execute` once the correct slugs are known.\n\n## `link` - Connect An Account\n\nUse `link` when `execute` reports that a toolkit is not connected, or when the user explicitly wants to authorize an account.\n\n```bash\ncomposio link gmail\ncomposio link googlecalendar --no-browser\n```\n\nKey flags:\n- `--alias`: Assign an alias to the connected account. Required when creating an additional account for the same toolkit.\n\n- Retry the original `execute` command after linking succeeds.\n\n## `proxy` - Raw API Access\n\nUse `proxy` when a toolkit supports a raw API operation that is easier than finding a dedicated tool slug.\n\n```bash\ncomposio proxy https://api.github.com/user --toolkit github --account work --method GET </dev/null\n```\n\nKey flags:\n- `--account`: Select which connected account to use by alias, word_id, or account id.\n\n## `run` - Scripting, LLMs, and Programmatic Workflows\n\nFor programmatic calls, loops, output plumbing, or anything beyond a single tool call, prefer `composio run`.\n\n`composio run` executes an inline ESM JavaScript/TypeScript snippet with authenticated `execute()`, `search()`, `proxy()`, and the experimental `experimental_subAgent()` helper pre-injected. No SDK setup required.\n\nChain multiple tools:\n```bash\ncomposio run '\n  const me = await execute(\"GITHUB_GET_THE_AUTHENTICATED_USER\");\n  const emails = await execute(\"GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS\", { max_results: 1 });\n  console.log({ login: me.data.login, fetchedEmails: !!emails.data });\n'\n```\n\nFan out with Promise.all:\n```bash\ncomposio run '\n  const [me, emails] = await Promise.all([\n    execute(\"GITHUB_GET_THE_AUTHENTICATED_USER\"),\n    execute(\"GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS\", { max_results: 5 }),\n  ]);\n  console.log({ login: me.data.login, emailCount: emails.data.messages?.length });\n'\n```\n\nFeed tool output into an LLM and get structured JSON back:\n```bash\ncomposio run --logs-off '\n  const emails = await execute(\"GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS\", { max_results: 5 });\n  const brief = await experimental_subAgent(\n    `Summarize these emails and count them.\\n\\n${emails.prompt()}`,\n    { schema: z.object({ summary: z.string(), count: z.number() }) }\n  );\n  console.log(brief.structuredOutput);\n'\n```\n\n- Use top-level `execute --parallel` instead when the user only needs a few independent tool calls and does not need script logic.\n\n## Auth\n\n```bash\ncomposio whoami   # check current session\ncomposio login    # authenticate if whoami fails\n```\n\n## Escalate Only When Needed\n\nIf the user is stuck on top-level commands or needs fallback inspection commands, load [references/troubleshooting.md](references/troubleshooting.md).\n\nIf the user explicitly asks about developer projects, auth configs, connected accounts, triggers, logs, orgs, or projects, load [references/composio-dev.md](references/composio-dev.md). `composio dev` is not the default end-user path.\n---\nname: using-21nco-github\ndescription: Uses the thyaravind GitHub account for repositories under dev/n or with a 21nCo origin. Use for any GitHub CLI, pull request, issue, release, or repository operation in those repositories.\n---\n\n# Using 21nCo GitHub\n\nFor any repository whose path is under `dev/n` or whose Git remote belongs to `21nCo`:\n\n- Run every `gh` command with `GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other`.\n- Verify `GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other gh auth status` reports `thyaravind` as the active account before making changes.\n- Never use the default GitHub account or silently fall back to another account.\n- Use the existing `21nCo` remote for pushes. If `thyaravind` lacks permission, stop and report the denial instead of creating a fork or alternate remote.\n148:- git worktree list --porcelain, gh pr list, GH_CONFIG_DIR, 21nCo/super-functions, 21nCo/superfunctions, docs/http-decode-params, sfns-4-rex-upstream, prunable-worktree, PR #188, PR #179, PR #170\n158:- At the September 17 snapshot, `superfunctions-dev`/`docs/http-decode-params` matched clean PR #188; SFNS-4/`sfns-4-rex-upstream` matched dirty PR #179; `/private/tmp/pr170-refetch-fix.h2yq4m` was missing and prunable, associated with PR #170. [Task 1]\n247:# Task Group: September 16 Skillplane PR #38 bounded DataFn date-cursor remediation\n248:scope: Use for the exact bounded `pr-review-fix` workflow or date-valued DataFn HTTP cursor pagination defects in Skillplane.\n301:- SFNS-4, PR #179, pr-refetch-fix, reviewThreads, adapterNamespace, Retry-After, tenantId, SecFn readJson, e200f50d, 511c02a\n320:# Task Group: September 16 Skillplane SKI-17 read-only review and Linear acceptance completeness\n321:scope: Use for strict read-only review of Skillplane DataFn upgrade work, especially when local code looks complete but acceptance criteria may require deployed-region verification.\n349:# Task Group: September 16 Skillplane Linear issue verification and published-contract blocker\n380:- When direct Skillplane/Linear MCP fails with `oauth_token_invalid_grant`, retrieve the hosted workflow via Composio and read the issue through `orca linear issue --current --full --json`; do not substitute cached instructions. [Task 1][Task 2]\n389:# Task Group: September 15 Superfunctions PR #170 bounded remediation and dirty-dev reconciliation\n390:scope: Use for live hosted `pr-refetch-fix` work on McpFn PR #170, or scoped publication/reconciliation from a dirty, stale Superfunctions dev checkout.\n393:## Task 1: Harden PR #170 redaction/export invariants in a bounded hosted round, success\n403:- PR #170, pr-refetch-fix, reviewThreads, GH_CONFIG_DIR, gate:mcpfn-release, McpFnRemoteCredentialLease, cleanupPhase, redaction, 8b23aaa, 1e45b794\n417:- when the user invokes `use-skillplane PR #170 pr-refetch-fix` -> retrieve the exact live hosted workflow; make one snapshot/fix/verify/commit/push pass, verify the required head once, then stop without refetching reviews, polling CI, or merging. [Task 1]\n423:- Use `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other` for GitHub commands. Page every GraphQL `reviewThreads` cursor: PR #170’s first 100-thread result had `hasNextPage: true`; only a three-page, 284-thread snapshot was complete. [Task 1]\n465:## Task 1: Diagnose Skillplane MCP visibility and Codex MCP removal, partial\n469:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/15/rollout-2026-09-15T13-28-31-01a0a413-1d4e-75b2-b09c-73af08420dc3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T08:05:33+00:00, thread_id=01a0a413-1d4e-75b2-b09c-73af08420dc3, configured Skillplane was not model-visible)\n490:- when the user asks to check Skillplane MCP tools -> distinguish enabled/configured registration from model-visible callable tools; use direct MCP first and Composio CLI fallback if unavailable. [Task 1][ad-hoc note]\n496:- `codex mcp list`/`get` only establish configuration; tool inventory establishes model visibility. If direct Skillplane MCP is unavailable, retrieve the live hosted workflow with the configured Composio fallback rather than cached local instructions. [Task 1][ad-hoc note]\n503:- Do not claim Skillplane access from a configured endpoint alone. `curl: (6) Could not resolve host: mcp.skillplane.dev` was sandbox-only evidence, and the escalation was aborted. [Task 1]\n673:# Task Group: September 13 Skillplane release, PR remediation, worktree sync, and reuse boundaries\n674:scope: Use for Skillplane tagged CLI publication, bounded live-review remediation, approved worktree cleanup, or deciding whether Superfunctions/CliFn is contract-compatible.\n685:- PR #23, reviewThreads(first:100), GH_CONFIG_DIR, pr-refetch-fix, projections, SQLite writer lock, SkillEditor, CompositionPanel, SonarQube, 7715373, 83058246\n719:- when the user says “splane pr review fix” -> use live direct Skillplane MCP when available, otherwise Composio; classify current findings, take one bounded review/fix/verify/push round, and stop without post-push polling. [Task 1]\n722:- when the user asks whether Skillplane can use Superfunctions or says “how about clifn?” -> inspect actual package contracts and preserve product-owned security/domain behavior rather than equating similar plumbing. [Task 4]\n730:- Prefer `@superfunctions/observability` and possibly `@superfunctions/http-hono` as narrow infrastructure candidates. Do not replace Skillplane search/storage/MCP/CLI security contracts: signed authorization-filtered cursors, immutable digest-verified bundles, Keychain/Secret Service credentials, `O_NOFOLLOW` filesystem safety, and transport-error redaction are product-owned. CliFn fits repeated scripts more than the local-runtime command graph. [Task 4]\n736:- Do not use CliFn credentials or generic runner errors as-is: its INI API-key store and thrown-message serialization conflict with Skillplane's secret-store and redaction requirements. [Task 4]\n791:# Task Group: September 13 Skillplane worktree cleanup and PR #21 synchronization\n792:scope: Use for evidence-backed Skillplane worktree inventory/removal or reconciling stale primary-checkout changes with a squash-merged PR.\n847:scope: Use for live hosted Skillplane PR-quality review, one bounded remediation round, or an explicitly authorized Superfunctions merge.\n858:- splane, PR #174, PR #177, SFNS-3, OAuth invalid_grant, Composio CLI, 21n/pr-quality-analysis@1.0.0, pr-refetch-fix, gate:reviewfn-release, package-lock, d4de3791\n862:- when direct Skillplane MCP fails with OAuth `invalid_grant` -> retrieve the exact hosted workflow through Composio CLI before declaring access blocked; do not substitute cached local instructions. [Task 1]\n906:# Task Group: September 12 Skillplane hosted PR quality analysis and publication\n907:scope: Use for `splane pr-quality-analysis` of open Skillplane PRs, exact-head probes, Notion publication, and review provenance.\n910:## Task 1: Review open Skillplane PRs #17, #20, and #21, success\n920:## Task 2: Remediate open Skillplane review findings in one bounded round, success\n938:- If direct Skillplane MCP is unavailable, discover Composio schemas once, retrieve the live