fix, structural report validation, optional inspector artifact keys, remote-target redaction helpers, and failure normalization. The prior throwing-`kind` cleanup thread is addressed and resolved. `git diff --check 80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1...HEAD` passed. Focused Vitest execution was unavailable because the repository lockfile blocks a clean install and the isolated workspace depends on unreleased `@mcpfn/client@0.0.4`. <!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --> <sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/35443246488/job/105897661544) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 5255776601,\n    \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n    \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-09-19T12:48:48Z\",\n    \"body\": \"\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 5255762575,\n    \"user\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\",\n    \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-09-19T12:41:37Z\",\n    \"body\": \" ### 💡 Codex Review Here are some automated review suggestions for this pull request. **Reviewed commit:** `9ee45f4385`      <details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary> <br/> [Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you - Open a pull request for review - Mark a draft as ready - Comment \\\"@codex review\\\". If Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍. Codex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".              </details>\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 5255760353,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-09-19T12:40:27Z\",\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:review-summary:start --> **1 issue found across 6 files (changes from recent commits).** <!-- cubic:review-summary:end --> <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents (unresolved issues)</summary> ```text Check if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately. <file name=\\\"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\\\"> <violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts:463\\\"> P2: When a target error supplies a nonstandard `phase`, suite finalization treats the legitimate failure as a credential-structure collision and throws instead of returning the bounded incomplete report. Add the actual failure phase to the guard candidates before capture, or only enforce this check for the fixed structural phase values.</violation> </file> ``` </details> <sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/170/ai_pr_review_github_delivery_873046500cacf88e31aa76f52a69ee81353f826567026ce27b036aaa3b712fc9?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F170)</sub> <!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_github_delivery_873046500cacf88e31aa76f52a69ee81353f826567026ce27b036aaa3b712fc9:9ee45f4385f3b354f0e27396fe0e86dafa5ee41f:0fc54562-fcc2-542e-91ad-95b6ba996323 -->\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 5255359562,\n    \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n    \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-09-19T10:29:21Z\",\n    \"body\": \"> [!IMPORTANT] > The suite refactor can bypass cleanup after a target session is already live. **Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `cf76637a`, covering the behavioral delta in `80ba0261`. - **Preserved structural-collision cleanup** — Added a reportless cleanup-owner error and CLI handling so unsafe artifacts remain omitted while cleanup stays retryable. - **Refactored suite execution** — Extracted diagnostic collection, connected execution, artifact projection, and client close handling. - **Refactored hosted authorization** — Split authorization, token exchange, refresh, and rejection-envelope validation into phase-specific helpers. - **Hardened artifact boundaries** — Preserved inspector schema keys, tightened cache-directive checks, and extracted bounded credential-redaction helpers. <!-- Pullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 80ba0261; if commits have landed on codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910 since, treat every specific bug, file, or line callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it. - Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review) - Files reviewed: 61 - Commits reviewed: 70 - Base: dev (2867c68f) - Head: codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910 (80ba0261) - Reviewed commits:   - 80ba0261 — fix(mcpfn): close review and analyzer findings (incremental delta; full PR context reviewed through this commit) - Prior pullfrog review: cf76637a (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5249315211) --> <!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --> <sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" \"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 5255354305,\n    \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n    \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-09-19T10:27:34Z\",\n    \"body\": \"\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 5255348648,\n    \"user\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\",\n    \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-09-19T10:25:56