I](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/170/ai_pr_review_github_delivery_87f6a2928cff69047c408f1334ce1558011e41a6b409fde086a67fafe67468f7?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F170)</sub> <!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_github_delivery_87f6a2928cff69047c408f1334ce1558011e41a6b409fde086a67fafe67468f7:cf76637ada4ba0263e36f30c23a278826c48dd0a:47c61d9f-3ebe-5e12-b906-aab16497065f -->\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 5249315211,\n    \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n    \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-09-18T15:06:28Z\",\n    \"body\": \"> [!IMPORTANT] > Structural report-key collisions can discard retryable cleanup ownership. **Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `dfaeef0d`, covering the seven-file artifact-boundary hardening delta in `cf76637a`. - **Stabilized CLI failure classification** — Made classified diagnostic writes best-effort and covered a persistently rejecting `stderr` sink. - **Protected target descriptors** — Added a shared structural-redaction boundary for client event and diagnostic target descriptors. - **Rejected structural credential collisions** — Added explicit required-key collision errors and distinguished redaction from serialization projection failures. - **Expanded regressions** — Added target discriminator and required report-key collision coverage. <!-- Pullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against cf76637a; if commits have landed on codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910 since, treat every specific bug, file, or line callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it. - Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review) - Files reviewed: 61 (7 changed in the incremental commit) - Commits reviewed: 69 (1 since the prior review) - Base: dev (2867c68f) - Head: codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910 (cf76637a) - Reviewed commits:   - cf76637a — fix(mcpfn): harden artifact failure boundaries - Prior pullfrog review: dfaeef0d (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#pullrequestreview-5248475385) --> <!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --> <sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align:\"\n  }\n]\nlatest_inline\n[\n  {\n    \"id\": 4053223553,\n    \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-19T12:48:48Z\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4053223553\",\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n    \"line\": 322,\n    \"original_line\": 317,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed by making the fallback descriptor read safe inside the guarded projection/close path and adding a regression that verifies the connected target closes exactly once. <!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --> <sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/35443246488/job/105897661544) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 4053209957,\n    \"user\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-19T12:41:37Z\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4053209957\",\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts\",\n    \"line\": 51,\n    \"original_line\": 51,\n    \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject unsupported structured Authorization credentials** When a custom provider supplies a structured Authorization scheme other than Basic or Bearer—for example, `Digest ... response=\\\"opaque-secret\\\"`—the code records only the entire parameter block before returning here, not independently reflectable credential components such as the response digest. If the server includes that parsed component alone in a diagnostic or tool payload, it will not match any redaction pattern and can reach reports or inspector artifacts unchanged. Fresh evidence after adding Cookie parsing is that other accepted structured Authorization schemes remain unparsed; either reject unsupported schemes or register their credential-bearing components. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 4053207798,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-19T12:40:28Z\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4053207798\",\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n    \"line\": 463,\n    \"original_line\": 463,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=2e1aec08-1d67-4452-ada9-8437a1783bd0 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=0fc54562-fcc2-542e-91ad-95b6ba996323 --> <!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --> P2: When a target error supplies a nonstandard `phase`, suite finalization treats the legitimate failure as a credential-structure collision and throws instead of returning the bounded incomplete report. Add the actual failure phase to the guard candidates before capture, or only enforce this check for the fixed structural phase values. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts, line 463: <comment>When a target error supplies a nonstandard `phase`, suite finalization treats the legitimate failure as a credential-structure collision and throws instead of returning the bounded incomplete report. Add the actual failure phase to the guard candidates before capture, or only enforce this check for the fixed structural phase values.</comment> <file context> @@ -362,6 +366,115 @@ function projectSuiteArtifacts( +  if (report.failure) { +    assertStructureKeys(report.failure, guard); +    guard.assert(report.failure.layer); +    if (report.failure.phase) guard.assert(report.failure.phase); +  } +  for (const event of report.timeline) { </file context> ``` </details>\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 4052889913,\n    \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-19T10:29:20Z\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4052889913\",\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n    \"line\": 322,\n    \"original_line\": 317,\n    \"body\": \"**[P1] Keep fallback projection inside the guarded cleanup path** Constructing `fallback` reads the arbitrary `target.kind` before this function enters its `try`. If that getter/proxy throws after the client has connected, `runTargetSuite()` exits before `closeSuiteClient()` and can leave the transport or credential owner live; guard this read and add a post-open throwing-kind regression. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # Preserve cleanup when target metadata access throws ## Affected sites - `mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts:304-317` — `initialTargetDescriptor()` reads `target.kind` while `fallback` is created outside the projection guard. - `mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts:433-435` — projection runs after connection but before the only `closeSuiteClient()` call. ## Required outcome - Arbitrary target metadata access must not escape after connection without attempting client cleanup. - A safe incomplete report should be produced when possible, while any failed cleanup remains retryable. ```` </details>\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 4052884967,\n    \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-19T10:27:34Z\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4052884967\",\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 390,\n    \"body\": \"Addressed in 80ba026 by retaining the cleanup owner in `McpFnTargetSuiteArtifactCleanupError` and adding combined collision/retry coverage. <!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --> <sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/35437126199/job/105881585044) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 4052880086,\n    \"user\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-19T10:25:56Z\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4052880086\",\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n    \"line\": 329,\n    \"original_line\": 325,\n    \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Validate fallback report structure with the target redactor** When a custom target fails before reaching `connected`, this early return bypasses `client.preserveArtifactStructure()` and the target-owned redactor. For example, a target whose opaque credential is `incomplete` can fail during `open()`, after which the suite serializes `status: \\\"incomplete\\\"`; the final `redactTargetCredentials()` pass knows only credentials registered by `authenticatedHttpTarget`, so the custom credential remains exposed. Fresh evidence beyond the earlier target-kind issue is this non-connected fallback branch, which skips validation for every fixed report discriminator; validate those structural values while the custom hook is still available or fail the artifact. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 4052873779,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-19T10:23:38Z\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4052873779\",\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/inspector/src/index.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 243,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=a052d67b-f905-485e-8b31-06c93082dca8 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=3f2b0c8e-464a-550e-ac0b-0b595abbdda1 --> <!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --> P2: When a credential equals `status`, `incompleteReason`, or `variables`, complete exports fail even when those optional fields are not emitted. Validate optional structural keys only when the corresponding field is actually added. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/inspector/src/index.ts, line 243: <comment>When a credential equals `status`, `incompleteReason`, or `variables`, complete exports fail even when those optional fields are not emitted. Validate optional structural keys only when the corresponding field is actually added.</comment> <file context> @@ -238,6 +238,16 @@ export class McpFnInspector {      const scenario = createMcpFnScenario(name, operation, result); +    // Top-level scenario keys are authored schema, not payload. If a credential +    // collides with one of them, no replayable typed artifact can be emitted. +    for (const key of [ +      ...Object.keys(scenario), +      \\\"status\\\", </file context> ``` </details> ✅ Addressed in [`9ee45f4`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/9ee45f4385f3b354f0e27396fe0e86dafa5ee41f)\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 4047959467,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-18T15:07:07Z\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4047959467\",\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 390,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=cb20f140-b9f3-4dd8-a1f8-e7e83edc5da8 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=47c61d9f-3ebe-5e12-b906-aab16497065f --> <!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --> P1: When final report redaction collides with a credential after `client.close()` failed, this branch discards the retryable cleanup owner. Preserve the cleanup error and retry handle before surfacing the structural-serialization failure. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts, line 390: <comment>When final report redaction collides with a credential after `client.close()` failed, this branch discards the retryable cleanup owner. Preserve the cleanup error and retry handle before surfacing the structural-serialization failure.</comment> <file context> @@ -367,15 +381,22 @@ async function runTargetSuite(options: RunMcpFnTargetSuiteOptions): Promise<McpF      finalized = enforceReportCap(redactTargetCredentials(options.target, report, { preserveKeys: true }), maxReportBytes);    } catch (error) { +    if (error instanceof McpFnStructuralCredentialCollisionError) { +      throw new McpFnClientError( +        \\\"MCPFN_OPERATION_FAILED\\\", +        \\\"Target report cannot be serialized because a credential conflicts with required artifact structure\\\", </file context> ``` </details> ✅ Addressed in [`80ba026`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1)\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 4047954117,\n    \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-18T15:06:27Z\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4047954117\",\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 390,\n    \"body\": \"**[P1] Preserve the retained cleanup owner on this failure path** This immediate throw bypasses the `retainedCleanup` handoff below, so when structural collision and credential/transport cleanup fail together, callers receive no `retryCleanup()` capability and cannot complete release. Preserve access to the pending cleanup owner while still failing without serializing the credential-colliding report. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # Keep cleanup retryable when report structure is unsafe ## Affected sites - `mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts:285-307` — captures failed close/revocation ownership in `retainedCleanup`. - `mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts:389-394` — throws the structural-collision error before ownership is transferred. - `mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts:407` — the normal `McpFnTargetSuiteCleanupError` handoff is unreachable on this branch. ## Required outcome - A required-key credential collision must remain a safe hard failure. - If cleanup also failed, the thrown failure must retain a callable, serialized retry owner without exposing the unsafe report. - Add a combined structural-collision plus failed-cleanup regression that retries cleanup successfully. ```` </details>\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 4047938404,\n    \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-18T15:04:30Z\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4047938404\",\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts\",\n    \"line\": 329,\n    \"original_line\": 305,\n    \"body\": \"Addressed in cf76637 by making classified diagnostics best-effort and covering persistent stderr rejection. <!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --> <sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com