n the corresponding field is actually added.</comment> <file context> @@ -238,6 +238,16 @@ export class McpFnInspector {      const scenario = createMcpFnScenario(name, operation, result); +    // Top-level scenario keys are authored schema, not payload. If a credential +    // collides with one of them, no replayable typed artifact can be emitted. +    for (const key of [ +      ...Object.keys(scenario), +      \\\"status\\\", </file context> ``` </details> ✅ Addressed in [`9ee45f4`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/9ee45f4385f3b354f0e27396fe0e86dafa5ee41f)\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jybjm\",\n    \"isResolved\": true,\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts\",\n    \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-18T15:07:07Z\",\n    \"outdated\": true,\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4047959467\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=cb20f140-b9f3-4dd8-a1f8-e7e83edc5da8 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=47c61d9f-3ebe-5e12-b906-aab16497065f --> <!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --> P1: When final report redaction collides with a credential after `client.close()` failed, this branch discards the retryable cleanup owner. Preserve the cleanup error and retry handle before surfacing the structural-serialization failure. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/testing/src/suite.ts, line 390: <comment>When final report redaction collides with a credential after `client.close()` failed, this branch discards the retryable cleanup owner. Preserve the cleanup error and retry handle before surfacing the structural-serialization failure.</comment> <file context> @@ -367,15 +381,22 @@ async function runTargetSuite(options: RunMcpFnTargetSuiteOptions): Promise<McpF      finalized = enforceReportCap(redactTargetCredentials(options.target, report, { preserveKeys: true }), maxReportBytes);    } catch (error) { +    if (error instanceof McpFnStructuralCredentialCollisionError) { +      throw new McpFnClientError( +        \\\"MCPFN_OPERATION_FAILED\\\", +        \\\"Target report cannot be serialized because a credential conflicts with required artifact structure\\\", </file context> ``` </details> ✅ Addressed in [`80ba026`](https://g\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jwvKs\",\n    \"isResolved\": true,\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts\",\n    \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-18T15:04:30Z\",\n    \"outdated\": false,\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4047938404\",\n    \"line\": 329,\n    \"body\": \"Addressed in cf76637 by making classified diagnostics best-effort and covering persistent stderr rejection. <!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --> <sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/35359486263/job/105646926366) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jyW37\",\n    \"isResolved\": false,\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts\",\n    \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-18T15:03:35Z\",\n    \"outdated\": false,\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4047930620\",\n    \"line\": 517,\n    \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject parameterized cache-prevention directives** Fresh evidence after adding the token-response header checks is that `hasHeaderDirective()` accepts malformed values such as `Cache-Control: no-store=false` and `Pragma: no-cache=false` by discarding everything after `=`. Those directives do not satisfy the required `no-store`/`no-cache` response values, yet the hosted regression reports the token exchange as passed; require these argument-free directives to have no parameter. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jyW3y\",\n    \"isResolved\": false,\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/inspector/src/index.ts\",\n    \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-18T15:03:35Z\",\n    \"outdated\": false,\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4047930609\",\n    \"line\": 256,\n    \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Validate top-level scenario keys before export** When an active target credential equals a top-level scenario key such as `name`, this mapping redacts only the corresponding value and copies the key verbatim. Consequently, `exportScenario()` returns an artifact containing the exact credential even though nested argument keys are scrubbed; validate the fixed scenario keys with the target redactor or fail the export on a structural collision. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jwwv5\",\n    \"isResolved\": false,\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/client/src/client.ts\",\n    \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-18T13:48:39Z\",\n    \"outdated\": true,\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4047301468\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve or omit diagnostic target discriminators** When a target credential equals `kind` or overlaps the target's `kind` value, payload-mode redaction rewrites that required property name or discriminator, but the diagnostic is still dispatched without incrementing the omission count. Fresh evidence after suite-level target-kind reconstruction is that live diagnostics still take this path, so inspector and suite timelines can report `timelineComplete: true` while containing a malformed or misidentified `event.target`; validate and reconstruct the target kind or mark the diagnostic as omitted. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jwwv0\",\n    \"isResolved\": false,\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/src/remote-target.ts\",\n    \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-18T13:48:39Z\",\n    \"outdated\": true,\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4047301459\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject credentials matching preserved schema keys** When an opaque credential equals or is contained in a required envelope key—for example, an API key of `timeline`—`preserveStructuralKey()` records the matching pattern, and this filter removes it from the final serialized-output check while the literal key remains in the report. Fresh evidence after the discriminator-value collision check is that schema key names themselves are still exempt, so target-suite and inspector JSON can expose the credential; reject these credential/key collisions rather than excluding their patterns. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n  }\n]\nlatest_reviews\n[\n  {\n    \"id\": 5255779459,\n    \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n    \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-09-19T12:49:56Z\",\n    \"body\": \"> ✅ No new issues found. Reviewed `80ba0261..9ee45f43`, including the guarded target-suite cleanup fix, structural report validation, optional inspector artifact keys, remote-target redaction helpers, and failure normalization. The prior throwing-`kind` cleanup thread is addressed an