onger Not Attempted, all three new review roots have coordinated repairs, and no local regression remains; hosted reviewers/analyzers have not yet assessed the new head.\n- Valid blocking root causes before / after: 3 new review roots plus 10 valid analyzer subfamilies / 0 deliberately deferred valid code roots, with hosted verification pending a future round.\n- New defects: top-level scenario key leakage, parameterized anti-cache directive acceptance, and cleanup-owner loss during structural report collision.\n- Recurring families: credential-boundary structural safety and cleanup ownership recurred; both were repaired at their shared producer/consumer boundaries.\n- Fix-induced regressions: none found by 371 complete affected-package tests, four typechecks, rebuilt package consumers, whole-batch diff review, or the Node 22 release gate.\n- Clean streak: `0` (reset by new/actionable roots, recurring families, this code-changing round, and the changed PR head after the assessment).\n- Head stability: the snapshot remained at `cf76637ada4ba0263e36f30c23a278826c48dd0a` during assessment; the single commit and push advanced local, remote, and PR head together to `80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1` in the one allowed comparison.\n\n## Round 10 termination\n\n- Result: nonterminal recurring run. A future separately scheduled clean assessment must verify the new head, review dispositions, and analyzer/check state; this code-changing round cannot count toward the clean streak.\n- Automation `4442e7f3-60f4-4125-a8e4-c818ac40fc82` remains disabled from the earlier retrieval-discovery stop and was not silently re-enabled during this manual round.\n- No post-push review refetch, CI poll, reviewer wait, thread resolution, review dismissal, merge, or second fix loop was performed.\n\n## Round 11 assessment\n\n- Hosted workflow: `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.2.0`, revision `4`, digest `sha256:8781c1c12fe9d5902337d6cf21bfbac49dd3a94c7eadd46bf2622db350444022` (published identity verified through Skillplane via Composio before repository mutation).\n- Mode: assessment reset. Round 11 is a separately invoked single review round; the prior clean streak remains `0`.\n- Snapshot / head: local, upstream, every review page, and PR head were stable at `80ba026172a774ea95277393becffa35c9892fc1`. The complete one-time snapshot contains 332 threads (93 unresolved: 33 current and 60 outdated-only), 228 reviews, 64 issue comments, 373 raw inline comments, 11 current Sonar issues, and 18 check contexts. All thread and nested-comment pagination was terminal.\n- Shared invariant: a credential-bearing typed artifact may emit only the authored keys and discriminator values actually present, after the live target redactor proves each exact structural string safe; a projection failure must never bypass transport cleanup, and analyzer-only refactors must preserve credential, lifecycle, ownership, and report semantics.\n- Producers / consumers: inspector scenario export produces replay artifacts; custom targets and live client sessions produce redacted descriptors, diagnostics, scenario results, and cleanup ownership; target-suite projection/finalization produces direct-library, JSON, JUnit, and CLI evidence; shared credential scrubbers and report normalizers feed all of those consumers.\n- Failure boundaries: optional scenario fields that are validated but never emitted; custom redaction state cleared during close; fallback descriptor access through hostile getters after connect; structural collisions in fixed report keys/discriminators; base64 comparison, recursive scrub traversal, failure normalization, and suite orchestration maintainability changes.\n- Coordinated repair: validate optional inspector keys only at their emission branches; capture live custom-redactor safety for exact report structural candidates before close and enforce it against only the final emitted structure; place projection and structural capture behind unconditional cleanup; then repair