/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T14-45-31-01a07b26-bb2c-7b32-95a4-8fb6b484fad0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T07:43:24+00:00, thread_id=01a07b26-bb2c-7b32-95a4-8fb6b484fad0, complete comparative report was not delivered; PR #170 symptom-patching convergence failure documented)\n  1675\t\n  1676\t### keywords\n  1677\t\n  1678\t- GH_CONFIG_DIR, gh pr list, PR #144, PR #145, PR #149, PR #150, PR #151, PR #152, PR #153, PR #155, PR #170, reviewThreads, Sonar, convergence, root-cause\n  1679\t\n  1680\t## Task 2: Evaluate PR #144 and its follow-up fixes, success\n  1681\t\n  1682\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1683\t\n  1684\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/08/rollout-2026-09-08T13-09-19-01a07ff5-06bb-73e2-8e7c-f4c4a0ffa83e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-08T07:42:07+00:00, thread_id=01a07ff5-06bb-73e2-8e7c-f4c4a0ffa83e, final head not merge-ready)\n  1685\t\n  1686\t### keywords\n  1687\t\n  1688\t- PR #144, DataFn, null-normalization, aggregate-query, date-bounds, timezone, better-sqlite3, `TZ=Asia/Kolkata`, field-builders\n  1689\t\n  1690\t## Task 3: Evaluate PR #170 and all subsequent fixes, partial\n  1691\t\n  1692\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1693\t\n  1694\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/15/rollout-2026-09-15T12-28-36-01a0a3dc-41d4-7c01-b6af-ad11344d98ef.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T07:58:13+00:00, thread_id=01a0a3dc-41d4-7c01-b6af-ad11344d98ef, read-only assessment was started but no final verdict delivered)\n  1695\t\n  1696\t### keywords\n  1697\t\n  1698\t- PR #170, MCP-1, transport-neutral conformance, aa08ef72e, reviewThreads(first:100), isOutdated, JUnit, --visible-tools, redaction, ESM/CJS, GH_CONFIG_DIR\n  1699\t\n  1700\t## User preferences\n  1701\t\n  1702\t- when asking for PR review, the user expects “findings along with the quality of the code changes” -> provide concrete defects and an explicit quality assessment; remain read-only unless remediation is separately authorized. Respect explicit exclusions across review, edits, comments, and reporting. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  1703\t- when the user asks to evaluate “PR #170 and all subsequent PR fixes” -> assess both history and exact current head, enumerate all commits/review surfaces/checks, and finish the requested verdict before pursuing unrelated PR material. [Task 3]\n  1704\t- when remediation repeatedly finds adjacent variants, the user asked to “strive for convergence and broader look” -> reset to the shared invariant/subsystem rather than publish another one-example symptom patch. [Task 1]\n  1705\t- when comparing implementations, the user steers toward authoritative Linear issues/architecture plans and asks for the problem and both approaches “in simplest terms” -> use those documents as acceptance criteria and give a plain-language model before the distinction. [Task 1]\n  1706\t- when the user says “give me descriptive question” -> provide a directly reusable question with issue context, the mismatch, and concrete follow-up asks rather than a fragment. [Task 1]\n  1707\t\n  1708\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1709\t\n  1710\t- Use `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other`; narrow GitHub queries, fetch exact heads, inspect targeted diffs/logs, and classify CI, source inspection, and runtime probes as distinct evidence. A bounded review collection does not cap analysis completeness: when related blockers recur, inspect sibling paths and repair the shared invariant before the one authorized publication step. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  1711\t- DATA-6 favors parse/validate once into a versioned discriminated protocol representation, then an exhaustive structural selector visitor. A parallel raw-payload switch can drift from route parsing; require execution/extraction shared-representation evidence. Structural selectors are not an inventory of relation-derived execution effects. [Task 1]\n  1712\t- For UIF-2 project mutation, distinguish generator-owned from merge-owned files, do not overwrite unmanaged generated-output paths, do not hash all of consumer-owned `package.json` for dependency merging, and make dry-run plan the same artifacts/dependencies/metadata as commit mode. [Task 1]\n  1713\t- PR #144’s foundation is good (const-safe builders, literal types, persisted-null replace clears), but its final head has cross-path null-normalization, aggregate, timezone/date-validation, and excess-option-key gaps; focused tests passing did not establish merge readiness. [Task 2]\n  1714\t- For PR #170, paginate `pullRequest.reviewThreads(first:100,after:$endCursor)` and separate `isOutdated` from current unresolved threads; snapshot base/head OIDs, commits, local exact-head source, and hosted checks independently. The captured head `aa08ef72e` was open/mergeable but `UNSTABLE`, with 34 current unresolved threads and 10 pending checks; do not call it merge-ready from focused tests or resolved threads. [Task 3]\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0c31e-6a96-7383-bda9-a191f2448a61","create_time":1789981213.93731}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
