rets(token, secrets);\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"threadId\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6kSmAh\",\n    \"isResolved\": false,\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/testing/tests/suite.test.ts\",\n    \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-21T09:06:39Z\",\n    \"outdated\": false,\n    \"line\": 233,\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4060652211\",\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=db65da18-e0ea-4ce7-a04c-0dc64acf7ca3 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=d3e4fe20-f21f-5274-9f92-129710836b2d -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":7} -->\\nP3: The test's stated purpose — proving the authored failure phase is safe before emission — only exercises the pass-through path. No credential is registered on the target and the authored phase never collides with a registered variant, so the fail-closed branch is never reached: `captureSuiteStructureGuard` would mark \\\"vendor-phase\\\" safe because the custom redactor leaves non-Error strings unchanged and the built-in scrubber has nothing registered. A regression that silently dropped `guard.assert(report.failure.phase)` in `assertSuiteReportStructure` (suite.ts) would still pass this test. Strengthen the test so it verifies the safety claim: register a credential equal to the authored phase (or make the redactor replace the phase with a marker that equals a registered variant) and assert that the suite fails closed — either rejects with `McpFnStructuralCredentialCollisionError`/atomic rejection, or emits a report without the unproven phase. The adjacent fail-closed tests cover kind collisions and a throwing redactor, but not the phase value path this test claims to guard.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/testing/tests/suite.test.ts, line 233:\\n\\n<comment>The test's stated purpose — proving the authored failure phase is safe before emission — only exercises the pass-through path. No c