\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/testing/tests/suite.test.ts, line 233:\\n\\n<comment>The test's stated purpose — proving the authored failure phase is safe before emission — only exercises the pass-through path. No credential is registered on the target and the authored phase never collides with a registered variant, so the fail-closed branch is never reached: `captureSuiteStructureGuard` would mark \\\"vendor-phase\\\" safe because the custom redactor leaves non-Error strings unchanged and the built-in scrubber has nothing registered. A regression that silently dropped `guard.assert(report.failure.phase)` in `assertSuiteReportStructure` (suite.ts) would still pass this test. Strengthen the test so it verifies the safety claim: register a credential equal to the authored phase (or make the redactor replace the phase with a marker that equals a registered variant) and assert that the suite fails closed — either rejects with `McpFnStructuralCredentialCollisionError`/atomic rejection, or emits a report without the unproven phase. The adjacent fail-closed tests cover kind collisions and a throwing redactor, but not the phase value path this test claims to guard.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -219,6 +219,21 @@ it(\\\"does not repeat successful custom cleanup after an open failure\\\", async () =\\n+  expect(report).toMatchObject({\\n+    ok: false,\\n+    status: \\\"incomplete\\\",\\n+    failure: { phase: \\\"vendor-phase\\\" },\\n+  });\\n+});\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4060652211\",\n    \"commit_id\": \"d12812dfae99cc0905aa93365f9b9ed5c42065f2\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 4060653884,\n    \"user\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-21T09:06:56Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-21T09:06:56Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/examples/external-http-server.mjs\",\n    \"line\": 15,\n    \"original_line\": 15,\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Handle invalid Host headers inside the error boundary**\\n\\nWhen a client or conformance Host-manipulation probe sends a syntactically invalid `Host` value, this `new URL()` call throws before the handler's `try` block. Because the HTTP listener is async and Node does not consume its returned promise, the rejection can become an unhandled rejection and terminate the external fixture instead of returning a controlled 4xx response. Move URL construction into the guarded block or validate the Host header first.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4060653884\",\n    \"commit_id\": \"d12812dfae99cc0905aa93365f9b9ed5c42065f2\"\n  }\n]\n{\n  \"total\": 3,\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"key\": \"REDACTED\",\n      \"rule\": \"typescript:S3696\",\n      \"severity\": \"MAJOR\",\n      \"type\": \"CODE_SMELL\",\n      \"component\": \"21nCo_super-functions:mcpfn/cli/src/index.ts\",\n      \"line\": 84,\n      \"message\": \"Expected an error object to be thrown.\",\n      \"status\": \"OPEN\",\n      \"creationDate\": \"2026-09-18T11:12:20+0000\",\n      \"updateDate\": \"2026-09-18T11:12:49+0000\",\n      \"textRange\": {\n        \"startLine\": 84,\n        \"endLine\": 84,\n        \"startOffset\": 14,\n        \"endOffset\": 25\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"REDACTED\",\n      \"rule\": \"typescript:S3696\",\n      \"severity\": \"MAJOR\",\n      \"type\": \"CODE_SMELL\",\n      \"component\": \"21nCo_super-functions:mcpfn/testing/src/client.ts\",\n      \"line\": 62,\n      \"message\": \"Expected an error object to be thrown.\",\n      \"status\": \"OPEN\",\n      \"creationDate\": \"2026-09-15T11:24:47+0000\",\n      \"updateDate\": \"2026-09-15T11:26:07+00