d during this manual round.\n- No post-push review refetch, CI poll, reviewer wait, thread resolution, review dismissal, merge, or second fix loop was performed.\n\n## Round 12 assessment\n\n- Hosted workflow: `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.2.0`, revision `4`, digest `sha256:8781c1c12fe9d5902337d6cf21bfbac49dd3a94c7eadd46bf2622db350444022` (published identity verified through Skillplane via Composio before repository mutation).\n- Mode: assessment reset. Round 12 is a separately invoked single review round; the prior clean streak remains `0`.\n- Snapshot / head: local, upstream, every review page, and PR head were stable at `9ee45f4385f3b354f0e27396fe0e86dafa5ee41f`. The complete one-time snapshot contains 334 threads (93 unresolved: 32 current and 61 outdated-only), 232 reviews, 64 issue comments, 376 raw inline comments, 5 current Sonar issues, and 18 check contexts. All thread and nested-comment pagination was terminal.\n- Shared invariant: every credential-derived value that a peer can reflect independently must be registered with the live target redactor, or ambiguous structured credentials must fail closed before transport; every structural string actually emitted in a typed report, including a dynamic normalized failure phase, must be proven safe by that same live redactor; cleanup ownership must survive either failure boundary.\n- Producers / consumers: authorization and proxy-authorization headers produce whole credentials and independently reflectable auth-param values consumed by target, diagnostic, report, and JUnit redaction; target-open failures produce normalized failure phases consumed by suite report structure validation; the remote-target lease and suite finalizer own cleanup across both paths.\n- Failure boundaries: quoted auth-param values with escapes or commas, unquoted component values, malformed or ambiguous parameter lists, simple custom opaque schemes, Basic decoding, a target-supplied nonstandard failure phase, and close-time cleanup after discovery or structural rejection.\n- Coordinated repair: retain whole-token and Basic component registration; parse non-Basic structured auth-param lists deterministically, register raw and decoded component values, and reject malformed lists within the existing lease cleanup boundary; pass the normalized connection failure into structural-guard capture so the exact emitted phase is proven before close; remove the two valid analyzer smells without changing behavior.\n- Verification criteria: focused structured-authorization redaction and malformed-release regressions; a custom failed-open dynamic-phase report regression; complete affected testing-package tests/typecheck/build; Node 22 release gate; `git diff --check`; whole-batch diff review; and one final local/remote/PR-head comparison. Hosted review/check surfaces will not be fetched again this round.\n\n### Round 12 defect families\n\n| Stable family | Root cause / affected contract | Disposition | First seen | Last attempted | Repair / evidence state |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `MCP170-AUTHORIZATION-STRUCTURED-COMPONENTS` | Non-Basic structured authorization values register only the whole parameter block, allowing an independently reflected component to escape redaction | Actionable; recurring credential-discovery family | round 12 | round 12 | Bounded auth-param component discovery and malformed-input rejection selected |\n| `MCP170-DYNAMIC-FAILURE-PHASE-GUARD` | Suite structure capture omits a target-supplied normalized failure phase that final validation emits | Actionable; recurring structural-safety family | round 12 | round 12 | Exact connection-failure phase capture selected |\n| `MCP170-SONAR-GUARD-INITIALIZATION` | Suite orchestration initializes the structural guard with a value that is always overwritten before normal return | Valid analyzer finding | round 12 | round 12 | Definite control-flow assignment selected |\n| `MCP170-SONAR-REDACTION-NESTED-TERNARY` | Redaction object traversal nests role selection inside a conditional expression | Valid analyzer finding; recurring redaction-maintainability family | round 12 | round 12 | Explicit entry-role selection selected |\n| `MCP170-SONAR-THROW-THIS` | Three findings flag intentional retry-owner self-rejection | Invalid analyzer interpretation | round 10 | round 12 | Exact error identity remains the cleanup ownership token; preserve behavior |\n\n- Snapshot dispositions before mutation: 2 new unresolved current review threads deduplicate to 2 actionable root causes. Five current Sonar issues deduplicate to 2 valid maintainability roots and 3 invalid retry-owner findings. Older valid blockers and dispositions remain preserved; outdated status was not used as proof.\n- Required-check snapshot: 18 contexts comprised 13 successful, 1 neutral, 3 skipped, and 1 pending CodeRabbit context; there were no failing contexts. Sonar Quality Gate passed and `reviewDecision` was empty. No check polling is permitted.\n- Convergence state: not clean. Two new/actionable roots, recurring credential-discovery and structural-safety families, two valid analyzer findings, and the pending required check reset the clean streak to `0` despite the stable snapshot head.\n\n## Round 12 snapshot dispositions\n\n- Fixed: 2 new review root causes and 2 valid Sonar findings. `MCP170-AUTHORIZATION-STRUCTURED-COMPONENTS` now discovers quoted, escaped, decoded, raw-inner, and unquoted values from bounded non-Basic/Bearer auth-param lists while preserving simple opaque custom schemes and Basic decoding; malformed structured syntax fails inside the existing credential-lease cleanup boundary. `MCP170-DYNAMIC-FAILURE-PHASE-GUARD` now proves the normalized connection failure's exact emitted phase safe while the live target redactor remains available. The two analyzer findings received definite structural-guard assignment and explicit redaction entry-role selection.\n- Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale): 91 older unresolved threads retain their prior current-code dispositions (30 current and 61 outdated-only at this snapshot). Outdated status, resolved-thread counts, and acknowledgement-only comments were not used as proof.\n- Invalid / Accepted Risk: the 3 remaining Sonar `throw this` findings are invalid because exact error identity is the cleanup ownership token; the older payload-key-redaction finding retains its prior invalid disposition. No accepted risks.\n- Not Attempted: 0 valid code root causes. Both new review roots and both valid current Sonar findings were attempted in the single coordinated batch; hosted reviewer/analyzer confirmation is deferred to a future separately scheduled snapshot because post-push refetch is forbidden.\n- Unassessed: 0 captured threads, nested comments, review bodies, issue comments, raw inline comments, or current Sonar issues.\n\n## Round 12 verification evidence\n\n- Focused regressions: 37 target-suite tests and 92 remote-target tests passed (129 total). New cases prove dynamic normalized failure phases are admitted only after live-redactor classification; quoted, escaped, decoded, raw-inner, and unquoted structured authorization components redact; malformed auth-param lists reject; and their credential lease is revoked exactly once. Existing simple custom-scheme and Basic behavior remained green.\n- Complete affected-package suite: all 241 `@mcpfn/testing` tests passed. The package typechecked and built successfully under Node 22.\n- Release gate: the final `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed every reported dependency/package test, typecheck, and build; Playwright; mixed-entry redaction; official conformance; examples; ESM/CJS imports; dry-run packs; packed-consumer installation; and round trips. The first gate attempt identified only an absent pinned Playwright browser; installing that exact test runtime resolved the environment gap, and the final gate passed against the final code state.\n- `git diff --check` passed. Whole-batch review covered all four code/test files and decomposed the structured-credential parser to avoid a new complexity hotspot. The ledger remained untracked and will not be staged or committed.\n- Required-check snapshot: the single pre-mutation snapshot contained 18 contexts: 13 successful, 1 neutral, 3 skipped, and 1 pending CodeRabbit context. Sonar Quality Gate passed with 2 valid and 3 invalid current findings. No hosted checks or reviews were fetched after the snapshot.\n- Fix-induced regressions: the first focused dynamic-phase test incorrectly exercised the client's intentional raw-open normalization to `transport-connect`; the final test exercises the actual target-redactor normalization boundary. No regression remained after focused tests, the complete package suite, typecheck/build, whole-diff review, or the final release gate.\n\n## Round 12 convergence\n\n- Trend: improving but nonterminal. All selected review and valid analyzer roots have coordinated repairs and no local regression remains, but this code-changing round cannot be clean and the sole immediate check snapshot contained a pending reviewer context.\n- Valid blocking root causes before / after: 2 new review roots plus 2 valid analyzer findings / 0 deliberately deferred valid code roots, with hosted verification pending a future separately scheduled assessment.\n- New defects: structured authorization component leakage and omission of a dynamic normalized failure phase from the live structural-safety candidate set.\n- Recurring families: credential discovery and structural safety recurred; both were repaired at shared producer/finalization boundaries.\n- Clean streak: `0` (reset by new/actionable roots, recurring families, this code-changing round, and the pending required check in the sole snapshot).\n- Head stability before mutation: the complete snapshot stayed at `9ee45f4385f3b354f0e27396fe0e86dafa5ee41f` throughout assessment. Final local/remote/PR head evidence will be recorded after the one allowed push and one allowed comparison.\n\n## Round 12 completion\n\n- Commit / push: one commit `d12812dfae99cc0905aa93365f9b9ed5c42065f2` (`fix(mcpfn): harden credential report safety`) and one successful push through existing `origin` to `codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910`.\n- Head verification (one comparison only): local head, `origin/codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910`, and PR 170 head all equal `d12812dfae99cc0905aa93365f9b9ed5c42065f2`; PR 170 remained open. The branch was `+0/-0`, and the only remaining worktree item was the untracked `.conduct/` ledger directory.\n- Head stability: the assessed head remained `9ee45f4385f3b354f0e27396fe0e86dafa5ee41f` through selection and verification; the single commit and push advanced local, remote, and PR head together to `d12812dfae99cc0905aa93365f9b9ed5c42065f2` in the one allowed post-push comparison.\n- Result: nonterminal recurring run. A future separately scheduled assessment must inspect the new head's complete review/check surfaces once; this code-changing round cannot count toward the clean streak.\n- Automation `4442e7f3-60f4-4125-a8e4-c818ac40fc82` remains disabled from the earlier retrieval-discovery stop and was not silently re-enabled during this manual round.\n- No post-push review refetch, CI poll, reviewer wait, thread resolution, review dismissal, merge, or second fix loop was performed.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":9875},"formatted_output":"import { randomUUID, timingSafeEqual } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport { createServer } from \"node:http\";\nimport { McpServer } from \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/server/mcp.js\";\nimport { WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport } from \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/server/webStandardStreamableHttp.js\";\n\nconst MAX_REQUEST_BYTES = 1_048_576;\nconst apiKey = process.env.MCPFN_EXTERNAL_API_KEY;\nif (!apiKey) throw new Error(\"MCPFN_EXTERNAL_API_KEY is required\");\n\nconst sessions = new Map();\nconst httpServer = createServer(async (incoming, outgoing) => {\n  const url = new URL(\n    incoming.url ?? \"/\",\n    `http://${incoming.headers.host ?? \"127.0.0.1\"}`,\n  );\n  if (url.pathname !== \"/mcp\") {\n    outgoing.writeHead(404).end(\"Not found\");\n    return;\n  }\n  if (!matchesSecret(incoming.headers[\"x-api-key\"], apiKey)) {\n    // Reject before reading any request body.\n    outgoing.writeHead(401, {\n      \"content-type\": \"application/json; charset=utf-8\",\n      \"cache-control\": \"no-store\",\n      \"www-authenticate\": 'ApiKey realm=\"mcpfn-external-fixture\"',\n    }).end(JSON.stringify({ error: \"invalid_credential\" }));\n    return;\n  }\n  const declaredLength = Number(incoming.headers[\"content-length\"] ?? \"0\");\n  if (Number.isFinite(declaredLength) && declaredLength > MAX_REQUEST_BYTES) {\n    outgoing.writeHead(413).end(\"Request body too large\");\n    return;\n  }\n  try {\n    const request = await toWebRequest(incoming, url);\n    const handled = await handleMcpRequest(request);\n    try {\n      await sendWebResponse(outgoing, handled.response);\n    } finally {\n      await handled.release?.();\n    }\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (String(error).includes(\"Request body too large\")) {\n      outgoing.writeHead(413).end(\"Request body too large\");\n    } else if (outgoing.headersSent) {\n      outgoing.destroy();\n    } else {\n      outgoing.writeHead(500).end(\"Internal Server Error\");\n    }\n  }\n});\n\nawait new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n  httpServer.once(\"error\", reject);\n  httpServer.listen(0, \"127.0.0.1\", resolve);\n});\nconst address = httpServer.address();\nif (!address || typeof address === \"string\") {\n  throw new Error(\"External MCP fixture did not bind a TCP port\");\n}\nprocess.stdout.write(`http://127.0.0.1:${address.port}/mcp\\n`);\n\nasync function handleMcpRequest(request) {\n  const sessionId = request.headers.get(\"mcp-session-id\");\n  if (sessionId) {\n    const session = sessions.get(sessionId);\n    if (!session) {\n      return {\n        response: Response.json({\n          jsonrpc: \"2.0\",\n          error: { code: -32001, message: \"Session not found\" },\n          id: null,\n        }, { status: 404 }),\n      };\n    }\n    return { response: await session.transport.handleRequest(request) };\n  }\n\n  const mcp = new McpServer(\n    { name: \"official-sdk-external-fixture\", version: \"1.0.0\" },\n    { capabilities: { tools: {} } },\n  );\n  mcp.registerTool(\n    \"external_identity\",\n    { description: \"Return proof from a non-McpFn-native MCP server.\" },\n    async () => ({\n      content: [{ type: \"text\", text: JSON.stringify({ authenticated: true }) }],\n      structuredContent: { authenticated: true },\n    }),\n  );\n  let initializedSessionId;\n  let released = false;\n  let transport;\n  const release = async () => {\n    if (released) return;\n    released = true;\n    if (initializedSessionId) sessions.delete(initializedSessionId);\n    await mcp.close();\n  };\n  transport = new WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport({\n    sessionIdGenerator: randomUUID,\n    enableJsonResponse: true,\n    onsessioninitialized: async (id) => {\n      initializedSessionId = id;\n      sessions.set(id, { mcp, transport, release });\n    },\n    onsessionclosed: release,\n  });\n  try {\n    await mcp.connect(transport);\n    const response = await transport.handleRequest(request);\n    return initializedSessionId ? { response } : { response, release };\n  } catch (error) {\n    await release();\n    throw error;\n  }\n}\n\nasync function toWebRequest(incoming, url) {\n  const chunks = [];\n  let size = 0;\n  for await (const chunk of incoming) {\n    const buffer = Buffer.isBuffer(chunk) ? chunk : Buffer.from(chunk);\n    size += buffer.length;\n    if (size > MAX_REQUEST_BYTES) throw new Error(\"Request body too large\");\n    chunks.push(buffer);\n  }\n  const body = Buffer.concat(chunks);\n  return new Request(url, {\n    method: incoming.method,\n    headers: new Headers(Object.entries(incoming.headers).flatMap(nodeHeaderEntries)),\n    ...(body.length ? { body } : {}),\n  });\n}\n\nfunction nodeHeaderEntries([name, value]) {\n  if (Array.isArray(value)) return value.map((entry) => [name, entry]);\n  return value === undefined ? [] : [[name, value]];\n}\n\nasync function sendWebResponse(outgoing, response) {\n  outgoing.writeHead(response.status, Object.fromEntries(response.headers));\n  if (!response.body) {\n    outgoing.end();\n    return;\n  }\n  const reader = response.body.getReader();\n  for (;;) {\n    const chunk = await reader.read();\n    if (chunk.done) break;\n    outgoing.write(Buffer.from(chunk.value));\n  }\n  outgoing.end();\n}\n\nfunction matchesSecret(received, expected) {\n  if (Array.isArray(received) || typeof received !== \"string\") return false;\n  const left = Buffer.from(received);\n  const right = Buffer.from(expected);\n  return left.length === right.length && timingSafeEqual(left, right);\n}\n\nasync function shutdown() {\n  await Promise.allSettled([...sessions.values()].map((session) => session.release()));\n  await new Promise((resolve) => httpServer.close(resolve));\n}\n\nprocess.once(\"SIGTERM\", () => { void shutdown(); });\nprocess.once(\"SIGINT\", () => { void shutdown(); });\n    }\n    if (normalizedHeader === \"cookie\") addCookieSecrets(raw, secrets);\n  }\n  return secrets;\n}\n\nfunction addAuthorizationSecrets(raw: string, secrets: Set<string>): void {\n  const trimmed = raw.trim();\n  const separator = trimmed.search(/\\s/);\n  if (separator <= 0) return;\n  const scheme = trimmed.slice(0, separator).toLowerCase();\n  const token = trimmed.slice(separator).trim();\n  if (token) secrets.add(token);\n  if (scheme !== \"basic\") {\n    if (scheme !== \"bearer\") addAuthorizationParameterSecrets(token, secrets);\n    return;\n  }\n  if (!/^[\\dA-Za-z+/]+={0,2}$/.test(token)) return;\n  const decoded = Buffer.from(token, \"base64\");\n  // Round-trip validation avoids interpreting malformed tokens as credentials.\n  if (stripBase64Padding(decoded.toString(\"base64\")) !== stripBase64Padding(token)) return;\n  for (const encoding of [\"utf8\", \"latin1\"] as const) {\n    const pair = decoded.toString(encoding);\n    const colon = pair.indexOf(\":\");\n    if (colon < 0) continue;\n    for (const value of [pair, pair.slice(0, colon), pair.slice(colon + 1)]) {\n      if (value) secrets.add(value);\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nconst authorizationParameterName = /^[!#$%&'*+.^_`|~\\dA-Za-z-]+$/;\n\ninterface ParsedAuthorizationValue {\n  cursor: number;\n  components: string[];\n}\n\nfunction skipAuthorizationWhitespace(token: string, cursor: number): number {\n  while (token[cursor] === \" \" || token[cursor] === \"\\t\") cursor += 1;\n  return cursor;\n}\n\nfunction parseQuotedAuthorizationValue(token: string, start: number): ParsedAuthorizationValue {\n  let cursor = start + 1;\n  let decoded = \"\";\n  while (cursor < token.length && token[cursor] !== '\"') {\n    if (token[cursor] === \"\\\\\") {\n      cursor += 1;\n      if (cursor >= token.length) {\n        throw new TypeError(\"Authorization credential parameters must use balanced quotes\");\n      }\n    }\n    decoded += token[cursor];\n    cursor += 1;\n  }\n  if (token[cursor] !== '\"') {\n    throw new TypeError(\"Authorization credential parameters must use balanced quotes\");\n  }\n  cursor += 1;\n  const rawValue = token.slice(start, cursor);\n  return {\n    cursor,\n    components: [rawValue, rawValue.slice(1, -1), decoded].filter(Boolean),\n  };\n}\n\nfunction parseUnquotedAuthorizationValue(token: string, start: number): ParsedAuthorizationValue {\n  let cursor = start;\n  while (cursor < token.length && token[cursor] !== \",\") cursor += 1;\n  const value = token.slice(start, cursor).trim();\n  if (!value || /\\s/.test(value) || value.includes('\"')) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"Authorization credential parameters must contain valid values\");\n  }\n  return { cursor, components: [value] };\n}\n\nfunction parseAuthorizationParameter(token: string, start: number): ParsedAuthorizationValue {\n  let cursor = skipAuthorizationWhitespace(token, start);\n  const nameStart = cursor;\n  while (cursor < token.length && token[cursor] !== \"=\" &&\n    token[cursor] !== \" \" && token[cursor] !== \"\\t\" && token[cursor] !== \",\") cursor += 1;\n  const name = token.slice(nameStart, cursor);\n  cursor = skipAuthorizationWhitespace(token, cursor);\n  if (!authorizationParameterName.test(name) || token[cursor] !== \"=\") {\n    throw new TypeError(\"Authorization credential parameters must use name=value syntax\");\n  }\n  cursor = skipAuthorizationWhitespace(token, cursor + 1);\n  if (cursor >= token.length) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"Authorization credential parameters must contain values\");\n  }\n  const parsed = token[cursor] === '\"'\n    ? parseQuotedAuthorizationValue(token, cursor)\n    : parseUnquotedAuthorizationValue(token, cursor);\n  return { ...parsed, cursor: skipAuthorizationWhitespace(token, parsed.cursor) };\n}\n\nfunction addAuthorizationParameterSecrets(token: string, secrets: Set<string>): void {\n  const firstEquals = token.indexOf(\"=\");\n  if (firstEquals < 1 || !authorizationParameterName.test(token.slice(0, firstEquals).trim())) return;\n  let cursor = 0;\n  while (cursor < token.length) {\n    const parsed = parseAuthorizationParameter(token, cursor);\n    for (const component of parsed.components) secrets.add(component);\n    cursor = parsed.cursor;\n    if (cursor === token.length) return;\n    if (token[cursor] !== \",\") {\n      throw new TypeError(\"Authorization credential parameters must be comma separated\");\n    }\n    cursor = skipAuthorizationWhitespace(token, cursor + 1);\n    if (cursor === token.length) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"Authorization credential parameters must not end with a comma\");\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction stripBase64Padding(value: string): string {\n  let end = value.length;\n  while (end > 0 && value[end - 1] === \"=\") end -= 1;\n  return value.slice(0, end);\n}\n\nfunction addCookieSecrets(raw: string, secrets: Set<string>): void {\n  // Cookie values are independently reflectable even though the request\n  // authenticates with the complete header. RFC 6265 cookie values cannot\n  // contain comma or semicolon, so both delimiters cover combined entries.\n  for (const part of raw.split(/[;,]/)) {\n    const pair = part.trim();\n    if (!pair) continue;\n    const equals = pair.indexOf(\"=\");\n    if (equals < 1) {\n  };\n  const full = await run();\n  const cap = Math.max(1024, new TextEncoder().encode(JSON.stringify(full)).byteLength + 128);\n  expect(cap).toBeLessThan(new TextEncoder().encode(JSON.stringify(full, null, 2)).byteLength);\n  const bounded = await run(cap);\n  expect(bounded.ok).toBe(true);\n  expect(bounded.droppedResults).toBe(0);\n  expect(new TextEncoder().encode(JSON.stringify(bounded)).byteLength).toBeLessThanOrEqual(cap);\n});\n\nit(\"does not repeat successful custom cleanup after an open failure\", async () => {\n  const cleanup = vi.fn(async () => {\n    if (cleanup.mock.calls.length > 1) throw new Error(\"cleanup repeated\");\n  });\n  const report = await runMcpFnTargetSuite({ target: customTarget({\n    kind: \"failed-open\", open: async () => { throw new Error(\"cannot open\"); }, cleanup,\n  }) });\n  expect(report.ok).toBe(false);\n  expect(cleanup).toHaveBeenCalledOnce();\n  expect(report.incompleteReason).not.toContain(\"Target cleanup failed\");\n});\n\nit(\"proves a target-supplied failure phase safe before emitting it\", async () => {\n  const report = await runMcpFnTargetSuite({ target: customTarget({\n    kind: \"failed-open\",\n    redact: <T>(value: T): T => value instanceof Error\n      ? { name: value.name, message: value.message, phase: \"vendor-phase\" } as T\n      : value,\n    open: async () => { throw new Error(\"cannot open\"); },\n  }) });\n  expect(report).toMatchObject({\n    ok: false,\n    status: \"incomplete\",\n    failure: { phase: \"vendor-phase\" },\n  });\n});\n\n\nit.each([\"metadata\", \"failure\"])(\"applies custom target redaction to finalized suite %s\", async mode => {\n  const secret = \"custom-owned-secret\";\n  const server = createMcpFnServer({\n    info: { name: secret, version: \"1.0.0\" },\n    registry: new McpFnRegistry().register({\n      name: \"visible-tool\", description: \"Fixture tool\", inputSchema: { type: \"object\" },\n      handler: async () => structuredResult({ ok: true }),\n    }),\n  });\n  const target = customTarget({\n    kind: \"custom\",\n    descriptor: { label: secret },\n    redact: <T>(value: T): T => {\n      const plain = value instanceof Error ? { name: value.name, message: value.message } : value;\n      return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(plain).replaceAll(secret, \"[REDACTED]\")) as T;\n    },\n    open: async () => {\n      const [clientTransport, serverTransport] = InMemoryTransport.createLinkedPair();\nscripts/test-mcpfn-registry-install.mjs:35:    path.join(repoRoot, \"mcpfn/examples/external-http-server.mjs\"),\nscripts/test-mcpfn-registry-install.mjs:36:    path.join(root, \"external-http-server.mjs\"),\nscripts/test-mcpfn-registry-install.mjs:102:const server = spawn(process.execPath, [\"external-http-server.mjs\"], {\nscripts/test-mcpfn-registry-install.mjs:136:const server = spawn(process.execPath, [\"external-http-server.mjs\"], {\nmcpfn/cli/tests/cli.test.ts:429:      new URL(\"../../examples/external-http-server.mjs\", import.meta.url),\nscripts/test-mcpfn-external-server.mjs:13:const serverSource = path.join(repoRoot, \"mcpfn/examples/external-http-server.mjs\");\nmcpfn/testing/tests/suite.test.ts:222:it(\"proves a target-supplied failure phase safe before emitting it\", async () => {\nmcpfn/testing/tests/remote-target.test.ts:382:it(\"scrubs independently reflected structured authorization parameters\", async () => {\nmcpfn/testing/tests/remote-target.test.ts:408:])(\"rejects malf