{"timestamp":"2026-09-21T17:41:47.855Z","ordinal":6305,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0b3f5-d570-7a72-b668-401efd539e3b","turn_id":"01a0c508-53ab-7801-a347-b8e3419372fb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-80a4f97a-5723-4511-a943-9aa0e37fd1f0","process_id":"64210","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"Round 13 assessment|Round 12 completion|Round 11 termination\" .conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md && tail -n 50 .conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'Round 13 assessment|Round 12 completion|Round 11 termination' .conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md","query":"Round 13 assessment|Round 12 completion|Round 11 termination","path":"pr-170-remediation-ledger.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"tail -n 50 .conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md","name":"pr-170-remediation-ledger.md","path":".conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"198:## Round 13 assessment\n609:## Round 11 termination\n666:## Round 12 completion\n- Verification criteria: focused structured-authorization redaction and malformed-release regressions; a custom failed-open dynamic-phase report regression; complete affected testing-package tests/typecheck/build; Node 22 release gate; `git diff --check`; whole-batch diff review; and one final local/remote/PR-head comparison. Hosted review/check surfaces will not be fetched again this round.\n\n### Round 12 defect families\n\n| Stable family | Root cause / affected contract | Disposition | First seen | Last attempted | Repair / evidence state |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `MCP170-AUTHORIZATION-STRUCTURED-COMPONENTS` | Non-Basic structured authorization values register only the whole parameter block, allowing an independently reflected component to escape redaction | Actionable; recurring credential-discovery family | round 12 | round 12 | Bounded auth-param component discovery and malformed-input rejection selected |\n| `MCP170-DYNAMIC-FAILURE-PHASE-GUARD` | Suite structure capture omits a target-supplied normalized failure phase that final validation emits | Actionable; recurring structural-safety family | round 12 | round 12 | Exact connection-failure phase capture selected |\n| `MCP170-SONAR-GUARD-INITIALIZATION` | Suite orchestration initializes the structural guard with a value that is always overwritten before normal return | Valid analyzer finding | round 12 | round 12 | Definite control-flow assignment selected |\n| `MCP170-SONAR-REDACTION-NESTED-TERNARY` | Redaction object traversal nests role selection inside a conditional expression | Valid analyzer finding; recurring redaction-maintainability family | round 12 | round 12 | Explicit entry-role selection selected |\n| `MCP170-SONAR-THROW-THIS` | Three findings flag intentional retry-owner self-rejection | Invalid analyzer interpretation | round 10 | round 12 | Exact error identity remains the cleanup ownership token; preserve behavior |\n\n- Snapshot dispositions before mutation: 2 new unresolved current review threads deduplicate to 2 actionable root causes. Five current Sonar issues deduplicate to 2 valid maintainability roots and 3 invalid retry-owner findings. Older valid blockers and dispositions remain preserved; outdated status was not used as proof.\n- Required-check snapshot: 18 contexts comprised 13 successful, 1 neutral, 3 skipped, and 1 pending CodeRabbit context; there were no failing contexts. Sonar Quality Gate passed and `reviewDecision` was empty. No check polling is permitted.\n- Convergence state: not clean. Two new/actionable roots, recurring credential-discovery and structural-safety families, two valid analyzer findings, and the pending required check reset the clean streak to `0` despite the stable snapshot head.\n\n## Round 12 snapshot dispositions\n\n- Fixed: 2 new review root causes and 2 valid Sonar findings. `MCP170-AUTHORIZATION-STRUCTURED-COMPONENTS` now discovers quoted, escaped, decoded, raw-inner, and unquoted values from bounded non-Basic/Bearer auth-param lists while preserving simple opaque custom schemes and Basic decoding; malformed structured syntax fails inside the existing credential-lease cleanup boundary. `MCP170-DYNAMIC-FAILURE-PHASE-GUARD` now proves the normalized connection failure's exact emitted phase safe while the live target redactor remains available. The two analyzer findings received definite structural-guard assignment and explicit redaction entry-role selection.\n- Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale): 91 older unresolved threads retain their prior current-code dispositions (30 current and 61 outdated-only at this snapshot). Outdated status, resolved-thread counts, and acknowledgement-only comments were not used as proof.\n- Invalid / Accepted Risk: the 3 remaining Sonar `throw this` findings are invalid because exact error identity is the cleanup ownership token; the older payload-key-redaction finding retains its prior invalid disposition. No accepted risks.\n- Not Attempted: 0 valid code root causes. Both new review roots and both valid current Sonar findings were attempted in the single coordinated batch; hosted reviewer/analyzer confirmation is deferred to a future separately scheduled snapshot because post-push refetch is forbidden.\n- Unassessed: 0 captured threads, nested comments, review bodies, issue comments, raw inline comments, or current Sonar issues.\n\n## Round 12 verification evidence\n\n- Focused regressions: 37 target-suite tests and 92 remote-target tests passed (129 total). New cases prove dynamic normalized failure phases are admitted only after live-redactor classification; quoted, escaped, decoded, raw-inner, and unquoted structured authorization components redact; malformed auth-param lists reject; and their credential lease is revoked exactly once. Existing simple custom-scheme and Basic behavior remained green.\n- Complete affected-package suite: all 241 `@mcpfn/testing` tests passed. The package typechecked and built successfully under Node 22.\n- Release gate: the final `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed every reported dependency/package test, typecheck, and build; Playwright; mixed-entry redaction; official conformance; examples; ESM/CJS imports; dry-run packs; packed-consumer installation; and round trips. The first gate attempt identified only an absent pinned Playwright browser; installing that exact test runtime resolved the environment gap, and the final gate passed against the final code state.\n- `git diff --check` passed. Whole-batch review covered all four code/test files and decomposed the structured-credential parser to avoid a new complexity hotspot. The ledger remained untracked and will not be staged or committed.\n- Required-check snapshot: the single pre-mutation snapshot contained 18 contexts: 13 successful, 1 neutral, 3 skipped, and 1 pending CodeRabbit context. Sonar Quality Gate passed with 2 valid and 3 invalid current findings. No hosted checks or reviews were fetched after the snapshot.\n- Fix-induced regressions: the first focused dynamic-phase test incorrectly exercised the client's intentional raw-open normalization to `transport-connect`; the final test exercises the actual target-redactor normalization boundary. No regression remained after focused tests, the complete package suite, typecheck/build, whole-diff review, or the final release gate.\n\n## Round 12 convergence\n\n- Trend: improving but nonterminal. All selected review and valid analyzer roots have coordinated repairs and no local regression remains, but this code-changing round cannot be clean and the sole immediate check snapshot contained a pending reviewer context.\n- Valid blocking root causes before / after: 2 new review roots plus 2 valid analyzer findings / 0 deliberately deferred valid code roots, with hosted verification pending a future separately scheduled assessment.\n- New defects: structured authorization component leakage and omission of a dynamic normalized failure phase from the live structural-safety candidate set.\n- Recurring families: credential discovery and structural safety recurred; both were repaired at shared producer/finalization boundaries.\n- Clean streak: `0` (reset by new/actionable roots, recurring families, this code-changing round, and the pending required check in the sole snapshot).\n- Head stability before mutation: the complete snapshot stayed at `9ee45f4385f3b354f0e27396fe0e86dafa5ee41f` throughout assessment. Final local/remote/PR head evidence will be recorded after the one allowed push and one allowed comparison.\n\n## Round 12 completion\n\n- Commit / push: one commit `d12812dfae99cc0905aa93365f9b9ed5c42065f2` (`fix(mcpfn): harden credential report safety`) and one successful push through existing `origin` to `codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910`.\n- Head verification (one comparison only): local head, `origin/codex/mcp-1-transport-neutral-conformance-0910`, and PR 170 head all equal `d12812dfae99cc0905aa93365f9b9ed5c42065f2`; PR 170 remained open. The branch was `+0/-0`, and the only remaining worktree item was the untracked `.conduct/` ledger directory.\n- Head stability: the assessed head remained `9ee45f4385f3b354f0e27396fe0e86dafa5ee41f` through selection and verification; the single commit and push advanced local, remote, and PR head together to `d12812dfae99cc0905aa93365f9b9ed5c42065f2` in the one allowed post-push comparison.\n- Result: nonterminal recurring run. A future separately scheduled assessment must inspect the new head's complete review/check surfaces once; this code-changing round cannot count toward the clean streak.\n- Automation `4442e7f3-60f4-4125-a8e4-c818ac40fc82` remains disabled from the earlier retrieval-discovery stop and was not silently re-enabled during this manual round.\n- No post-push review refetch, CI poll, review