ferred analyzer family.\n- New defects: inspector cleanup ownership and public-client token-error status handling; secondary I/O replacement is a recurrence of cleanup ownership.\n- Recurring families: cleanup ownership recurred for the third scheduled assessment; the reset-trigger subsystem assessment established a complete coordinated repair before mutation.\n- Fix-induced regressions: none after focused regressions, affected-package typechecks, complete diff review, and the release gate. One initial root-level Vitest command bypassed package configs and failed before collection because compile-time version defines were absent; configured package scripts superseded it and passed.\n- Oldest deferred blocker: `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY` from round 1. It remains Not Attempted and therefore prevents a clean assessment despite terminal hosted checks.\n- Clean streak: `0` (reset by actionable/new findings, a recurring family, this code-changing round, and the deferred analyzer family).\n- Head stability: the complete snapshot stayed at `eda8c5b01fa394e35174a88a6bdca078d793ec8c`; the authorized round then advanced local, remote, and PR head together to `9371beeb842106255854ee40f951819fb72ebed8` in the one allowed comparison.\n\n## Round 3 verification evidence\n\n- Focused testing: 20 CLI cleanup/redaction regressions and 53 hosted-authorization regressions passed.\n- Typechecks: `@mcpfn/cli` and `@mcpfn/testing` passed.\n- Release gate: `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed all package tests/builds, Playwright, official conformance, mixed-entry redaction, examples, ESM/CJS imports, package dry-runs, packed-consumer installation, and round trips.\n- `git diff --check`: passed; the whole seven-file code/test batch was reviewed before staging.\n- Hosted CI/reviewer state will not be refetched or polled after this snapshot.\n\n## Round 3 termination\n\n- Result: nonterminal recurring run; automation remains enabled for a future sepa