{"timestamp":"2026-09-21T17:50:41.835Z","ordinal":6455,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016ab16e4bc4b087d0bcb3e270cd494c34","status":"completed","call_id":"call_D06oWGfduxjTVm1YxLoh57aL","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170/.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md\\n@@\\n - Convergence state: not clean. Three new/actionable roots and recurring credential-grammar and structural-safety families reset the clean streak to `0` despite the stable head and terminal successful check snapshot.\\n+\\n+## Round 13 snapshot dispositions\\n+\\n+- Fixed: 3 new review root causes. `MCP170-AUTHORIZATION-CREDENTIAL-GRAMMAR` now recognizes the complete token68 alphabet plus terminal padding before auth-param discovery while retaining whole-token redaction. `MCP170-DYNAMIC-FAILURE-PHASE-EVIDENCE` now exercises both safe pass-through and target-redactor collision rejection. `MCP170-EXTERNAL-FIXTURE-REQUEST-BOUNDARY` now delegates from a synchronous Node listener to one guarded async handler, returns 400 for an invalid request URL, and retains 401/404/413/500 behavior.\\n+- Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale): 92 older unresolved threads retain their prior current-code dispositions (31 current and 61 outdated-only at this snapshot). Pullfrog's no-new-issues review was acknowledgement evidence, not a substitute for current-code assessment; outdated status was not used as proof.\\n+- Invalid / Accepted Risk: the 3 current Sonar `throw this` findings remain invalid because exact error identity is the cleanup ownership token; the older payload-key-redaction finding retains its prior invalid disposition. No accepted risks.\\n+- Not Attempted: 0 valid code root causes. All 3 new review roots were attempted in the single coordinated batch; hosted reviewer confirmation is deferred to a future separately scheduled snapshot because post-push refetch is forbidden.\\n+- Unassessed: 0 captured threads, nested comments, review bodies, issue comments, raw inline comments, or current Sonar issues.\\n+\\n+## Round 13 verification evidence\\n+\\n+- Focused regressions: 38 target-suite tests and 94 remote-target tests passed (132 total). The tests distinguish padded token68 from structured auth parameters and prove both accepted and colliding target-authored phases.\\n+- External fixture: `node scripts/test-mcpfn-external-server.mjs` passed against the real child server. A malformed `Host: [invalid` received 400, a subsequent `/not-found` request received 404, and the same process then completed two authenticated scenarios plus the expected unauthenticated failure.\\n+- Complete affected-package suite: all 244 `@mcpfn/testing` tests passed. The package typechecked and built successfully under Node 22; both changed `.mjs` files passed `node --check`.\\n+- Release gate: the final `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed every reported dependency/package test, typecheck, and build; Playwright; the external authenticated server probe; mixed-entry redaction; official conformance; examples; ESM/CJS imports; dry-run packs; packed-consumer installation; and round trips. The first attempt identified only the ephemeral missing Playwright headless-shell cache; reinstalling the pinned runtime resolved that environment gap, and the unchanged batch passed.\\n+- `git diff --check` passed. Whole-batch review covered all five code/test files, their request/error boundaries, and the credential/report consumers. The ledger remained untracked and will not be staged or committed.\\n+- Required-check snapshot: the single pre-mutation snapshot contained 18 terminal contexts: 14 successful, 1 neutral, and 3 skipped; Sonar Quality Gate, CodeRabbit, Cubic, and Pullfrog were successful. No hosted checks or reviews were fetched after the snapshot.\\n+- Fix-induced regressions: none found by focused tests, the real fixture process, the complete testing package suite, typecheck/build, syntax checks, whole-diff review, or the release gate.\\n+\\n+## Round 13 convergence\\n+\\n+- Trend: improving but nonterminal. All 3 new review roots have coordinated repairs and no local regression remains, but this code-changing round cannot be clean and hosted reviewers have not assessed the resulting head.\\n+- Valid blocking root causes before / after: 3 new review roots / 0 deliberately deferred valid code roots, with hosted confirmation pending a future separately scheduled assessment.\\n+- New defects: token68/auth-param grammar ambiguity, missing fail-closed evidence for dynamic failure phases, and an unguarded external-fixture request parse.\\n+- Recurring families: credential grammar and structural safety recurred; both were repaired at their shared classification/evidence boundaries. The external fixture defect was repaired at the complete request boundary rather than only moving one expression.\\n+- Clean streak: `0` (reset by new/actionable roots, recurring families, this code-changing round, and the pending post-publication assessment).\\n+- Head stability before mutation: the complete snapshot stayed at `d12812dfae99cc0905aa93365f9b9ed5c42065f2` throughout assessment and local verification. Final local/remote/PR head evidence will be recorded after the one allowed push and one allowed comparison.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0c508-53ab-7801-a347-b8e3419372fb","create_time":1790012992.400568}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-21T17:50:41.887Z","ordinal":6456,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0b3f5-d570-7a72-b668-401efd539e3b","turn_id":"01a0c508-53ab-7801-a347-b8e3419372fb","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-1582a59e-68c6-4998-9d7c-1bca0a3b3ff0","changes":{"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170/.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -673 +673,28 @@\n - Convergence state: not clean. Three new/actionable roots and recurring credential-grammar and structural-safety families reset the clean streak to `0` despite the stable head and terminal successful check snapshot.\n+\n+## Round 13 snapshot dispositions\n+\n+- Fixed: 3 new review root causes. `MCP170-AUTHORIZATION-CREDENTIAL-GRAMMAR` now recognizes the complete token68 alphabet plus terminal padding before auth-param discovery while retaining whole-token redaction. `MCP170-DYNAMIC-FAILURE-PHASE-EVIDENCE` now exercises both safe pass-through and target-redactor collision rejection. `MCP170-EXTERNAL-FIXTURE-REQUEST-BOUNDARY` now delegates from a synchronous Node listener to one guarded async handler, returns 400 for an invalid request URL, and retains 401/404/413/500 behavior.\n+- Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale): 92 older unresolved threads retain their prior current-code dispositions (31 current and 61 outdated-only at this snapshot). Pullfrog's no-new-issues review was acknowledgement evidence, not a substitute for current-code assessment; outdated status was not used as proof.\n+- Invalid / Accepted Risk: the 3 current Sonar `throw this` findings remain invalid because exact error identity is the cleanup ownership token; the older payload-key-redaction finding retains its prior invalid disposition. No accepted risks.\n+- Not Attempted: 0 valid code root causes. All 3 new review roots were attempted in the single coordinated batch; hosted reviewer confirmation is deferred to a future separately scheduled snapshot because post-push refetch is forbidden.\n+- Unassessed: 0 captured threads, nested comments, review bodies, issue comments, raw inline comments, or current Sonar issues.\n+\n+## Round 13 verification evidence\n+\n+- Focused regressions: 38 target-suite tests and 94 remote-target tests passed (132 total). The tests distinguish padded token68 from structured auth parameters and prove both accepted and colliding target-authored phases.\n+- External fixture: `node scripts/test-mcpfn-external-server.mjs` passed against the real child server. A malformed `Host: [invalid` received 400, a subsequent `/not-found` request received 404, and the same process then completed two authenticated scenarios plus the expected unauthenticated failure.\n+- Complete affected-package suite: all 244 `@mcpfn/testing` tests passed. The package typechecked and built successfully under Node 22; both changed `.mjs` files passed `node --check`.\n+- Release gate: the final `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed every reported dependency/package test, typecheck, and build; Playwright; the external authenticated server probe; mixed-entry redaction; official conformance; examples; ESM/CJS imports; dry-run packs; packed-consumer installation; and round trips. The first attempt identified only the ephemeral missing Playwright headless-shell cache; reinstalling the pinned runtime resolved that environment gap, and the unchanged batch passed.\n+- `git diff --check` passed. Whole-batch review covered all five code/test files, their request/error boundaries, and the credential/report consumers. The ledger remained untracked and will not be staged or committed.\n+- Required-check snapshot: the single pre-mutation snapshot contained 18 terminal contexts: 14 successful, 1 neutral, and 3 skipped; Sonar Quality Gate, CodeRabbit, Cubic, and Pullfrog were successful. No hosted checks or reviews were fetched after the snapshot.\n+- Fix-induced regressions: none found by focused tests, the real fixture process, the complete testing package suite, typecheck/build, syntax checks, whole-diff review, or the release gate.\n+\n+## Round 13 convergence\n+\n+- Trend: improving but nonterminal. All 3 new review roots have coordinated repairs and no local regression remains, but this code-changing round cannot be clean and hosted reviewers have not assessed the resulting head.\n+- Valid blocking root causes before / after: 3 new review roots / 0 deliberately deferred valid code roots, with hosted confirmation pending a future separately scheduled assessment.\n+- New defects: token68/auth-param grammar ambiguity, missing fail-closed evidence for dynamic failure phases, and an unguarded external-fixture request parse.\n+- Recurring families: credential grammar and structural safety recurred; both were repaired at their shared classification/evidence boundaries. The external fixture defect was repaired at the complete request boundary rather than only moving one expression.\n+- Clean streak: `0` (reset by new/actionable roots, recurring families, this code-changing round, and the pending post-publication assessment).\n+- Head stability before mutation: the complete snapshot stayed at `d12812dfae99cc0905aa93365f9b9ed5c42065f2` throughout assessment and local verification. Final local/remote/PR head evidence will be recorded after the one allowed push and one allowed comparison.\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170/.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1790013041884,"completed_at_ms":1790013041887}}
