e verified commit/push; convergence deferred)\n   640\t\n   641\t### keywords\n   642\t\n   643\t- 9ee45f4385f3b354f0e27396fe0e86dafa5ee41f, credential-redaction, structural-collision, cleanup-ownership, 332 threads, 93 unresolved, gate:mcpfn-release, .conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md\n   644\t\n   645\t## User preferences\n   646\t\n   647\t- when the user invokes `use-skillplane PR #170 pr-refetch-fix` -> retrieve the exact live hosted workflow; make one snapshot/fix/verify/commit/push pass, verify the required head once, then stop without refetching reviews, polling CI, or merging. [Task 1]\n   648\t- when the user says “Commit and push directly to origin dev only those changes” -> use a clean worktree and an explicit file allowlist; never stage the whole dirty checkout. [Task 2]\n   649\t- when the user asks what to preserve versus delete and then says “proceed” -> classify every path, preserve unique evidence, and use recoverable Trash only for clearly obsolete artifacts. [Task 2]\n   650\t- for convergence requests, count root causes rather than comments, preserve deferred findings in a compact untracked ledger, and terminate after the one authorized hosted round. [Task 3]\n   651\t\n   652\t## Reusable knowledge\n   653\t\n   654\t- Use `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other` for GitHub commands. Page every GraphQL `reviewThreads` cursor: PR #170’s first 100-thread result had `hasNextPage: true`; only a three-page, 284-thread snapshot was complete. [Task 1]\n   655\t- Treat credential-safe redaction, omission accounting, structural integrity, and replayable inspector exports as one contract. Reject variable-expanded and scrubbed duplicate keys before `Object.fromEntries()` silently drops data; never echo a resolved key that could be a credential; export a collision-free `${UPPER_CASE_VARIABLE}` marker or an explicitly incomplete safe artifact. [Task 1]\n   656\t- `npm run gate:mcpfn-release` is the validated Node 22 release gate. Local green gate and matching pushed heads do not prove hosted CI or merge readiness. [Task 1]\n   657\t- Track credential cleanup dynamically: revoke failures are `token-revocation`, disposal failures after successful revoke are `transport-close`; redact reconstructed fields including target `kind`, and keep CLI failure safe when cleanup has no report. [Task 1]\n   658\t- For a stale dirty dev checkout: fetch `origin/dev`, create a clean detached worktree, stage the exact allowlist, verify the commit parent equals the fetched tip, push `HEAD:dev`, verify remote SHA, and explain that the original checkout remains stale until separately reconciled. Compare apparent changes byte-for-byte to remote before treating them as unique. [Task 2]\n   659\t- Complete `reviewThreads` pagination and verify stable head before edits. In round 11, optional inspector keys were checked only when emitted, custom redactor/fallback safety was checked against final output, and suite projection/structure capture moved behind unconditional cleanup; Node 22 full `gate:mcpfn-release` passed before the sole commit/push. [Task 3]\n   660\t\n   661\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   662\t\n   663\t- Do not treat `hasNextPage: true` as a complete review snapshot, use Jest-only `--runInBand` with Vitest, weaken an invariant for a colliding fixture, or claim merge readiness while post-push checks remain pending. A branch-remote push can precede the PR API head; record that state as unverified/stale. [Task 1]\n   664\t- Do not reformat installer-managed generated hook files without authorization. Do not use `rm -rf` for cleanup; archive meaningful evidence and use `/usr/bin/trash` for recoverable deletion. [Task 2]\n   665\t- Do not declare convergence after a code-changing round: round 11 ended clean-streak 0 with PR open and reviewer/analyzer confirmation deferred. Update stale tests to reject unprovable structure, but validate an actually emitted dynamic fallback rather than unused candidates. [Task 3]\n  1