{"timestamp":"2026-09-22T05:51:39.551Z","ordinal":6541,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0b3f5-d570-7a72-b668-401efd539e3b","turn_id":"01a0c7ab-235a-7900-93f6-a63dbefa6872","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-7d3e45ae-3847-45f0-92e8-778ed748c3ff","process_id":"15846","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,240p' /Users/serro/.agents/skills/skillplane/SKILL.md && sed -n '1,280p' /Users/serro/.agents/skills/composio-cli/SKILL.md && sed -n '1,240p' /Users/serro/.agents/skills/using-21nco-github/SKILL.md && rg -n \"PR #170|pr-refetch-fix|clean streak|convergence|GH_CONFIG_DIR\" /Users/serro/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | head -n 70"],"cwd":"file:///Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,240p' /Users/serro/.agents/skills/skillplane/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":"/Users/serro/.agents/skills/skillplane/SKILL.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,280p' /Users/serro/.agents/skills/composio-cli/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":"/Users/serro/.agents/skills/composio-cli/SKILL.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,240p' /Users/serro/.agents/skills/using-21nco-github/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":"/Users/serro/.agents/skills/using-21nco-github/SKILL.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'PR #170|pr-refetch-fix|clean streak|convergence|GH_CONFIG_DIR' /Users/serro/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md","query":"PR #170|pr-refetch-fix|clean streak|convergence|GH_CONFIG_DIR","path":"MEMORY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"---\nname: use-skillplane\ndescription: Use skillplane to resolve skill\n---\n\n# Skillplane\n\nSkillplane is user's hosted skills platform. Retrieve user's skill using the slug or skill name provided and use that to execute the requested task.\n\nNOTE: Always retrieve and read the hosted skill first before working on the task. If the skill is not found, return an error message indicating the skill could not be located.\n\n## Using skillplane\nTry these in this order to communicate with user's Skillplane for skill retrieval, creation, amend etc.\n1. Direct Skillplane MCP if available and authenticated\n2. Direct Skillplane CLI if available and authenticated\n3. Via Composio CLI if available and authenticated\n4. Via Rex CLI if available and authenticated\n\n## Using tools mentioned in skillplane skills\nWhen executing a skill retrieved from Skillplane, use the tools referenced within the skill's definition to complete the task. Example tools: Linear, Notion, etc. Tool/Integrations resolution order:\n1. Direct integrations or MCP if available and authenticated\n2. Via Orca CLI if available and authenticated\n3. Via Composio CLI if available and authenticated\n4. Via Rex CLI if available and authenticated\n---\nname: composio-cli\ndescription: Help users operate the published Composio CLI to find the right tool, connect accounts, inspect schemas, execute tools, subscribe to trigger events with `composio listen`, script workflows with `composio run`, and call authenticated app APIs with `composio proxy`. Use when the user asks how to do something with `composio`, wants to run a known tool slug, needs to discover a slug with `composio search`, fix a missing connection with `composio link`, inspect tool inputs with `--get-schema` or `--dry-run`, troubleshoot top-level CLI flows, or explicitly needs `composio dev` guidance.\n---\n\n<!-- AUTO-GENERATED: edit skills-src/composio-cli/index.ts and rebuild -->\n<!-- release-channel: stable -->\n\n# Composio CLI\n\n## Default Workflow\n\n1. Start with `composio execute <slug>` whenever the slug is known.\n2. If several independent tool calls must happen at once, use `composio execute -p/--parallel` with repeated `<slug> -d <json>` groups.\n3. If `execute` says the toolkit is not connected, run `composio link <toolkit>` and retry.\n4. If the arguments are unclear, run `composio execute <slug> --get-schema` or `--dry-run` before guessing.\n5. Reach for `composio search \"<task>\"` only when the slug is unknown. `search` accepts one or more queries, so batch related discovery work into a single command when useful.\n\n## `execute` - Run A Tool\n\nUse `execute` when the tool slug is already known.\n\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_GET_THE_AUTHENTICATED_USER -d '{}'\n```\n\nInspect required inputs without executing:\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE --get-schema\n```\n\nPreview safely:\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE --skip-connection-check --dry-run -d '{ owner: \"acme\", repo: \"app\", title: \"Bug report\", body: \"Steps to reproduce...\" }'\n```\n\nPass data from a file or stdin:\n```bash\ncomposio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE -d @issue.json\ncat issue.json | composio execute GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE -d -\n```\n\nUpload a local file:\n```bash\ncomposio execute SLACK_UPLOAD_OR_CREATE_A_FILE_IN_SLACK \\\n  --file ./image.png \\\n  -d '{ channels: \"C123\" }'\n```\n\nRun independent tool calls in parallel:\n```bash\ncomposio execute --parallel \\\n  GMAIL_SEND_EMAIL -d '{ recipient_email: \"a@b.com\", subject: \"Hi\" }' \\\n  GITHUB_CREATE_AN_ISSUE -d '{ owner: \"acme\", repo: \"app\", title: \"Bug\" }'\n```\n\nKey flags:\n- `--get-schema`: Inspect required arguments without executing the tool.\n- `--dry-run`: Preview the request shape without performing the action.\n- `--file`: Inject a local file path into a tool that exposes exactly one uploadable file argument.\n- `--parallel`: Execute multiple independent tool calls in the same invocation.\n- `--account`: Select which connected account to use by alias, word_id, or account id when multiple accounts exist for the same toolkit.\n\n- `--file` only works when the tool exposes a single uploadable file input. Otherwise use explicit `-d` JSON.\n\n## `search` - Find The Slug\n\nUse `search` only when the tool slug is not already known.\n\n```bash\ncomposio search \"create a github issue\"\ncomposio search \"send an email\" --toolkits gmail\ncomposio search \"send an email\" \"create a github issue\"\ncomposio search \"my emails\" \"my github issues\" --toolkits gmail,github\n```\n\n- Batch related discovery work into one `search` invocation, then move back to `execute` once the correct slugs are known.\n\n## `link` - Connect An Account\n\nUse `link` when `execute` reports that a toolkit is not connected, or when the user explicitly wants to authorize an account.\n\n```bash\ncomposio link gmail\ncomposio link googlecalendar --no-browser\n```\n\nKey flags:\n- `--alias`: Assign an alias to the connected account. Required when creating an additional account for the same toolkit.\n\n- Retry the original `execute` command after linking succeeds.\n\n## `proxy` - Raw API Access\n\nUse `proxy` when a toolkit supports a raw API operation that is easier than finding a dedicated tool slug.\n\n```bash\ncomposio proxy https://api.github.com/user --toolkit github --account work --method GET </dev/null\n```\n\nKey flags:\n- `--account`: Select which connected account to use by alias, word_id, or account id.\n\n## `run` - Scripting, LLMs, and Programmatic Workflows\n\nFor programmatic calls, loops, output plumbing, or anything beyond a single tool call, prefer `composio run`.\n\n`composio run` executes an inline ESM JavaScript/TypeScript snippet with authenticated `execute()`, `search()`, `proxy()`, and the experimental `experimental_subAgent()` helper pre-injected. No SDK setup required.\n\nChain multiple tools:\n```bash\ncomposio run '\n  const me = await execute(\"GITHUB_GET_THE_AUTHENTICATED_USER\");\n  const emails = await execute(\"GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS\", { max_results: 1 });\n  console.log({ login: me.data.login, fetchedEmails: !!emails.data });\n'\n```\n\nFan out with Promise.all:\n```bash\ncomposio run '\n  const [me, emails] = await Promise.all([\n    execute(\"GITHUB_GET_THE_AUTHENTICATED_USER\"),\n    execute(\"GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS\", { max_results: 5 }),\n  ]);\n  console.log({ login: me.data.login, emailCount: emails.data.messages?.length });\n'\n```\n\nFeed tool output into an LLM and get structured JSON back:\n```bash\ncomposio run --logs-off '\n  const emails = await execute(\"GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS\", { max_results: 5 });\n  const brief = await experimental_subAgent(\n    `Summarize these emails and count them.\\n\\n${emails.prompt()}`,\n    { schema: z.object({ summary: z.string(), count: z.number() }) }\n  );\n  console.log(brief.structuredOutput);\n'\n```\n\n- Use top-level `execute --parallel` instead when the user only needs a few independent tool calls and does not need script logic.\n\n## Auth\n\n```bash\ncomposio whoami   # check current session\ncomposio login    # authenticate if whoami fails\n```\n\n## Escalate Only When Needed\n\nIf the user is stuck on top-level commands or needs fallback inspection commands, load [references/troubleshooting.md](references/troubleshooting.md).\n\nIf the user explicitly asks about developer projects, auth configs, connected accounts, triggers, logs, orgs, or projects, load [references/composio-dev.md](references/composio-dev.md). `composio dev` is not the default end-user path.\n---\nname: using-21nco-github\ndescription: Uses the thyaravind GitHub account for repositories under dev/n or with a 21nCo origin. Use for any GitHub CLI, pull request, issue, release, or repository operation in those repositories.\n---\n\n# Using 21nCo GitHub\n\nFor any repository whose path is under `dev/n` or whose Git remote belongs to `21nCo`:\n\n- Run every `gh` command with `GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other`.\n- Verify `GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-other gh auth status` reports `thyaravind` as the active account before making changes.\n- Never use the default GitHub account or silently fall back to another account.\n- Use the existing `21nCo` remote for pushes. If `thyaravind` lacks permission, stop and report the denial instead of creating a fork or alternate remote.\n251:- 21nCo/super-functions, PR #183, PR #184, PR #185, PR #186, PR #187, PR #188, PR #189, PR #198, GH_CONFIG_DIR, reviewThreads(first:100), isResolved, isOutdated, SonarCloud, Node 18\n269:- Use `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other` for this private repository. Query paginated GraphQL `pullRequest.reviewThreads(first:100, after:$cursor)`; current unresolved (`isResolved == false && isOutdated == false`) threads are blockers, while outdated unresolved threads are separate. [Task 1]\n279:scope: Use when creating or verifying recurring Orca automations for a PR remediation workflow, especially when the user requests bounded convergence rather than an open-ended loop.\n282:## Task 1: Create a recurring PR #170 bounded remediation automation, success\n286:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T15-00-34-01a0b3da-775b-7a23-99f7-756289048919.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T10:24:08+00:00, thread_id=01a0b3da-775b-7a23-99f7-756289048919, automation created and read back)\n290:- Orca, orca automations create, --workspace-mode existing, --reuse-session, pr-refetch-fix, PR-170, rrule, Asia/Kolkata\n296:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T15-00-34-01a0b3da-775b-7a23-99f7-756289048919.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T10:24:08+00:00, thread_id=01a0b3da-775b-7a23-99f7-756289048919, thin pinned-dependency skill published)\n304:- when the user requested `every 30 min $use-skillplane pr-refetch-fix PR 170 until convergence` -> authorize one bounded remediation round per activation with explicit convergence/self-disable rules, not an open-ended review loop. [Task 1]\n306:- when the user said “refer existing pr-refetch-fix skill instead of copying” and required existing-session reuse -> compose against the pinned hosted skill and make `--reuse-session` an invariant. [Task 2]\n318:# Task Group: September 18 Superfunctions PR #179 and #133 blocked convergence assessments\n319:scope: Use for one bounded hosted remediation/convergence assessment when the remaining queue exposes cross-cutting root causes; preserve the untracked ledger and disable automation when coordinated repair is not safe.\n322:## Task 1: Assess PR #179 convergence without symptom patches, partial\n326:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/SFNS-4, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T16-30-28-01a0b42c-c4ea-7b61-a3b7-c7fffb0ed31d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T11:13:16+00:00, thread_id=01a0b42c-c4ea-7b61-a3b7-c7fffb0ed31d, broad root-cause queue; no mutation)\n330:- PR #179, SFNS-4, pr-refetch-fix, 321 threads, 60 current unresolved, root-causes, SonarQube, pr179-remediation-ledger.json, automation disabled\n332:## Task 2: Assess PR #133 convergence, disable automation, and set dependency-gated next steps, partial\n336:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-18T11-00-30-gEnj-pr133_convergence_blocked_next_steps.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-133, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T16-30-30-01a0b42c-ce2e-7173-9c5a-e6070f3586d5.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-21T08:40:34+00:00, thread_id=01a0b42c-ce2e-7173-9c5a-e6070f3586d5, no mutation; dependency-gated plan and automation disablement verified)\n340:- PR #133, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.2.0, revision-4, digest, config-loader-semantics, dev-watch-output-ancestor, search-scope-override-validation, PR #170, PR #171, remediation-ledger\n345:- when requesting convergence, count deduplicated root causes, inspect recurring/deferred families and shared invariants, preserve a compact untracked ledger, and disable automation when repair is blocked. [Task 1][Task 2]\n356:- Do not infer convergence from an earlier local zero count or classify unassessed threads as fixed/stale. When coordinated repair cannot be established, stop without edits/commits/pushes and retain the ledger. [Task 1][Task 2]\n372:- git worktree list --porcelain, gh pr list, GH_CONFIG_DIR, 21nCo/super-functions, 21nCo/superfunctions, docs/http-decode-params, sfns-4-rex-upstream, prunable-worktree, PR #188, PR #179, PR #170\n390:- Derive the repository slug from `git remote -v`: this checkout is `21nCo/super-functions`, not `21nCo/superfunctions`. For every `dev/n` GitHub command use `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other`. [Task 1]\n392:- At the September 17 snapshot, `superfunctions-dev`/`docs/http-decode-params` matched clean PR #188; SFNS-4/`sfns-4-rex-upstream` matched dirty PR #179; `/private/tmp/pr170-refetch-fix.h2yq4m` was missing and prunable, associated with PR #170. [Task 1]\n508:- pr-review-fix, PR #38, SKI-17, @datafn/server@0.1.3, cursor-pagination, Date, HTTP-serialization, createCursorStableReadAdapter, combined, regional, GH_CONFIG_DIR\n519:- Use `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other` as `thyaravind` for `dev/n`/21nCo GitHub work; do not fork if permissions fail. [Task 1]\n550:- SFNS-4, PR #179, pr-refetch-fix, reviewThreads, adapterNamespace, Retry-After, tenantId, SecFn readJson, e200f50d, 511c02a\n640:# Task Group: September 15 Superfunctions PR #170 bounded remediation and dirty-dev reconciliation\n641:scope: Use for live hosted `pr-refetch-fix` work on McpFn PR #170, or scoped publication/reconciliation from a dirty, stale Superfunctions dev checkout.\n644:## Task 1: Harden PR #170 redaction/export invariants in a bounded hosted round, success\n654:- PR #170, pr-refetch-fix, reviewThreads, GH_CONFIG_DIR, gate:mcpfn-release, McpFnRemoteCredentialLease, cleanupPhase, redaction, 8b23aaa, 1e45b794\n670:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-18T10-00-27-D3ej-pr170_round11_structural_redaction_cleanup_remediation.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T15-30-27-01a0b3f5-d570-7a72-b668-401efd539e3b.jsonl, updated_at=20