mpleted\nWall time 0.4 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"   561\t- `packages/datafn/src/server.ts` now passes `input.database.adapter` directly to `createDatafnServer`; `@datafn/server@0.1.3` preserves `Date` instances and nested arrays during relation omission. `domainModelAliases` in `packages/db/src/client.ts` retains the regional compatibility fix. [Task 1]\n   562\t- When `orca linear issue --current --full --json` reports `linear_no_linked_issue`, use `orca linear search` and retrieve the candidate issue explicitly. SKI-17 code/local regression scope was satisfied, but acceptance remains incomplete until skill detail, `SKILL.md`, and version history are verified and recorded in India, US, and EU. [Task 1]\n   563\t- Keep unrelated untracked Entire files out of an issue-specific commit. Their ESLint project-service parsing errors are separate from normal package typechecks. [Task 1]\n   564\t\n   565\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   566\t\n   567\t- A local review can be correct yet incomplete if it skips the tracker’s deployment acceptance criteria. Do not call SKI-17 acceptance-complete from local tests/package checks alone. [Task 1]\n   568\t\n   569\t# Task Group: September 16 Skillplane Linear issue verification and published-contract blocker\n   570\tscope: Use for `work-linear-issue` hosted workflow, determining whether an issue is already complete, or deciding whether a published AuthFn/DataFn contract supports implementation.\n   571\tapplies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/orca/workspaces/skillplane/*; reuse_rule=Linear state, PR heads, and package publication are live; retrieve the hosted workflow and inspect the complete issue before editing.\n   572\t\n   573\t## Task 1: Verify SKI-17 was already completed and merged, success\n   574\t\n   575\t### rollout_summary_files\n   576\t\n   577\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-16T11-53-05-Y8rx-ski_17_already_completed_and_merged_verification.md (cwd=/Users/serro/orca/workspaces/skillplane/ski-17-upgrade-skillplane-to-released-datafn-and, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/16/rollout-2026-09-16T17-23-05-01a0aa10-3955-7cf0-ad58-903933efe48b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-16T11:58:27+00:00, thread_id=01a0aa10-3955-7cf0-ad58-903933efe48b, SKI-17 Done and PR #38 merged; no duplicate work)\n   578\t\n   579\t### keywords\n   580\t\n   581\t- SKI-17, work-linear-issue, Orca Linear, oauth_token_invalid_grant, PR #38, e3ec4f6, 9483e27, origin/main\n   582\t\n   583\t## Task 2: Stop SKI-16 at unpublished AUTH-2 placement-context API, partial\n   584\t\n   585\t### rollout_summary_files\n   586\t\n   587\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-16T12-00-46-4nKt-ski_16_blocked_on_authfn_placement_context_api.md (cwd=/Users/serro/orca/workspaces/skillplane/ski-16-adopt-ticket-protected-direct-regional-da, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/16/rollout-2026-09-16T17-30-46-01a0aa17-4388-7d52-9744-5ce9cd46370d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-19T07:44:51+00:00, thread_id=01a0aa17-4388-7d52-9744-5ce9cd46370d, correctly blocked; clean worktree preserved)\n   588\t\n   589\t### keywords\n   590\t\n   591\t- SKI-16, AUTH-2, DATA-4, placement-context, routeProvider, authfn@0.2.0, @authfn/multi-region@0.1.1, @datafn/server@0.1.3\n   592\t\n   593\t## User preferences\n   594\t\n   595\t- when the user invokes the hosted `work linear issue` workflow with an exact Linear URL -\u003e retrieve the live workflow and use the complete issue as authoritative scope before editing. [Task 2]\n   596\t- when an issue is already Done with a merged PR -\u003e avoid duplicate branches, commits, comments, pushes, PRs, and reruns; report existing evidence and remaining gaps. [Task 1]\n   597\t\n   598\t## Reusable knowledge\n   599\t\n   600\t- When direct Skillplane/Linear MCP fails with `oauth_token_invalid_grant`, retrieve the hosted workflow via Composio and read the issue through `orca linear issue --current --full --json`; do not substitute cached instructions. [Task 1][Task 2]\n   601\t- SKI-17 PR #38 head `9483e27` merged as `e3ec4f6` in `origin/main`; prior local validation exists, while India/US/EU dev verification and cancelled SonarCloud remain explicit historical gaps. [Task 1]\n   602\t- DATA-4 direct-route APIs are published, but `authfn@0.2.0` / `@authfn/multi-region@0.1.1` lack the required AUTH-2 placement-context issuer. The current canonical client boundary is `/datafn`; do not locally recreate the missing credential contract. [Task 2]\n   603\t\n   604\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   605\t\n   606\t- Do not begin implementation from an issue title or stale branch; first inspect Linear, PR, clean checkout, package exports, and required published versions. [Task 1]\n   607\t- Stop before edits when a required upstream consumer contract exists only in source/unreleased work. Record exact package/version gap and resume only after publication or explicit authorization for an artifact/SHA. [Task 2]\n   608\t\n   609\t# Task Group: September 15 Superfunctions PR #170 bounded remediation and dirty-dev reconciliation\n   610\tscope: Use for live hosted `pr-refetch-fix` work on McpFn PR #170, or scoped publication/reconciliation from a dirty, stale Superfunctions dev checkout.\n   611\tapplies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev and /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170; reuse_rule=PR threads, heads, hosted checks, and checkout state must be revalidated live; preserve unrelated dirty state.\n   612\t\n   613\t## Task 1: Harden PR #170 redaction/export invariants in a bounded hosted round, success\n   614\t\n   615\t### rollout_summary_files\n   616\t\n   617\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-15T12-55-27-j4bW-pr_170_bounded_redaction_cleanup_remediation.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/09/15/rollout-2026-09-15T18-25-27-01a0a522-f7e4-7422-a0fb-002c30b622cc.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-16T12:17:41+00:00, thread_id=01a0a522-f7e