omments, 369 raw inline comments, and 18 check contexts.\n.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md:467:- Shared invariant: every emitted typed artifact must preserve credential-free authored keys and discriminators or fail closed; cleanup ownership must remain callable even when no safe artifact can be serialized; OAuth success evidence must accept only exact argument-free anti-cache directives; behavior-preserving maintainability work must keep these boundaries intact.\n.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md:468:- Producers and consumers: scenario creation plus inspector export feed replay artifacts; target/session close plus suite finalization feed direct callers and CLI JSON/JUnit/stdout; hosted OAuth response parsing feeds exchange and refresh case results; redaction, authorization, report, orchestration, CLI, and Node/Web adapters feed tests and required analysis.\n.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md:469:- Failure boundaries: fixed-key credential collisions cannot produce a typed scenario/report; structural report failure can coincide with a failed cleanup lease; parameterized cache directives do not prove anti-caching; broad analyzer refactors can regress credential redaction, lifecycle phases, bounded serialization, or exit classification.\n.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md:471:- Verification criteria: focused inspector, hosted-authorization, target-suite, report, CLI, conformance, adapter, and redaction regressions; affected package typechecks/builds; complete Node 22 release gate; `git diff --check`; one local/upstream/PR head comparison after at most one push. Hosted review/check surfaces will not be fetched again this round.\n.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md:477:| `MCP170-SCENARIO-KEY-STRUCTURE` | Inspector validates scenario discriminator values but not authored top-level keys, allowing a key-equal credential to survive export | Actionable | round 10 | round 10 | Coordinated key-boundary repair selected; regression uses credential `name` |\n.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md:480:| `MCP170-SONAR-REDACTION-DECOMPOSITION` | Redaction/credential helpers contain duplicated bounds, regex, and deeply nested traversal/lifecycle logic | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 11 findings grouped under shared credential/redaction contract |\n.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md:482:| `MCP170-SONAR-SUITE-ORCHESTRATION` | Suite orchestration contains dense comparisons, fallbacks, and control flow | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 5 findings grouped under report/lifecycle behavior preservation |\n.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md:487:| `MCP170-SONAR-INSPECTOR` | Secret-marker generation and export fallback selection contain avoidable constructs | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 2 findings grouped under replayable placeholder behavior |\n.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md:489:| `MCP170-SONAR-CUSTOM-TARGET-TYPE` | Custom-target redactor field redundantly combines optional syntax with `undefined` | Valid, coordinated analyzer work | round 1 | round 10 | 1 type-contract cleanup |\n.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md:493:- Convergence state: not clean. Three new review roots, the recurring cleanup-ownership family, and the now-assessed analyzer families reset the clean streak to `0` even though the snapshot head was stable and required checks were terminal.\n.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md:495:## Round 10 snapshot dispositions\n.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md:499:- Invalid / Accepted Risk: the older property-key-redaction finding remains invalid based on observed payload-key behavior. The analyzer's retry-owner `throw this` family is invalid because object identity is the ownership token; the suite instance was removed incidentally by a shared retry helper, while the three remaining instances preserve required owner identity. No accepted risks.\n.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md:500:- Not Attempted: 0 valid code root causes. The 34 va