it runScenarios(client, [{\nmcpfn/testing/tests/testing.test.ts:239:        name: \"redacts verifier errors\",\nmcpfn/testing/tests/testing.test.ts:248:      expect(JSON.stringify(redactedFailure)).not.toContain(\"secret\");\nmcpfn/testing/tests/testing.test.ts:249:      expect(JSON.stringify(redactedFailure)).not.toContain(\"access_token=token\");\nmcpfn/testing/tests/testing.test.ts:250:      expect(JSON.stringify(redactedFailure)).toContain(\"REDACTED\");\nmcpfn/testing/tests/testing.test.ts:254:        name: \"deferred live smoke\",\nmcpfn/testing/tests/testing.test.ts:259:        incompleteReason: \"Requires controlled live-provider credentials\",\nmcpfn/testing/tests/testing.test.ts:476:      name: \"deferred\",\nmcpfn/testing/tests/testing.test.ts:503:        { name: \"create\", kind: \"tools.call:task\", tool: \"deferred\", task: { ttl: 5_000 } },\nmcpfn/testing/tests/testing.test.ts:693:  it(\"does not inherit selected credential environment variables into conformance\", () => {\nmcpfn/testing/tests/testing.test.ts:704:  it(\"injects credentials through a fixed loopback conformance proxy\", async () => {\nmcpfn/testing/tests/testing.test.ts:774:    })).rejects.toThrow(/at least one credential header/);\nmcpfn/testing/tests/testing.test.ts:777:  it(\"rejects invalid authenticated conformance URLs before acquiring credentials\", async () => {\nmcpfn/testing/tests/testing.test.ts:783:      credential: {\nmcpfn/testing/tests/reports.test.ts:11:  it(\"preserves structured failure fields while redacting sensitive details\", () => {\nmcpfn/testing/tests/reports.test.ts:39:  it(\"redacts names and messages, removes invalid XML controls, and bounds JUnit\", () => {\nmcpfn/testing/tests/reports.test.ts:67:  it(\"handles redaction truncation beyond 1000 results\", () => {\nmcpfn/testing/README.md:20:- bounded, redacted scenario and target-suite reports;\nmcpfn/testing/README.md:24:Official conformance validates protocol behavior. McpFn scenarios validate product behavior. Production MCP servers should run both. For a protected local endpoint, use `runAuthenticatedOfficialConformance({ url, credential })`; it requires a literal loopback upstream, binds a temporary loopback-only streaming proxy, pins every request to the configured upstream path, injects bounded credential headers without printing them, and closes the proxy and attempts credential revocation/disposal after the pinned official runner exits. Credential cleanup retries up to three times. If all attempts fail, it throws `McpFnConformanceCleanupError`; retain that error and call `await error.retryCleanup()` after the provider recovers. The error contains no raw credential fields, and a successful retry releases the retained lease.\nmcpfn/testing/README.md:61:`authenticatedHttpTarget()` accepts a URL plus either a static credential or an\nmcpfn/testing/README.md:63:credential and may revoke and dispose it. McpFn applies the headers only to the\nmcpfn/testing/README.md:64:fixed target, refuses redirect following, excludes credentials from target\nmcpfn/testing/README.md:65:descriptors and reports, and releases the credential exactly once even when\nmcpfn/testing/README.md:78:    credential: {\nmcpfn/testing/README.md:89:Use a provider instead of a static credential for short-lived OAuth access\nmcpfn/testing/README.md:108:Import the transport-level testkit from `@mcpfn/testing/auth`. The application adapter owns only credential issuance and revocation; McpFn owns the common rejection and lifecycle matrix.\nmcpfn/testing/README.md:127:    async revoke(credential) {\nmcpfn/testing/README.md:128:      await skillplaneTestAuth.revokeApiKey(credential);\nmcpfn/testing/README.md:171:When credentials come from environment variables, pass their names in `sensitiveEnvironmentVariables` to authenticated official conformance. Those names are removed case-insensitively before the upstream runner is spawned. The library cannot infer the source of arbitrary provider-returned headers.\nmcpfn/testing/README.md:174:`stdio: \"inherit\"` is requested, so credential values can be removed before output\nmcpfn/testing/README.md:175:is returned. `outputDir` is rejected before credentials are acquired because the\nmcpfn/testing/README.md:176:upstream runner writes raw artifacts directly. Persist the returned redacted result\nmcpfn/testing/README.md:180:Authenticated targets provide credential-aware redaction to client diagnostic/event listeners and inspector snapshots and exports while their credentials are active. Export raw operation results before closing the client; application-facing protocol return values retain their original contents. Recorded inspector events are scrubbed before storage.\nmcpfn/testing/README.md:182:When authenticated conformance cleanup exhausts retries, `McpFnConformanceCleanupError.result` retains the original runner stdout, stderr, exit code (or 1 for an otherwise successful run), and failure. A separate `cleanupFailure` records cleanup exhaustion; the overall result is failed. The CLI persists this redacted result before exiting nonzero.\nmcpfn/testing/README.md:188:`McpFnTargetSuiteCleanupError`. Its `report` contains the bounded, redacted failed\nmcpfn/testing/README.md:189:snapshot. Retain the error and call `await error.retryCleanup()` to retry the\nmcpfn/testing/src/auth-core.ts:31:  revoke?(credential: McpFnAuthCredential): void | Promise<void>;\nmcpfn/testing/src/auth-core.ts:36:    | \"missing-credential\"\nmcpfn/testing/src/auth-core.ts:37:    | \"invalid-credential\"\nmcpfn/testing/src/auth-core.ts:38:    | \"valid-credential\"\nmcpfn/testing/src/auth-core.ts:40:    | \"expired-credential\"\nmcpfn/testing/src/auth-core.ts:43:    | \"revoked-credential\";\nmcpfn/testing/src/auth-core.ts:67:    credential: McpFnAuthCredential,\nmcpfn/testing/src/auth-core.ts:186:  let credential: McpFnAuthCredential | undefined;\nmcpfn/testing/src/auth-core.ts:188:    credential = await prepare();\nmcpfn/testing/src/auth-core.ts:189: