error boundary, allowing malformed Host input to reject the listener promise | Actionable external-fixture resilience defect | round 13 | round 13 | Synchronous listener plus fully guarded handler and real malformed-Host probe selected |\n| `MCP170-SONAR-THROW-THIS` | Three findings flag intentional retry-owner self-rejection | Invalid analyzer interpretation | round 10 | round 13 | Exact error identity remains the cleanup ownership token; preserve behavior |\n\n- Snapshot dispositions before mutation: 3 new unresolved current threads deduplicate to 3 actionable root causes. Three current Sonar issues are the preserved invalid retry-owner family. Older valid blockers and dispositions remain preserved; outdated status was not used as proof.\n- Required-check snapshot: all 18 contexts were terminal: 14 successful, 1 neutral, and 3 skipped. Sonar Quality Gate passed, CodeRabbit was successful, and `reviewDecision` was empty. No check polling is permitted.\n- Convergence state: not clean. Three new/actionable roots and recurring credential-grammar and structural-safety families reset the clean streak to `0` despite the stable head and terminal successful check snapshot.\n\n## Round 13 snapshot dispositions\n\n- Fixed: 3 new review root causes. `MCP170-AUTHORIZATION-CREDENTIAL-GRAMMAR` now recognizes the complete token68 alphabet plus terminal padding before auth-param discovery while retaining whole-token redaction. `MCP170-DYNAMIC-FAILURE-PHASE-EVIDENCE` now exercises both safe pass-through and target-redactor collision rejection. `MCP170-EXTERNAL-FIXTURE-REQUEST-BOUNDARY` now delegates from a synchronous Node listener to one guarded async handler, returns 400 for an invalid request URL, and retains 401/404/413/500 behavior.\n- Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale): 92 older unresolved threads retain their prior current-code dispositions (31 current and 61 outdated-only at this snapshot). Pullfrog's no-new-issues review was acknowledgement evidence, not a substitute for curr