values; the client authors inspector snapshot and timeline envelope primitives; the suite authors primary and fallback report envelopes; JSON/JUnit writers, direct `snapshot()` callers, CLI consumers, and cleanup-retry owners consume those artifacts; the external fixture child emits stderr consumed by probe diagnostics.\n+- Failure boundaries: numeric and boolean credentials colliding with snapshot/report envelope fields; stored timeline events that must not be passed through a custom redactor twice; primary report finalization falling back after a serialized primitive collision; retained cleanup ownership on fail-closed paths; and HTTP probe timeouts with a live or failed child process.\n+- Coordinated repair: extend structural-value validation to string, number, and boolean authored values; validate each inspector-authored primitive at construction while continuing to clone already-redacted stored events without replaying their hooks; pass the suite fallback through the same built-in target-credential scrub and fail closed on any credential-safety failure; add focused numeric/boolean regressions; include fixture stderr in probe-timeout errors; and remove the two valid new analyzer findings without changing authorization grammar.\n+- Verification criteria: focused inspector, suite, and remote-target regressions; external fixture execution; complete affected package tests/typechecks/builds; Node 22 release gate; `git diff --check`; whole-batch diff review; and one final local/remote/PR-head comparison. Hosted review/check surfaces will not be fetched again this round.\n+\n+### Round 14 defect families\n+\n+| Stable family | Root cause / affected contract | Disposition | First seen | Last attempted | Repair / evidence state |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| `MCP170-NONSTRING-STRUCTURAL-CREDENTIAL-SAFETY` | Inspector-authored numeric/boolean envelope values bypass per-field string redaction, and suite fallback finalization bypasses the final credential-aware scrub | Actionable; recurring structural-safety family; two comments deduplicated to one root | round 14 | round 14 | Coordinated inspector/suite finalization repair selected |\n+| `MCP170-EXTERNAL-PROBE-DIAGNOSTIC-CONTEXT` | External fixture probe timeout omits retained child stderr, obscuring failure state | Actionable diagnostics defect | round 14 | round 14 | Thread stderr reader through probe helper and timeout selected |\n+| `MCP170-AUTHORIZATION-STATIC-ANALYSIS` | The authorization discovery helper crossed the configured complexity threshold and the token68 slash spelling triggers a valid maintainability finding | Actionable analyzer family; no runtime-contract change | round 14 | round 14 | Basic decoding extraction and equivalent slash spelling selected |\n+| `MCP170-SONAR-THROW-THIS` | Three findings flag intentional retry-owner self-rejection | Invalid analyzer interpretation | round 10 | round 14 | Exact error identity remains the cleanup ownership token; preserve behavior |\n+\n+- Snapshot dispositions before mutation: 3 new unresolved current threads deduplicate to 2 actionable review root causes; 2 new current Sonar findings are valid and join one maintainability family; 3 older current Sonar findings retain the invalid retry-owner disposition. Older valid blockers and dispositions remain preserved; outdated status was not used as proof.\n+- Required-check snapshot: all 18 contexts were terminal, but Pullfrog completed with `FAILURE`; 13 were successful, 1 neutral, and 3 skipped. Sonar Quality Gate, CodeRabbit, and Cubic were successful, and `reviewDecision` was empty. No check polling is permitted.\n+- Convergence state: not clean. New/actionable roots, a recurring structural-safety family, and the failed required Pullfrog check reset the clean streak to `0` despite the stable head.\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170/.conduct/pr-