yzer confirmation is deferred to a future separately scheduled snapshot because post-push refetch is forbidden.\n+- Unassessed: 0 captured threads, nested comments, review bodies, issue comments, raw inline comments, or current Sonar issues.\n+\n+## Round 14 verification evidence\n+\n+- Focused regressions: 33 authenticated inspector artifact tests plus 39 target-suite and 94 remote-target tests passed (166 total). New cases prove numeric/boolean authenticated credentials cannot survive in inspector snapshot primitives and a primitive collision cannot escape through a suite fallback.\n+- Complete affected-package suites: all 45 `@mcpfn/client`, 43 `@mcpfn/inspector`, and 245 `@mcpfn/testing` tests passed (333 total). All three packages typechecked and built successfully under Node 22.\n+- External fixture: `node scripts/test-mcpfn-external-server.mjs` passed against the real child server, including malformed-Host 400, subsequent 404/server survival, two authenticated scenarios, expected unauthenticated failure, and JSON/JUnit artifacts.\n+- Release gate: the final `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed every reported dependency/package test, typecheck, and build; Playwright; mixed-entry redaction; official conformance; examples; ESM/CJS imports; dry-run packs; packed-consumer installation; and round trips.\n+- `git diff --check` and the changed script's syntax check passed. Whole-batch review covered all seven code/test files, the final artifact boundaries, custom-hook single-application rule, cleanup ownership, authorization grammar equivalence, and child-process diagnostic flow. The ledger remained untracked and will not be staged or committed.\n+- Required-check snapshot: the single pre-mutation snapshot contained 18 terminal contexts: 13 successful, 1 failed Pullfrog context, 1 neutral, and 3 skipped; Sonar Quality Gate, CodeRabbit, and Cubic were successful. No hosted checks or reviews were fetched after the snapshot.\n+- Fix-induced regressions: none. One initial test assertion incorrectly treated the thrown client error's own `retryable: false` metadata as a persisted suite report; the security contract is that no fallback report is returned, and the final regression asserts that fail-closed result. A parallel package-validation attempt also read the client's prior declaration output before its concurrent rebuild completed; dependency-ordered inspector typecheck/build passed without a code change. No regression remained after focused tests, complete suites, dependency-ordered typechecks/builds, external process execution, whole-diff review, or the release gate.\n+\n+## Round 14 convergence\n+\n+- Trend: improving but nonterminal. All selected review and valid analyzer roots have coordinated repairs and no local regression remains, but this code-changing round cannot be clean, the sole immediate snapshot contained a failed required check, and hosted reviewers have not assessed the resulting head.\n+- Valid blocking root causes before / after: 2 deduplicated new review roots plus 1 analyzer maintainability family / 0 deliberately deferred valid code roots, with hosted confirmation and Pullfrog recovery pending a future separately scheduled assessment.\n+- New defects: non-string structural credential collisions across inspector/suite finalization, missing fixture timeout context, and two authorization-helper maintainability findings.\n+- Recurring families: structural credential safety recurred and was repaired across both affected finalization consumers. The fixture diagnostic and authorization maintainability families were repaired at their shared helper boundaries.\n+- Clean streak: `0` (reset by new/actionable roots, a recurring family, this code-changing round, and the failed required check in the sole snapshot).\n+- Head stability before mutation: the complete snapshot stayed at `1da218dd32d80731fb3d59349e83bd58656f97d4` throughout assessment and local verification. Final local/remote/PR head evidence will be recorded after the one allowed push and one allowed comparison.\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170/.conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1790057191048,"completed_at_ms":1790057191049}}
